2 CONT *'''A genealogical and heraldic history of the extinct and dormant baronetcies ...    By John Burke, Sir Bernard Burke
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=LKIKAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA87&lpg=PA87&dq=George+Browne+1483&source=bl&ots=4TOUz1a9fJ&sig=hQxyWw8O05RE7JqgevDemme1ruY&hl=en&ei=rM_lS47ZC4L6sgP0n_XQCw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=2&ved=0CBkQ6AEwATg
2 CONC K#v=onepage&q=George%20Browne%201483&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 87
2 CONT *   SIR ANTHONY BROWNE, created a knight of the Bath at the coronation of RICHARD II. married, and had two sons, Sir Richard, his heir, and Stephen, lord mayor of London in 1430. The elder
2 CONT *   SIR ROBERT BROWNE, living temp. HENRY V. was father of
2 CONT *'''   SIR THOMAS BROWNE, treasurer of the household to HENRY VI. and sheriff of Kent in 1444 and 1460. He m. Eleanor, daughter and sole heir of Sir Thomas Fitz-Alan, of Beechworth Castle, brother of John, Earl of Arundel, and had
2 CONC  issue,
2 CONT **	I. GEORGE (Sir), his heir.
2 CONT **	II. William, whose son removed to Tavistock. This line is extinct.
2 CONT **	III. Robert (Sir), knt. m. Mary, daughter of Sir William Mallet, knt., and had an only daughter and heiress, Eleanor, wife, first, of Sir Thomas Fogge, and secondly, of Sir William Kempe.
2 CONT **	IV. Anthony (Sir), standard-bearer of England, esquire of the body, governor of Queenboro' Castle, and constable fo the castle of Calais. From this eminent person derive the LORDS MONTAGU, the heiress of which distinguished fam
2 CONC ily, the Hon. ELIZABETH MARY BROWN, wedded WILLIAM STEPHEN POYNTZ, esq. M.P. (See BURKE'S Extinct Peerage and Commoners.)
2 CONT **	I. Catherine, m. to Humphry Sackville of Buckhurst.
2 CONT *Sir Thomas was s. by his eldest son,
2 CONT *   SIR GEORGE BROWNE, knt. of Beechworth Castle, sheriff of Kent in 1481, who espousing the cause of the Earl of Richmond, was included in the proclamation for apprehending the Duke of Buckingham and his associates, and being soo
2 CONC n after taken, suffered decapitation in London anno 1483. he m. Elizabeth, daughter of Sir William Pason, and widow of Richard Lord Poynings, and was s. by his son,
2 CONT *_______________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Info from Earls of Arubdel 7.          JOHN d'Arundel ([135 1]-at sea 15/16 Dec 1379, bur Lewes Priory).  He was summoned to parliament in 1377, whereby he is held to have become Lord Arundel.  He was Marshal of England in 1377, a
2 CONC nd 9 Apr 1378.  He was drowned in the Irish Sea, having been shipwrecked after defeating the French fleet off the coast of Cornwall[1 06].  m (17 Feb 1359) as her first husband, ELEANOR Baroness Mautravers, daughter of Sir JOHN Ma
2 CONC utravers & his wife Gwenthlian --- ([1345]-10 Jan 1405, bur [Lewes Priory]).  She was declared co-heiress (eventually sole heiress) of her grandfather Lord Mautravers 16 Feb 1365.  She married secondly (dispensation 9 Sep 1384) as
2 CONC  his second wife,Reynold Cobham Lord Cobham.  John & his wife had four children:  a)          JOHN d'Arundel (30 Nov 1364-14 Aug 1390, bur Missenden Abbey).  He succeeded his father in 1379 as Lord Arundel, but was never summoned 
2 CONC to parliament [107].  m (before 1387) as her first husband,ELIZABETH le Despencer, daughter of EDWARD le Despencer Lord Despencer & his wife Elizabeth Burghersh (-10/11 Apr 1408, bur [Tewkesbury Abbey]).  The Chronica de Fundatori
2 CONC bus et Fundationeof Tewkesbury Abbey names “Cecilia…Elizabeth…Annam…et Margaretam” as the four daughters of “Edwardus…secundus, filius…Edwardi” and his wife, born after their two older brothers, adding that Elizabeth was “dominam 
2 CONC de la Sowch et relictam domini Johannis de Arundell” [108].  She married secondly William La Zouche Lord Zouche of Haryngworth.  John & his wife had four children:  i)           JOHN d'Arundel (Ditt on Manor, Stoke Pogis, Buckingh
2 CONC amshire 1 Aug 1385-21 Apr 1421, bur Arundel).  He succeeded his paternal grandmother in 1405 as Lord Mautravers.  He succeeded his cousin in 1415 as Earl of Arundel.  -         see below.  ii)          EDMUND .  iii)         Sir T
2 CONC HOMAS FitzAlan of Beechwood .  m ---.  The name of Sir Thomas´s wife is not known.  Sir Thomas & his wife had one child:  (a)        ELEANOR .  m  Sir THOMAS Browne .  Treasurer of the household of King Henry V.  b)          WILLI
2 CONC AM .  c)          THOMAS or EDWARD .  d)          HENRY .  e)          MARGARET (-3 Jul 1438).  A manuscript narrating the foundation of Rievall Abbey records that “Willielmus de Roos” married “Margaretam filiam domini Johannis de
2 CONC  Arundell”, by whom he was father of “Johannem, Willielmum, Thomam, Robertum et Ricardum, Beatricem, Aliciam, Margaretam et Elizabetham”, and that he died “apud Belverum 1 Sep 1414” where he was buried[109 ].  m (licence 9 Oct 139
2 CONC 4) WILLIAM de Ros Lord Ros, son of THOMAS de Ros Lord Ros & his wife Beatrice de Stafford of the Earls of Stafford ([1368/69]-Belvoir 1 Sep 1414, bur Belvoir Priory).  
2 CONT
2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/tree/33578497/person/28052814000/media/20?pgnum=1&pg=32914&pgpl=pid%7cpgNum
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Eleanor FITZALAN, daughter and co- heir of Sir Thomas Fitz‑Alan of Beechworth/Betchworth Castle, (the brother of John, Earl of Arundel).  From ca 1431, her name became Browne. She had 7 children with her first husband, Sir Thomas 
2 CONC Browne. After Sir Thomas Browne was arrested and executed for treason, she married Sir Thomas Vaughn. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor and Thomas Browne were ancestors of the poet, Percy Bysshe Shelley. Another descendant of theirs is the American Abolitionist, John Brown.
2 CONT
2 CONT On the death of Eleanor's father, Thomas FitzAlan, Betchworth Castle passed from the FitzAlans to the Brownes, who occupied it until 1690.
2 CONT
