2 CONT
2 CONT ***************************************************************** Eleanor Fitzalan1 F, #184396 Last Edited=17 Aug 2007
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor Fitzalan is the daughter of Sir Thomas Fitzalan.1 She married, firstly, Sir Thomas Browne circa 1431.2 From circa 1431, her married name became Browne.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Eleanor Fitzalan and Sir Thomas Browne 1.Robert Browne2 b. 1435 2.Katherine Browne2 b. 1435 3.Thomas Browne2 b. 1437 4.Sir George Browne+1 b. 1439 5.William Browne2 b. 1441 6.Sir Anthony Browne+1 b. 29 Jun 1443, d. 19 
2 CONC Nov 1506 7.Jane Browne2 b. 1445
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations 1.[S15] George Edward Cokayne, editor, The Complete Baronetage, 5 volumes (no date (c. 1900); reprint, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 1983), volume II, page 28. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Baronetage. 2.
2 CONC [S2313] Rob Underhill, "re: Stanley Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger Lundy, 9 June 2007. Hereinafter cited as "re: Stanley Family." From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p18440.htm#i184396
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Eleanor was a daughter of Sir Thomas FitzAlan of Betchworth, Earl of Arundel and Steward of the Household of King Henry VI. 
2 CONT * Sir Thomas' father was Sir John FitzAlan, 2nd Lord Arundel, born 30 November 1364 and died 14 August 1390. Sir John's lineage can be traced back to King Henry III and his vast Plantagenet ancestry, which includes King John "Lack
2 CONC land," King Henry II and Queen Eleanor of Aquitaine, etc.
2 CONT * Sir Thomas' mother was Elizabeth Despenser, died 10 April 1408. Elizabeth's ancestry can be traced back to the 800s, to the Danish Viking invaders & conquerors of Normandy and consists of numerous barons and earls.
2 CONT
