2 CONT *Last Edited=28 Dec 2008
2 CONT *'''     Anne Browne is the daughter of Sir Anthony Browne and Lady Lucy Neville.1 She married Charles Brandon, 1st Duke of Suffolk, son of Sir William Brandon and Elizabeth Bruyn.1
2 CONT *'''      Her married name became Brandon.1
2 CONT *'''Child of Anne Browne and Charles Brandon, 1st Duke of Suffolk
2 CONT ** 1.Lady Mary Brandon+1 b. 1510, d. bt 1540 - 1544
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S37] BP2003 volume 1, page 1103. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37]
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p24777.htm#i247764
2 CONT *_____________________________
2 CONT *'''Charles Brandon, 1st Duke of Suffolk, 1st Viscount Lisle KG (c.1484 – 22 August 1545) was the son of Sir William Brandon and Elizabeth Bruyn. Through his third wife Mary Tudor he was brother-in-law to Henry VIII. His father wa
2 CONC s the standard-bearer of Henry Tudor, Earl of Richmond (later King Henry VII) and was slain by Richard III in person at the battle of Bosworth Field. Suffolk died of unknown causes at Guildford.
2 CONT *Charles Brandon was the second but only surviving son[1] of Sir William Brandon, Henry Tudor's standard-bearer at the Battle of Bosworth Field, where he was slain by Richard III. His mother, Elizabeth Bruyn (d. March 1494), daugh
2 CONC ter and co-heiress of Sir Henry Bruyn (died 1461).[2][a]
2 CONT *Charles Brandon was brought up at the court of Henry VII. He is described .... etc.
2 CONT *Before 7 February 1507 he married Margaret Neville (born 1466), widow of Sir John Mortimer (d. before 12 November 1504),[12][13][14] and daughter of John Neville, 1st Marquess of Montagu, slain at the Battle of Barnet, by Isabel 
2 CONC Ingaldesthorpe, daughter and heiress of Sir Edmund Ingaldsthorpe, by whom he had no issue. The marriage was declared void about 1507 by the Archdeaconry Court of London, and later by papal bull dated 12 May 1528.[12] Margaret (née
2 CONC  Neville) subsequently married Robert Downes, gentleman.[5][15]
2 CONT *'''In early 1508 in a secret ceremony at Stepney, and later publicly at St Michael's, Cornhill,[5] he married Margaret Neville's niece, Anne Browne (d.1511), daughter of Sir Anthony Browne, Standard Bearer of England 1485, by his
2 CONC  first wife, Eleanor Ughtred,[16] the daughter of Sir Robert Ughtred (c.1428-c.1487) of Kexby, North Yorkshire[17] and Katherine Eure, daughter of Sir William Eure of Stokesley, Yorkshire, by whom he had two daughters:[18]
2 CONT ** Anne Brandon (1507–1557), who married firstly Edward Grey, 4th Baron Grey of Powis,[19] and after the dissolution of this union, Randal Harworth.
2 CONT ** Mary Brandon (1510 – c. 1542), who married Thomas Stanley, 2nd Baron Monteagle.[19]
2 CONT *He contracted to marry Elizabeth Grey, 5th Baroness Lisle (1505–1519). He was thus created 1st Viscount Lisle of the third creation in 1513, but the contract was annulled, and he surrendered the title before 1519 or in 1523.
2 CONT *In May 1515 he married Mary Tudor, Queen Dowager of France (18 March 1496 – 25 June 1533), by whom he had two sons who died young, and two daughters:
2 CONT ** Lord Henry Brandon (11 March 1516 – 1522).[19]
2 CONT ** Lady Frances Brandon (16 July 1517 – 20 November 1559), who married Henry Grey, Marquess of Dorset, by whom she was the mother of Lady Jane Grey.[19]
2 CONT ** Lady Eleanor Brandon (1519 – 27 September 1547), who married Henry Clifford, 2nd Earl of Cumberland.[19]
2 CONT ** Henry Brandon, 1st Earl of Lincoln (c. 1523 – 1 March 1534).[19]
2 CONT *On 7 September 1533 he married Catherine Willoughby, 12th Baroness Willoughby de Eresby (1 April 1520 – 19 September 1580), by whom he had two sons, both of whom died young of the sweating sickness:
2 CONT ** Henry Brandon, 2nd Duke of Suffolk (18 September 1535 – 14 July 1551).[19]
2 CONT ** Charles Brandon, 3rd Duke of Suffolk (1537 – 14 July 1551).[19]
2 CONT *After Brandon's death his widow married Richard Bertie.
2 CONT *He had a number of illegitimate children
2 CONT ** Sir Charles Brandon, who married Elizabeth Pigot, widow of Sir James Strangways.[19]
2 CONT ** Frances Brandon, who married firstly William Sandon, and secondly Andrew Bilsby.[19]
2 CONT ** Mary Brandon, who married Robert Ball of Scottow, Norfolk.[19]
2 CONT *The romance between Mary Tudor and Charles Brandon is fictionalised in When Knighthood Was in Flower, by American author Charles Major  .... etc.
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_Brandon,_1st_Duke_of_Suffolk
2 CONT *______________________________
2 CONT *Sir Anthony Browne (29 June 1443[1] - c. 17 November 1506) was the son of Sir Thomas Browne and Eleanor FitzAlan. He served as standard-bearer to Henry VII, and Lieutenant of Calais.
2 CONT *Anthony Browne, born at Betchworth Castle,[1] was a younger son of Sir Thomas Browne and Eleanor Arundel, daughter of Sir Thomas Arundel, third son of John de Arundel, 2nd Baron Arundel (d. 14 August 1390), and Elizabeth le Despe
2 CONC nser (d. 10 or 11 April 1408). He was a younger brother of Sir George Browne.[2][3]
2 CONT *During the reign of Henry VII, he was Standard Bearer of England,[4] Governor of Queenborough Castle, and Constable of Calais.
2 CONT *He died at Calais. .... etc.
2 CONT *Sir Anthony Browne married firstly Eleanor Ughtred, daughter of Sir Robert Ughtred (c.1428-c.1487)[8][9] of Kexby, North Yorkshire, and Katherine Eure, daughter of Sir William Eure, by whom he had an '''only daughter, Anne Browne
2 CONC , who married Charles Brandon, 1st Duke of Suffolk.[10][9]
2 CONT *He married secondly Lucy Neville, widow of Sir Thomas Fitzwilliam of Aldwark, North Yorkshire, Yorkshire, and daughter of John Neville, 1st Marquess of Montagu, and Isabel Ingaldesthorpe, by whom he had two sons and two daughters
2 CONC :[11][4]
2 CONT ** Sir Anthony Browne (1500-1548); a courtier to Henry VIII.
2 CONT ** Henry Browne.
2 CONT ** Elizabeth Browne, Countess of Worcester, who married, as his second wife, Henry Somerset, 2nd Earl of Worcester.[12] She was the principal witness against Anne Boleyn, and there were rumours that she had been a mistress of Henr
2 CONC y VIII.[13]
2 CONT ** Lucy Browne, who married firstly John Cutts, and secondly Thomas Clifford.
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sir_Anthony_Browne_(died_1506)
