1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Eleanor Browne''', c.1491-after August 21, 1560 was the daughter of Robert Browne (b.c.1433) of Chilham, Kent and Mary or Margaret '''Mallet'''. She married first Thomas Fogge, porter of Calais (d.August 16,1512
2 CONC ), by whom she had two daughters, Anne and Alice, and second Sir William Kempe (c.1487-January 28, 1535) of Ollantigh, Kent and Spains Hall in Finchingfield, Essex. Their children were Emeline (d. before 1538), Thomas (d. March 7,
2 CONC  1591), John, Edward, Anthony (d.1597), Francis (d.1597), George (d.1570+), Cecily, Faith, Mary, and Margaret. As Eleanor Kempe, Eleanor served in Katherine Parr's household from 1543-1547 and was one of the longest serving and mo
2 CONC st loyal of Mary Tudor’s ladies. She was part of Mary’s household by 1547 and was still there in 1558 when the queen died. Eleanor’s will is dated August 21, 1560.
