2 CONT >The estate descended in Sir Hugh's direct male line for seven generations. In 1540 the owner of the house, another Sir Hugh Hastings, died without a male heir. His daughter, Ann, married the son of his old friend, Sir Anthony Bro
2 CONC wne, Henry VIII's Master of the Horse and owner of Battle Abbey. Elsing hence passed to the Browne family for the next 400 years.
