2 PLAC Scot's Hall, Kent, England
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Reginald Scott, born 1513 in Scott Hall, Kent England; died February 13, 1553/54 in Scott Hall, Kent England; married Emeline Kempe in Scott Hall, Kent, England."
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Kempe-2 shows varying birth dates etc:
2 CONT Emmeline Kempe, who married Sir Reynold Scott (c.1511 - 16 December 1554) of Scott’s Hall in Smeeth, Kent, probably before 1535 as her son Thomas came into his estates in 1556, suggesting he was of age then.[1] They had one son, S
2 CONC ir Thomas Scott (c.1537 – 30 December 1594), who married Elizabeth Baker, daughter of Sir John Baker (c.1489–1558), Speaker of the House of Commons, and two daughters, Katherine Scott, who married John Baker (c.1531-c.1604), son o
2 CONC f Sir John Baker (c.1489–1558), Speaker of the House of Commons, by whom she was the mother of the chronicler, Sir Richard Baker (c.1568–1645), and Anne Scott, who married Walter Mayney (d.1577) of Spilsill manor, Staplehurst, Ken
2 CONC t.
2 CONT
2 CONT Emmeline Kempe died before 1542, at which date Sir Reynold Scott married secondly, Mary Tuke, the daughter of Sir Brian Tuke (d.1545) of Layer Marney, Essex, by Grissell Boughton (d.1538), daughter of Nicholas Boughton of Woolwich
2 CONC . (See Richardson, Douglas, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd ed., 2011, Vol. IV, pp. 1-3; the ODNB articles on Sir John Baker (c.1489-1558), Sir Richard Baker (c.1568- 1645), and Sir Brian Tuke; and the History of Parliament entry for Jo
2 CONC hn Baker (c.1531- c.1604) at John Baker.)[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Father Sir William Kempe, Sheriff of Kent1,7,8,4,9,6 b. 1487, d. 28 Jan 1539
2 CONT Mother Eleanor Browne1,7,8,4,9,6 b. c 1485
2 CONT Emelyn Kempe was born circa 1517 at of Ollantigh, Wye, Kent, England.10 She married Sir Reginald Scott, Sheriff of Kent, Captain of Calais & Sangatte, son of Sir John Scott, Sheriff of Kent, Burgess of New Romney and Anne Pympe, b
2 CONC efore 1537; They had 1 son (Sir Thomas) and 2 daughters (Katherine, wife of John Baker; & Anne, wife of Walter Mayney).1,7,3,4,5,6 Emelyn Kempe died before 1542.4,6
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT Sir Reginald Scott, Sheriff of Kent, Captain of Calais & Sangatte b. c 1512, d. 16 Dec 1554
2 CONT Children
2 CONT Sir Thomas Scott, Sheriff of Kent+1,4,6 b. c 1537, d. 30 Dec 1594
2 CONT Catherine Scott11,1 b. c 1540 See Will for Reginald Scott for more Children https://archive.org/stream/memorialsoffamil00scot#page/178/mode/2up/search/Reginald+Scott
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT ↑ History of Parliament Online, entry for 'SCOTT, Sir Thomas (c.1535-94), of Scot's Hall, Smeeth, Kent'
2 CONT ↑ THE NATIONAL ARCHIVES PROB 11/43/638, p. 3
2 CONT Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry: A Study in Colonial and Medieval Families, 5 vols, ed. Kimball G. Everingham. Salt Lake City: the author, 2013. vol. IV, pages 279-280, OLLANTIGH 14, Eleanor Brown.
2 CONT “Scott of Scots Hall”, by James Renat Scott, F.S.A., London, 1876.
