1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1509-1558/member/sackville-william-1509-56 SACKVILLE, William (by 1509-56), of Bletchingley and Dorking, Surr.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Family and Education
2 CONT
2 CONT b. by 1509, 1st s. of Edward Sackville of Bletchingley by Jane, da. of Sir Roger Kynaston of Myddle and Hordley, Salop. m. (1) 1535, Rose (d.1545), da. of Sir John Gaynesford of Crowhurst, Surr., wid. of Sir George Puttenham of Sh
2 CONC erfield, Hants, 2s. 1da., (2) disp. 15 Feb. 1546, Eleanor, da. of Thomas Shirley of West Grinstead, Suss., wid. of Henry Browne of Betchworth, Surr. suc. fa. 1535.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Offices Held
2 CONT
2 CONT Yeoman, the chamber by 1530, sewer by 1544-53; escheator, Surr. and Suss. 1544-5; j.p. Surr. 1547-d.; commr. relief 1550; Queen’s trainbearer 1554.2
2 CONT
2 CONT Sackville died intestate on 19 May 1556. He seems to have owed a good deal of money, for his widow cited his debts to the Queen and others in seeking a reversal of judgment for debt against him in the common pleas. His son John, w
2 CONC ho was rising 20 at Sackville’s death, also went to Chancery about part of his inheritance in Cardiganshire.5
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://groups.google.com/g/soc.genealogy.medieval/c/lrs05-MLP9Q
2 CONT SACKVILLE, William (Sakwyle,) esq., and Helinore Browne, of the dioces of
2 CONT Winchester. 15 Feb. 1545/6. Faculty Office of Abp of Canterbury
2 CONT Joseph Foster’s London marriages Licences.1521-1869, p 1173
2 CONT
2 CONT William SACKEVYLE, sewer of the Chamber, and Eleanor his wife, late the
2 CONT wife of Henry, son of Matthew Browne, knight, and Richard BROWNE, [ac:
2 CONT perhaps Henry’s br] v. Thomas BROWNE, son and heir of the said Henry.: Manor of
2 CONT Borough (i.e. Burghclere or Borough Court in Odiham ?), HANTS.
2 CONT (PRO C 1/1315/1)
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT * 1. Date of birth estimated from first reference. C. J. Phillips, Sackville Fam. i. 108 [in copyright]; Vis. Salop (Harl. Soc. xxix), 295; Vis. Surr. (Harl. Soc. xliii), 9, 93-94; Manning and Bray, Surr. i. 592; iii. p. cxxi; Fac
2 CONC . Off. Reg. 1534-49, ed. Chambers, 270; U. Lambert, Bletchingley, ii. 493-5; C142/110/148.
2 CONT * 2.LP Hen. VIII, v, xix, xx, CPR, 1547-8, p. 90; 1553, p. 357; 1553-4, p. 24; 1554-5, p. 357; Stowe 571, f. 30v.
2 CONT * 3.Surr. Arch. Colls. v. 265; LP Hen. VIII, xiv, xix; St.Ch.2/29/151; 3/3/49; Req.2/9/2, 10/228, 15/71; CPR ; 1549-51, p. 108; 1553, pp. 115, 272; Surr. Fines (Surr. Rec. Soc. xix), 83, 84, 93.
2 CONT * 4.LP Hen. VIII, xix, xx; Archaeologia, xii. 379; CPR, 1553, p. 286; Augmentations (Univ. Wales Bd. of Celtic Studies, Hist. and Law ser. xiii), 5.
2 CONT * 5. C1/1469/1, 1473/6; 142/110/148.
