1 OCCU Reverend, Vicar between 1561 and 1616 in Horley, Surrey Co., ENG, Pastor Of The Parish Church In Horley For 50 Years
1 TITL Rev
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} # ID: I28250
2 CONT
2 CONT # Name: William Browne
2 CONT
2 CONT # Sex: M
2 CONT
2 CONT # Birth: FEB 1533/34 in Ifield, Sussex Co., England
2 CONT
2 CONT # Death: 14 NOV 1613 in England
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: John Browne b: ABT 1508 in England
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Jone ?...? b: ABT 1510 in England
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 Magdalene Elficke b: ABT 1538 in England
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. Joseph Browne b: ABT 1560 in England
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. Benjamin Browne b: ABT 1565 in Ifield, Sussex Co., England
2 CONT
2 CONT Rev. William BROWNE was born about 1530 in ENG. (4610) He was educated Pembroke College in 1546 in Cambridge, Cambridge Co., ENG. He was Vicar between 1561 and 1616 in Horley, Surrey Co., ENG. (4611) He died on 14 Nov 1615 in Horl
2 CONC ey, Surrey Co., ENG.(4612)
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to Magdalene (Mrs. William Browne) about 1561 in ENG. (4613) Children were: Rev. Joseph BROWNE, Benjamin BROWNE.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT  WILLIAM2 BROWNE (John1), son of (1) John1 and Mrs. Jane (BROWNE) BROWNE, was born on 1 Feb. 1533/4 in Horley[2, 29], died on 14 Nov. 1613 in Horley[2] and was buried on 16 Nov. 1613 in Horley[2]. He married (1st) in Horley, in 15
2 CONC 60, MAGDALENE ELSICK[31], who was born in 1538 in Horley[2, 27], died on 7 Sept. 1604 in Horley[2, 24], and was buried on 7 Sept. 1604 in Horley. He married (2nd) on 16 Oct. 1604, MARGARET BONNYK, who was born circa 1540. [1, 20]
2 CONT
2 CONT Pastor Of The Parish Church In Horley For 50 Years - http://www.ea.ucla.edu/~jill/gen/html/d0002/g0000046.html#I2073
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of: William2 BROWNE and Magdalene ELSICK:
2 CONT
2 CONT 	11	i.	PHOEBE3 BROWNE, b. circa 1560 in Rusper, Sussex, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT 	12	ii.	JOSEPH BROWNE, b. in 1562 in Horley, Essex, England, d. on 15 Oct. 1633 in Rusper.
2 CONT
2 CONT married (Mrs.) Elizabeth Stone 12 Feb 1606/07, Rusper, Sussex, England - bryant.mills@worldspan.com
2 CONT
2 CONT +	13	iii.	EDWARD, b. in 1570 in Inkberrow, Worcestershire, England, d. on 24 Jan. 1649 in Inkberrow; m. (WK-2) JANE LIDE.
2 CONT
2 CONT 	14	iv.	SARAH BROWNE, b. in 1569 in Horley, Essex.
2 CONT
2 CONT +	15	v.	BENJAMIN, b. on 12 Oct. 1571 in Horley, Surrey, d. on 28 Aug. 1638; m. SARAH LECHFORD on 8 Oct. 1596 in Horley, Surrey.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. kmidyette@qwest.net, "DAR Application for Marion Pettegrow".
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. www.teleport.com/ddonahue/donahue; bryant.mills@worldspan.com says Feb-1533/34 3. www.teleport.com/ddonahue/donahue; bryant.mills@worldspan.com 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. www.teleport.com/ddonahue/donahue; bryant.mills@worldspan.com
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. www.teleport.com/ddonahue/donahue; bryant.mills@worldspan.com says Feb-1533/34
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. www.teleport.com/ddonahue/donahue; stan page@bigfoot.com
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Pastor Of The Parish Church In Horley For 50 Years - http://www.ea.ucla.edu/~jill/gen/html/d0002/g0000046.html#I2073 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT From WikiTree http://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Browne-545
2 CONT
2 CONT "Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT The father of Rev. Joseph Browne, clerk and pastor of the parish of Rusper, and of Rev. Benjamin Browne of the parish of Ifleld, both parishes in co. Sussex, was the Rev. William Browne, who for over fifty years was pastor of the 
2 CONC parish church in Horley, co. Surrey, Eng. Queen Mary's death occurred in 1558, and although Mr. Browne's incumbency of the parish dates only from June 26, 1561, under the patronage of Queen Elizabeth, and in the third year of her 
2 CONC reign, yet his early years were contemporary with the life and reign of Queen Mary. He died Nov. 14,1615.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the History of Surrey, by Manning and Bray, three folio volumes, published in London. 1809, is a very full description and history of this old church in Horley, where the aged pastor and his two wives were buried. The first inc
2 CONC umbent of this church, Walter de Stoteford, was instituted Jan. 21, 1283.
2 CONT
2 CONT In vol. 2, p. S02, appears a copy of an inscription in Latin, Including a family chart also in Latin, as it appeared on a Sussex black marble stone against the north wall of the Chancel: 
2 CONT
2 CONT MEMORI/E SACRUM OVURL' BROWN" PASTOR HU'8 KCL'E P'SPACIUM QUINQUAGINT' ANNORUM OBIIT 14° MOVRMBR18 1615, MAGDALENE UXOR EJUS PRIMA EXPIRAVIT SEPTLMO SEPTEMB' 1604, ET MAKGAKETA SPOU8A ULTIMA CECIDIT 17° IT.IIK. 1611.
2 CONT
2 CONT Reverend William Browne, born in England, in February 1534, died in Horley, Surrey, England, 14 Nov 1613, aged seventy-nine years and eight months. Her married first, about 1560, Magdalen ______, who was buried in Horley, 7 Sept 1
2 CONC 604. He married secondly, Margaret _____, who was buried there, 17 Feb 1611-12.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rev. William Browne was Vicar of Horley from 1563 to 1613. He was probably that William Browne who matriculated a pensioner from Pembroke College in March 1546. (Alumni Cantabrigiensis.)
2 CONT
2 CONT The Register of Horley, between 1578 and 1645, cites but three Browne burials:
2 CONT
2 CONT *     1604 Madlyn Browne the wife [of] Wm Browne was buryed the 7 September 
2 CONT *     1611-12 Margaret Browne wife of William Browne was buried the 17 of February 
2 CONT *     1613 Mr William Browne clerke vicar of Horley having lived there the space of fiftie years being of the age  of fourescore years lacking foure monthes departed this mortall life and fourtenth day of November and was buryed t
2 CONC he 16th of the same month.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources accessed 8/28/14
2 CONT # Family Central http://www.familycentral.net/index/search.cfm?ref1=4741:5677
2 CONT # RootsWeb's World Connect http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=elsangel7&id=I19879
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Reverend Browne was vicar of the parish church in Horley, Surrey, England for about fifty years (1563-1613).
