1 OCCU Clothier
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1540 - Married
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/LDYQ-6PT/details
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=124342155
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	1510 Suffolk, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 	Dec., 1579 Suffolk, England
2 CONT
2 CONT John Mawle of Stoke Nayland, Suffolk, England was probably born in Stoke Nayland about 1510. He was most likely the son of John Mawle, senior, who was buried at Stoke Nayland in 1560. There was a Christine "wife of John Maull" who
2 CONC  was was buried just after the elder John. She was probably the wife of John senior and the mother of John junior. The wife who survived John junior, was the mother of his children, and died in 1586 was named Margaret. There is a 
2 CONC hint in her will that her family name was Abbes, in which case she was probably the daughter of George Abbes of Stoke Nayland.
2 CONT
2 CONT John junior was a prosperous clothier who owned considerable property in the Stoke Nayland area. From their wills, it can be presumed that John junior died in late 1579 and Margaret died in 1586. John the son is buried in the chur
2 CONC chyard of St. James' Church in Nayland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Spouse:
2 CONT   Margaret Abbes Mawle (1520 - 1587)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Children:
2 CONT   Margaret Mawle Barker (1540 - 1590)*
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: St James Churchyard Nayland Babergh District Suffolk, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Created by: Jauers Record added: Jan 29, 2014 Find A Grave Memorial# 124342155
