1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Frances, da. of Lord John Grey of Pirgo, Essex, married William Cooke (d 1589) 4s. inc. William Cooke II 3da.
2 CONT
2 CONT >His will, made 6 Mar. 1588 and proved 9 Dec. 1589, is that of a wealthy man. He left £1,000 each to his elder daughters, £800 to the youngest, and smaller legacies to his three sons upon whom he entailed his lands. ‘The afflicted
2 CONC  French and Dutch church’ received £10. Henry Killigrew, Sir Henry Grey, Francis Bacon, James Morice and Francis Rome were executors, and Lord Burghley was overseer. Thomas Windebank and Vincent Skinner were among the witnesses. T
2 CONC his ‘most zealous and virtuous gent.’ died 14 May 1589 and was buried at St. Martin-in-the-Fields on the 19th.2
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1558-1603/member/cooke-william-i-1589
