1 NOTE The name Bowne is a contraction of De Bohun, and the family is evidently descended from Humphrey De Bohun, who arrived in England with William the Conqueror in 1066.  The De Bohuns were Seigneurs de Bohun in the arrondissement of 
2 CONC St. Lo.  There have been Bownes in Derbyshire since the Doomsday Survey, and their principal abode was at Monyash in the Hundred of High Peak, a scant ten miles from the birthplace of the founder of the family on Long Island.
