1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mildred Sackville, daughter of Richard Sackville, Esq., of Withyham, Sussex, by Isabel, daughter of John Digges, Esq., married as his second wife William FitzWilliam, Knight, and they had three sons, Christopher, F
2 CONC rancis and Thomas, and two daughters, Eleanor (wife of Nicholas Strange, Knight,) and: 
2 CONT =Mary (wife of John Shelley). 
2 CONT She was born at Buckhurst, Sussex, England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary FitzWilliam, widow of John Shelley (died 1550), of Michelgrove (in Clapham), Sussex, and daughter of William FitzWilliam, Knight of Milton, Northamptonshire, married second, as his second wife, John Guildford, Knight, of Hemp
2 CONC sted (in Benenden), Kent, Great Bromley, Essex, etc. Bailiff of Winchelsea, Burgess (M>P.) for Gatton, 1529, etc. etc. [3] They had one son, Richard.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==comments==
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of John Shelley, Esq, written 5 Oct 1550 (5 Oct. 4 Edward VI) names " ... my 4 daughters Elinor, Mary, Bryget and Margaret ...".  6, [http://www.geni.com/people/Alma-Anne-Shirley/6000000006444364022 Anne Shelley] wife to Sir 
2 CONC Richard Shirley of Wiston, in-Sussex, Knt.  was born about 1500, daughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/John-Shelly/6000000006444777266?through=6000000006444364022 John Shelley, MP] (b 1448) & [https://www.geni.com/people/Elizab
2 CONC eth-Shelley/6000000006444758292?through=6000000006444364022 Elizabeth Michelgrove].  The pedigree appears in error.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Douglas Richardson, Mary FitzWilliam was the daughter of William's second wife, Mildred Sackville. William and his first wife Anne Hawes had two daughters, Anne and Ellizabeth (wife of Thomas Brudenell, Knight), and t
2 CONC wo sons, William, Knight, and Richard, Esq. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: http://www.wikitree.com/wiki/FitzWilliam-245
2 CONT
2 CONT John Shelley’s marriage to Mary Fitzwilliam renewed his family’s relationship with Sir Anthony Cooke, a descendant of Henry Belknap, who had married her half-sister.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1509-1558/member/shelley-william-1479-1549
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://fortunatusfamilia.com.au/getperson.php?personID=I08544&tree=tree1
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of John Shelley of Michelgrove, Sussex 27 April 1551 PROB 11/34
2 CONT
2 CONT >JOHN SHELLEY, esq. Vol. 94, No. 53. Lewes, 5 Oct. (? 5) Edward VI. Died 4 Edward VI. Heir, son William S., aged 12. Lands in Shepley. J. S., son and heir of "William Shelley, knt., Mary, wife of J. S. and daughter of "Wm. FitzWil
2 CONC liams, knt. J. S. seized of manor of Knell, co. Sussex. Made will 8 Aug. 1550 as J. S. of Mychelgrove, esq. to be buried in Church of Clapham my manor of Stondon Hall, co. Essex, my manors of Wolston and Marston, co. Warwick, Mary
2 CONC  my wife my manor of Chalfyn, co. Herts, my uncle Kychard Shelley's lands in Eudgwicke, my brother Thomas S. and Mary his wife son William under 21 my daughters and younger children my two sons John S. and Eichard S. my manors of 
2 CONC Exton Bassett and Luces in co. Wilts to son Eichard my father S r W m Shelley my 4 daughters Elinor, Mary, Bryget and Margaret my sister Margaret ray uncle parson Shelley my uncle Edward Shelley.
2 CONT
