1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://groups.google.com/g/soc.genealogy.medieval/c/lrs05-MLP9Q
2 CONT Sister "Marye Dannet" named in the will of Katherine (Browne) Hill was
2 CONT presumably her Sackville half-sister.
2 CONT
2 CONT I find there is marriage license issued 3 Oct. 1582 to Thomas Dannett,
2 CONT Esq., of the City of London, and Mary Sackville, spinster, of same
2 CONT [Reference: Huntingdon Library Quarterly, 5 (1941): 289].
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Sackville was evidently the daughter of William Sackville, of
2 CONT Bletchingley and Polesden Lacy (in Dorking), Surrey, Burgess (M.P.)
2 CONT for Bletchingley, Surrey, 1542, Yeoman of the Chamber, before 1530,
2 CONT Sewer of the Chamber, before 1544–53, Escheator of Surrey and Sussex,
2 CONT 1544–5, Queen’s trainbearer, 1554, by his 2nd wife, Eleanor, daughter
2 CONT of Thomas Shirley, of West Grinstead, Sussex.
2 CONT
2 CONT I assume Mary Sackville is the Mary Sackville, daughter of Sackville,
2 CONT baptized 22 Nov. 1556, at Dorking, Surrey, which record is an item
2 CONT extracted from the parish registers and found in the International
2 CONT Genealogical Index. If so, Mary was presumably born posthumously, as
2 CONT her father, William Sackville, died 19 May 1556.
2 CONT
2 CONT KATHERINE HILL [ac: nee Browne] of Dorking, widow, gentlewoman. 12 April,
2 CONT 38 Eliz. [1596] Brothers Roger Browne, Richard Browne of Cranley. [ac:
2 CONT Cranleigh] Niece Hellen Browne dau. of brother Richard. Sister Blakden.
2 CONT Son-in-law Richard Hill. Sister Marye Dannet. Brother Alexander Browne and
2 CONT his dau. Katherine Browne. God-son Edmonde Browne son of my brother Jasper
2 CONT Browne. Niece Elizabeth Browne dau. of Jasper Browne. God-dau. Katherine
2 CONT Chamberlaine. John Stone’s widow. Cousin Carrant. [ac: Dannett?] Maid
2 CONT Bennet Gonner, Cousin Elynor Strely. Niece Ellinor Browne dau. of Alexander
2 CONT Browne. Residue to Edmonde Browne son of Jasper Browne and Katherine
2 CONT Chamberlaine god-dau. Executors. Ring with a signet. Witn. John Muncke,
2 CONT William Symon, Ann Dannett and Mary Fitzwilliam, Alexander Brown. Proved 17
2 CONT April 1596.
