1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sir Edward Bray, MP, married 3rd, by May 1539, Jane, da. of Sir Matthew Browne† of Betchworth, Surr., wid. of Sir Francis Poynings.  He died Dec 1 1558:
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Bray made his will on 16 Aug. 1558 and died on the following 1 Dec. He appointed as executors his wife and his brother-in-law George Browne, and as supervisor John Caryll. He asked to be buried in Cranleigh church, of which he w
2 CONC as patron, and bequeathed the bulk of his lands to his wife, with the proviso that if his elder son Edward interfered with her possession she was to have all his lands in fee simple. Edward Bray was to receive a manor at Ewhurst i
2 CONC n Surrey on condition that he discharged a debt of £60, for which he had already received money only to spend it elsewhere. Bray’s mistrust of his son was justified: for many years after his death Edward Bray, who fell progressive
2 CONC ly into debt, disputed the terms of the will.8"
2 CONT
2 CONT -------
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1509-1558/member/bray-sir-edward-1492-1558
2 CONT * * 8.  PCC 47 Welles; C142/118/8.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT The portrait, painted in 1735 is one of the daughters. As more information comes we should learn which daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
