2 CONT
2 CONT Individual Record FamilySearch™ Ancestral File v4.19 
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry CAPELL (AFN: 9GVN-98)  Pedigree 
2 CONT  SeFamily and Education bap. 3 May 1579, 1st s. of Sir Arthur Capell (d.1632) of Rayne, Essex and Hadham, Herts. by his 1st w. Margaret, da. of Lord John Grey of Pirgo. Gd.-s. of Henry Capell I. m. (1) 11 Aug. 1600, Theodosia, da.
2 CONC  of (Sir) Edward Montagu I of Boughton, Northants., 2s. 4da.; (2) Dorothy (d.1651), da. of John Aldersey of Aldersey, Cheshire and of London, wid. of Sir Thomas Hoskins of Oxted, Surr., 1s. 3da. Kntd. 1603.
2 CONT
2 CONT Offices Held
2 CONT
2 CONT J.p. Essex by 1622.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography Capell’s return for Boston is explained by an entry in the minute book of the corporation under 1 Oct. 1601:
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry Capell, at the suit of Mr. Roger Manners [I] esquire, is elected ... upon condition that he shall come to be made a freeman of the borough before Friday next. This condition was fulfilled on 9 Oct. Capell’s father, a friend 
2 CONC of Sir Robert Cecil, was an executor of Manners’s will in 1607.
2 CONT
2 CONT Capell died intestate and v.p. at Little Hadham on 29 Apr. 1622 and was buried at Rayne. He left as his heir a son Arthur, aged 18. Administration of his goods was granted to his widow on 8 May 1622.
2 CONT
2 CONT Vis. Essex (Harl. Soc. xiii), 171; Vis. Northants. (Harl. Soc. lxxxvii), 137; Vis. Cheshire (Harl. Soc. lix), 5; Chauncy, Herts. i. 313; D. Warrand, Herts. Fams. 92-3, 107; APC, July 1621-May 1623, p. 156; Boston corp. min. bks. 1
2 CONC , f. 379a; PCC 95 Hudleston; VCH Herts. iv. 52; C142/396/148. 
2 CONT
