2 CONC s born in 1603.  His baptism, along with those of his next three siblings are recorded in either Wing, or in Warnham, Sussex, where the Carylls lived.  Mary's baptism has not yet been found, but she is listed as the fifth and youn
2 CONC gest child in a Carryl family tree in an appendix to a comprehensive history of the village of Warnham.  Logically, she could not have been born before 1609.
