2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor Bagenal [1]
2 CONT *F, #264929, 
2 CONT *d. November 1632
2 CONT *Last Edited=24 Jan 2010
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor Bagenal was the daughter of Dudley Bagenal and Mabel Fitzgerald.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, firstly, Sir Thomas Colclough, son of Sir Anthony Colclough and Clare Agard, in 1612.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, secondly, Lucas Plunkett, 1st Earl of Fingall, son of Christopher Plunkett, 8th Lord Killeen and Genet Dillon.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died in November 1632.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1612, her married name became Colclough.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Her married name became Plunkett.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Eleanor Bagenal and Sir Thomas Colclough
2 CONT *1. Anthony Colclough+[2]
2 CONT *2. John Colclough [2]
2 CONT *3. Mabel Colclough [2]
2 CONT *4. Dudley Colclough+[2] b. 1613, d. 1663
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S47] Hugh Montgomery-Massingberd, editor, Burke's Irish Family Records (London, U.K.: Burkes Peerage Ltd, 1976), Bagenal, page 45. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Irish Family Records.
2 CONT *2. [S47] Hugh Montgomery-Massingberd, Burke's Irish Family Records.
