2 CONC  Lord Willoughby de Eresby, and the heirs males of their bodies successively"
2 CONT *suc. by	son
2 CONT *note	Member of Parliament for Reigate 1628-29;  Sheriff of Northamptonshire 1636, when he supported the raising of "ship money";  raised a troop of Horse for the King;  with fines and sequestrations he was said to have lost over 
2 CONC £50,000 in the King's cause;  sold the manor of Coombe Nevill in Kingston-upon-Thames, co. Surrey, and other estates in order to recoup some of the costs
