1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Bridget Fitzgerald:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p5986.htm#i59858
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Bridget FitzGerald [1]
2 CONT *F, #59858, 
2 CONT *b. circa 1590, 
2 CONT *d. between 1661 and 25 December 1682
2 CONT *Last Edited=23 Jun 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.06%
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Bridget FitzGerald was born circa 1590.[2] She was the daughter of Henry FitzGerald, 2nd/12th Earl of Kildare and Lady Frances Howard.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, firstly, Robert O'Donnell, 1st Earl of Tyrconnell before 1606.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, secondly, Nicholas Barnewall, 1st Viscount Barnewall of Kingsland, son of Sir Patrick Barnewall and Mary Bagnall, before 7 July 1617.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died between 1661 and 25 December 1682.[1],[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT From before 1606, her married name became O'Donnell.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT From before 7 July 1617, her married name became Barnewall.[1] As a result of her marriage, Lady Bridget FitzGerald was styled as Viscountess Barnewall of Kingsland on 29 June 1646.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Lady Bridget FitzGerald and Nicholas Barnewall, 1st Viscount Barnewall of Kingsland
2 CONT *1. Henry Barnewall, 2nd Viscount Barnewall of Kingsland+[1] d. 1 Jun 1688
2 CONT *2. Hon. Richard Barnewall+[3]
2 CONT *3. Hon. Mabel Barnewall+[4]
2 CONT *4. Colonel James Barnewall+[5]
2 CONT *5. Mary Barnewall+[6] d. May 1642
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Lady Bridget FitzGerald and Robert O'Donnell, 1st Earl of Tyrconnell
2 CONT *1. Hugh O'Donnell, Baron Donegall [2] b. c 1 Oct 1606, d. c 1 Jul 1642
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 428. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *2. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 2, page 2299. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
