1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Catherine Maunsell1===
2 CONT * b abt 1606 of Margam, Glamorganshire, Wales
2 CONT * daughter of Christopher Maunsell and Anne Worsley.2,1 
2 CONT * married Reverend Marmaduke Mathew.1  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT The same History of Barnstable indicates that little is known about the family of Marmaduke Matthews. They name his wife as Katherine and point out she was a witness of the will of Gabriel Whelden. The History suggest that his chi
2 CONC ldren might have included Michaiah Matthews, another signer of Gabriel Whelden's will. A Mordecai Matthews "was one of the two" [?] who graduated 1655 from Harvard. At the same time, a younger Matthews, perhaps his brother was in 
2 CONC a lower class. Neither was charged tuition after June 8, 1655, supporting the possibility that they returned to England as well. One Mordecai Mathews was a minister at Roinolston in Glamorganshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://daibach-welldigger.blogspot.com/2012/03/puritan-prophet-from-swansea.html Marmaduke Matthews: The Puritan Prophet from Swansea]:
2 CONT
2 CONT While Matthews faithfully served the Colony out of his devotion to the Gospel, his heart seems always to have been filled with an awareness of the greater need which still characterised his homeland, which during the early 1640’s 
2 CONC was being torn apart by civil war. He first considered going home in about 1648, but his '''wife''' refused, saying she was not willing to move ‘from a land of peace to a seat of war and a field of blood’. He was also aware that P
2 CONC arliament had banned preachers like himself because they were not Presbyterian. At about this time, the settlers of Pequot asked him to consider becoming their minister, but Matthews responded to them by saying that that his wife’
2 CONC s ‘unwillingness to go beyond seas in these destructive days’ was still a big reason for him to stay in New England. The invitation from Pequot he saw as a confirmation that he should stay longer, as he put it himself:  ‘to tack a
2 CONC bout ... and harbour in America a while longer’.  However, he declined the invitation from the people of Pequot and went to serve the church in Malden instead, a comunity which is now part of the northern suburbs of the sprawling 
2 CONC city of Boston.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://boards.ancestry.com/thread.aspx?mv=flat&m=961&p=localities.northam.usa.states.massachusetts.counties.plymouth Rev. Matthews of Barnstable, Lynn and Maulden] 
