2 CONT *'''     Mary Kempe was born circa 1593 at Olantigh Manor, Wye, Kent, England; Youngest daughter of 1st marriage.2,3 She married Sir Dudley Digges, Ambassador to Russia, Burgess of Tewkesbury, son of Thomas Digges, Esq., Muster-Ma
2 CONC ster-General of the Armies in the Low Countries and Anne St. Leger, circa 1609 at of Chilham, Kent, England; They had 8 sons (Thomas, Esq; John; Dudley; Francis; Edward, Esq; Leonard; Herbert; & Richard) & 3 daughters (Anne, wife 
2 CONC of Anthony Hammond, Esq., & of Sir George Juxon; Elizabeth, wife of Arnold Brayning; & Mary).2,3,4,5,6,7 Mary Kempe was buried on 1 May 1631 at Chilham, Kent, England.4,6
2 CONT *'''Family	Sir Dudley Digges, Ambassador to Russia, Burgess of Tewkesbury b. c 1583, d. 18 Mar 1639
