1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Anna Kempe1
2 CONT *'''F, #52487, b. 19 June 1589
2 CONT *Father      Sir Thomas Kempe1 b. 7 Nov 1551, d. b 10 Dec 1607
2 CONT *Mother     Dorothy Thompson1,2 b. c 1555
2 CONT *'''     Anna Kempe was christened on 19 June 1589 at Olantigh Manor, Wye, Kent, England.1 She was buried on 13 March 1631 at Swavesey Church, Cambridge, Cambridgeshire, England.1
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S61] Unknown author, Family Group Sheets, Family History Archives, SLC.
2 CONT * 2.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 277.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1746.htm#i52487 _______________________
2 CONT *    Sir Thomas Kempe was christened on 7 November 1551 at Wye, Kent, England.2,4,7 He married Anne circa 1582 at of Kent, England; Three children born to this marriage, including 1 son, Isaac.2,4 Sir Thomas Kempe married Dorothy 
2 CONC Thompson, daughter of John Thompson, Esq., Sheriff of Bedfordshire & Buckinghamshire, Burgess of New Windsor, Auditor of the Exchequer and Dorothy Gilbert, before 19 June 1589 at of Chilham, Kent, England; They had 4 daughters (''
2 CONC 'Anne, wife of Sir John Cutts'''; Dorothy, wife of Sir Thomas Chicheley; Mary, wife of Sir Dudley Digges; & Amy, wife of Sir Henry, 1st Baronet Skipwith).2,3,4,5,6,7,8 Sir Thomas Kempe died before 10 December 1607; Buried at Wye, 
2 CONC Kent.2,4,7
2 CONT *Family 1      Anne d. b 19 Jun 1589
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Isaac Kempe10 b. 1 Oct 1586
2 CONT *Family 2      Dorothy Thompson b. c 1555
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **'''Anna Kempe10 b. 19 Jun 1589
2 CONT **Amy Kempe2,11,4,5,7,8 b. 6 Aug 1591
2 CONT **Dorothy Kempe2 b. c 1592
2 CONT **Mary Kempe+12,2,3,4,6,7 b. c 1593
2 CONT
