1 NOTE {geni:about_me} XI. Agnes, born on the sixteenth of January, 1547, married in 1566 Sir Edward Stradling,q of St. Donat’s. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Stradling,_Edward_(DNB00)_ DNB] Dictionary of National Biography, 1885-1900, Volume 55 "Stradling, Edward" by Daniel Lleufer Thomas
2 CONT
2 CONT >He died without issue on 15 May 1609, leaving his estate to his adopted son and great-nephew, Sir John Stradling [q. v.], who had married his wife's niece. He was buried in the private chapel at St. Donat's, where his heir and hi
2 CONC s widow Agnes, second daughter of Sir Edward Gage of Hengrave, Suffolk, whom he married in 1566, placed an inscription to his memory; she died 1 Feb. 1624, and was buried in the same chapel.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
