1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 6. John Shelley of Michelgrove, Esq. the eldest son, married Mary, daughter of Sir William Fitz-Williams, Knt. and Maud his wife, daughter of Sir Richard Sackvile of Buckhurst, Knt. (who surviving him, married Sir 
2 CONC Robert Guldeford, Knt.) by whom he had two sons and six daughters; 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==1, William, ==
2 CONT
2 CONT who married to his first wife, Jane, daughter and heir of Lingen of Sutton, in Herefordshire, Esq. and secondly Mary, daughter of Thomas Wriothesley, earl of Southampton, relict of ■ Lister, Esq. son and heir of Sir Martin Lister,
2 CONC  Knt. but left no issue. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was attainted for treason, committed Dec. 15, 25 Eliz. whereby his estate was forfeited to the crown during his life, for he did not die till April 15, 39 Eliz. when, by virtue of an entail, the estates both in Sussex and Warwi
2 CONC ckshire descended to his brother John, of whom hereafter. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Wriothesley (d. December 1561), who married firstly, Richard Lyster, grandson of Sir Richard Lyster, and secondly, William Shelley of Michelgrove;[9] 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 9.  Dugdale reverses the order of her marriages.
2 CONT
2 CONT John (died 15 December 1550), father of William (not the same person as William Shelley of Hertford, also a prisoner in the Tower in 1580), who was attainted 15 December 1582 for complicity in Charles Paget's treasons, but not exe
2 CONC cuted, and died 15 April 1597, being succeeded by his son John, created a baronet in 1611;
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://fortunatusfamilia.com.au/getperson.php?personID=I08544&tree=tree1
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of Sir William Shelley of Clapham, Sussex Date 08 February 1549 Catalogue reference PROB 11/32
2 CONT Will of John Shelley of Michelgrove, Sussex 27 April 1551 PROB 11/34
2 CONT
2 CONT >WILLIAM SHELLEY, esq. Vol. 124, No. 164. (Proof of age.) Clapham, 19 Sept. 1 Elizabeth. Jurors state that W. S., son and heir of John Shelley, esq., deceased, is aged 21 years and 5 days on this date.
2 CONT
2 CONT (date of birth is 14 September 1537)
2 CONT
2 CONT From A P Baggs, C R J Currie, C R Elrington, S M Keeling and A M Rowland, 'Clapham', in A History of the County of Sussex: Volume 6 Part 1, Bramber Rape (Southern Part), ed. T P Hudson (London, 1980), pp. 10-21 http://www.british-
2 CONC history.ac.uk/vch/sussex/vol6/pt1/pp10-21 [accessed 9 June 2015].
2 CONT
2 CONT >John's son William was imprisoned in 1580 for recusancy, (fn. 86) and was attainted in 1586-7 for his part in Throckmorton's plot. (fn. 87) Sentence of death was commuted, however, (fn. 88) and he was released from the Tower in 1
2 CONC 596. (fn. 89) The family estates were leased by the Crown to John and Henry Shelley, Sir John Caryll and others, (fn. 90) but in 1604 they were restored to William Shelley's nephew John on payment of £11,000. (fn. 91)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===comments===
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth:	 September 14, 1518 Michel Grove, Sussex, England removed June 2015.  His uncle [http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1509-1558/member/shelley-richard-151314-87 Richard Shelley], younger brother of his father, ha
2 CONC s known dates of 1513/14 - 1587
2 CONT
