1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Margaret Shelley==
2 CONT * Birth:	abt 1540  Mitchelgrove, Sussex, England
2 CONT * Parents:	John Shelley (1506 - 1550) & Mary FitzWilliam
2 CONT * Husband:  Edward Gage  of Bently, Sussex, England
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://books.google.com/books?id=fVE9AQAAMAAJ&lpg=PA102&ots=eAHnxT4JFJ&dq=James%20Gage%20-%20married%20Jane%2C%20daughter%20of%20James%20Delves%20and%20widow%20of%20John%20Bellingham.&pg=PA102#v=onepage&q=James%20Gage%20-%2
2 CONC 0married%20Jane%2C%20daughter%20of%20James%20Delves%20and%20widow%20of%20John%20Bellingham.&f=true The Gages of Bentley, Framfield, Sussex]:
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Gage, his [James Gage & Jone Delves] heir, married Margaret, daughter of John (not William) Shelley, of Michelgrove (cf. 10 S. W. '56). There is an odd divergence in the published accounts of their monument in Framfield Chu
2 CONC rch, and perhaps some Sussex reader 'of N. &. will give a full description of it. According to the Rev. H. R. Hoe-re (Sussex Arch. Coll., iv. 296—7), “ behind him are three sons, behind her five daughters, above are their names.” 
2 CONC On the other hand, the Rev. E. Turner says (ibid., xxiii. 159) that the brass has “ the figures of a man_and a woman and of their six children upon it ” ; and that the first half of the inscription runs :—
2 CONT
2 CONT >" the body of Edward Gage, Esq', and Margaret his wife (daughter of Sir [sic] John Shelley, of Michelgrove). who had three sons and seven daughters, and died Anno Domini 1595."
2 CONT
2 CONT The three sons and one of the daughters appear to have predeceased their father. The six surviving daughters, together With their mother, are given in the pedigree Harl. Soc. Publ., liii. 9, to their father’s cousin John, eldest s
2 CONC on of Sir Edward Gage, K.B., of Firle; and in Ga e’s ‘ Hengrave ’ (p. 237) and in Burke’s Peerage’ their mother is represented as wife of the said Sir Edward’s fifth son Edward, and mother of his children John and Elizabeth. Broth
2 CONC er Foley (‘ Records S.J.,’ v. 78) supposes the tomb to be that of Edward Gage of Firle !
2 CONT
2 CONT Of the six surviving daughters, 
2 CONT * (1) Mary married John Crispe, of Ore, Sussex. 
2 CONT * (2)1 Dorothy, whose name also occurs as Ruth, married Thomas Alcock (whom Be , ‘ Sussex Genealogies,’ 294, calls Alwick), of Rampton, Cambs, who in April, 1593, had been about 32 weeks in the Marshalsea for recusancy (Strype, ‘ 
2 CONC Ann.,’ iv. 258). 
2 CONT * (3) Margaret married George Smyth, of the Bishopric of Durham. 
2 CONT * (4) Mildred married Augustine Belson, of Stokenchurch, Oxon, a recusant (‘Cal. S. P. Dom., 1598—1601,’ p. 524), and surviving him died in 1624, aged 49, and was buried at Clapham, Sussex, (Cartwright, ‘ Sussex,’ ii. 85). * (5) P
2 CONC hilippa married Andrew Bendlowes, of Essex, also a recusant (‘ Cal. S. P.,’ 100. cit.) 
2 CONT * (6) '''Elizabeth married Anthony Skinner, of Rowing~ ton''', Warwickshire, who received licence to go beyond the seas with his family on 12 Aug.. 1606 (‘Cal. S. P. Dom. Add, 1580—1625,’ p. 486).
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://fortunatusfamilia.com.au/getperson.php?personID=I08544&tree=tree1
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of John Shelley of Michelgrove, Sussex 27 April 1551 PROB 11/34
2 CONT
2 CONT >JOHN SHELLEY, esq. Vol. 94, No. 53. Lewes, 5 Oct. (? 5) Edward VI. Died 4 Edward VI. Heir, son William S., aged 12. Lands in Shepley. J. S., son and heir of "William Shelley, knt., Mary, wife of J. S. and daughter of "Wm. FitzWil
2 CONC liams, knt. J. S. seized of manor of Knell, co. Sussex. Made will 8 Aug. 1550 as J. S. of Mychelgrove, esq. to be buried in Church of Clapham my manor of Stondon Hall, co. Essex, my manors of Wolston and Marston, co. Warwick, Mary
2 CONC  my wife my manor of Chalfyn, co. Herts, my uncle Kychard Shelley's lands in Eudgwicke, my brother Thomas S. and Mary his wife son William under 21 my daughters and younger children my two sons John S. and Eichard S. my manors of 
2 CONC Exton Bassett and Luces in co. Wilts to son Eichard my father S r W m Shelley my 4 daughters Elinor, Mary, Bryget and Margaret my sister Margaret ray uncle parson Shelley my uncle Edward Shelley.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==comments==
2 CONT
2 CONT last updated April 2015
2 CONT
2 CONT Not to be confused with [http://www.geni.com/people/wife-of-Edward-Gage/6000000033193353679 wife of Edward Gage] of Firle.
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p2432.htm#i73087
2 CONT **Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, 2nd Edition 
2 CONT **Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition
2 CONT
2 CONT "Sir William Shelley, Justice of the Court of Common Pleas & Alice Belknap had 7 sons (including John; Sir Richard; Sir Edward; Thomas; & Sir James) and 7 '''(sic: 6)''' daughters (including Katherine, wife of Henry Browne, Esq; E
2 CONC lizabeth, wife of Sir Roger Copley; Frances; ..,)
2 CONT
2 CONT  > "& Margaret, wife of Edward Gage)." This is incorrect; there's a source misprint.  The Margaret Shelley who married Edward Gage was the daughter of JOHN Shelley of Michelgrave.
2 CONT
