1 NAME William /Browne/ III
2 GIVN William
2 SURN Browne
2 NSFX III
2 _MARNM Browne
1 NAME William /Browne/
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 29 NOV 1593
2 PLAC Rusper, Sussex, , England
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 2 JUL 1650
2 ADDR
3 CITY Hempstead
3 CTRY New Netherland
1 OCCU Schoolmaster at Rusper, England
1 TITL Rev.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===William Browne
2 CONT * Birth Date: before  Dec 5, 1585455
2 CONT * Birth Place: Harley, Surrey, England
2 CONT * Death Date: 1660
2 CONT * Death Place: Long Island, New York
2 CONT * Father: Rev.  Joseph Browne (ca1562-<1633)
2 CONT * Mother: Margery  Patching (<1564-<1616)
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouses
2 CONT 1Jane Mills456
2 CONT Father Thomas  Mills (-ca1629)
2 CONT Mother Unknown
2 CONT Marr Date Jun 20, 1611
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT # Joseph 
2 CONT #  John
2 CONT #  Jane
2 CONT #  Phoebe (<1620-1664)
2 CONT #  Mary
2 CONT #  Thomas
2 CONT #  Henry
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT William Brown married Jane (Mills) Burgess on June 20 in either the year 1611 or 1617 in Rusper, County Sussex, England depending on the transcription utilized.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT William Browne, schoolmaster of Rusper in 1627, who “came over” in 1645, finally settled at Southampton by 1648, and died there in 1650. There's a paper that proves William Browne came from Rusper:
2 CONT
2 CONT “April 3d, 1627. Mary Worffelde, widow of William Worffelde, of Rusper, Sussex Co., he late deceased, yeoman. Bound in £640 – to Wm. Browne, Schoolmaster of Rusper, to faithfully administer and execute the last will and testament 
2 CONC of William Worffelde; on her bond are Wm. Browne & William Willett of Horsham, Sussex Co., yeomen. Mentions George, Lord Bishop of Chirchester, signed in presence of Joseph Browne, John Bardine (?) and Wm. Simined (?).”
2 CONT
2 CONT “The following I took from my father’s, Joshua Hempstead’s, Esqr’s. papers: My grandmother was the daughter of old William Brown; he (formerly) lived in Essex (Surrey), and town of Rusper, in England. Come (He came) over to New En
2 CONC gland in the year 1645; her (Phebe Lee’s) grandmother came also, and (said) grandmother died with the small-pox on board, and the (William Brown and wife’s) eldest son John.”
2 CONT
2 CONT “In 1648, Oct 7, William Browne, with others, was chosen freeman of Southampton.” 
2 CONT
2 CONT “1648, Nov. 6, William Browne and Robert Marvin, with others, in division of the “great plaine” Southampton.” 
2 CONT
2 CONT “1648, Feby. 8 (1649-50) Mr. William Browne, and ten others, are bound to pay for the house which they have bought from John Mulford.” 
2 CONT
2 CONT “Mch. 8, 1649 (1649-50) William Browne, and others, freeman of Southampton.” 
2 CONT
2 CONT “1650, July 2, William Browne, Register, Southampton.” 
2 CONT
2 CONT “1650, July 23, Administration granted to Robert Marvin and Mary his wife, upon estate of William Browne, just deceased. Evidently then he died quite suddenly, or after a brief illness, between July 2-23, 1650.” 
2 CONT
2 CONT “1650, July 24th. Inventory of his estate, total £160-0-8, includes Books £5, suggestive of William Browne, ex-schoolmaster of Rusper, England.” 
2 CONT
2 CONT It seems fair to conclude that William Browne was a man of education and superior social rank, measured by Colonial standards, though he possessed but a moderate fortune; that he first appeared in Southampton, L. I., probably when
2 CONC  advanced in years, with his son-in-law Robert Marvin in 1648; that since he owned no land in town, he resided with Marvin; that he was a merchant or trader, Secretary to Supreme Court and Register. He died in July, 1650, between 
2 CONC the 2nd and 23rd day.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had 3 Children that come over:
2 CONT * “Eldest son John,” died of small-pox on voyage over to America 1645.
2 CONT * Henry b. 1625; died 1703, Feb. 20, Providence R.I.; m. (1) Waite Waterman, dau. of Richard; m. (2) Hannah (Field) Mathewson, widow of James Mathewson, and dau. of John Field, lived at Providence, had three (3) sons (See Austin’s
2 CONC  Gen. Dict., R.I. for a complete account).
2 CONT * Phebe b. ---; d. 1664, Dec. 22nd, at Northampton, Mass; m. (1) Thomas Lee, in England; he died 1645 with small-pox leaving three (3) children, Phebe, Jane and Thomas; m. (2) about 1657 Greenfield Larrabee he died leaving five (5
2 CONC ) children, Greenfield, John, Elizabeth, Joseph and Sarah; Joseph died young; m. (3) about 1661, James Cornish and had two sons, James and one still-born, with which Phebe (Brown) Lee-Larrabee-Cornish died in child-bed at Northamp
2 CONC ton.
2 CONT * Mary b. --; d. --; m. 1648 Robert Marvin, lived at Southampton and Hempstead, L.I.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT * Records and Papers of the New London County Historical Society, Volume 3
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Potential Parents:
2 CONT Joseph Browne b. c 1562, d. 15 Oct 1633
2 CONT Margery Patching b. 17 Feb 1564, d. 15 Nov 1605</line><line /><line>2/2/21</line><line /><line>***Update***
2 CONT Reverand Joseph Browne     1561–1633     LBQX-VSZ​​
2 CONT Marriage: 15 February 1584 Horley, Surrey, England
2 CONT Margery-Mary Patching     1564–1605     LBQC-KH3</line><line /><line>3/6/22
