1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Sarah Browne==
2 CONT * Birth: ABT 1600 in Ifield, Sussex Co., England
2 CONT * Death: in England
2 CONT * Father: Benjamin Browne b: ABT 1565 in Ifield, Sussex Co., England
2 CONT * Mother: Sara Lechford b: 1573 in Ifield, Sussex Co., England
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT # Pardon Tillinghast b: ABT 1593 in Streat, Sussex Co., England Married: BEF 1622 in Ifield, Sussex Co., England
2 CONT
2 CONT Children include
2 CONT
2 CONT *    1. Has Children Pardon Tillinghast b: 16 MAR 1621/22 in Beachey Head, Sussex Co., , England
2 CONT *    2. Has No Children John Tillinghast b: ABT 1625 in England
2 CONT *    3. Has No Children Sarah Tillinghast b: 15 NOV 1627 in England
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT SARAH4 BROWNE (Benjamin3, William2, John1), daughter of (15) Benjamin3 and Sarah (LECHFORD) BROWNE, was born on 24 Aug. 1600 in Ifield[1], and died between 1629 and 1710. She married in Streat, on 26 Nov. 1622, (AJY-2) PARDON JOHN
2 CONC  TILLINGHAST, son of (AJY-1) John and Alice (PARDON) TILLINGHAST, who was born on 29 Jan. 1600 in Streat, and died circa 1665. [1, 20]
2 CONT Children: See (AJY-2) Pardon John TILLINGHAST
2 CONT
2 CONT THE ROYAL ANCESTRY CONNECTION TO THE TILLINGHAST LINE Posted by: Elton L. Powell (ID *****3093) 	Date: August 30, 2002 at 18:56:48
2 CONT   	of 329
2 CONT
2 CONT For many years there has been an effort of some of the Tillinghast descendents to find a blood connection to British Royalty. Unfortunately for some of these they obviously found the earliest effort to make a Royal connection to K
2 CONC ing Edward III which in all cases has turned out to be WRONG. This effort had been put forth by a Dr.Wiess in a set of volumns called, "The American Genealogist", 'TAGS, if you will. The Doctor later admitted his error and stated 
2 CONC that there was no provable connection through a Mrs Tichbourne. As I have stated in other messages, I have not found any marriage between a Tillinghast and a Tichbourne. Right now there are only some 100 messages on this Tillingha
2 CONC st Message board and all could be read in a reasonable length of time. Pay particular attention to these.
2 CONT #'s 25 / 29 / 66 / 68 / 69 / 82 / 94 / 97 / & 99. I am not the expert but I can report on what I have found and I have already passed along this info to others; Mss.Debbie Richardson; Mr.Todd Lawrence; etc. And I stated on where I
2 CONC  found it. But there IS a Tillinghast connection to the Royal Blood of Britain and a Mss Vaughn in Britain researched it. It goes through the wife of the 1st Pardon Tillinghast, the beer barrel maker,[cooper if you will]. Kg EDWAR
2 CONC D I; 1239-1307 -M- Princess MARGARITTE, dau. / Kg. Philip III of France. Issue: THOMAS de BROTHERTON, Earl of Norfolk. 1301-1338 -M- ALICE de HALLES, dau./Sir Roger de Halles. Issue: MARGARET PLANTEGENET, Duchess of Norfolk; -M- J
2 CONC OHN, 4th Baron Seagrave. Issue: ELIZABETH SEAGRAVE, dau.& heir. -M- JOHN, 4th Baron Mowbray Issue: ELEANOR MOWBRAY; -M- JOHN, 5th Baron de Welles. Issue: EDO de WELLES; -M- MAUDE de GREYSTOCK, dau./Ralph, 5th /Baron de Greystock. 
2 CONC Issue: SIR LIONEL de WELLES; 6th Baron de Welles, K. G.{Knight of the Garter]. -M- CECILIA,[or Joan] DAU./ROBERT WATERTON of Methley. Issue: ELEANOR de WELLES, -M- THOMAS, Lord Hoo, K.G./ Chancellor to France. Issue: ANNA de HOO, 
2 CONC dau. & co-heir; -M- Sir ROGER de COPLEY,[15th in descent from King Athelred II. Issue: ANN COPLEY; -M- WILLIAM LUSHER, Lord of Rodsell Manor. Issue: GEORGE LUSHER, Gentleman, -M- Alice...........Issue: ANNE LUSHER; -M- Sir RICHARD
2 CONC  LECHFORD,Knight, of Shellwood Manor in Leigh, Surrey County. Issue: SARAH LECHFORD, -M- Rev. BENJAMIN BROWNE, Vicar of Ifiel County, Sussex. Issue: SARAH BROWNE, bn.1600- dd. ? ; -M- PARDON TILLINGHAST, yeoman and cooper of Strea
2 CONC t, Sussez County, bn. 1601
2 CONT
2 CONT Notice that this connection is made through Sarah Browne, the emigrant's mother. The name, Tillinghast , has not always been spelled this way. And the earliest that I have found it even in its earliest forms,[like Tyllynghrst, etc
2 CONC .] is about 800 AD. At a later date I will give what info I have on earlier antecedents but I never found a continual'bloodline' in this family. [Somebody! Please go to England].
2 CONT
2 CONT Elton.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sarah and Pardon were married on 26 November 1622 in Streat, Sussex, England.
