1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Family and Education==
2 CONT b. c.1544, 1st s. of Richard Townshend of Brampton by Catherine, da. and coh. of Sir Humphrey Browne. educ. Trinity Coll. Camb. 1553 m. (1) Ursula, da. of Sir Christopher Heydon, s.p.; (2) c.1564, Jane, da. of Sir Michael Stanhope
2 CONC †, 2s. John and Robert suc. gt.-gd.-fa. Sir Roger Townshend† 1551. Kntd. 1588. He died at Stoke Newington on 30 June 1590, and was buried at St. Giles, Cripplegate.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT [http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1558-1603/member/townshend-roger-1544-90 History of Parliament Online]
