1 OCCU Came to America July 2, 1635 on a ship named Paule, Came to America July, 2 1635 on a ship named "Paul/Paule"
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Let us look at the facts at Yorktown in Virginia. Here,though the land has been harried by Hessian and English invaders and has suffered severely in the Civil War, the records are fortunately in excellent condition
2 CONC . In the county records a Henry Wade appears as early as 1646. There is a will of Armiger Wade who lived in York county in 1644, and was burgess in 1657, and the Clerk of the County and Circuit Courts reports the frequent occurren
2 CONC ce of the names of Armiger Wade, Edward Wade, Thomas Wade, William Wade, John Wade, Richard Wade,
2 CONT James Wade, Joseph Wade and Mildred Wade.  
2 CONT
2 CONT These, as surely as human speculation can be correct, were descendants of that worthy Armigel W'ade of England, who was no inconsiderable figure in the history of his own land.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000222944827899 Original Will Probate of Edward Wade Date 9 Nov 1675 ]
2 CONT Virginia, U.S., Wills and Probate Records
2 CONT
2 CONT Name Edward Wade
2 CONT Probate Date 9 Nov 1675
2 CONT Probate Place York, Virginia, USA
2 CONT Inferred Death Year 1675
2 CONT Inferred Death Place Virginia, USA
2 CONT Item Description Deeds, Orders, Wills, No 6-7, 1677-1687
2 CONT Individuals Listed (Name) Relationship
2 CONT Edward Wade
2 CONT Dorothy Hancocke
2 CONT Daughter
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Wade
2 CONT Grandson
2 CONT
2 CONT Jane Wade
2 CONT Wife
2 CONT
2 CONT Jane Lundy
2 CONT Daughter
2 CONT
2 CONT William Wade
2 CONT Son 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendants of Edward Wade
2 CONT There is strong evidence that the immigrant ancestor to Virginia for this Wade family was a
2 CONT descendant of Armagil/Armigel Wade/Waad. Armagil was born 1514 in Kilnsey, near
2 CONT Coniston, Yorkshire, England, and died June 20, 1568. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation No. 1
2 CONT 1. Edward1 Wade was born 1611, London, England, and died Bet. November 09, 1675 -April 24, 1677 in Virginia. He married Jane 1635 in Virginia. She was born 1615.
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of Edward Wade, pages 11-13, 9 November 1675, proved 24, April 1677 at Court for York County:
2 CONT "Edward Wade of Hampton Parish in York Co. To be buried in the orchard I now live by my family. To my son William Wade 100 acres of land in Hampton Parish. To my grandson Samuel Bond 150 acres at the head of ware Creek in New Kent
2 CONC  County, but if he should die without issue, then to my daughter Jane the wife of Jeremiah Laundy. To my wife Jane, two servants, William Greystoke and Anne Elmore, and my old grey gelding. To William Wade, my son, furniture and o
2 CONC ne servant, John Constant. To my grandchild, Edward Wade, one mare foal, my mare Rose. To my daughter Dorothy, the wife of Thomas Huncocke, the first mare foal that my old mare shall bring forth. to my son Edward Wade one cow betw
2 CONC een five and six years old. My wife Jane Wade, ex'ix..."
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Edward Wade and Jane are:
2 CONT + 2 i. Edward2 Wade II, born Abt. 1640 in York County, VA; died April 20, 1682.
2 CONT 3 ii. Margaret Wade, born Abt. 1641.
2 CONT 4 iii. Dorothy Wade, born Abt. 1650.
2 CONT 5 iv. Jane Wade, born Abt. 1652 
2 CONT 6 v. William Wade, born 1655; died Aft. 1692 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://edavidarthur.tripod.com/AncestorsAndDescendantsfEdwardWade.pdf 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Immigrated Sept 1635 on Ship Paule
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT SOURCE:http://kueber.us/p812.htm#i16229
2 CONT
2 CONT First Located: 1635, London, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Wade emigrated from England to Virginia on board the ship Paule in July, 1635, Aged 24 years. Leonard Betts, Master, bound to Virginia per certificate from the Minister of Gravesend of their Conformitie to the Church of Eng
2 CONC land.
2 CONT
2 CONT Info from National Archieves Ships List - American Genealogical Research Society.
2 CONT
2 CONT York County Records, Book 2 from "Virginia Colonial Abstracts", Volume 1, by Beverly Fleet.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Book 2 ends in 1648 but the next book, called Book 1 begins 1652. Therefore, four years are skipped.
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 88:
2 CONT
2 CONT (Amount) Due to the estate of Reverend Geo. Hopkins Dec 1644. 84 tytheable persons at 1 bushel per poll is 56 barr, 4 bush. (Various Names)
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 89:
2 CONT
2 CONT Elias Richardson
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Wade
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Harrison
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 129:
2 CONT
2 CONT Indenture 10 September 1640 between Wm Caynehooe of Cheskeack, Clerk, Signed 1642
2 CONT
2 CONT Reassigned, 27 October 1642 and Signed.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Deny assigns all rights to this lease. 27 ___ 1643. Witness Edward Wade
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 195:
2 CONT
2 CONT Bill Dated 9 October 1646. Chas. Deny to pay Edward Wade 1600 lbs tobo. 10 October next. Signed. Witness Robert Harrison, Edw. Jenkins. Deny to bind 3 cows as security.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the following source, some of the patents are the same as above. This is just a different source, but since it goes further, it also includes Edward Wade making his own patent by 1662. If he was the first Edward mentioned in th
2 CONC e colonial records, he would be about 50 years old. When he made one of his pattents he refers to land owned by Francis Burwell who also had Thomas Hampton as a neighbor. At this time, Edward lived in Hampton Parish, York County. 
2 CONC This is the first time Edward Wade and Thomas Hampton are shown living near each other. Therefore sometime after this date, it would be easy to imagin that one of Edward's sons married Thomas Hampton's daughter, Mary.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cavaliers and Pioneers
2 CONT
2 CONT Patent Book Number 1, Part II
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Martin, 250 acres, Lower New Nor. Co. 12 October 1638, Beg in Eliz. R. due for his own per. adv. & trans. of his wife Elizabeth martin, Edward Wade, Robert Masters, Rebecca Smith.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Wade received land Patent 1662, Diascund Swamp, Chickahominy River, York County, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT Cavaliers and Pioneers, Volume 1, Patent Book 5, Pages 342, 351 and 543
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Wade was in Virginia by 18 March 1662 when, as Mr. Edward Wade, he received a patent for 350 acres of land when were part of a tract of 2000 acres belonging to Mr. Francis Burwell. Wade's parcel adjoined lands of John Johns
2 CONC on and Adam Miles.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 18 June 1663 Mr. Edward Wade acquired 150 acres in York County which formerly had belonged to William Cainho who died with the land reverting to the king. A patent to John Overstreet on 07 September 1667 described his 37 acres 
2 CONC of land as being in Hampton Parish, York County, adjacent to Edward Wade, Jeoffrey Moore, Thomas Dennet and Zachary Padeyes.
2 CONT
2 CONT York County Records - Book 1, continued from "Virginia Colonial Abstracts", Volume 1, by Beverly Fleet.
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 342:
2 CONT
2 CONT Martin Baker to Edward Wade (sic) 100 acres, 5 September 1652. Witness Adam Myles, John Fripps recorded July 1650 by then clerk, Robert Bouth, Second assignment 24 June 1675 by Thos. Ballard, Cl. Cur.
2 CONT
2 CONT Records of York County, William Mary Quarterly, volume 26, Number 1 (July 1917), Pages 27-37.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Hatton's Contempt of Court 24 October 1662
2 CONT
2 CONT Whereas William Hatton (who formerly complained of by Mr. Edmond Peeters (sic) one of his Majesties Justices for contemning his warrant) was this day presented to the court by Edward Wade, Church warden of Hampton Parish.
2 CONT
2 CONT The fact that Edward Wade was addressed as "Mr." in his patents indicates that he was a man of some stature and importance in the colony.
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation/Service: 1668, Church Warden, Church of England, Hampton Parish, York County, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of Edward Wade
2 CONT
2 CONT Pages 11-13, 9 November 1675, Proved 24 April 1677 at Court for York County
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Wade of Hampton Parish in York Co. To be buried in the orchard I now live by my family. To my son William Wade 100 acres of land in Hampton Parish. To my grandson Samuel Bond 150 acres at the head of Ware Creek in New Kent 
2 CONC County, but if he should die without issue, then to my daughter Jane the wife of Jeremiah Laundy. To my wife Jane, two servants, William Greystoke and Anne Elmore, and my old grey gelding. To William Wade, my son, furniture and on
2 CONC e servant, John Constant. To my grandchild Edward Wade, one mare foal, my mare Rose. To my daughter Dorothy, the wife of Thomas Huncocke (?) the first mare foal that my old mare shall bring forth. To my son Edward Wade one cow bet
2 CONC ween five and six years old. My wife Jane Wade, ex'ix. To William Swinnerton 20/-, Witnesses: John Constant, William Swinnerton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Estate Administration: April 24, 1677, York County, Virginia.1 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Immigrated from London, England on ship 'Paul' in July 1635 to Virginia at the age of 24. He is the only Wade listed on the ship.
2 CONT  the Wade family came to Big Sandy from Bedford County Tenn, via immigration from England to Virginia to Bedford County Tenn and ultimately settling at Big Sandy.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT === Will: will was proved April 24, 1677 in  ===
2 CONT Will: will was proved April 24, 1677 in York County court Immigration: 2 JUL 1635 Edward Wade emigrated from England to Virginia on board the ship Paule in July 02, 1635, age 24 years. Received Land Patent 1662 for 350 acres on Di
2 CONC ascund Swamp, Chickahominy River, York County, Virginia. Church Warden 1668. Will dated November 9, 1675. Proved April 24 1677 at York County Court. Edward Wade I - Taken from Excerpt by Kenneth Reedy (http://www.genealogy.com/for
2 CONC um/surnames/topics/wade/4674/) Re: Edward Wade,lll b.abt 1660 VA By Kenneth Reedy May 04, 2002 at 09:20:14 In reply to: Edward Wade,lll b.abt 1660 VA Joy 4/06/02
2 CONT
2 CONT There is much debate about who Edward Wade's parents were but the fo
2 CONT === Notes for EDWARD WADE: from Elaine Waite ===
2 CONT Notes for EDWARD WADE: from Elaine Waiters Baptised: Church of England FirstLocated: 1635, London, England Edward Wade emigrated from England to Virginia on board the ship Paule in July, 1635, Aged 24 years. Leonard Betts, Master,
2 CONC bound to Virginia per certificate from the Minister of Gravesend of their Conformitie to the Church of England. Info from National Archives Ships List - American Genealogical Research Society. York County Records, Book 2 from "Vir
2 CONC ginia Colonial Abstracts", Volume 1, by Beverly Fleet. Note: Book 2 ends in 1648but the next book, called Book 1 begins 1652. Therefore, four years are skipped. Page 88: (Amount) Due to the estate of Reverend Geo. Hopkins Dec 1644
2 CONC . 84 tytheable persons at 1 bushel per poll is 56 barr, 4 bush. (Various Names) Page89: Elias Richardson Edward Wade Richard Harrison Page 129: Indenture 10September 1640 between Wm Caynehooe of Cheskeack, Clerk, Signed 1642 Reass
2 CONC igned, 27 October 1642 and Signed. Charles Deny assigns all rights to this lease.27 ___ 1643. Witness Edward Wade Page 195: Bill Dated 9 October 1646. Chas. Deny to pay Edward Wade 1600 lbs tobo. 10 October next. Signed. Witness R
2 CONC obert Harrison, Edw. Jenkins. Deny to bind 3 cows as security. In the following source, some of the patents are the same as above. This is just a different source, but since it goes further, it also includes Edward Wade making his
2 CONC  own patentby 1662. If he was the first Edward mentioned in the colonial records, he would be about 50 years old. When he made one of his pattents he refers to land owned by Francis Burwell who also had Thomas Hampton as a neighbo
2 CONC r. At this time,Edward lived in Hampton Parish, York County. This is the first time Edward Wadeand Thomas Hampton are shown living near each other. Therefore sometime afterthis date, it would be easy to imagine that one of Edward'
2 CONC s sons married ThomasHampton's daughter, Mary. Cavaliers and Pioneers Patent Book Number 1, Part II Robert Martin, 250 acres, Lower New Nor. Co. 12 October 1638 , Beg in Eliz. R. due for his own per. adv. & trans. of his wife Eliz
2 CONC abeth martin, Edward Wade, Robert Masters, Rebecca Smith. Edward Wade received land Patent 1662, Diascund Swamp, Chickahominy River, York County, Virginia Cavaliers and Pioneers, Volume 1, Patent Book 5, Pages 342, 351 and 543 Edw
2 CONC ard Wade was in Virginia by 18 March 1662 when, as Mr. Edward Wade, he received a patent for 350 acresof land when were part of a tract of 2000 acres belonging to Mr. Francis Burwell. Wade's parcel adjoined lands of John Johnson a
2 CONC nd Adam Miles. On 18 June 1663 Mr. Edward Wade acquired 150 acres in York County which formerly had belonged to William Cainho who died with the land reverting to the king. A patent to John Overstreet on 07 September 1667 describe
2 CONC d his 37 acres of land as being inHampton Parish, York County, adjacent to Edward Wade, Jeoffrey Moore, Thomas Dennet and Zachary Padeyes. York County Records - Book 1, continued from "Virginia Colonial Abstracts", Volume 1, by Be
2 CONC verly Fleet. Page 342: Martin Bakerto Edward Wade (sic) 100 acres, 5 September 1652. Witness Adam Myles, John Fripps recorded July 1650 by then clerk, Robert Bouth, Second assignment 24 June 1675 by Thos. Ballard, Cl. Cur. Records
2 CONC  of York County, William Mary Quarterly, volume 26, Number 1 (July 1917), Pages 27-37. William Hatton's Contempt of Court 24 October 1662 Whereas William Hatton (who formerly complained of by Mr.Edmond Peeters (sic) one of his Maj
2 CONC esties Justices for contemning his warrant)was this day presented to the court by Edward Wade, Church warden of Hampton Parish. The fact that Edward Wade was addressed as "Mr." in his patents indicates that he was a man of some st
2 CONC ature and importance in the colony. Occupation/Service: 1668, Church Warden, Church of England, Hampton Parish, York County, Virginia Will of Edward Wade Pages 11-13, 9 November 1675, Proved 24 April 1677 at Court for York County 
2 CONC Edward Wade of H
2 CONT === Life Sketch ===
2 CONT Wade sailed to America on the ship Paule in July 1635 at the age of 24  his name is on a list of passengers   the captain was Leonard Betts  destination VA
