1 NAME Abraham /Graves/
2 GIVN Abraham
2 SURN Graves
2 _MARNM Graves
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE BEF 1649
2 ADDR
3 CITY Lynn
3 STAE Massachusetts
3 CTRY American Colonies
1 DEAT
2 DATE 16 JUN 1729
2 ADDR
3 CITY Andover
3 STAE Massachusetts
3 CTRY American Colonies
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Source: http://www.gravesfa.org/gen083.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham Graves (13) was born about 1649 at Lynn, Mass. He first married Anna Hayward on 28 June 1677 in Concord, Mass.  He secondly married Sarah Dunton, daughter of Nathaniel Dunton of Andover, formerly of Reading, Mass., on 12 S
2 CONC ept. 1705.  They lived at the south end of Andover, where he died 16 June 1729 at age 80.  Sarah, his wife, died 21 June 1750 in Andover in her 91st year.  (R‑10, R‑201, R‑206)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children - Graves, by Anna Hayward
2 CONT
2 CONT     57.   Elizabeth Graves, b. 26 June 1678 (Concord, Mass.).
2 CONT
2 CONT     58.   Sarah Graves, b. 7 Nov. 1680, m. Richard Barker, 2 Aug. 1705.
2 CONT
2 CONT     59.   Samuel Graves, b. 31 Dec. 1682, d. young.
2 CONT
2 CONT +60.   Samuel Graves, b. 3 Jan. 1684, m(1) Sarah Perkins, m(2) Martha Bond, 29 Jan. 1725, d. 1747.
2 CONT
2 CONT +61.   Thomas Graves, b. 19 Dec. 1685, m. Ursilla Wilson, 5 Feb. 1708.
2 CONT
2 CONT +62.   Eleazer Graves, b. 10 March 1689/90, m(1) '''Sarah Dunton, 9 Nov. 1709,''' m(2) Hannah Evans, 28 May 1735, d. 28 March 1745.
2 CONT
2 CONT +63.   John Graves, b. 11 June 1691, m. Elizabeth Bean, c. 1724, d. 1790.
2 CONT
2 CONT     64.   Ester Graves, b. 11 June 1691, d. 8 Dec. 1739.  Twin of John.  (Source: Vital records of Andover, Mass.)
2 CONT
2 CONT +65.   William Graves, m. Elizabeth Bean, c. 1727.
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE!!!
2 CONT
2 CONT The higlighted Sarah Dunton married to Eleazer is not the same as the one married to Abraham. See below a passage from http://www.americanancestors.org/A_Dunton_Update/
2 CONT
2 CONT A Sarah Dunton who m. Andover 12 Sept. 1705 Abraham Graves, and d. there a widow 21 June 1750 in 91st year, was the elder Nathaniel’s sister (b. Reading 28 March 1660), not his daughter (as per K.V. Graves, Samuel Graves...of Lynn
2 CONC , Massachusetts [1985], p. 17), or widow. '''The Sarah Dunton who m. Andover 9 Nov. 1709 her stepbrother Eleazer Graves (Abraham’s son by first wife Anna Hayward) and d there 10 April 1723, was apparently a child of Sarah (Dunton)
2 CONC  Graves by an unknown father, born long before the elder Sarah’s marriage'''. According to W.F. Bucknam, Elizabeth2 Dunton (1658-1740) (Samuel1; sister of Nathaniel and Sarah above and wife of Nathaniel Evans [1650-1710]) , was “a
2 CONC  young lady of whom tradition says that her temper was less amiable than her looks, which occasioned the remark among his neighbors, that Evans had spoiled his family for the sake of a pretty face” (“Reading, Mass. Families” [mss.
2 CONC  at NEHGS, nd.], 1:191).
