1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Source: http://www.gravesfa.org/gen083.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Capt. Ebenezer Graves (14) was born about 1651 in Lynn, Mass.  He first married Mrs. Elizabeth (Stretton) Hopkins (her name also given as Eliphal Stratton), daughter of William Stretton and Elizabeth ‑‑, on 21 Aug. 1715 in Boston,
2 CONC  Mass.  She was born 26 April 1689 in Boston, died 15 April 1717, and was buried at Capps Hill Cem., Boston. He then married Sarah (Barrett) Howell, daughter of Samuel Barrett, on 14 Feb. 1718 in Boston.  He died in Ireland in May
2 CONC  1719, while on a voyage.  He was a mariner and owned shares of at least two ships.  He lived in Boston.  After he died, his widow Sarah married William Russell on 2 Oct. 1724.
