2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Died after 15 May 1710 at about age 50 in Beverly, Essex, Massachusetts [uncertain]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Amy (aka Emma) Graves, daughter of Mark Graves and Elizabeth (---) Graves, was born in 20 Jun 1659 in Andover, Massachusetts.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Emma married her first husband, John Bond on 23 Nov 1681[3] in Beverly, Massachusetts.[4][5][6] Amy and John Bond had the following children:[7][8]
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth, b.21 Mar 1685;
2 CONT Martha, b.5 Sep 1687;
2 CONT Edward, b.10 Jan 1689.
2 CONT John Bond died before 16 Apr 1694, when administration of his estate was granted,[7] and probably before 23 Jun 1691, when Emma was called "widow" Bond on admission of the Beverly church.[8] Emma married her second husband, Benjam
2 CONC in Haskell, on 10 Jun 1698 in Beverly, Massachusetts.[4][9][10]
2 CONT
2 CONT "Amee Bond alias Hascoll" was last found when she was named in a quitclaim deed executed by her children on 15 May 1710.[8] Her date and place of death are unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Graves-682
2 CONT
2 CONT Emma (Graves) Haskell (1659 - aft. 1710)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Emma "Amy" Haskell formerly Graves aka Bond===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 20 Jun 1659 in Andover, Essex, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Mark Graves and Amy (UNKNOWN) Graves [uncertain]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister of Abraham Graves, Ebenezer Graves, Mary (Graves) Haskell, Dorcas (Graves) Abbott, Hannah Graves, Ruth Graves, Sarah Graves, Mark Graves, Hester Graves [half], Mark Graves [half], Margaret A. (Graves) McRory [half] and Thom
2 CONC as Graves [half]
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of John Bond — married 23 Nov 1681 (to 23 Jun 1691) in Beverly, Essex, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Benjamin Haskell — married 10 Jun 1698 in Beverly, Essex, Massachusett
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of Elizabeth (Bond) Pride, Martha (Bond) Sawyer and Edward Bond I
2 CONT
2 CONT
