2 CONT SURELY CHARLES CITY CO. FOR EARLY CLAY FAMILY REFERS TO S.E. CHESTERFIELD CO.!:
2 CONT feb 2006 internet http://www.womacknet.net/map/colonial/colonial.htm
2 CONT 16 july 2002 internet http://www.stanscrib.50megs.com/curles.html
2 CONT (presumably readily available at Library of VA, if you ask for it?)
2 CONT showed an early 1600's land patent names map of area from what is now
2 CONT southeastern suburbs of Richmond, about 30  miles Southeastward and about
2 CONT 20 miles straight south almost as far as petersburg VA:
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT THE SOUTHEAST CORNER OF TODAY'S CHESTERFIELD CO. WAS IN CHARLES CITY CO IN
2 CONT EARLY 1600'S! East of the following line was in Charles city Co. then, not in
2 CONT Henrico Co.!: roughly from 2 miles west of Interstate 295 on today's northern
2 CONT boundary of Chesterfield Co. (Farrar's Island in the James River)
2 CONT down to a point 3 miles west of Interstate 95 at
2 CONT today's southern boundary of chesterfield Co. at west edge of Petersburg VA;
2 CONT More technically the line was a radius presumably drawn from some point 25
2 CONT miles east near the present-day 3 county boundary of Prince George Co/ Surry
2 CONT Co./ Charles  City co. VA and the line was drawn southward from the SE corner
2 CONT of Farrar's Island on the James River, but the above method using straight-line
2 CONT estimates from modern Interstate locations is better, unless you were to have
2 CONT the old Curles map to look at;
1 NOTE CAVEAT:
2 CONT There were many Richard Cocke men in 1600s in Henrico Co. VA, two of whom were
2 CONT even half-brothers!
2 CONT Use the above Volume 1 to learn ot distinguish the many different Richard
2 CONT Cockes of 1600s in VA;
2 CONT ------------------------
