1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Sir Capell Bedell, 1st Baronet''' (c. 1598 – 14 December 1643), was an English politician.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Parents: Sir Thomas Bedell, of Hamerton, Huntingdonshire, by Winifred Capell, daughter of Sir Arthur Capell, Hadham, Hertfordshire.
2 CONT * Wife: Alice Fanshawe, daughter of Sir Henry Fanshawe. He died in December 1643. As he had no sons the baronetcy died with him.
2 CONT * Children: Mary married Thomas Leventhorpe, 3rd Bnt.Wife: Alice Fanshawe, daughter of Sir Henry Fanshawe. 
2 CONT * Children: Mary Bedall who married Thomas Leventhorpe, 3rd Bnt.
2 CONT * He died in December 1643. As he had no sons the baronetcy died with him. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * He was created a baronet, of Hamerton in the County of Huntingdon, on 3 June 1622. 
2 CONT * He later represented Hertfordshire in Parliament in 1626 and Huntingdonshire from 1628 to 1629 and again in 1640. 
2 CONT * Between 1632 and 1633 he served as High Sheriff of Cambridgeshire and Huntingdonshire. 
2 CONT
2 CONT REF:
2 CONT *[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capell_Bedell Wikipedia]
