1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Lady Penelope Wriothsley''' was born on November 8, 1598 in Tichfield, Hampshire, England. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-12347978 Henry Wriothesley, 3rd Earl of Southampton] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-24
2 CONC 551894 Elizabeth Wriothesly, Countess of Southampton]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Penelope married [https://www.geni.com/profile-12347859 William Spencer, 2nd Baron Spencer of Wormleighton] in 1617 in Tichfield, Hampshire, England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Together they had the following children (as of 23 January 2025, list needs checking):
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-78291498 Elizabeth Spencer]; Hon Elizabeth Spencer (b. 16 Feb 1617/8; dsp. 11 Aug 1672), mar. (1) 4 Dec 1634 John [Craven], 1st Baron Craven, (2) 7 Jul 1648 Hon Henry Howard, of Revensby, co. Lincol
2 CONC n (dsp. 1663), 3rd son of Thomas [Howard], 1st Earl of Berkshire, and (3) as his second wife William [Crofts], 1st Baron Crofts 
2 CONT #  [https://www.geni.com/profile-12348009 Henry Spencer, 1st Earl of Sunderland and 3rd Earl Spencer]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34645993266 Ann Spencer]; Hon Anne Spencer, mar. Sir Robert Agborough later Townshend, of Hem, co. Denbigh, and had issue 
2 CONT #  [https://www.geni.com/profile-78291678 Alice Spencer]; Hon Alice Spencer (bapt. 29 Dec 1625; d. bef. 1712), mar. Henry [Moore], 1st Earl of Drogheda, and had issue 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-54358838 Baroness Margaret Spencer]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-49041815 Lady Margaret Ashley Spencer, Countess of Shaftesbury]; Hon Margaret Spencer (bapt. 19 Jan 1627; dsp. 1693), mar. 30 Aug 1655 as his third wife Anthony [Ashley-Cooper], 1st Earl of Shaftesb
2 CONC ury 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-24550474 Hon. Robert Spencer, 1st (and last) Viscount Teviot]  Hon Robert Spencer, Member of Parliament for Great Bedwin 1660 and for Brackley 1661-79, a Commissioner of Appeals for regulating the E
2 CONC xcise 1662-89, cr. 20 Oct 1685 Viscount of Teviot (Peerage of Scotland), Commissioner of the Privy Seal 1685-86/7 (bapt. 2 Feb 1628/9; dsp. by suicide 20 May 1694), mar. Jane Spencer (d. 10 Jun 1689; bur. at Yarnton, co. Oxford), 
2 CONC 1st dau. and cohrss. of Sir Thomas Spencer, 3rd Bt., of Yarnton, co. Oxford, by his wife Jane Garrard, dau. of Sir John Garrard, 2nd Bt., of Lamer, co. Hertford 
2 CONT #  [https://www.geni.com/profile-78291655 Hon. William Spencer]; Hon William Spencer, of Ashton, co. Lancaster, mar. Hon Elizabeth Gerard, only dau. of Dutton [Gerard], 3rd Baron Gerard, by his second wife Lady Elizabeth O'Brien, 
2 CONC 3rd dau. and cohrss. of Henry [O'Brien], 4th Earl of Thomond, and had issue 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34645993241 Thomas Spencer];
2 CONT #  [https://www.geni.com/profile-34645993286 Katherine Spencer]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34735883731 Mary Margaret Spencer]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on July 16, 1667 in Brighton, Sussex, England and was buried in July 1667 in Brington, Northamptonshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Penelope Wriothsley Wriothsley is Edward III, king of England's 8th great granddaughter.
2 CONT ----
