1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Parents not known.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT Francis Browne was born before 1625 in England, and he died shortly before 3 February 1691 (will proved) in South Farnham Parish, Old Rappahannock County, Virginia. This information is based on will records for Francis Browne foun
2 CONC d at the website Early Settlers of Southern Maryland and Virginia's Northern Neck Counties.
2 CONT
2 CONT Perhaps because of his name Francis, it is sometimes suggested that he was the son of Francis Browne, 2nd Viscount Montagu or related to the Viscount Montagu's - there is absolutely no truth to these statements.
2 CONT
2 CONT Francis Browne first appears in Rappahannock County, Virginia as a land owner in 1648. The records would seem to indicate that he owned 1,100 acres on the Rappahannock River near Piscataway Creek.
2 CONT
2 CONT Francis paid taxes in Lancaster County, Virginia Colony, based on his labor force. The county assessed him for two tithables, 24 Oct 1653,[1] for three tithables, 6 Feb 1655,[2] again for three tithables, 7 Dec 1655,[3] and for tw
2 CONC o tithables, 5 Nov 1656.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Both land records and his will indicate that his wife's name was Elizabeth. She is often said to be Elizabeth Allen, though it is uncertain as to why she is given this LNAB. His will names two sons, four daughters, and one grandso
2 CONC n.
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth
2 CONT Born: Before 1625.[citation needed]
2 CONT Marriage and Children
2 CONT Married: Elizabeth .[citation needed][5]
2 CONT Children of Francis and Elizabeth Browne:
2 CONT His will names 2 sons and 4 daughters.
2 CONT # Sarah Browne. (who married Thomas Munday),
2 CONT # Elizabeth Browne. (who married Robert Mills),
2 CONT # Rebecca Browne. (who married John Mills, Junior),
2 CONT # Mary Browne. (whose husband, if any, is not known),
2 CONT # Francis Browne. (who married Elizabeth Allen), and
2 CONT # Daniel Browne. (who married Jane Copeland).
2 CONT
2 CONT Death
2 CONT Died: Between 10 Nov 1690 and 3 Feb 1691 in South Farnham Parish, Rappahannock County, Virginia.
2 CONT Dates his will was made and proved.
2 CONT Will of Francis Browne of South Farnham, Rappahannock County.[6]
2 CONT Made 10 November, 1690; proved 3 February, 1691.
2 CONT
2 CONT Summary:
2 CONT - my Loving wife Elizabeth
2 CONT - my two sons ffrancis and Daniel
2 CONT - my fower daughters Elizabeth, Sarah, Mary and Rebecca
2 CONT - Daniel Brown the son of my son Francis Brown
2 CONT - Godsons Joseph and John Edmondson
2 CONT - Godson Francis Brown the son of Daniell Brown senior my neighbour
2 CONT - Godson Francis Graves the son of Francis Graves
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Children
2 CONT 2 sons, 4 daughters:
2 CONT # Francis Brown "II" (married Elizabeth Allen),  
2 CONT # Sarah Brown (married Thomas Munday),  
2 CONT # Elizabeth Brown (possibly married a Mr. Mills?),  
2 CONT # Mary Brown (married Robert Mills),  
2 CONT # Daniel Brown "I" (married Jane Copeland) and  
2 CONT # Rebecca Brown (married John Mills, Junior).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Francis Brown "II" fathered a son who we call Daniel Brown "II" (married Elizabeth Coleman and died in Culpeper Co., VA in the 1740s). 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I30311&tree=Tree1
2 CONT Elizabeth Allen,   b. Bef 1640, England d. 10 Mar 1701, South Farnham Parish, Old Rappahannock County, Virginia  (Age > 61 years) 
2 CONT Marriage	Bef 1656 	South Farnham Parish, Old Rappahannock County, Virginia  
2 CONT Children 	
2 CONT 1. Sarah Browne,   b. Bef 1656, South Farnham Parish, Old Rappahannock County, Virginia 
2 CONT 2. Francis Browne,   b. Bef 1658, South Farnham Parish, Old Rappahannock County, Virginia d. 11 Apr 1709, South Farnham Parish, Essex County, Virginia - probate 
2 CONT 3. Elizabeth Browne,   b. Bef 1660, South Farnham Parish, Old Rappahannock County, Virginia 
2 CONT 4. Rebecca Browne,   b. Bef 1660, South Farnham Parish, Old Rappahannock County, Virginia 
2 CONT 5. Mary Browne,   b. Bef 1660, South Farnham Parish, Old Rappahannock County, Virginia d. Aft 1690, South Farnham Parish, Essex County, Virginia  (Age > 32 years)  
2 CONT 6. Daniel Browne,   b. Bef 1660, South Farnham Parish, Old Rappahannock County, Virginia d. 10 Sep 1708, South Farnham Parish, Essex County, Virginia - probate  (Age > 48 years)  
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes 	
2 CONT Wills of Old Rappahannock County, Virginia, 1656-1692 page 147
2 CONT BROWN, FRANCIS, 10 November, 1690; 3 February, 1691.
2 CONT In the name of God Amen
2 CONT I ffrancis Brown senior in the parish of South ffarnham in the County of Rapp being very sick and weake of body butt of perfect sense and memory doe make this my Last Will and Testament in manner and forme ffolowing I give and beq
2 CONC ueath my souk unto Al-mighty God that gave it me with a sure and certayne hope of a joy-full Resurrection through the merits of my Blessed Lord and Saviour Jesus Christ and my body unto my mother the earth to be decently interred 
2 CONC and for my worldly Estate in manner and form following after my just and Lawfall debts are satisfied.
2 CONT
2 CONT I give and bequeath unto my son ffrancis Brown after mine and my Loving wife Elizabeth decease all that necke of Land Lying on the north side of my devident of Land I now live on bounded as followeth that is to say strayt away thr
2 CONC ough and mild field from the Run of the deviling branch the mill road which goes to my son Daniel goes over & for a small branch neare my ould dwelling house called by the name of the spring branch which sayd Land I give and beque
2 CONC ath unto my said son ffrancis to him and his heirs forever.
2 CONT I also give and bequeath unto my son Daniel Brown after my and my Loving wife Elizabeth decease all that Rest of my land I am now possessed with all my plantation and housing to him and his heires to have and to hould in fee simpl
2 CONC e for ever also itt is my will and dealer that my household goods be equally divided between my two sons ffrancis and Daniel both in quality and goodness to them and their heirs to have and to hould in fee simple for ever also it 
2 CONC is my will and desier there be a row of orchard trees planted along ye sayd ould field to devide the above sayd Land. I also give and bequeath unto my sons ffrancis and Daniel my parcell of Land Lying on the south side of pescataw
2 CONC ay Creeke called by the name of ye wading place poynt equally between them and their heirs forever I alsoe give and bequeath unto my fower daughters Elizabeth, Sarah, Mary and Rebecca one shilling apeace to be payd them by my lawf
2 CONC ul executor or executrix I also give and bequeath unto Daniel Brown the son of my son Francis Brown one feather bed with the furniture belonging unto itt to him and his heirs forever after my and my "sites decease.
2 CONT I give and bequeath unto my Loving wife Elizabeth all the Rest of my moveable Estate that I am now possessed with to have and to hould without any Lett or molestation to her and her heirs forever I also give and bequeath unto my f
2 CONC lower Godsons that is Joseph and John Edmondson and Ffras Brown the son of Daniell Brown senior my neighbour and ffra Graves the son of Ffras Graves deceased to every one of them one pocket bible of fine or six shillings price to 
2 CONC be truly payd them after my decease by my Law-full executor or executrix I alsoe apoynt my Loving wife Elizabeth my sole and whole executrix of this my Last will and testament and this my Last will to cut off and disannull all ffo
2 CONC rmer wills whatsoever as witness my hand and seal this 10th day of novher 1690
2 CONT signed sealed and delivered FRANCIS BROWN Seal in the presence of us JOHN FERGUSON, THO WHEELER Probst est sacrum in Cur. Com. Rappa. 3° die ffeby ano 1691
2 CONT Test Wm COLSTON Cl. Recorded 26 Feb. 1691.
2 CONT ===
2 CONT 1653-1800 Lancaster County, Virginia Wills [Ida J. Lee];
2 CONT COLE, Francis. Will. 1 July 1658. Rec. 1 October 1658.
2 CONT Wife Alice (all plantation where I now live) Daughters Frances and Mary; Francis Brown, son of Francis Brown; Mr. Roger Radford. John Burroughs, servant. Extrs. Wife and daughter Frances. Wits: Roger Radford, Edward Dale. W.B. 2, 
2 CONC Page 54.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===
