2 CONT posted 5 years ago by Bill Davidson as comment on
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Browne-3977
2 CONT
2 CONT This Francis Brown family in Essex Co., VA is represented by DNA Group 10 at the Brown DNA Project (at Family Tree DNA). As a matter of fact, the lady who is the primary Admin for that DNA Project is a member of that Group (her fa
2 CONC ther is a "Y DNA match" to DNA Group 10). There is some evidence to suggest that Francis Brown "I" (died 1691/1692 in Essex Co., VA) was married to Elizabeth Cole. His son, who we call Francis Brown "II," was married to an Elizabe
2 CONC th Allen. That Elizabeth Allen should not be confused with the other Elizabeth Allen who was one of the apparent three wives of a William Brown in the area. That William Brown does not appear to have been related to Francis Brown 
2 CONC "I." The children of Francis Brown "I" (and their apparent spouses) were Francis Brown "II" (married Elizabeth Allen), Sarah Brown (married Thomas Munday), Elizabeth Brown (possibly married a Mr. Mills?), Mary Brown (married Rober
2 CONC t Mills), Daniel Brown "I" (married Jane Copeland) and Rebecca Brown (married John Mills, Junior). Francis Brown "II" fathered a son who we call Daniel Brown "II" (married Elizabeth Coleman and died in Culpeper Co., VA in the 1740
2 CONC s). Daniel Brown "I" fathered sons who we call Abraham Brown "I" (married Mary Tribble and died in Caroline Co., VA around 1735), Henry Brown "I" (married Keziah Jones and died in Essex Co., VA around 1734) and Francis Brown "III"
2 CONC  (married Christiana unknown and died in Chesterfield Co., VA in the 1750s). Daniel Brown "I" also fathered four daughters named Mary Brown (married John Rutherford), Elizabeth Brown, Sarah Brown (married Henry Boughan, Senior) an
2 CONC d Jane Brown. ~ Bill Davidson
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/brown/44471/
2 CONT Daniel Brown & Francis Neville-Hampshire Co., VA
2 CONT By Bill Davidson April 15, 2012 at 05:39:18
2 CONT The lineage of the Daniel Brown who was married to a Frances and who migrated from Culpeper Co., VA to Hampshire Co., VA in the late-1760s or so is as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 Francis Brown "I" (died 1691/1692 in Essex Co., VA) + Elizabeth ('''apparently Elizabeth Cole''')
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 Francis Brown "II" (died about 1708 in Essex Co., VA) + Elizabeth Allen
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: The above Francis Brown "II" had a brother who we call Daniel Brown "I," and Daniel Brown "I" married Jane Copeland.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 Daniel Brown "II" (born circa-1677; died about 1747 in Culpeper Co., VA) + Elizabeth Coleman (a daughter of Robert Coleman, Junior and Ann Spilsby, and a granddaughter of Robert Coleman, Senior and Elizabeth Grizzell)
2 CONT
2 CONT 4 Daniel Brown "III" (born circa-1715; left his Will in Hampshire Co., VA in 1780) + Frances (presumably Frances Neville, but I don't know if her maiden name has actually been proven)
2 CONT
2 CONT 5 The above-referenced Will of Daniel Brown "III" mentioned the following five children: Daniel ("IV"), Thomas, Sarah, Ann and Mary.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: There was also a Coleman Brown who was killed by Indians in Hampshire Co., VA in 1774.It would not be very surprising if he was yet another son of Daniel Brown "III" and Frances.There were at least two other men in this over
2 CONC all Brown family back in Culpeper Co., VA who were also named Coleman Brown.
2 CONT
2 CONT I see some posts on this message board about a Thomas C. Brown and an "associated" Nathaniel Brown in Hampshire Co., VA.Perhaps Thomas C. (Coleman?) Brown was the Thomas Brown who was shown as a son of Daniel Brown "III" in the ab
2 CONC ove-referenced Will in 1780 (though I have seen other information on the internet that claimed that the middle initial of "C" stood for something else).No one named Nathaniel Brown, however, was mentioned in that Will.It is possib
2 CONC le, however, that the above-mentioned Coleman Brown who was killed by Indians in 1774 could have also fathered some children of his own (but I do not know when that Nathaniel Brown was born, nor if that Coleman Brown was old enoug
2 CONC h to have been his potential father).Depending on when they were born, maybe Thomas C. Brown and Nathaniel Brown were sons of Daniel Brown "IV" and/or sons of his brother Thomas Brown.With a common name like "Brown," however, it w
2 CONC ould not be too surprising if there was more than just one overall Brown family in the area.
2 CONT ----
