2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page for Hon. Mary Browne:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p2535.htm#i25350
2 CONT
2 CONT Hon. Mary Browne[1]
2 CONT *F, #25350, 
2 CONT *b. circa 1593, 
2 CONT *d. 13 November 1692
2 CONT *Last Edited=31 Oct 2005
2 CONT
2 CONT Hon. Mary Browne was born circa 1593. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, firstly, William Paulett, Viscount St. John, son of William Paulett, 4th Marquess of Winchester and Lady Lucy Cecil, before 17 February 1613/14.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, secondly, Hon. William Arundell, son of Thomas Arundell, 1st Baron Arundell of Wardour and Mary Wriothesley, before 22 October 1627.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 13 November 1692.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Anthony Maria Browne, 2nd Viscount Montagu and Jane Sackville.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT From before 17 February 1613/14, her married name became Paulett.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT From before 22 October 1627, her married name became Arundell.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Hon. Mary Browne and Hon. William Arundell
2 CONT *1. Mark Arundell1
2 CONT *2. Charles Arundell+1
2 CONT *3. Mary Arundell1 d. 24 Dec 1698
2 CONT *4. Katherine Arundell1 d. 4 Mar 1642
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S21] L. G. Pine, The New Extinct Peerage 1884-1971: Containing Extinct, Abeyant, Dormant and Suspended Peerages With Genealogies and Arms (London, U.K.: Heraldry Today, 1972), page 10. Hereinafter cited as The New Extinct Pee
2 CONC rage.
2 CONT *2. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume XII/2, page 766. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *__________________
2 CONT *Anthony-Maria Browne (1574–1629) was an English peer during the Tudor and Stuart period.
2 CONT *He was born in 1574, the son of Anthony Browne (22 July 1552 – 29 June 1592),[1] eldest son of Anthony Browne, 1st Viscount Montagu, and Mary Dormer. He became the Second Viscount Montagu at the age of 18 on the death of his gran
2 CONC dfather in 1592,[2] from whom he inherited an estate worth between £3600 and £5400 per annum.[3]
2 CONT *In 1591 Browne married Jane Sackville, daughter of Thomas Sackville, 1st Earl of Dorset, and by her had issue:[4]
2 CONT ** Francis Browne (died young).
2 CONT ** Anthony Browne (died young).
2 CONT ** Francis Browne, 3rd Viscount Montague, who married Elizabeth Somerset, the daughter of Henry Somerset, 1st Marquess of Worcester.
2 CONT **'''''' Mary Browne, who married firstly, William Paulet (d.1621), Lord St. John, eldest son of William Paulet, 4th Marquess of Winchester, and secondly, William Arundell, esquire, of Horningsham, Wiltshire, second son of Thomas 
2 CONC Arundell, 1st Baron Arundell of Wardour, and Mary Wriothesley, the daughter of Henry Wriothesley, 2nd Earl of Southampton, by Mary Browne, daughter of Anthony Browne, 1st Viscount Montague.
2 CONT ** Catherine Browne, who married William Tyrwhit.
2 CONT ** Mary Browne (d. January 1685), who married Robert Petre, 3rd Baron Petre (d. October 1638).
2 CONT ** Frances Browne, who married John Blomer.
2 CONT ** Anne Browne, who became a nun.
2 CONT ** Lucy Browne, who became a nun.
2 CONT *Anthony-Maria Browne was arrested in connection with the Gunpowder Plot and spent about a year in the Tower of London.
2 CONT *He wrote a book on how to manage a nobleman's household entitled "A Booke of Orders and Rules".[5]
2 CONT *He died on 23 October 1629 and is buried in Midhurst Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Footnotes
2 CONT ** 1.^ Richardson, Douglas, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd ed., vol. III, pp. 228-9.
2 CONT ** 2.^ Cockayne,G.E. Complete Peerage Reprinted Gloucester 2000 Vol.IX p.100
2 CONT ** 3.^ Elzinga 2004; Scott 1854, p. 173.
2 CONT ** 4.^ Questier 2006, p. 522; Richardson I 2011, p. 45; Scott 1854, p. 173.
2 CONT ** 5.^ Scott 1854, p. 173.
2 CONT
2 CONT *References
2 CONT **Elzinga, J.G. (2004). Browne, Anthony, first Viscount Montagu (1528–1592). Oxford Dictionary of National Biography. Retrieved 8 December 2012. (subscription required)
2 CONT ** Questier, Michael C. (2006). Catholicism and Community in Early Modern England. Cambridge: Cambridge University Press.
2 CONT ** Richardson, Douglas (2011). Magna Carta Ancestry: A Study in Colonial and Medieval Families, ed. Kimball G. Everingham. I (2nd ed.). Salt Lake City. ISBN 1449966373
2 CONT ** Scott, Sibbald David, ed. (1854). "A Booke of Orders and Rules of Anthony Viscount Montague in 1595". Sussex Archaeological Collections (London: John Russell Smith) VII: 173-212. Retrieved 8 December 2012.
2 CONT
