1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From her English Wikipedia page:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elizabeth_Plunkett,_Countess_of_Fingall
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Plunkett, Countess of Fingall
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth O'Donnell (1604 – c. 1630) was the 1st Countess of Fingal. She was the daughter[1] of Prince Rory O'Donnell, 1st Earl of Tyrconnell, and Lady Bridget FitzGerald, daughter of Henry FitzGerald, 12th Earl of Kildare. After 
2 CONC her father's death in 1608, her mother married Nicholas Barnewall, 1st Viscount Kingsland, and had more children. Meanwhile, Elizabeth married Luke Plunkett, 1st Earl of Fingall.[2] They lived at Killeen Castle, County Meath in Ir
2 CONC eland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Given her probable very young age, some sources suggest that this Elizabeth may have been a FitzGerald, the Countess Lady Bridget’s sister, and not her daughter, however no evidence is given [3] She may have been a child-bride, an
2 CONC d is said to have died in London very shortly after her marriage. Her lineage as daughter (possibly pre-marital) of Rory O'Donnell, 1st Earl of Tyrconnell, and his wife Lady Bridget FitzGerald, has been repeatedly cited in various
2 CONC  peerage directories, such as Lodge's (1827, and re-issued in 1907),[4] Foster's (1881),[5] Cokayne's (1926),[6] and Burke's (1980).[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Fingall was also married on three other occasions. He had married in 1628 Eleanor Bagenal, who died leaving no children. His son by a later marriage to Susanna Brabazon, Christopher Plunkett, 2nd Earl of Fingall, married Mabe
2 CONC l Barnewall, half-sister of Elizabeth. Thus Elizabeth was 1st Countess of Fingall, and her much younger half-sister became Countess of the 2nd Earl of Fingall. Another half-sister, Mary Barnewall married Nicholas Preston, 6th Visc
2 CONC ount Gormanston, whereby Elizabeth was both his half-sister-in-law, and already his 3rd cousin through their common ancestor, Gerald FitzGerald, 9th Earl of Kildare. She was also aunt of Jenico Preston, 7th Viscount Gormanston, wh
2 CONC o was a 1st cousin of Luke Plunkett, 3rd Earl of Fingall, also her nephew. Lucas Plunkett's last wife was Margaret St. Lawrence, daughter of Nicholas St Lawrence, 9th Baron Howth. Plunkett died 29 March 1637; Margaret died the fol
2 CONC lowing November.
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT *1. Meehan, C. P. The Fate and Fortunes of the Earls of Tyrone and Tyrconnel (1870). Meehan observes of the Countess of Tyrconnell (Bridget) that “by the earl of Tyrconnel she had one son, Hugh, who succeeded to his father’s title
2 CONC , and two daughters, Eliza and Mary” (footnote, page 246)
2 CONT *2. Carty, Mary Rose. History of Killeen Castle, published by Carty/Lynch, Dunsany, County Meath, Ireland, April 1991 (ISBN 0-9517382-0-8) - page 18 refers to Elizabeth O'Donnell as 1st Countess of Fingall (Fingal). She was a daug
2 CONC hter of Rory O'Donnell, 1st Earl of Tyrconnell
2 CONT *3. Lee, Sidney, ed. Dictionary of National Biography, Vol. XLI (Nichols-O’Dugan), published by Macmillan and Co., London and New York, 1895. See page 446
2 CONT *4. Lodge's Peerage, Baronetage, and Knightage for the British Empire for 1907, by Edmund Lodge, Esq., Late Norroy King-of-Arms, 76th edition, published by Kelly's Directories Ltd., High Holborn, London (1st edition was published 
2 CONC by College of Arms, 1827)
2 CONT *5. The Peerage, Baronetage, and Knightage of the British Empire for 1881, by Joseph Foster, published by Nichols & Sons, Westminster, 1881
2 CONT *6. The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, extant, extinct or dormant, by George Edward Cokayne, Volume V, published by The St. Catherine Press, London, 1926
2 CONT *7. Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 105th edition, 4th impression, published by Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books), Ltd, 1980 [ISBN 0-85011-034-3]
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Lady Elizabeth Fitzgerald (questionable parentage):
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p35436.htm#i354357
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Elizabeth FitzGerald [1]
2 CONT *F, #354357
2 CONT *Last Edited=29 Apr 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.06%
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Elizabeth FitzGerald was the daughter of Henry FitzGerald, 2nd/12th Earl of Kildare and Lady Frances Howard.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Lucas Plunkett, 1st Earl of Fingall, son of Christopher Plunkett, 8th Lord Killeen and Genet Dillon, before 1611.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died, without issue.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT From before 1611, her married name became Plunkett.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 2, page 2299. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
