2 CONT =Hugh O'Donnell=
2 CONT
2 CONT Titular King of Tír Conaill, and son of Rory O'Donnell, 1st Earl of Tyrconnell whose title was however attainted.
2 CONT Aodh (Hugh), was three weeks shy of his first birthday he sailed from Lough Swilly during the Flight of the Earls, and was raised in Leuven. In time he joined the service of the King of Spain, and was killed in action when his shi
2 CONC p engaged a French vessel in August or September 1642 and caught fire. He left no immediate heirs, although the Earldom, were it not attainted in 1614, would have passed by remainder to his uncle Cathbharr, whose line was extinct 
2 CONC by then, and thence, to his 1st cousin Donal Oge O'Donnell, according to the terms of the letters patent.
