1 OCCU Viscountess Mountgarret
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT '''Edmund Butler''', 2nd Viscount Mountgarret (c. 1562 – 1602), was the son of Richard Butler, 1st Viscount Mountgarret and Eleanor Butler.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edmund_Butler,_2nd_Viscount_Mountgarret
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Grany, Grania, or '''Grizzel FitzPatrick''', daughter of Barnaby Fitzpatrick, 1st Baron Upper Ossory.[2][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Among their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Richard Butler, 3rd Viscount Mountgarret (1578 - 1651) [1]
2 CONT # Helen Butler, who married her second cousin, Walter Butler, 11th Earl of Ormond
2 CONT # Anne Butler, who married Edward Butler, 1st Viscount Galmoye[4]
2 CONT # Margaret Butler, who married Oliver Grace of Carney, County Tipperary [5]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT His sister Eleanor married Thomas Butler, 4th Baron Cahir.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p3319.htm#i33188
2 CONT
2 CONT Grizel FitzPatrick  F, #33188 Last Edited=8 Feb 201
2 CONT
2 CONT Grizel FitzPatrick was the daughter of Barnaby FitzPatrick, 1st Baron of Upper Ossory and Elizabeth O'Connor.1 She married Edmund Butler, 2nd Viscount Mountgarret, son of Richard Butler, 1st Viscount Mountgarret and Ellen Butler.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Her married name became Butler. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After her marriage, Grizel FitzPatrick was styled as Viscountess Mountgarret on 20 December 1571. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Grizel FitzPatrick and Edmund Butler, 2nd Viscount Mountgarret
2 CONT
2 CONT # Hon. Helen Butler+1 d. 28 Jan 1631/32
