2 CONC est that his children might have included Michaiah Matthews, another signer of Gabriel Whelden's will. A Mordecai Matthews "was one of the two" [?] who graduated 1655 from Harvard. At the same time, a younger Matthews, perhaps his
2 CONC  brother was in a lower class. Neither was charged tuition after June 8, 1655, supporting the possibility that they returned to England as well. One Mordecai Mathews was a minister at Roinolston in Glamorganshire.
