1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *''''''The history and antiquities of the county of Buckingham (1847) Vol. 4
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/details/historyantiquiti04lips
2 CONT **		PEDIGREE OF DIGBY. From Harl. MSS. 1364.
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/historyantiquiti04lips#page/145/mode/1up
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/historyantiquiti04lips#page/146/mode/1up
2 CONT **CHART
2 CONT * 1. EVERARD DIGBY, "de alta proditione attinctus, an. 1605; quia nefandissimis illis incendiariis ad principem at patriam uno tartarei fulminis ictu toltendum horrenda consilia scelerate sociavit." mar. MARY, sole dau. and heir o
2 CONC f William Mulsho, of Golthurst. ch: 1. SIR KENELM DIGBY, 2. SIR JOHN DIGBY, Knt, major-General in the King's Army in the West; killed at the Battle of Longport, in Somersetshire, 9 July 1645.
2 CONT **      1. SIR KENELM DIGBY, Knt., of Gothurst, Co. Bucks; died in 1665, aet. 62. mar. VENETIA ANASTATIA, dau. and co-heir of Sir Edward Stanley, K.B., of Tongue Castle, Co. Salop; died May 1663, aet. 33; bur. in Ch. Ch. London. c
2 CONC h: 1. KENELM DIGBY, born in 1611; killed at St. Neot's, fighting for the King, 9 July 1648; died s. p., ''''''2. JOHN DIGBY'''''', 3. GEORGE, 4. EDWARD, ob. jur.,  5. MARGERY, mar. to Edward Dudley, Esq., of Clopton, Co. Northampt
2 CONC on.
2 CONT ***''''''	2. JOHN DIGBY, Esq. of Gothurst. mar. (1) CATHARINE, eldest surviving dau. of Henry Earl of Arundel. (2) MARGARET, fourth dau. of Edward Longueville, Esq., of Wolverton, Co. Bucks. ch: 1. MARGARET MARIA, 2. CHARLOTTA THE
2 CONC OPHILA
2 CONT ****		1. MARGARET MARIA, dau. and co-heir. Sold her share to Gayhurst in 1704. mar. SIR JOHN CONWAY, Knt. of Bodreythem, Co. Flint.
2 CONT ****		2. CHARLOTTA THEOPHILA, dau. and co-heir. Sold her share of Gayhurst in 1704. mar. RICHARD MOSTYN, Esq., of Penbedw, Co. Flint.
