1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir John Fortescue, Baronet [S 1636] of Salden</strong>, 1st son and heir, baptized 13 July 1614, at Mursley; reverted to the ancient religion of the family; succeeded to the Baronetcy in September 1656. He married firstl
2 CONC y, Margaret, daughter of Thomas (Arundell), 1st Baron Arundell of Wardour, by his 2nd wife, Anne, daughter of Miles Philipson. she died s.p.m. 1638. He married secondly, in or before 1644, Mary, daughter of Sir William Stoner of S
2 CONC toner, Oxon, by Elizabeth, daughter of Sir Thomas Lake, Secretary of State to James I. She was baptized 11 November 1622. He married thirdly, Elizabeth, daughter of Lord William Howard. She died s.p.s. 1674. He was buried 14 June 
2 CONC 1683, at Mursley."
2 CONT
2 CONT 2nd Baronet of Salden House. 'Reverted to the ancient religion of his family.'
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptized at Mursley, Buckinghamshire, July 13, 1614.
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n435/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 416
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/182356111/john-fortescue
