1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "Sir Francis Fortescue, Baronet [S 1636] of Salden, cousin and heir male, being son of Francis Fortescue, the only surviving son of <strong>Sir Edward Fortescue</strong>, (buried at Mursley, 14 February 1662), younger son of the 1
2 CONC st Baronet. He was born about 1662, succeeded to the Baronetcy in 1717. He married before 7 May 1713, Mary, daughter of Henry Huddleston, of Sawston, co Cambridge (who died 1714/5), by Mary, daughter of Richard Bastock, of Wixhall
2 CONC , Salop. He died s.p. at Bath, 9 and was buried 11 November 1729, at Salden, aged 67, when the Baronetcy became dormant, he being 'the last male descendant of Queen Elizabeth's minister and so far as we know of Sir Adrian Fortescu
2 CONC e also'."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n435/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 416
2 CONT
