1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Skipwith-64
2 CONT
2 CONT Diana Skipwith was the fifth child and second daughter of Sir Henry Skipwith and his first wife Amy Kempe.
2 CONT
2 CONT Although Diana may have been addressed as 'Lady Diana' in America, this was only a courtesy title. The children of Knights did not inherit any title and, with the exception of the eldest son, or eldest surviving son, the children 
2 CONC of Baronets also did not inherit any title.
2 CONT
2 CONT Most of the information about Diana and Edward Dale's family came from several sources: "the Maiden Family of Virginia and Allied Families, 1623-1991" by Sarah Finch Maiden Rollins who copied most of the information from the book 
2 CONC "The Descendants of Capt. Thomas Carter of "Barford", Lancaster County, Virginia, (1912)", Joseph Lyon Miller. Other sources include the LDS, Family History Center and computer genealogy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Diana came to Virginia around 1652-1655 with her younger brother Graye/Grey. Legal documents in Lancaster County, Virginia, testify to her presence there in 1655. There is no record of Diana having married Edward Dale in England. 
2 CONC Edward Dale is said to have had three children, but whether Diana was the mother of all three has been disputed. The available documentary evidence can be used to support arguments either way and hinge on the question of whether D
2 CONC iana was referred to as 'Skipwith' both before (as one would expect) and after her marriage to Edward Dale. Given the paucity of documentary evidence, it seems unlikely that, in spite of what some may claim, the issue will ever be
2 CONC  settled beyond all reasonable doubt. Inevitably this means that genealogists, especially those who claim to be descended in some way, may choose their preferred option and record it as fact.
2 CONT
2 CONT Diana would appear to have died after Edward, since in his epitaph (recorded in the Carter Prayer Book) it mentions Diana as "left a little while to Mourne him". Diana and Edward were probably buried in the churchyard of the nearb
2 CONC y Church of England they attended, St. Mary's White Chapel. The tomb has not been located. Diana was about seventy years old when her husband died. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In article <88.e890cf.278ddc48@aol.com>, Joemaryjoa@aol.com wrote:
2 CONT  Hi Group: Since I have a copy of the 1674 deed in which Diana Skipwith refers to Daniel Harrison as her son in law, I thought that it would be of interest to the group to see the exact wording of this deed. This deed was obtained
2 CONC  by me at the Lancaster County, VA courthouse, and the photocopy was made by the Clerk of the Court. I have left blank spaces for the words that I could not make out. The spelling is exactly as it is written in the deed.
2 CONT
2 CONT This deed appears in Lancaster County, VA Deed Book 4, page 201- 202, and reads as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT  "Know all men by their presents that I Edward Dale of the County of Lancaster in Virginia, Gent., as well for and in consideration of a marriage already had and solemnized between Thomas Carter of the same county, Mercht. of the 
2 CONC one parte and Katherine his wife, daughter of me aforesaid Edward Dale of the other parte as also for diverse good causes and considerations mee thereunto moveing have given, granted, afirmed, bargained, solde, enfeoffed and confi
2 CONC rmed and doe by these presents for mee, my heirs and assignes and administes and of them give grante _____ bargain ____ enfeoofe and confirmed  unto aforesaid Thomas Carter and Katherine his wife and their heirs, all that plantati
2 CONC on whereon the said Thomas Carter now lives together with all houses, edifices, orchards, gardens, ffences, and outhouses thereunto belonging and appertaining or with the same now and occupied or enjoyed which said premises are se
2 CONC tt scituated lyeing and being in the aforesaid County of Lancaster  _____ _____ together by _____ _____ ffive hundred acres of land more or leff and me now in the occupation of the aforesaid Thomas Carter or his assignes to have a
2 CONC nd to hold the _____ plantation and premises _____ ____ and ____ of their appertenances unto the said Thomas and Katherine and their heirs to the  _____ only ye use and behalf of them the said Thomas and Katherine, their heirs and
2 CONC  assignes forever and to none other ufe or ufes intents or purposes whatsoever with waranty against all persons whatsoever claming by from or under mee the said Edward or my heirs with ____ ____ make further mentione of the  premi
2 CONC ses unto the said Thomas and Katherine and their heirs when a  whereupon lawfully required. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In witness whereof I the said Edward Dale have thereunto set my hand and seale Dated the 4th of December Ao Domo 1674.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Edward Dale His Seale
2 CONT
2 CONT ________ Charles Howell Sign. Mary _______ Sign.
2 CONT
2 CONT Recognit in Court, County  Lancaster _____ _____
2 CONT  _____ _____ December Ano Dom 1674. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Record
2 CONT  ____ ____ ____ ____ John Stretchley County Clerk
2 CONT
2 CONT Mentioned that I Diana the wife of the within mentioned Edward Dale for voluntarily and freely without any manner of compulsion toward the sale of said within mentioned and do hereby relinquish my right of dower to any of the said
2 CONC  within mentioned and doe hereby authorize my sonne in law Mr. Daniel  Harrison my lawful attorney acknowledge this my ____ in the Court of  Lancaster in witness whereof have foreunto sett my hand and seale this 8th day of Decembe
2 CONC r, Ao Dom 1674.
2 CONT
2 CONT Diana Dale Ye Seale In _____
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Howell p. Signature Mary ____ p. Signature
2 CONT
2 CONT Recognit in Court County  ______ ______ December Ao Dom 1674.  Record > _____  doe _____
2 CONT
2 CONT John Stretchley, County Clerk"
2 CONT
