2 CONT Will written October 28, 1710, Norfolk Co., Va, See Brief Abstraacts of Norfolk Co. Will 1710-1753, p. 14  Will names wife Alice  and children Stanhope, Solomon, Henry, Jr. and Jane (Jane married William Shipp).  ... unto my Elder
2 CONC  Son Standhope Butt the Land he now Lives upon to the Cypress branch beginning at the head of ye branch and Soe Running East to the Land of Roger Honsden ... with a provissor he my Said Son Doth not Molest his brother, Sollomon Bu
2 CONC tt of the Manner plantation, which if he Doth, he Shall forfeit all the Land that I have given and bequeathed unto him and to return to my Son Sollmon Butt.  ...unto my Son Henry Butt that Tract of Land knowne and Called Cutt the 
2 CONC name of the wallnutt neck and Soe running from the walnutt neck to aa branch Called the Long Beacon Ridge branch which Devides my Land & from the Land of my brother Richard Buttand Soe running up the Said branch to branch that is 
2 CONC called the Hummacker brtanch and from the Hummacker branch Die South to the Cypress Swamp which Said Land ...  ...unto my Son Sollomon Butt the plantation I now Live upon being the remaining part of the Land Left me by my father..
2 CONC .  ...unto my Son Henry Butt all that tract of Land Commonly known and Called by the name of Timber Neck and granted to me by Pattent Dated the fourth of August 1675 which said Land...  ...unto mny son Sollomon But the north Sid o
2 CONC f ye Cypress branch bounding upon my Standhope Butts Land....Likewise ....that tract of Land Commonly knowne and Called by the name oif Ireland...  ...unto my Son Henry Butt my Long Gunn and new Short Gunn Carbine pistells and hol
2 CONC sters a Reapur   {p. 15}...unto my Son Sollomon Butt my next Longest Gunn and Musquitt & Clubb; & one Reaper...  ...unto my Grand Daughters that is to Say, Sarah Elizabeth Katherine & Jane, the Daughters of my Daughter Jane which 
2 CONC married William, Ship each of them a Ewe a peice . ..  ...unto my Loveing wife Alice Butt my Two Negrows ...  ...my Two Sons Henry & Sollomon Butt Executors...  Witnesses: Thos Butt William Butt Ann Butt Henry But & Seal. Probated
2 CONC  Will May 18, 1711, Norfolk, VA
