2 CONT * 32. C2/Jas.I/S4/62; 2/Jas.I/H28/5; APC, 1621-3, p. 34.
2 CONT * 33. PROB 11/152, ff. 156v-157; J.E. Jackson, Hungerford Fam. Collections, iii. 8-9.
2 CONT * 34. Add. 33412, ff. 76-7.
2 CONT * 35.Vis. Som. (Harl. Soc. xi), 23; Add. 33412, f. 80; R. Atkins, Ancient and Present State of Glos. 210-11; J. Burke, Commoners, iii. 473; R.C. Hoare, Wilts. v. 46.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1604-1629/member/hungerford-anthony-1567-1627
2 CONT
2 CONT See also: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1558-1603/member/hungerford-anthony-1567-1627
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Anthony HUNGERFORD (Sir Knight), was born before 29 Oct 1564, in Great Bedwin, Wiltshire, England, and died 27 Jun 1627, in Blackbourton, Oxfordshire, England.  He was the son of Anthony HUNGERFORD (Sir Knight), and Bridget SHELLE
2 CONC Y. He married in 1595, Lucy Hungerford, his fifth cousin. Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. Edward HUNGERFORD (Sir Knight) 
2 CONT * 2. Bridget HUNGERFORD 
2 CONT * 3. Jane HUNGER-FORD 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Anthony Hungerford was descended from Walter HUNGERFORD (1º B. Hungerford of Farleigh), who was born 22 Jun 1378, Farleigh-Hungerford, Somersetshire, England, and died on 9 Aug 1449, and was buried in Salisbury Cathedral, Wiltshir
2 CONC e.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 1627 In the name of God Amen, in the three and twentieth day of June in the year of our Lord, one thousand five hundred Twentie and seven, I Sir Anthonie Hungerford of Black Bourton in the countie of Oxon... Sir John Hungerford my
2 CONC  brother, my son Anthonie Hungerford, Dame Sara my late wife, Gyles Hungerford my son, John Hungerford my son, my son Sir Edward Hungerford, Knight, my loving son in Lawe Robert Strange, Esquier, daughters Sarah & Sicilea [Cecilia
2 CONC ?], my three sons John, Henrie & Giles Hungerford, my sone Edward being my eldest son, John Hungerford my servant, Symon Croker my children's school master, Edward the plough boy, Mistress Bridget Strainge sister to my son in law 
2 CONC Robert Strainge, Executors Edward Hungerford [son] , loving son in lawe John Southby.
2 CONT
