2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://boards.ancestry.com/surnames.hungerford/206.2.1/mb.ashx Re: Ann Hungerford and Joos Lee, in England and Mass.] Posted:	28 Oct 2008 4:02AM
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Anne, the daughter of Sir Anthony & Bridget (Shelley) Hungerford, was buried on 9 May 1583 in Great Bedwyn, Wiltshire without ever being married per the Rev. J. E. Jackson(1805-1891) papers. His research is housed in the Wiltshi
2 CONC re Society Library in Devizes. He is probably the best source for the Hungerford family of England."
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT ===This looks to be fictional===
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://capecodgenes.com/web%20cards/ps08/ps08_296.html
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 HKTD-28; bd 7 perhaps related to Thomas HUNGERFORD  Birth: ABT. 1602; Bremhill, Wiltshire, England
2 CONT 821 b. place
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://boards.ancestry.com/surnames.hungerford/206.2.1/mb.ashx Re: Ann Hungerford and Joos Lee, in England and Mass.] Posted:	28 Oct 2008 4:02AM Classification: Query
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Anne, the daughter of Sir Anthony & Bridget (Shelley) Hungerford, was buried on 9 May 1583 in Great Bedwyn, Wiltshire without ever being married per the Rev. J. E. Jackson(1805-1891) papers. His research is housed in the Wiltshi
2 CONC re Society Library in Devizes. He is probably the best source for the Hungerford family of England. He makes no mention of Joos Lee that I've been able to find--which doesn't mean this couple didn't exist."
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://boards.ancestry.com/thread.aspx?mv=flat&m=206&p=surnames.hungerford Re: Ann Hungerford and Joos Lee, in England and Mass.] Posted:	30 Oct 2010 12:29PM
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Tryphosa Lee and Stephen Tracy are in my family tree as well.  However, Tryphosa's parents are unknown at this time. "The Adventurous Tryphosa (Lee) Tracy" by Robert S. Wakefield published in "The American Genealogist" is the mo
2 CONC st complete discussion of Tryphosa to my knowledge."
2 CONT
2 CONT From Who was Tryphosa/Trifasa Lee(Le):
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the wife of Stephen Tracy--their betrothal is recorded in the records of Leyden.(Image) Beyond that the intriguing record of her life invites a lot of speculation--even that she could have been related to the vanished Nich
2 CONC olas Lee.
2 CONT
2 CONT First of all, the targetted list of Pilgrim marriages (see below) shows that the Pilgrim Lees were associated by marriage with Samuel Fuller. (He married [http://www.geni.com/people/Bridget-Fuller/6000000003149834824?through=60000
2 CONC 00006444700295 Bridget Lee,] daughter of Josephine Lee and sister of [http://www.geni.com/people/Samuel-Lee/6000000008447860449?through=6000000006444700295 Samuel Lee].) There is also a John Lee and a Jane Lee in Leyden.(See the m
2 CONC arriage and guarantor lists.) '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Tryphosa-Tracy/6000000006444493068?through=6000000002928604177 Tryphosa Lee] is not known to be related to the other Lees.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
