1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Jerico Preston:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p12273.htm#i122727
2 CONT
2 CONT Jenico Preston, 5th Viscount Gormanston [1]
2 CONT *M, #122727, 
2 CONT *b. circa 1585, 
2 CONT *d. 14 March 1629/30
2 CONT *Last Edited=25 Jun 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT Jenico Preston, 5th Viscount Gormanston was born circa 1585.[2] He was the son of Christopher Preston, 4th Viscount Gormanston and Catherine FitzWilliam.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Margaret St. Lawrence, daughter of Nicholas St. Lawrence, 8th Baron Howth and Margaret Barnewall.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 14 March 1629/30.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded to the title of 5th Viscount Gormanston [I., 1478] on 24 January 1599/0.[2] He succeeded to the title of 8th Lord Preston of Gormanston [I., 1370] on 24 January 1599/0.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Jenico Preston, 5th Viscount Gormanston and Margaret St. Lawrence
2 CONT *1. Hon. Mary Preston [1] d. bt Mar 1665 - Jun 1666
2 CONT *2. Nicholas Preston, 6th Viscount Gormanston+[2] b. c 1608, d. 28 Jul 1643
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S15] George Edward Cokayne, editor, The Complete Baronetage, 5 volumes (no date (c. 1900); reprint, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 1983), volume I, page 240. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Baronetage.
2 CONT *2. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 2, page 1601. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT == Other References ==
2 CONT * Burke, Bernard, Sir. [http://archive.org/stream/genealogicalhera00inburk#page/500/mode/2up A genealogical and heraldic dictionary of the peerage and baronetage of the British Empire]. London : Harrison 1869. page 500
