2 CONT [https://static.secure.website/wscfus/263661/uploads/charles_barcroft_info.pdf “Barcroft Info”]
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Barcroft married 1st Dorothy Crosbie on 20 Feb 1632/33 at St. Olave's of Southwark in London. She was the daughter of John Crosbie of St. Albans in Hertfordshire. She apparently died a short time after the birth of her dau
2 CONC ghter Elizabeth. history of Southwark
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Barcroft married second ca 1634-36 Elizabeth. In Calendar of State Papers: Colonial America and the West Indies 1675-6, Addenda 1574-1674 p. 83, #189 an entry for 8 March 1639 about "Elizabeth, wife of Charles Barcroft of 
2 CONC Old Ford, Middlesex" to the effect that in August 1636 her husband abandoned his trade in London and went to Virginia "where he yet lives." The entry goes on to note that "his brother John Barcroft was there deceased" and that Cha
2 CONC rles Barcroft "merchant" was sending her yearly expenses. On his departure for Virginia, she had gone to live with her father and mother at Whitechapel where she stayed about a year. The entry concluded that "she denies any unlawf
2 CONC ul familiarity with John Barcroft, Thomas Bulkeley, or any other lewd person."
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Barcroft married a third wife named Magdalen ca 1640.
2 CONT
