2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Phebe Fenner was christened 05 Jan 1633 in Horley, Sussex, England.[1] Her parents were Arthur and Sarah (Browne) Fenner.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Phebe's parents died by about 1645, and she and several siblings arrived in New England about 1646, based on her brother Arthur's marriage in Providence in 1646. Her brothers Arthur and William settled in Rhode Island, and sibling
2 CONC s John and Sarah in Connecticut. Phebe likely lived with one of her siblings until she was of age.[2][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Phebe married, as his second wife, William Ward, on 28 March 1660, in Middletown, Hartford, Connecticut Colony.[4][5] Phebe is listed as the wife of William Ward in the TAG 15:84 article cited above.
2 CONT
2 CONT William and Phebe had children:[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas (1661), married Anna (Hannah) Tapping
2 CONT Phebe (1663), married Samuel Hall
2 CONT William (1665), married Abigail Collins
2 CONT Sarah (1667), married Benjamin Hand
2 CONT Ann (1671), married James Tapping
2 CONT Dorothy (1672), married Samuel Cooper
2 CONT George (1672), died young
2 CONT Susannah (1674), married John Southmayd
2 CONT John (1678), married Margaret Hubbard
2 CONT There are discrepancies between the compiled Middletown town records on FamilySearch (Barbour Collection) and the compiled church records for Middletown. The former does not list a son George, and the latter places Sarah's birth y
2 CONC ear as 1662.
2 CONT
2 CONT Phebe died 01 Sep 1691 in Middletown.[5] Find A Grave: Memorial #58068680
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
