1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Phebe Brown''', (also known as Phoebe Browne) was born before 1 October 1620, the date of her baptism, at Rusper, Sussex, England.  She died as Phebe Cornish on 22 December 1664 at Northampton, Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of William Browne and his wife Jane Mills.  Jane Mills had previously married John Burgis or Burges.
2 CONT
2 CONT Phebe Brown married three times:
2 CONT * m. (1) Thomas Lee, in England; he died 1645 with small-pox leaving three (3) children, Phebe, Jane and Thomas; 
2 CONT * m. (2) about 1657 Greenfield Larrabee he died leaving five (5) children, Greenfield, John, Elizabeth, Joseph and Sarah; Joseph died young; 
2 CONT * m. (3) about 1661, James Cornish and had two sons, James and one still-born, with which Phebe (Brown) Lee-Larrabee-Cornish died in child-bed at Northampton.  James Cornish survived her, and died  29 Oct 1698 at about age 84 in W
2 CONC indsor, Hartford, Connecticut.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Lee born ?, married before 1640, Phebe Brown In Rusper, England.  He died of smallpox on their ship to New England in 1645. Her parents traveled with the Lees, and  Phebe’s mother also died of smallpox on that voyage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children  of Thomas Lee and Phebe Brown, baptized at Rusper, England: (Hartford Times 4/22/1959) 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Jane Lee Baptized 9/12/1640, Rusper, England Married (1) Samuel Hyde of Norwich, Conn,, (2) John Birchard. 
2 CONT # Phoebe Lee Baptized 5/20/1642, Rusper, England, married John Large of Long Island 
2 CONT # Lieut.  Thomas Lee E.A.,, Baptized 9/29/1644, married (1) Sarah Kirkland, (2) Mary De Wolf (1676)
2 CONT
2 CONT When she married Greenfield Larrabee, Phebe was identified as the widow of Thomas Lee and the daughter of William Brown of Ruskin, England, Saybrook, CT, and South Hampton and Hempstead, Long Island.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children with Greenfield Larrabee (from http://boards.ancestry.com/thread.aspx?mv=flat&m=134&p=surnames.larrabee), according to Saco Valley Settlements:
2 CONT
2 CONT # GREENFIELD,2 b. Apr. 20, 1648; m. Alice, dau. of Thomas Burke, in March, 1672, and settled in Norwich, Conn., on the eastern side of the river near his father-in-law. In this place he prospered, acquired extensive lands, and bro
2 CONC ught up a family of children as will presently appear. His name is found on many early documents. Alice, his wife, d. Nov. 23, 1729. He d. Feb. 3, 1739, rising 90.
2 CONT # JOHN,2 second son of Greenfield, 1st, b. Feb. 23, 1649; removed to Windham, Conn., from Norwich with a family. In 1697, he had broken land, built a house, and established himself upon a tract granted him on condition that he bui
2 CONC ld upon it and run the ferry for seven years. He was admitted and enrolled as one of the inhabitants of Windham, May 30, 1693. Children's names with third generation.
2 CONT # ELIZABETH,2 b. Jan. 23, 1652.
2 CONT # JOSEPH,2 b. in March, 1655; d. Aug. 10, 1657.
2 CONT # SARAH,2 b. Mar. 3, 1658; m. John Fox, of Concord, June 20, 1678.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/Grace-Cooke/6000000002341349572?through=6000000003086534779 was not daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Greenfield-Larrabee/6000000001562946924?through=6000000002341349572 & https://www.geni.com/peo
2 CONC ple/Phebe-Cornish/6000000002237743491?through=6000000002341349572.  They did not have a child called Grace.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Children with James Cornish:
2 CONT #  James Cornish, b. 1663; d. 2 April 1740, m. 1) Elizabeth Thrall 2) Hannah Hilliard, widow of Thomas Humphrey
2 CONT # one still-born, b. 1664.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/memories/LZZN-D4J
2 CONT
2 CONT From Joshua Hempstead's diary p 684. April 10, 1757.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Lee Sr. came from Rusper, Sussex, vicinity of Kenilworth, England. He embarked for America with his wife Phoebe, and three children, Thomas Jr., Jane and Phoebe in the year 1645. Together with the Lees were the Reverend Wil
2 CONC liam Brown and Jane (Burgis) his wife, father and mother of Mrs Lee, and their Children, a son and a daughter. On the passage both Mr. Lee and Mrs. Brown died of smallpox and were buried at sea. Mrs. Lee and her children together 
2 CONC with her father Reverend Brown, settled in Saybrook, as all of this region was then called, where the Browns remained for a time, afterwards going elsewhere but leaving the Lees there. As the Lees have lived at this place from a t
2 CONC ime which the memory of man runneth not, their holdings going back of any known records, it is believed by most familiar with the family history that they came to Land already secured by Thomas Lee, first, either by a previous vis
2 CONC it or through his old friend and neighbor in England, Matthew Griswold, first, who had just taken up land adjoining the Lee holding on the South.  The brief stay of the Reverend Mr. Brown at Saybrook may well have been for the pur
2 CONC pose of seeing his widowed daughter settled on the estate selected for her by her late husband.  Widow Phoebe (Brown) Lee married 2nd Greenfield Larrabee, probably in 1647. Their daughter Elizabeth married Joshua Hempstead, father
2 CONC  of the diarist Joshua. Phoebe married (3) James Cornish.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000188025319889&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
