2 CONT ANCESTRY OF HANNAH (TILLINGHAST) ABORN
2 CONT
2 CONT Pardon Tillinghast, b. 1622 at Seven Cliffs, Sussex Co., England.
2 CONT He served in Cromwell's Army.  Came to Providence abt, 1646.  He was
2 CONT Deputy 1672-1700.  Member of Town Council 1688-1707.  April 14,
2 CONT 1711, he deeded his house called Baptist meeting house, "situated
2 CONT between the Town Street and salt water, together with the lot whereon
2 CONT said meeting house standeth, to the Church and their successors, for the
2 CONT Christian love, good will and affection which I bear to the Church of
2 CONT Christ in said Providence, the which I am in fellowship with, and have
2 CONT the care of as being elder of said Church."
2 CONT He d. Jan. 29, 1718.  His will, proved Feb. 11, 1718, says: "I
2 CONT do bequeath my life and spirit into the hands of the Fountain of life and
2 CONT Father of spirits, from whom I received it, and my body to the
2 CONT dust from whence it came, in hope of a resurrection to eternal life,"
2 CONT Inventory, L1,542, 4s, 3d.  He was buried in his own lot at the south
2 CONT end of town.  He m. (2nd) April 16, 1664, Lydia, dau. of Philip and
2 CONT Lydia (Masters) Taber.  Their son
2 CONT Joseph Tillinghast, b. Aug. 11, 1677, in Provedence, m. (2nd) abt.
2 CONT 1721, Mary, dau. of Abraham Paris, of Barbados, mariner, and widow
2 CONT of -- Hendron, d. Dec. 1, 1763.  Their son ( his 12th child)
2 CONT Daniel Tillinghast, b. June 2, 1732, in Newport, m. Hannah, dau. of
2 CONT Robert and Amey (Crawford) Gibbs. Their dau.
2 CONT Hannah Tillinghast, m. Samuel Aborn.
