2 DATE AFT 19 APR 1699
2 PLAC Old Village Cemetery
2 ADDR
3 CITY Dedham
3 STAE Massachusetts
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 19 APR 1699
2 ADDR
3 CITY Dedham
3 STAE Massachusetts
3 CTRY Colonial America
1 OCCU Weaver, Farmer
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Additional Information for Robert Ware, Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE: See booklet, "The Descendants of Robert Ware of Dedham, Norfolk Co., Massachusetts" for this line of the Ware Family.  A copy is on file Maine State Library, LMA Bldg, Augusta, Maine.  I also have a copy in my files.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Ware had lands granted to hum in Dedham 6. 12. 1642 (Feb. 6, 1642-3).  He was made a Freeman on May 26, 1647; was a member of the Artillery Company in 1644.  He lived and died in Dedham, though three of his sons -- John, Na
2 CONC thaniel, and Robert -- removed to Wollomonopoag, incorporated as Wentham in 1673.  His name stands second in point of wealth on the tax list.  His will, made February 25, 1698, was proved May 11, 1699.  The inventory taken May 3, 
2 CONC was L250 2 10.  (Copy of his will is in the booklet referenced above.) Was born in England and immigrated to Virginia Colony with his father and brother, Peter.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Citing This Record "Pedigree Resource File," database, FamilySearch (http://familysearch.org/pal:/MM9.2.1/S56R-221 : accessed 2014-01-10), entry for Robert /Ware/, Jr..
2 CONT  ===============================================
2 CONT John /Ware/ birth:  6 October 1646   death:  7 April 1718  
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel /Ware/ birth:  7 October 1648   death:  10 July 1724  
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret /Ware/ birth:  14 February 1651   death:  22 July 1664  
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert /Ware/ birth:  1 August 1653   death:  16 September 1724  
2 CONT
2 CONT Esther /Ware/ birth:  28 September 1655   death:  3 September 1734  
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel /Ware/ birth:  30 September 1657   death:   
2 CONT
2 CONT Ephraim /Ware/ birth:  5 November 1659   death:  26 March 1753  
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth /Ware/ birth:  19 November 1661   death:   
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph /Ware/ birth:  8 September 1663   death:  22 September 1663  
2 CONT
2 CONT Ebenezer /Ware/ birth:  28 October 1667   death:  1765  
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Robert Ware, the immigrant ancestor of the Ware family of Dedham, Needham and Wrentham, Mass., is presumed to have been b. in England. Where and when he was b. and who were his parents remain unknown to this descendant. He d. Apr.
2 CONC  19, 1699 at Dedham, Mass., his then age not of record.
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. 1) Mar. 24, 1644/5 at Dedham, Margaret Hunting, dau. of John Hunting, the first elder of the Dedham church, and his wife Esther Seaborn, b. or bapt. Sept. 21, 1628 at Hoxne in Suffolk, England. She d. Aug. 26, 1670 at Dedham
2 CONC , Mass.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert m. 2) May 3, 1676 at Dedham as her only husband, Hannah Jones, dau. of Thomas and Ellen Jones, b. Mar 28, 1636 at Dorchester, Mass. where she d. Apr. 20, 1721 (g.s.). There were no children of this marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Robert Ware and Margaret Hunting, all b. of record at Dedham, Mass., are:
2 CONT
2 CONT • i. Capt. John Ware, b. Oct 11, 1646, d. Apr. 7, 1718 at Wrentham, Mass.; m. 1) Dec. 10, 1668 at Dedham, Mary Metcalf, dau. of Michael Metcalf, Jr. and Mary Fairbanks, b. Aug. 15, 1646 at Dedham. She d. Mar. 22, 1676/7 at Dedham.
2 CONC  He m. 2) Mar. 24, 1678/9 at Dedham, the wid. Joanna (Gay) Kingsley, who d. Oct. 26, 1708 at Wrentham. He m. 3) Dec. 21, 1709 at Sherborn, Mass., the widow Dorothy Wood, who d. Dec. 10, 1728 at Sherborn.
2 CONT
2 CONT • ii. Nathaniel Ware, b. Oct. 7, 1648, d. July 10, 1724 at Wrentham, Mass.; m. Oct. 12, 1696 at Wrentham, Mary Wheelock, who subsequently had two additional husbands and d. Mar. 25, 1750 at Wrentham.
2 CONT
2 CONT • iii. Margaret Ware, b. Feb. 14, 1650/1, d. in her youth at Dedham, July 22, 1664.
2 CONT
2 CONT • iv. Mary Ware, b. in Mar. 1651/52; no further record available.
2 CONT
2 CONT • v. Robert Ware, Jr., b. Aug. 1, 1653, d. Sept. 16, 1724 at Wrenthan, Mass.; m. 1) June 4, 1677 at Dedham, Sarah Metcalf, dau. of Michael Metcalf, Jr. and Mary Fairbanks, b. Dec. 7, 1648 at Dedham. She was the mother of all of Ro
2 CONC bert's children, and d. Apr. 13, 1717 at Wrentham, Mass. He m. 2) Feb. 26, 1719/20 at Wrentham, Elizabeth Holbrook, who d. July 28, 1723 at Wrentham.
2 CONT
2 CONT • vi. Esther Ware, b. Sept. 28, 1655, d. Sept. 3, 1734 at Wrentham, Mass.; m. May 13, 1673 at Dedham, Rev. Samuel Man, first minister of the Wrentham, Mass. church, s. of William Mann and Mary Jarred, b. July 6, 1647 at Cambridge,
2 CONC  Mass. He d. May 22, 1719 at Wrentham, Mass.
2 CONT
2 CONT • vii. Samuel Ware, b. Sept. 30, 1657, d. betw. Mar. 6 and Mar. 22, 1730/1 at Dedham; m. 1) July 21, 1690 at Dedham, Elizabeth Rice, who d. Nov. 18, 1719 at Dedham. He m. 2) July 27, 1721 at Dedham, Sarah (Fuller)(Day) Carpenter, 
2 CONC dau. of Lieut. Thomas Fuller and Hannah Flower, b. May 7, 1659 at Dedham where she d. Mar. 31, 1736. She was the successive widow of Ralph Day, Jr. of Dedham and Capt. John Carpenter of Rehoboth, Mass., Woodstock, Conn. and lastly
2 CONC  Dedham, Mass.
2 CONT
2 CONT • viii. Ephraim Ware, b. Nov. 5, 1659, d. Mar. 26, 1753 at Needham, Mass.; m. July 13, 1685 at Needham, Mass., Hannah Herring, who d. July 10, 1738 at Needham.
2 CONT
2 CONT • ix. Elizabeth Ware, b. Nov. 19, 1661.
2 CONT
2 CONT • x. Joseph Ware, b. Sept. 13, 1663, d. in infancy Sept. 22, 1663.
2 CONT
2 CONT • xi. Ebenezer Ware, b. Oct. 28, 1667, d. in Jan. 1765 at Needham, Mass.; m. Mar. 18, 1689/90 at Dedham, Martha Herring, who d. Jan. 30, 1709/10.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Robert Ware was born in 1611 in Glouchestershire, England. His parents were Robert WARE (1595 – 1659) and Jane WADE (1595 – ). He came from his English home to the colony of Massachusetts Bay some time before the autumn of 1642. T
2 CONC he earliest date at which the name in any form occurs on the Dedham Records, is 25 Nov 1642, when “Robert Weares is admitted to the purchase of Thomas Eames his house lott and three acres of land.  He married Margaret HUNTING 24 M
2 CONC ar 1645 in Dedham Mass. Six years after Margaret’s death, Robert, then about 51 years of age, married Hannah Jones 3 May 1676. Robert and Hannah lived long lives for their time. He became known as Robert Ware “the Aged.” He died i
2 CONC n Dedham on 19 Apr  1699, at 74 years of age, leaving an estate of more than 250 pounds.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Robert Ware, the immigrant ancestor of the Ware family of Dedham, Needham and Wrentham, Mass., is presumed to have been b. in England. Where and when he was b. and who were his parents remain unknown to this descendant. He d. Apr.
2 CONC  19, 1699 at Dedham, Mass., his then age not of record.
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. 1) Mar. 24, 1644/5 at Dedham, Margaret Hunting, dau. of John Hunting, the first elder of the Dedham church, and his wife Esther Seaborn, b. or bapt. Sept. 21, 1628 at Hoxne in Suffolk, England. She d. Aug. 26, 1670 at Dedham
2 CONC , Mass.
