2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Ware-111
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebecka Ware immigrated from the vicinity of Wrentham, Suffolk, England to New England with the family of Rev. John Phillips in 1638. Rev Phillips referred to Rebecca as his servant. Rebecka married Thomas Paine, a weaver and farm
2 CONC er, in 1640 at Dedham, Massachusetts. The were likely married by Rev. Phillips. Thomas was born 18 Jan 1612/13, probably at Wrentham, Suffolk, England. He was the son of Thomas Paine and Elizabeth Bloomfield.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Paine Jr. immigrated from Yarmouth, England to Salem, Massachusetts with his family. Thomas Paine Sr., a weaver from Wrentham, Suffolk, England, boarded the ship Mary Anne at Yarmouth, England in 1637 with his wife Elizabet
2 CONC h and six children: Thomas, John, Marey, Elizabeth, Dorothey and Sarah.[2] Thomas bought a vessel rather than sail in another's ship.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Thomas Paine and Rebecka Ware
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas and Rebecca had four children.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT # Rebecka Paine, b. 19 Sep 1642
2 CONT # Thomas Paine, b. 29 Mar 1644
2 CONT # John Paine, b. 27 Apr 1646
2 CONT # Elizabeth Paine, b. 6 Mar 1648
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Paine Jr. was a selectman of Dedham, Massachusetts where he lived for 46 years. He died at Dedham 2 Aug 1686, age 73, eight days after making his will. Rebecka survived him, as she is written into his will. He also leaves b
2 CONC equests to Thomas Patton, husband of his daughter Rebecka, deceased, a granddaughter Rebecka Patton, his daughter Elizabeth Hunting, and his sons Thomas Paine and John Paine.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage[1][2] Bef 23 Apr 1641 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # New England Marriages Prior to 1700  By Clarence Almon Torrey Page 562 < [https://books.google.com/books?id=mOgK8dM9qqUC&pg=PA552&lpg=PA552&dq=rebecca+ware+paine&source=bl&ots=ZhFk8fEFJm&sig=K-CEiShtoV55KGN4T6e4GSVYpr4&hl=en&sa=
2 CONC X&ved=0ahUKEwi60P_u65bKAhWISCYKHWK8Cqw4ChDoAQgbMAA#v=onepage&q=rebecca%20ware%20paine&f=false GoogleBooks] >
2 CONT # 1. Dedham (Massachusetts). Town Clerk; Julius Herbert Tuttle; Benjamin Fisher; and Don Gleason Hill. The early records of the town of Dedham, Massachusetts. (Dedham, Massachusetts: Dedham Transcript Press, 1886-1936), Vol. 2, p.
2 CONC  25.  ‘Thomas Paine & his wife Rebecka were received into ye co'munion of the church 23 of ye 2'd m. 1641. [Note: In old-styles dates, the second month is April. More info may be found here.]’
2 CONT #2.↑ 3. Thomas2 Payne, in Paine, Nathaniel Emmons; Henry Delavan Paine; and Horace Marshfield Paine. Thomas Payne of Salem and His Descendants: The Salem Branch of the Paine Family. (Haverhill, Mass.: Record Publishing Company, 19
2 CONC 28), 23. "Rev. John Phillips of Wrentham … wrote a letter to Gov. John Winthrop in which he stated among other things that 'Thomas Paine of Salem and my servant Rebecca Ware have been thrice published in marriage at Salem and Dedh
2 CONC am.' His letter was dated at Roxbury, 17 Oct. 1640. … no marriages were recorded on the town records of Dedham for the year 1640, but of this marriage in that year there can be no doubt." 
2 CONT # WikiTree contributors, "Rebecka (Ware) Paine (abt.1620-1687)," WikiTree: The Free Family Tree, (https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Ware-111 : accessed 21 June 2024).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/LZNK-92N/rebecca-ware-1620-1687
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebecca Ware
2 CONT Female
2 CONT 1620–3 March 1687
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Brief Life History of Rebecca
2 CONT
2 CONT When Rebecca Ware was born in 1620, in Wrentham, Suffolk, England, her father, Robert Ware Sr, was 31 and her mother, Margarye Ware, was 30. She married Thomas Paine on 17 October 1640, in Dedham, Norfolk, Massachusetts, United St
2 CONC ates. They were the parents of at least 2 sons and 2 daughters. She died on 3 March 1687, in Dedham, Suffolk, Massachusetts Bay Colony, British Colonial America, at the age of 67, and was buried in Cove Burying Ground, Eastham, Ba
2 CONC rnstable, Massachusetts, United States.
2 CONT
