2 CONT 10. THOMAS PAYNE, (III), of Dedham, Mass., son of Thomas (7,) (Chap. 11 and 1v.) B. in Cooklieor Wrentom (?,) Suffolk county, England,  born January 17, 1612. M. , 1640. D. in Dedham (?,) August 3, 1686, aged 74 years.  (JVife)— B
2 CONC . in , , 1615 (?.) D. in , 16 (?).
2 CONT
2 CONT Children. Probably all born in Dedham.
2 CONT # 57. Rebecca, b. September 19, 1642. (Chap. vn.)
2 CONT # 58. Thomas, b. March 19, 1644. (Chap. vm to x.)
2 CONT # 59. John, b. April 27, 1646. (Chap, x1.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Linen weaver. Emigrated in 1637, at 25 years of age, with his father's family, from Wrentom, England, to Salem, Mass. Removed to Dedham, Mass., probably about 1640. (Chap. 1v.)
