2 CONC  Family Trees] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 20 2019, 2:09:46 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT
2 CONT Perhaps sons Thomas and Andrew were twins.
2 CONT
2 CONT By 1680 some of Edward Wade's family are no longer living in York County but instead have moved just a few miles south to James City County. The reason becomes obvious. Mary Hampton Duke had married Edward Wade sometime after Nove
2 CONC mber 1670. She had a large estate in James City that had been given to her by her father Thomas Hampton. This estate next to Henry Duke became the home place for some of the Wades for years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cavaliers and Pioneers, Volume II, Patent Book 8, Page 328
2 CONT A patent dated 20 April 1694 to Mr. Edward Wade for 83 acres in James City County must pertain to Edward Wade II, James City County adjoins York County. This parcel was next to land of John Hixe on a branch of Warrany Swamp, land 
2 CONC formerly belonging to Mr. Collins, land of Gammase foy, Rockahock path and Warrany land.
2 CONT
2 CONT !THIS INFORMATION WAS TAKEN FROM "THE VENTURERS" BY VIRGINIA MEYNARD PAGE 24
2 CONT
2 CONT Toby Fetters's - Spouse of ninth great grandaunt Mary Rogness's - Spouse of ninth great grandaunt
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for EDWARD WADE II: from Elaine Waiters First Located: Father's Will Last Located: Before 1704 Rent Roll Will of Edward Wade (Father of Edward WadeII) Pages 11-13, 9 Nov 1675, Proved 24 Apr 1677 at Court for York County By 1
2 CONC 680 some of Edward Wade's family are no longer living in York County but instead have moved just a few miles south to James City County. The reason becomesobvious. Mary Hampton Duke had married Edward Wade sometime after November 
2 CONC 1670. She had a large estate in James City that had been given to her by her father Thomas Hampton. This estate next to Henry Duke became the home place for someof the Wades for years. Cavaliers and Pioneers, Volume II, Patent Boo
2 CONC k 8, Page 328 A patent dated 20 April 1694 to Mr. Edward Wade for 83 acres in JamesCity County must pertain to Edward Wade II, James City County adjoins York County. This parcel was next to land of John Hixe on a branch of Warrany
2 CONC  Swamp, land formerly belonging to Mr. Collins, land of Gammase foy, Rockahock path and Warrany land. Marriage 1 Children James Sr, Wade b: Abt 1665 in New Kent Co.,VA Edward III Wade b: Abt 1660 in VA Marriage 2 Mary Hampton Marr
2 CONC ied:Aft 1670 in Wilmington Parish,James City County,VA Children Thomas Wade b: Abt 1670 Andrew Wade b: Abt 1670 in VA Henry Wade b: Abt 1671 John Wade b:Abt 1672
2 CONT
2 CONT !BIRTH RECORD;  INFO FROM ANCESTRAL FILE #PVFF-JD MARRIAGE RECORD;  "            "            " DEATH RECORD;
2 CONT
