1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Mary Barker, wife of Isaac Stearns of Watertown, Arbella Passenger=
2 CONT
2 CONT Born Jan 1, 1604 in Stoke-by-Nayland, England, daughter of John Barker and Margaret Walter. She married Isaac Stearns by 1625, and they came to Massachusetts Bay with the Winthrop Fleetin 1630.  Died on Apr. 23, 1677 in Watertown,
2 CONC  Middlesex County, Massachusetts, USA.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 23 May 1665 "Goodwife Stearns Senior" was one of several Watertown residents warned to town meeting to answer for not "attending their seats in the meetinghouse appointed them by the town."  
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT # Mary Learned
2 CONT # Anna (Hannah) Freeman
2 CONT # John
2 CONT # Isaac
2 CONT # Sarah Stone
2 CONT # Samuel
2 CONT # Elizabeth Manning
2 CONT # Abigail Morse
2 CONT
2 CONT 8 children
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT This person migrated to New England during the Puritan Great Migration (1620-1640) By 1625 Mary Barker, daughter of John and Margaret (Walter) Barker of Stoke Nayland. On 23 May 1665 "Goodwife Stearns Senior" was one of several Wa
2 CONC tertown residents warned to town meeting to answer for not "attending their seats in the meetinghouse appointed them by the town". She died at Watertown on 23 April 1677.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Birth:  1603 Suffolk, England Death:  Apr. 23, 1677 Watertown Middlesex County Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Barker was born 1 Jan 1604 (1603 and 1604 are both used on Find a Grave site) in Stoke-by-Nayland, daughter of John and Margaret (Walter) Barker. She married Isaac Stearns Stoke by Nayland, Suffolk, 20 May 1622, and they came
2 CONC  to Massachusetts Bay with the Winthrop Fleetin 1630. On 23 May 1665 "Goodwife Stearns Senior" was one of several Watertown residents warned to town meeting to answer for not "attending their seats in the meetinghouse appointed th
2 CONC em by the town." She died at Watertown on 23 April 1677. (John Brooks Threlfall has identified the parents and other ancestors of Mary Barker.) They had 7 children: John, Mary Learned, Anna (Hannah) Freeman, Isaac, Sarah Stone, Sa
2 CONC muel, Elizabeth Manning, & Abigail Morse.  Source: Anderson's Winthrop Fleet.  Mary Barker was born 1 Jan 1604 in Stoke-by-Nayland, daughter of John and Margaret (Walter) Barker. She married Isaac Stearns Stoke by Nayland, Suffolk
2 CONC , 20 May 1622, and they came to Massachusetts Bay with the Winthrop Fleetin 1630. On 23 May 1665 "Goodwife Stearns Senior" was one of several Watertown residents warned to town meeting to answer for not "attending their seats in t
2 CONC he meetinghouse appointed them by the town." She died at Watertown on 23 April 1677. (John Brooks Threlfall has identified the parents and other ancestors of Mary Barker.) They had 7 children:  John, Mary Learned, Anna (Hannah) Fr
2 CONC eeman, Isaac, Sarah Stone, Samuel, Elizabeth Manning, &  Abigail Morse.  Source: Anderson's Winthrop Fleet.
