1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====Birth
2 CONT * ''Vital Records of Andover Massachusetts, to the End of the Year 1849''. Vol. I Births. Topsfield, Mass.: The Topsfield Historical Society, 1912. [https://archive.org/details/vitalrecordsofan01ando/page/27/mode/1up Archive.org, 
2 CONC p. 28]
2 CONT ** "George, s. George and Dorcas, Dec. 22, 1692."
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Marriage
2 CONT * "Massachusetts, Town Clerk, Vital and Town Records, 1626-2001", [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:QPZH-X4PV FamilySearch] (Sat Mar 09 20:43:54 UTC 2024), Entry for Geo Abbott and Mary Phillips, 29 Nov 1721.
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Book
2 CONT * "Abbot Genealogy." ''The Essex Antiquarian; a Quarterly Magazine Devoted to the Biography, Genealogy, History and Antiquities of Essex County, Massachusetts''. Vol. 1.  Salem, Mass.:1897. Archive.org, 
2 CONT ** '''On [https://archive.org/stream/essexantiquarian01perluoft#page/n51/mode/2up page 36]:'''
2 CONT *** Capt. George Abbot^, born in Andover June 7, 1655. Was a selectman of Andover, where he resided, and a man of Christian character. He married Dorcas Graves April 17, 1678; and died Feb. 26, 1735-6. His wife survived him, and d
2 CONC ied, his widow, Feb. 18, 1739-40, being "aged."
2 CONT *** Children, born in Andover: — 
2 CONT **** 24 — I. Sarah3, b. Aug. 26, 1679; d. Nov. 17, 1679. 
2 CONT **** 25 — II. Josephs, b. Oct. 7, 1680; d. young. 
2 CONT **** 26 — III. Marthas, b. Feb. 12, 1682-3; d. Dec. 4, 1683.
2 CONT **** 27 — IV. Hannahs, b. Feb. 27, 1684-5; m. Dea. John Osgood Sept. 16, 1708; and d. Dec. 25, 1774. He d.in 1765, aged eighty-three. 
2 CONT **** 28 — v. Daniels, b. Jan. 10, 1687-8.
2 CONT **** 29 — VI. Elizabeths, b. July 25, 1690; m. Benjamin Abbot
2 CONT **** 30 — VII. Georges, b. Dec. 22, 1692.
2 CONT **** 31 — VIII. Henrys, b. June 12, 1696.
2 CONT **** 32 — IX. Isaacs, b. April 4, 1699.
2 CONT ** '''[Differs somewhat with 36:] [https://archive.org/details/essexantiquarian01perluoft/page/n53/mode/2up page 39]:'''
2 CONT *** Capt. George Abbot3, born in Andover Dec. 22, 1692. He was a shoemaker in his early life, and lived on the homestead with his father, in Andover. He married Mary Phillips of Salem Nov. 29, 1721 ; and died March 19, 1768, aged 
2 CONC seventy-five. His wife survived him, and died Oct. 4, 1785, aged ninety-one.
2 CONT *** Children, born in Andover:— 
2 CONT **** 122 — I. Mary4, b. March 12, 1723; m. first, Stephen Abbot (86); and, second, Jonathan Abbot (180). 
2 CONT **** 123 — George4, b. Dec. 14, 1724.
2 CONT **** 124 — ELIZABETH4, b. Sept. II, 1726; d. Jan. 7, 1726-7.
2 CONT **** 125 — ELIZABETH4, b. Nov. 5, 1727; m., first, Benjamin Abbot (168) of Hollis; second, J. Pollard of Westford; and, third, Capt. Josiah Bowers of Billerica.
2 CONT **** 126 — Sarah4, b. Jan. 14, 1730; m. Rev. Nathan Holt of Danvers Aug. 4, 1757; and d. Dec. 26, 1797.
2 CONT **** 127 — Samuel4, b. Feb. 25, 1732.
2 CONT **** 128 — VII. HANNAH4, b. Dec. 14, 1733 ; m. William Foster, jr., Jan. 9, 1755; and d. March 26, 1820.
2 CONT
2 CONT ====17 July 1767 Last Will & Testament (not indexed as of 13 Jan 2026): [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-C9YY-Y9W4?lang=en&i=840 FamilySearch].
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ====FindAGrave®: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/122784917/george-abbot George Abbot 1692–1768]
2 CONT BIRTH: 22 Dec 1692 • Andover, Essex, Massachusetts
2 CONT DEATH: 19 Mar 1768 (aged 75) • Andover, Essex, Massachusetts
2 CONT BURIAL: South Church Cemetery, Andover, Essex County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT '''Inscription:''' "SACRED To the Memory of Cap. George Abbot, who died March 19, 1768, AEt. 76 and of Mary his wife who died Oct. 4, 1785 AEt. 91 years & 2 mo" — "The righteous shall be in everlasting remembrance."
2 CONT
