1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Her marriage to Jonathan Jennings is proven, as is her paternity which is Giles (not William) Parker. Please refer to the following sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/discussions/228367?msg=1461783 Discussion regarding her real paternity.]
2 CONT
2 CONT With regard to their sons, Edmund Jennings MP and Jonathan Jennings MP:
2 CONT
2 CONT Edmund Jennings, MP (1626-1691) of Ripon, Yorks. was the first son of Jonathan Jennings, Sr. by '''Elizabeth, daughter of Giles Parker of Newby,''' Yorks.. (Edmund and brother Jonathan Jennings, Jr. married daughters of Sir Edward
2 CONC  Barkham, Bt. of Tottenham, Mdx. and Southacre, Norf., Anne Barkham and Margaret Barkham). 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1660-1690/member/jennings-edmund-1626-91 History of Parliament Online]
2 CONT
2 CONT Again: "Jonathan Jennings barrister, died 24 August 1649 married '''Elizabeth Jennings daughter and co-heiress of Giles Parker of Newby, York Co., England.''' "
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/documentednoteso00doug/page/14/mode/2up?q=giles Documented notes on Jennings and allied families by Doughtie, Beatrice Mackey, b. 1899 (p.14 of the text)]
2 CONT
2 CONT And finally she is described the same way on the Jennings family pedigree:
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.google.com/books/edition/The_Visitation_of_the_County_of_Yorke_Be/ykNjAAAAcAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=0 The Visitation of the County of Yorke, Begun in 1665 and Finished in 1666 (ed. by Robert Davies) By William Dugdale (1859), p
2 CONC .58]
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000174023817897 Image of the Jennings of Rippon, Yorkshire pedigree chart]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Elizabeth Parker'''  born ABT 1606/7 in Newby or Ripon, Yorkshire, England Died: 1630 - England 
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: William Parker Lord Morley And Monteagle b: ABT 1575 in Newby, Yorkshire, England  Mother: Elizabeth Tresham b: ABT 1580 in Rushton, Dorsetshire, England
