1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Wikipedia Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>James Hamilton, Lord Paisley</strong> (d. bef. 1670) was the eldest son of James Hamilton, 2nd Earl of Abercorn and Katherine Clifton, 2nd Baroness Clifton.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 28 April 1653, in London, he married Catherine Lenthall, niece of William Lenthall, Speaker of the Long Parliament. They had one daughter:
2 CONT * Catherine Hamilton (c. 1653 – 24 May 1723), who married first William Lenthall of Burford, grandson of the Speaker (d. 1686), and second another relative, Charles Hamilton, 5th Earl of Abercorn.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Bodleian Library preserves one of his letters, from 1660, asking his uncle Sir George Hamilton, 1st Baronet for some preferment at the Restoration. However, he died before his father, so that his brother George succeeded as Ea
2 CONC rl of Abercorn."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: Wikipedia contributors, 'James Hamilton, Lord Paisley', <em>Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia</em>, 16 August 2012, 16:16 UTC, <http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=James_Hamilton,_Lord_Paisley&oldid=507704629> [acces
2 CONC sed 30 December 2012]
