1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Peyton, Henry, brother of Colonel Valentine Peyton (q. v.), was born in London, 1630-1631, was a citizen and merchant tailor of that city, came to Westmoreland county, Virginia, about 1656, and died there in 1659. 
2 CONC He married Ellen Partington, daughter of Richard Partington, of London, and left issue. [http://vagenweb.org/tylers_bios/vol1-29.htm Encyclopedia of Virginia Biography]
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT * B-9 Gentleman Henry Peyton came to Virginia in 1656 at the age of 26 and settled Westmoreland Co., procuring an estate of 1900 acres before his premature death just three years later. Most of his land holdings lay along the bank
2 CONC s of the Aquia Creek in what is now Stafford County. His father was Henry Peyton(1590-1656) of Lincoln's Inn. Henry Peyton the immigrant was the progenitor of the Westmoreland-Stanfford County, Virginia line of PEYTON. Page 9. Fro
2 CONC m book "PEYTONs Along the Aquia" page 19. 
