1 NOTE CAVEAT:
2 CONT There were many Richard Cocke men in 1600s in Henrico Co. VA, two of whom were
2 CONT even half-brothers!
2 CONT Use the above Volume 1 to learn ot distinguish the many different Richard
2 CONT Cockes of 1600s in VA;
2 CONT ------------------------
2 CONT and another good Cocke family tree at
2 CONT http://wc.rootsweb.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=jackpdean&id=I357
2 CONT version of 26 jun 2003 seen 18 march 2008;
1 NOTE Richard "the elder" to distinguish him from his young half-brother of the same
2 CONT name. He inherited the 640 acre "Bremo" plantation in Henrico from his father.
2 CONT SERVICE: a surveyor of the county and justice, 1678. A member of
2 CONT the county court 1678, 1680, 1699, and probably during all of this period.
2 CONT VA Gen 40: 243-248 Oct 1996 apparently shows that this Cocke family and the one
2 CONT of Princess Anne Co. seen in early Moseley records may be all the same one of
2 CONT Constantine area in Cornwall England.
1 NOTE of "The Low Grounds".
