1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.unc.edu/~rowlett/families/cocke.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT 10 '''William Cocke''', a son of Richard Cocke and Mary Aston, was born about 1657. There is much uncertainty concerning his wife or wives. The portion of his father's estate he inherited was called the "Low Grounds", so he is oft
2 CONC en known as William Cocke of the Low Grounds. He died in 1693, only about 36 years old, mentioning three children in his will. From the will it appears that the mother of his children had died and he had remarried. The first wife 
2 CONC is generally assumed to have been Jane Flowers [sic: Jane Clarke.  2nd wife: Sarah Flower.] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT From http://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/cocke/929/
2 CONT
2 CONT iii William Cocke of The Low Ground (eldest son)c. 1657-aft 13 Oct 1
2 CONT
2 CONT Married:
2 CONT * 1. Jane Clarke d. bef 16 June 1691 Issue: Mary, Elizabeth & William.
2 CONT * 2. Sarah Dennis 16 June 1691 d. bef 1 June 1695 ['''SIC: error - she married WILLIAM COCKE (3), son of Thomas''' (2)]
2 CONT * 3. Jane Flower [SIC: said to have been the 1st wife and mother of the children]
2 CONT
2 CONT === Research notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT 28 Feb 1684, William Cocke of Henrico, planter to Giles Carter of same, planter, 25 Lbs, 59 acres on Turkey Island Run next to William Cocke and his brother John Cocke. Jane, wife of William relinquishes dower. Henrico Co VA Deeds
2 CONC , 1677-1705, Wiesiger, p 28.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1691/6/16, Cocke, William, Sr & Sarah Dennis. Deeds wills, etc. 1688-1697. p 253 Marriages of Henrico Co, VA, 1680-1808, pg 20. (Note: not his Wife, Sarah Dennis is named as granddaughter of Katherine Banks Royall Isham, Colonial 
2 CONC Wills of Henrico Co VA, 1654-1737, Wiesiger, p 16.)
2 CONT 1693/10/13, Cocke, William, will rec 1693/2/1. wife extrx, not named. Son William, land, dts Mary & Elizabeth, Mother Mrs. Mary Clarke. Colonial Wills of Henrico Co VA 1654-1737,Wiesiger, pg 35,3
2 CONT
2 CONT "4. William Cocke born 1655; died 1693. He married first, Jane Clarke, in 1678; and second, Sarah Flower, about 1689. He left 3 children, William, Mary and Elizabeth. This William Cocke was no doubt the William Cocke, whose daught
2 CONC er Sarah in 1723 married Capt. Henry Wood." "Genealogy of the Cocke Family of Virginia" The Magazine of History and Biography 3, no. 4 (1896): 405-414. ( p 411). Retrieved from http://www.jstor.org/stable/4241922
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 28 Feb 1684, William Cocke of Henrico, planter to Giles Carter of same, planter, 25 Lbs, 59 acres on Turkey Island Run next to William Cocke and his brother John Cocke. Jane, wife of William relinquishes dower. Henrico Co VA Deeds
2 CONC , 1677-1705, Wiesiger, p 28.
2 CONT
2 CONT from Edward White 
2 CONT Mary Cocke’s father, William’s will, written in 1693, said she was under age, which would make her born after 1672. Obediah Smith, by law, would have been over 21 on August 3, 1692, when he was sued by Robert Beverly, making him b
2 CONC orn before 1671.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Source: Benjamin B Weisiger, III, Charles City County, Virginia Orders 1687-1695, 133, 413 in orig, 8/3/1692.
2 CONT
2 CONT The same day, an order was entered in the estate of John Smith mentioning Obediah and Mary Smith "son and daughter of John Smith, late deceased."
2 CONT Source: Weisiger, Charles City County, Virginia Orders 1687-1695, 130, 406 in orig, 8/3/1692.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thus they were married about that time even if Mary’s father’s will seems to differ about a year.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT "Genealogy of the Cocke Family of Virginia" The Magazine of History and Biography 3, no. 4 (1896): 405-414. ( p 411). Retrieved from http://www.jstor.org/stable/4241922
2 CONT
2 CONT > "4. William Cocke born 1655; died 1693. He married first, Jane Clarke, in 1678; and second, Sarah Flower, about 1689. He left 3 children, William, Mary and Elizabeth. This William Cocke was no doubt the William Cocke, whose daug
2 CONC hter Sarah in 1723 married Capt. Henry Wood."
2 CONT
2 CONT “Genealogy of the Cocke Family of Virginia.” The Virginia Magazine of History and Biography, vol. 4, no. 1, 1896, pp. 86–96. JSTOR, http://www.jstor.org/stable/4241941. Accessed 13 June 2024.
2 CONT
2 CONT THIRD GENERATION-Continued. 
2 CONT
2 CONT IV. THE CHILDREN OF WILLIAM COCKE.2
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. WILLIAM." He may have been a son of William Cocke2 by his first marriage with Jane Clarke. If so, he was born about 1679. If his mother was Sarah Flower, he was not born before I690. His two sisters were certainly by the seco
2 CONC nd wife. There was a " Captain William Cocke," of this period, who died in 1736. This may have been the person.
2 CONT * 2. MARY COCKE,S born c. I690; married Obadiah Smith; died I754. Her husband died I746. Their wills are on record in Henrico county. They left a son named Obadiah Smith (died 1765) and a son named Luke, who was the father of Obad
2 CONC iah* Smith' (lieutenant in the Revo- lution, and a man of considerable property), whose daughter, Lucy Smith, married James Powell Cocke6 in I777.
2 CONT * 3. ELIZABETH COCKE,3 born c. I692; married Lawrence Woodward. Their maternal uncle, John Flower, lived in James City county. In I629 Christopher Woodward was a Burgess for Westover, and there was a Captain Henry Woodward in the 
2 CONC French and Indian Wars, I755-57. The Rev. James Bacon, Eng., first cousin of the great Lord Bacon, married Martha Woodward, and had issue: Nathaniel Bacon, born I620; died I692; member Council in Virginia I657; Burgess for York I6
2 CONC 59; Acting Governor I689. This was not the ' Rebel."
2 CONT
