1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Do not confuse with his nephew,  https://www.geni.com/people/Richard-Cocke-of-Bremo/6000000026942654152
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Cocke the Younger; born between 1670 and 1675, was the son of Lt. Col. Richard Cocke and second wife Mary Aston. He married Elizabeth Littlebury and made his home at  'Old Man's Creek', Charles City County, Virginia. He di
2 CONC ed in 1720 in Henrico County, Virginia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >comment from https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=60500229
2 CONT >>"Some people have mistakenly placed Ann Bowler as another wife of THIS Richard Cocke The Younger. Ann did marry a man named Richard Cocke. But he was the son of Richard "The Elder" (Richard "The Younger's half brother.) In other
2 CONC  words, Ann Bowler married Richard the Younger's 1/2 nephew. Confusing the matter is that Ann's tombstone states that her husband was "Richard Cocke the Younger." This is in reference to her husband's father being named Richard al
2 CONC so. But it is easy to see how it could be confused with Elizabeth's husband."
2 CONT
2 CONT This Richard Cocke is called "the Younger" because his father had married before and had another son named Richard, who was called Richard Cocke, The Elder. It was not unusual in those days for brothers to have the same Christian 
2 CONC name if they had different mothers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Richard Cocke and Elizabeth: 
2 CONT *'''Anne Cocke''', m. Hon. Robert Bolling II.
2 CONT *Richard Cocke III; b. circa 1670; d. circa 1750.
2 CONT
2 CONT Links to additional material:
2 CONT *http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~marshall/esmd66.htm
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=60507200
2 CONT
