2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT <strong>Sir Walter Wrottesley, Bart. [1642]</strong>, of Wrottesley aforesaid, s. and h., b. about 1632, being aged 32 at the Visit, of Staffordshire in April 1663 : admitted to Lincoln's Inn, 11 May 1646 ; suc. to the Baronetcy, 
2 CONC 6 Nov. 1659. Sheriff of Staffordshire, 1666-67. He m. in or before 1658, Elizabeth, da. of Sir Thomas Wolrych, 1st Bart. [1641], by Ursula, da. of Thomas Oteley, of Pitchford, Salop. He d. in or before 1686. Will pr. June 1686.
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n213/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1902; Vol. II; page 195
