1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Elizabeth Spencer (1618–1672)
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Successively'': Baroness Craven of Ryton; Hon. Mrs. Henry Howard; Baroness Crofts.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents
2 CONT Father: William Spencer, 2nd Baron Spencer of Wormleighton (1591–1636)
2 CONT Mother: Lady Penelope Wriothesley (1598–1667)
2 CONT
2 CONT Vitals
2 CONT Birth: February 16, 1618 – Brington, Northamptonshire, England
2 CONT Death: August 11, 1672 (Age 54) – England
2 CONT Burial: St. Nicholas Churchyard, Little Saxham, Suffolk, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriages
2 CONT # John Craven, 1st Baron Craven of Ryton: Married 4 December 1634. He died in 1648.
2 CONT # Henry Howard: Married circa July 1648. He was the son of Thomas Howard, 1st Earl of Berkshire.
2 CONT # William Crofts, 1st Baron Crofts: Married after 1663. He was a prominent courtier to Charles II.
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Cautions & Identity Audits
2 CONT
2 CONT No Biological Issue: Despite three marriages, Elizabeth died without issue. Both the Barony of Craven (Ryton creation) and the Barony of Crofts became extinct upon the deaths of her respective husbands due to the lack of heirs.
2 CONT
2 CONT The "James Crofts" Distinction: Researchers should not conflate the lack of biological children with the presence of James Scott (the future Duke of Monmouth) in the household. While he used the surname "Crofts" while under the gu
2 CONC ardianship of Elizabeth’s third husband, William Crofts, he was the illegitimate son of Charles II and Lucy Walter, not a child of Elizabeth Spencer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Be wary of digital pedigrees or "family traditions" that attempt to attach children to these lines to bridge gaps in 17th-century colonial records. Clerical typos in secondary sources often misattribute nieces or nephews as childr
2 CONC en in this branch of the Spencer family.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources (Chicago Style)
2 CONT
2 CONT Cokayne, George E. The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct, or Dormant. Edited by Vicary Gibbs. Vol. 3. London: St. Catherine Press, 1913.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lundy, Darryl. "Hon. Elizabeth Spencer." The Peerage. Last modified August 7, 2020. http://www.thepeerage.com/p10540.htm#i105400.
2 CONT
2 CONT "William Crofts, 1st Baron Crofts." In The Diary of Samuel Pepys, edited by Phil Gyford. Accessed April 3, 2026. https://www.pepysdiary.com/encyclopedia/5125/.
