1 NOTE {geni:about_me} This Francis Brown family in Essex Co., VA is represented by DNA Group 10 at the Brown DNA Project (at Family Tree DNA). 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Named in his father's will.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Browne-5976
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT William Francis Browne (Francis II) was born about 1654 at Farnham Parish, Essex County, Virginia.
2 CONT Alternative birth {Birth: 1654 in Cowary, Sussex, England}
2 CONT
2 CONT Francis Browne died before 11 April 1709 at Essex County, Virginia which is the date his will was probated.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nov. 9, 1689-Mary Allen to her eldest daughter, Elizabeth Brown, wife of WILLIAM Brown, 451 acres of land being a part of a dividend of land taken up by Mary Allen's father, Thomas Page.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parentage? 
2 CONT He may have been the son of Francis Browne and Elizabeth Bannister.
2 CONT Francis Browne married Elizabeth Allen, daughter of Valentine Allen and Mary Page. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT See also:
2 CONT
2 CONT #     Early Colonial Settlers of Southern Maryland and Virginia's Northern Neck Counties 
2 CONT #     Francis Browne (bef. 1658 - 1709) - Early Colonial Settlers of Southern Maryland and Virginia's Northern Neck (retrieved from website 8 March 2019) 
2 CONT #     Virginia County Records, Virginia Wills 
2 CONT #     Francis Browne (1610 - 1682) Family Tree - FamilySearch.org 
2 CONT #     Francis Browne, 3rd Viscount Montagu - Peerage.com 
2 CONT #     Francis Brown, 3rd Viscount Montagu - Wikipedia 
2 CONT #     RootsWeb 
2 CONT #     Brown Society 
2 CONT #     Brydges, Egerton and Arthur Collins. Collins's Peerage (London: F.C. and J. Rivington, 1812), Vol. 1, p. 232. Lists Henry Somerset. Fifth Earl and 1st Marquis of Somerset, under Duke of Beaufort. Refers to "Pentley Court", p
2 CONC resumably the same place as Pauntley. See p. 232 marriage of Sir Henry Somerset to Anne Russell. Lists all their children, including (p. 233) "Lady Elisabeth, youngest daughter" who was wed to Francis Brown, Viscount Montague.  
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I28747&tree=Tree1
2 CONT Notes 	
2 CONT ===
2 CONT 1707-1711 Essex County, Virginia Deed & Will Book 13; [John Frederick Dorman]; Page 213.
2 CONT Will of Francis Brown of Southfarnham Parish in the County of Essex being sick and weak of body, dated 2 May 1708.
2 CONT Unto my loving wife Elizabeth all my land and plantation whereon I now live excepting one parcell of wood land that lyeth on the uper and westermost side of a branch called the Middle Branch which I appoint to be sold by my execut
2 CONC ors and the production thereof shall goe to pay all my debts. The remainder my loving wife Elizabeth Brown do hold dureing her naturall life and after her death if my son Daniel Brown is alive, he enjoy the land and plantation dur
2 CONC eing his naturall life and after his death the land to descend to Ann Brown the daughter of Daniel Brown, and for want of issue to descend to her sister Elizabeth Brown and for want of issue to the children of my son Daniel Brown 
2 CONC and Elizabeth his wife. If my son Daniel dye before his mother Elizabeth, then his present wife doe possess the land and plantation untill my grand daughter Ann Browne do attain to the age of eighteen years or day of marriage.
2 CONT Unto my granddaughter Anne Brown daughter to my son Daniel Brown one feather bed and bolster with rugg and blanketts, curtain and vallens all new, four cows, six new pewter dishes, one iron pot when she shall attain to the age of 
2 CONC eighteen years or on the day of her marriage.
2 CONT Unto my loving wife Elizabeth one Negro man Jack during her naturall life and after her decease to my son Daniel Brown, but if the said Negro should be alive at the death of my son Daniel Brown then my granddaughter Anne doe posse
2 CONC ss the Negro.
2 CONT All the rest of my personal estate unto my loving wife Elizabeth Brown, whom I appoint with my son Daniel Brown executor and executrix.
2 CONT Francis Brown
2 CONT Wit: Robert Coleman, Thomas (T) Brown.
2 CONT 11 April 1709. Proved by Robert Coleman and Thomas Brown.
2 CONT ===
2 CONT 1707-1711 Essex County, Virginia Deed & Will Book 13; [John Frederick Dorman]; Page 213.
2 CONT 11 April 1709. Bond of Elizabeth Brown as executrix of Francis Brown. Unto James Boughan of Essex County, Gent., in behalf of the Court. For £500 sterling. Securities, Robert Coleman and Daniel Brown.
2 CONT Elizabeth (E) Brown
2 CONT Robert Coleman
2 CONT Danll. Brown
2 CONT Wit: Ja. Alderson, Abr. Ayrton.
2 CONT 11 April 1709. Acknowledged.
2 CONT ===
2 CONT Wills of Old Rappahannock County, Virginia, 1656-1692 page 147
2 CONT BROWN, FRANCIS, 10 November, 1690; 3 February, 1691.
2 CONT In the name of God Amen
2 CONT I ffrancis Brown senior in the parish of South ffarnham in the County of Rapp being very sick and weake of body butt of perfect sense and memory doe make this my Last Will and Testament in manner and forme ffolowing I give and beq
2 CONC ueath my souk unto Al-mighty God that gave it me with a sure and certayne hope of a joy-full Resurrection through the merits of my Blessed Lord and Saviour Jesus Christ and my body unto my mother the earth to be decently interred 
2 CONC and for my worldly Estate in manner and form following after my just and Lawfall debts are satisfied.
2 CONT I give and bequeath unto my son ffrancis Brown after mine and my Loving wife Elizabeth decease all that necke of Land Lying on the north side of my devident of Land I now live on bounded as followeth that is to say strayt away thr
2 CONC ough and mild field from the Run of the deviling branch the mill road which goes to my son Daniel goes over & for a small branch neare my ould dwelling house called by the name of the spring branch which sayd Land I give and beque
2 CONC ath unto my said son ffrancis to him and his heirs forever.
2 CONT I also give and bequeath unto my son Daniel Brown after my and my Loving wife Elizabeth decease all that Rest of my land I am now possessed with all my plantation and housing to him and his heires to have and to hould in fee simpl
2 CONC e for ever also itt is my will and dealer that my household goods be equally divided between my two sons ffrancis and Daniel both in quality and goodness to them and their heirs to have and to hould in fee simple for ever also it 
2 CONC is my will and desier there be a row of orchard trees planted along ye sayd ould field to devide the above sayd Land. I also give and bequeath unto my sons ffrancis and Daniel my parcell of Land Lying on the south side of pescataw
2 CONC ay Creeke called by the name of ye wading place poynt equally between them and their heirs forever I alsoe give and bequeath unto my fower daughters Elizabeth, Sarah, Mary and Rebecca one shilling apeace to be payd them by my lawf
2 CONC ul executor or executrix I also give and bequeath unto Daniel Brown the son of my son Francis Brown one feather bed with the furniture belonging unto itt to him and his heirs forever after my and my "sites decease.
2 CONT I give and bequeath unto my Loving wife Elizabeth all the Rest of my moveable Estate that I am now possessed with to have and to hould without any Lett or molestation to her and her heirs forever I also give and bequeath unto my f
2 CONC lower Godsons that is Joseph and John Edmondson and Ffras Brown the son of Daniell Brown senior my neighbour and ffra Graves the son of Ffras Graves deceased to every one of them one pocket bible of fine or six shillings price to 
2 CONC be truly payd them after my decease by my Law-full executor or executrix I alsoe apoynt my Loving wife Elizabeth my sole and whole executrix of this my Last will and testament and this my Last will to cut off and disannull all ffo
2 CONC rmer wills whatsoever as witness my hand and seal this 10th day of novber 1690
2 CONT signed sealed and delivered FRANCIS BROWN Seal in the presence of us JOHN FERGUSON, THO WHEELER Probst est sacrum in Cur. Com. Rappa. 3° die ffeby ano 1691
2 CONT Test Wm COLSTON Cl. Recorded 26 Feb. 1691.
2 CONT ===
2 CONT 1701-1704 Essex County, Virginia Deed & Will Book; [Antient Press]; Page 101)
2 CONT IN THE NAME OF GOD Amen, I ELIZABETH BROWNE being sick & weake of body but of sound & perfect memory blessed and praised be Almighty God for the same doe make & ordaine this to be my last Will & Testamt. in manner & forme followin
2 CONC g, first & principally I comend my Soule into the hands of Almighty God who gave it hopeing through the pretious death & passion of or: blessed Lord and Saviour Jesus Christ to receive full pardon & forgiveness of all my sinns & a
2 CONC  joyfull Ressurecon at the last Day as for my body I committ to the Ground to be decently & Christianly buryed att the discretion of my Exer. hereafter named and as for the worldly goods that God of his Mercy hath lent me I will &
2 CONC  bequeath thm in manner & forme following (vizt.)
2 CONT Imprimis I give unto ROBERT MILLS the halfe part of the goods that now is att his house a Cow a Calfe and a horse & whatt tobaccoe is due to me except what is herein bequeathed, a pott, a kettle & fower pewter dishes
2 CONT Item I give unto EDMOND PAGITT SENIOR the other halfe pte: of the goods that is now att ROBERT MILLS and a Steere att my Son, FRANKE BROWNEs & one hoggshead of tobacco att BENJAMIN MATHEWS, a pott, a dripping pan, a spitt & four p
2 CONC ewter dishes
2 CONT Item I give unto JOHN MILLS the hdd. of tobo: due to me from him
2 CONT Item I give unto my Daugher, SARAH, twelve pence
2 CONT Item I give unto my Sonn; FRANCIS BROWNE, twelve pence
2 CONT Item I give unto my Son, DANIELL BROWNE, twelve pence and of this my last Will & Testamt. I make ROBERT MILLS and EDMOND PAGETT joynt Ezers. & doe hereby utterly
2 CONT disallow revoake and annuli all & every former Testamts. Wills Legacyes bequest and Exercr. by me in any wise before this time named willed & bequeathed, Rattifying & confirming this & none other to be my last Will &Testamt. In Wi
2 CONC tness whereof I have hereunto sett my hand and seale this second day of February 1698
2 CONT Signed sealed published declared and pronounced
2 CONT as her last Will and Testament in pr:sence of us ELIZABETH BROWNE
2 CONT THO: HUCKLESCUTT
2 CONT MARY HUCKLESCOTT
2 CONT FRANCES MILLS her marke
2 CONT Prov'd in Essex County Court ye 10th day of March 1701 by the oathes of MARY MUSCOE (formerly MARY HUCKLESCOTT) &FRANCES BYROM (formerly FRANCES MILLS) witnesses hereto & truely recorded Test FRANCIS MERIWETHER, Cl C
2 CONT ===
