1 NAME Edward /Morgan/ II
2 GIVN Edward
2 SURN Morgan
2 NSFX II
2 _MARNM Morgan
1 NAME Sir Edward Morgan, II, 2nd Baronet of Llantarnam
1 SEX M
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Ref: [http://wbo.llgc.org.uk/en/s-MORG-LLA-1561.html Welsh Biography Online]
2 CONT * Ref: [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sir_Edward_Morgan,_1st_Baronet Wikipedia article on the Baronet's of Llantarnam]
2 CONT
2 CONT *_________________
2 CONT *'''The History of Monmouthshire  By David Williams
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=veg-AQAAMAAJ&pg=PR11&dq=A+History+of+Monmouthshire&hl=en&sa=X&ei=GNrUUsCOKYWIogTQv4LADw&ved=0CGEQ6AEwCTgU#v=onepage&q=Morgan&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.127
2 CONT **   SIR EDWARD MORGAN of Lantarnam, Com. Mon. Baronet. Kydovor Vawr Lord of Kylfant, one of the peers of Wales, of the royal blood of the Britains, paternally defcended from Bely, King of Britain.
2 CONT *Kydovor Vawr, Lord of Kylfant. = Elen, daughter and heirefs to Llewelen. on of the peers of Wales.
2 CONT * Bledry, Lord Kalfant. = Clydwen, daughter and heirefs to Griffith ap Hydrych, Lord of Gwenvay.
2 CONT *Ivor ap Bledery de eodem. = Tangluft, daughter and heirefs to Howel, faid Lord of St. Clere.
2 CONT *Morgan Llewellin, Lord of St. Clere, and Tredegar. = Angharand, daugher and heirefs of Sir Morgan Meredith, Lord of Tredegar, Knight.
2 CONT * Philip Morgan of Lanfton, Com. Mon. Efq. a 2nd brother = Daughter and heirefs of Sir John Norris of Langfton, Knight.
2 CONT *Jenkin Philip of Langfton, Efq. = Cicely, daughter to Sir John Welfh, Knight.
2 CONT *Morgan Jenkin of Langfton, Efq. = Elizabeth, daughter to Roger Vaughan, Efq.
2 CONT *Pg.128
2 CONT *Sir Thomas Morgan of Pencoyd, Knt. Com. Mon. = Joan, daughter and heirefs to John Gwiflyn Herbert, of Itton, Efq.
2 CONT *John Morgan of Caerleon, fecond fon, Efq. = Elizabeth, daughter to Lewes ap Richard Wyn, of the Van. Com. Glamorgan, Efq.
2 CONT *William Morgan of Lantarnam, Efq. = Elizabeth, daughter to Sir Rees Maunfel, Knight.
2 CONT *Edward Morgan of Lantarnam, Efq. = Elizabeth daughter and heirefs to Hugh Smith, of Long Afhton, Com. Som. Efq.
2 CONT *William Morgan of Lantarnam, Efq. = Lady Frances, daughter to Earl of Worcefter.
2 CONT *Sir Edward Morgan of Lantarnam, Baronet. = Mary, daughter to Sir Frances Englefield, Bart.
2 CONT *'''Sir Edward Morgan of Lantarnam, Baronet, now living. = Frances, daughter to Thomas Morgan, of Maughen, Efq. 
2 CONT **		Edward Morgan, Efq. Heir-apparent.
2 CONT *__________________
2 CONT *'''A genealogical and heraldic history of the extinct and dormant baronetcies ...  By John Burke, John Bernard Burke (sir.)
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=K1kBAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA370&lpg=PA370&dq=baronetLlantarnam&source=bl&ots=E8TtZ2olal&sig=sPTN7EzpqKq_KY8tYZSOL-hCsOA&hl=en&sa=X&ei=HYjNUuW9M-ir2gWbjoEo&ved=0CEEQ6AEwBAv=onepage&q=baronet%20llantarnam&f=f
2 CONC alse#v=onepage&q&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.370
2 CONT *The second son,
2 CONT *   PHILIP MORGAN, esq. of Langston, acquired that estate in marriage with the daughter and heir of Sir John Norris, knt. of Penlline Castle. He was direct ancestor* of
2 CONT *   WILLIAM MORGAN, esq. sheriff for Monmouthshire in 1567, and M.P. in 1571, who was the first proprietor of Llantarnam. He m. Elizabeth, daughter of Sir Rees Mansel, knt. of Margam, and was s. by his son,
2 CONT *   EDWARD MORGAN, esq. of Llantarnam and Penrice, M. P. for Monmouthshire in 1586, who m. Elizabeth, daughter and heir of Hugh Smith, esq. of Long Ashton, in Somersetshire, and had a son and successor,
2 CONT *   WILLIAM MORGAN, esq. of Llantarnam, who m. the Lady Frances Somerset, daughter of Edward, Earl of Worcester, and was father of
2 CONT *   I. SIR EDWARD MORGAN, of Llantarnam, who was created a BARONET in 1642. He m. Mary, daughter of Sir Francis Englefield, bart, of Wotton Basset, in Whiltshire and was s. at his decease, 24th June 1653, by his son,
2 CONT *'''   II. SIR EDWARD MORGAN, of Llantarnam, living in 1661, who m. Frances daughter of Thomas Morgan, esq. of Mangham, and was s. by his son,
2 CONT *   III. SIR EDWARD MORGAN, of Llantarnam, who m. for his second wife, Mary, daughter of Humphrey Baskerville, esq. of Pontrilas, in the county of Hereford, and by that lady, who wedded, secondly John Grubham Howe, esq. father of 
2 CONC the first Lord Chedworth, had two daughters,
2 CONT **	ANNE, who died unm. bequeathing her moiety of the inheritance to John Howe, esq. who had married her mother, Lady Morgan.
2 CONT **	FRANCES, m. Edmund Bray, esq. eldest son of Sir Edmund Reginald Bray, of Barrington Park, Gloucestershire, and had issue,
2 CONT *	*The intervening descent was as follows:
2 CONT *	Philip Morgan, esq. of Langston = Gwenllian, daughter and heir of Sir John Norris, of Penlline Castle, Glamorganshire.
2 CONT *	Jenkin ap Phillip, of Langston = Cicely, daughter of Sir John Welsh, knt.
2 CONT *	Morgan ap Jenkin, (t) of Langston = Elizabeth, daughter of Sir Roger Vaughan.
2 CONT *	Sir Thomas Morgan, knt. of Pencoed = Joan, daughter and heir of John Gwilliam Herbert, of Itton.
2 CONT *	John Morgan, esq. of Caerleon, second son = Ely, daughter of Lewes ap Richard Gwynn, esq. of the Van.
2 CONT *	William Morgan, first of Llantarnam.
2 CONT **	(t) By his third wife, Morgan ap Jenkin had a son, John Morgan, esq. of Tredunnock, in Monmouthshire, ancestor of the MORGANS of TREDUNNOCK, now represented by Mrs. JANE HAWKINS.
2 CONT *_______________________
2 CONT *MORGAN, Sir Edward, 3rd Bt. (d.1682), of Llantarnam Abbey, Mon.
2 CONT *o.s. of '''Sir Edward Morgan, 2nd Bt. of Llantarnam by Frances, da. of Thomas Morgan''' of Machen, wid. of William Lewis of Llandewy Rhydderch. m. Mary, da. and coh. of Humphrey Baskerville of Pontrilas, Kentchurch, Herefs., 2da.
2 CONC  suc. fa. 3 July 1679.1
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1660-1690/member/morgan-sir-edward-1682
2 CONT *___________________
2 CONT *Thomas MORGAN
2 CONT *Born: ABT 1588, Tredagar, Monmouthshire, Wales
2 CONT *Died: 13 May 1664 
2 CONT *Father: William MORGAN (Sir) 
2 CONT *Mother: Elizabeth WINTER 
2 CONT *Married 1: Rachel HOPTON
2 CONT *Married 2: Elizabeth WINDHAM (d. 18 Oct 1666) (dau. of Thomas Windham)
2 CONT *Children: 
2 CONT **'''1. Frances MORGAN (b. ABT 1615) (m. Edward Morgan of Llantarnam) 
2 CONT **2. Anne MORGAN (m. Henry Morgan) 
2 CONT **3. William MORGAN (m. Blanche Morgan) 
2 CONT **4. Blanche MORGAN (m. Charles Vane) 
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/MORGAN.htm#Thomas MORGAN3
2 CONT *___________________
2 CONT *'''A history of the family of Morgan, from the year 1089 to present times ([1902?])
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/historyoffamilyo00morg
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/historyoffamilyo00morg#page/13/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.13
2 CONT *   VIII. LLEWELYN ap IVOR of Tredegar, Lord of St Clear, married Angharad, daughter of Sir Morgan ap Meredith, from the Welsh Lords of Caerleon, ap Griffith ap Meredith ap Rhys, who bore "Argent a lion rampant sable." Sir Morgan 
2 CONC died 1332, when Angharad was aged 32. They had : 1. Morgan. 2. Ivor Hael, whence MORGAN OF GWERN-Y-CLEPPA. 3. Philip, whence LEWIS OF ST. PIERRE. 
2 CONT *   IX. MORGAN of Tredegar and St. Clear, married Maud, daugter of Rhun ap Grono ap Llwarch, Lord of Cibwr. He died before 1384. Issue: 1. Llewelyn. 2. Philip, whence MORGAN OF LANGSTONE. 3. John, father of Gwenllian, married Davi
2 CONC d Goch ap David, 4. Christian, married Jevan ap Jenkin Kemeys. 5. Ann, married David Gwilim David of Rhiwperra. 6. Margaret, married Traherne ap Meyric of Merthyr. 7. A daughter, married Thomas ap Gwillim of Carnllwyd. 8. Elenor, 
2 CONC married Grono ap Howel Bennet. 
2 CONT *   X. LLEWELYN ap MORGAN of Tredegar and St. Clear, living 1387, married Jenet daughter and heir of David-vychan ap David of Rhydodyn, 1384-87. Issue: 1. Jevan. 2. Christy, married Madoc ap Jevan of Gelligaer. 3. —— , married Rog
2 CONC er ap Adam of St. Mellon's. 4. —— , married Madoc of Bassalleg. 5. —— , married Thomas Llewelyn. 6. Ann, married John ap Jenkin. 7. ——  , married  —— of Raglan. 8. ——  , married  ——  of Builth. 
2 CONT *   XI. JEVAN MORGAN, 1415-48, married Denise, or Elizabeth, daughter of Thomas ap Llewelyn-vychan of Lllangattog-on-Usk. Issue: 1. John. 2. David, 1442-48. 3. Jenkyn, 1454. 
2 CONT *   XII. SIR JOHN MORGAN, Knight of the Sepulchre, 1448, steward of Gwentlloog ; married Jenet, daughter and co-heir of John ap David Mathew of Llandaff. Issue: 1. Morgan. 2. Thomas, whence MORGAN OF MACHEN AND TREDEGAR. 3. John, 
2 CONC whence a BRANCH. 4. Lewis, 1491. 5. William Morgan, coroner, 1501, father or John of Newport, died 1541, father of William, 1541-1559. 6. Philip, 1491. 7. Elizabeth, married John Fiennes, 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/historyoffamilyo00morg#page/14/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.14
2 CONT *Lord Clinton and Say. 8. Jane, married William David Powel. 9. Mary, married Thomas Llewelyn-vychan of Rhiwperra. 10. Isabella, married James Kemeys of Began, ob. 1591. 
2 CONT *  XIII. SIR MORGAN JOHN, knighted 22 June, 1497. after Blackheath ; died in 1504; married Margaret, daughter of Sir Thomas Morgan of Pencoyd. Issue : 1. John. 2. Margaret.
2 CONT * XIV. JOHN MORGAN ; will dated 4 April, 1513 ; died about 1513 ; married Lettice, daughter of Sir George Herbert of St. Julian's. Issue : 1. William, M. P. for county 1556-57, sheriff 1565 ; will dated 8 August, 1568 ; died 1569,
2 CONC  s. p.; married Catherine, daughter of Thomas Bodenham. 2. John. 3. Joan, married Miles Mathew of Llandaff. By Felice, daughter of Thomas Richards : 4. John. 5. Nest, married John Henry Kemeys of Newport. 
2 CONT *  XV. JOHN MORGAN of Newport, 1545. married Elizabeth, daughter of Sir Edward Stradling. Issue: 1. Miles. 2. Elenor, married William Morgan. 
2 CONT *  XVI. MILES MORGAN, sheriff 1574 ; will dated June. 1578 ; proved 1581, s. p.; married Catherine, daughter of Rowland Morgan of Machen, in 1571 ; widow of Thomas Mathew. She afterwards married Henry Jones of the Inner Temple. Mi
2 CONC les was lost in America under Sir Humphrey Gilbert. His heir was his brother-in-law, Morgan of Machen. 
2 CONT **MORGAN OF MACHEN AND TREDEGAR.
2 CONT *  XIII. THOMAS, second son of Sir John Morgan, was of Machen; esquire of the body to Henry VII.; living 1538; married Elizabeth, daughter of Roger Vaughan of Porthaml. Issue: 1. Rowland. 2. Reynold, whence MORGAN OF LLANVEDW. 3. 
2 CONC John, whence MORGAN OF BASSALLEG. 4. Edmond, whence MORGAN OF PENLLWYN-SARTH. 5. Margaret, married 1st John Kemeys, 2d William Edmunds. 6. Barbara, married Sir Henry Seymour. 7. Maud, married John ap Rosser. 8, Jane, married 1st W
2 CONC illiam Gunter, 2d Richard ap Jenkin, 3d William Vaughan of Magor. 9. Constance, married William 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/historyoffamilyo00morg#page/15/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.15
2 CONT *Jones of Treowen. 10. Mary, married 1st Edward Williams, 2d Richard Herbert. 11. Elizabeth, married Edward James. 
2 CONT *  XIV. ROWLAND MORGAN of Machen, 1517-77, married Blanch, daughter of John Thomas of Llanarth. Settlement 11 Nov. 1517; sheriff 1557. Issue: 1. Thomas, 2. Henry, whence MORGAN OF ST. MELLON'S. 3. Catherine, married 1st Thomas Mat
2 CONC hew, 2d Miles Morgan, 3d Henry Jones. 4. Ann, married Philip Morgan of Gwern-y-Cieppa. 5. Mary, married Thomas Lewis of Rhiwperra. 6. Elizabeth, married Edward Kemeys of Cefn Mably.
2 CONT *  XV. THOMAS MORGAN of Machen and Tredegar, and of the , Middle Temple, 1567-77; sheriff 1581 ; M. P. for county 1589; will 1603; married Elizabeth, daughter of Roger Bodenham. Issue: 1. Sir William.  2. Edward, 1586, married Eli
2 CONC zabeth, daughter of Richard Thomas of Bertholley. 3. Sir John, died before 1610, married Florence, daughter and eventual heir of William Morgan of the Friars. They had William of the Friars, 1663, mayor of Newport, 1667, father of
2 CONC  Lewis Morgan, died about 1690, father of Lewis, died 1729, who sold the Friars. He was father of: (a) Blanch, married Richard Greensward ; (b) Catherine, married Anthony Williams. 4. David Morgan, whence a BRANCH. 5. Blanch, marr
2 CONC ied Edward Lewis of Van ; settlement 1585. 6. Catherine, married William Herbert of Coldbrook. 7. Elizabeth, married William Jones of Abergavenny. 8. Jane, married Rowland Morgan of Bassalleg. 9. Elizabeth, married William Blethyn
2 CONC  of Dynham. 10. Ann. 11. Margaret, married Henry Williams of Mathern. 
2 CONT *  XVL SIR WILLIAM MORGAN of Tredegar, knighted 1633; M. P. for county 1623-25; will 1650, proved 1653; sheriff 1612; aet 93 at death ; he received Charles I. at Tredegar, 16 and 17 July, 1645 ; married 1st Elizabeth, daughter of 
2 CONC Sir William Winter of Lidney, 2d Bridget, daughter of Anthony Morgan of Heyford, county Northampton, widow of Anthony Morgan of Llanvihangel Crucorney. Issue by first wife: 1. Thomas. 2. Edward of Kilfengan ; will 4 April 1660, pr
2 CONC oved Feb. 1661 ; married Elizabeth, daughter and heir of Charles James of Llandewi Rhydderch, had Elizabeth, daughter and 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/historyoffamilyo00morg#page/16/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.16
2 CONT *heir, married Henry Chambre of Court Morgan. 3. William, whence MORGAN OF RHYMNY. 4. Rowland of Risca; will 19 Dec. 1660, proved Feb. 1661 ; married Honora --- , and had Colonel William Morgan; buried at Bassalleg, 27 Oct. 1679. 
2 CONC 5. John, of the Temple in 1652 ; coel. 6. Mary, married George Lewis of St. Pierre. 7. Blanch, married John Carne of Ewenny. 8. Frances, married Charles Williams of Llangibby. 9. Mary, single; will 1687, 10. Elizabeth, married Wil
2 CONC liam Morgan of Dderw ; slie died 1638, he died 1649. By Sir William's second wife : 11. Anthony of Kilfengan, s. p. His widow was alive in 1673. 12. Mary, married Peler Farmer of London, who died 1691. They had Margaret, daughter 
2 CONC and heir, married John More, who sold Kilfengan 1707.
2 CONT *  XVII. THOMAS MORGAN, sheriff 1661; died 18 Oct. 1666 [13 May 1664], aet. 76; married 1st Rachel, daughter of Robert Hopton and widow of David Kemeys, 2d Elizabeth, daughter of Thomas Windham of Sandhills. Issue by 1st wife: 1. 
2 CONC Elizabeth, married Sir Trevor Williams of LIangibby; settlement 20 Oct. 1640 ; she died 1674. By the second wife.  2. William. 3. Thomas, 1659. 4. John, died young. 5. John of London, merchant; sheriff 1697;  M. P. for county 1701
2 CONC  ; died 1 Jan., buried at Machen 9 Jan. 1715, s. p. 6. Edward, s. p. 7. Trevor, 1680, s. p. 8. Lewis of Penylan, sheriff 1703, died 1706, s. p.; married Mary, daughter of — Edwards and heir of, her brother Thomas Edwards. 9. '''Fr
2 CONC ances, married 1st William Lewis of Llandewi-Rhydderch, 2d Sir Edward Morgan of Llantarnam'''. 10. Blanch, married Charles Van, 1650. 11.  Ann, married Henry Morgan of Penllwyn-Sarth. 12. Elizabeth, married Thomas Morgan of Llanrh
2 CONC ymny. 13. Rachel, married Henry Probert. 14. Mary, married William Thomas, of Llanbradach, 19 Nov. 1668. 15. Catherine, died 29 July 1724, aet. 73, s. p. 
2 CONT *  XVIII. WILLIAM MORGAN, M. P. for county 1659-60; died in London 28 April 1680 ; married 1st, 4 Nov. 1661, Blanch, daughter of William Morgan of Dderw, or Thurrow, county Brecon, king's attorney and judge for South Wales. She di
2 CONC ed 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/historyoffamilyo00morg#page/17/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.17
2 CONT *23 March 1673. He married 2d Elizabeth, daughter and co-heir of Edward Lewis of Van and Bourstall, widow of Sir Francis Darrell. Issue by Blanch : 1. Thomas, born 7 Sept. 1664; M. P. for county 1695-98; died 1699, s. p.; married 
2 CONC Martha, daughter of Sir Edward Mansel. They had : (a) William, born 1688, died 1699; (b) Martha, born 1692, died 1695; (c) William, born 17 Sept. 1665, died single, 1 Feb. 1683 ; buried in Westminster Abbey. 2. Charles, born 21 Fe
2 CONC b. 1666; died s. p. 3. Edward, born 3 March 1671, buried at Machen 3 March 1672. 4. John. 5. Blanch, born 16 Sept. 1669, died 11 Dec. 1682; buried at Hackney.  __________________________________
