1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''The royal families of England, Scotland, and Wales, with their descendants, sovereigns and subjects (1848)
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/royalfamiliesofe01burk
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/royalfamiliesofe01burk#page/n173/mode/1up
2 CONT **Lieut. Col. William Pearce. PEDIGREE L.
2 CONT *Lady Frances Somerset, dau. of Edward, Earl of Warcester. marr. William Morgan, Esq. of Llantarnam, co. Monmouth.; ch: Sir Edward (m. Mary Englefield) Morgan
2 CONT *Sir Edward Morgan, Bt., of Llantarnam, so created 1642. marr. Mary, dau. of Sir Francis Englefield.; ch: Elizabeth (m. Sir Philip Jones) Morgan
2 CONT *'''Elizabeth, dau. of Sir Edw. Morgan, Bart., of Llantarnam. marr. Sir Philip Jones, Knt., of Treowen, d. 1660.; ch: Wm. (m. Mary Anderton) Jones
2 CONT *Wm. Jones, Esq. of Llanarth, co. Monmouth. marr. Mary, dau. of Christopher Anderton, Esq. of Lostock.; ch: Elizabeth (m. David Lewis, Esq.) Jones.
2 CONT *Elizabeth Jones, dau. of Wm. Jones, Esq. of Llanarth. marr. David Lewis, Esq. of Llanthewy Court.; ch: Francis (m. Mary Morgan) Lewis, Es.
2 CONT *Francis Lewis, Esq. of Llanthewy Court, 1684.; marr. Mary, dau. and coheir of Thos. Morgan, Esq. of Lanrumney, co. Monmouth.; ch: Philip (m. Elizabeth Harris) Lewis, Esq.
2 CONT *
2 CONT *Jane, dau. of Sir Rowland Williams, Knt. marr. Sir Nicholas Kemeys of Kevan Mabley, Bart, the defender of Chepstow Castle.; ch: Mary (m. Thomas Morgan, Esq.) Kemeys
2 CONT *Mary, dau. of Sir Nicholas Kemeys, Bart. m. 1644. marr. Thomas Morgan, Esq. of Lanrumney. ch: Thomas (m2. Mary) Morgan, Esq.
2 CONT *Thomas Morgan, Esq. of Lanrumney. marr. Mary, his 2nd wife. ch: Mary (m. Francis Lewis, Esq.) Morgan
2 CONT *Mary, dau. and coheir of Thos. Morgan Esq. of Lanrumney, co. Monmouth. marr. Francis Lewis, Esq. of Llanthewy Court, 1684.; ch: Philip (m. Elizabeth Harris) Lewis, Esq.
2 CONT *_____________________
2 CONT *'''The History of Monmouthshire  By David Williams
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=veg-AQAAMAAJ&pg=PR11&dq=A+History+of+Monmouthshire&hl=en&sa=X&ei=GNrUUsCOKYWIogTQv4LADw&ved=0CGEQ6AEwCTgU#v=onepage&q=morgan&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.158
2 CONT ** PEDIGREE of the very ancient Family of JONES. .... Pg.156-159
2 CONT *Thomas ap David ap Jenkin, of Treowen, in the Marches of Wales, Efq. = Margaret, daughter of Morgan Kemeys, Efq.; ch: John (m. Anne Morgan) ap Thomas
2 CONT *John ap Thomas of Treowen, in the Marches of Wales, Efq. = Ann, daughter of David ap Gwillim Morgan of Arkfton, Efq.; ch: William (m. Conftance Morgan) John alias Jones
2 CONT *William John alias Jones, of Treowen, Efq. married his firft wife in 1520, ftiled in deeds, between 1570 and 1600, lord of the manors, Henrie, Obeth Caftle, Arnold, Llanarth, and Kevendugloid = Conftance, daughter of Thomas Morga
2 CONC n, of Machen and fifter of Rowland Morgan- firft wife; ch: (Pg.159 John (m. Anne Doddington) ; = Ann, daughter of Sir Walter Hawley, of Suffex, Knight, fecond wife.; ch: (Pg.159 Philip Jones of London ; = Elizabeth, daughter of Ri
2 CONC chard Herbert of Penkelly, Efq. third wife.; ch: (Pg.159 Blanch (m. Rowland Morgan of Machen) Jones)
2 CONT *Pg.159
2 CONT *John Jones of Treowen, Efq. fon and heir apparent in 1563; living 1605; died before 1609; = Ann, daughter of Giles Doddington of Somerfet, Efq. furvived her hufband, Will, dated in 1609.; ch: William (m. Jane Gwilliam) Jones
2 CONT *William Jones of Trewowen and Lanarth Court, Efq.; = Jane, fole daughter and heir-apparent, 1599, of Moor Gwilliam of Monmouth, Efq.; ch: Sir Philip (m. Elizabeth Morgan) Jones
2 CONT *'''Sir Philip Jones of Treowen, Knight, Lieutenant-Colonel of the troops raifed in Monmouthfhire, for King Charles the Firft: in the lift of compounders, publifhed in 1665, Sir Philip Jones of Treowen, Knight, and William his fon
2 CONC , are fet down at 1050l. This gentleman, his lady, and family were in Ragland Caftle, with the Marquis of Worcefter, when it furrendered to the Parliament forces. See Sanderfon;s Hiftory of Charles the Firft: ob. 1660.; = Elizabet
2 CONC h, daughter of Sir Edward Morgan of Lantarnam, Baronet; ch: William (m. Mary Anderton) Jones.
2 CONT *William Jones of Lanarth Court and Treowen, Efq. died in 1667; = Mary, daughter to Chriftopher Anderton of Loftock co. Lancafter, by Althea, daughter of Sir Francis Smith; ch: Philip (m. Anne Baffet) Jones
2 CONT *Philip Jones of Lanarth Court, and Treowen, Efq.; = Ann, daughter of Anthony Baffet of London, Efq.; ch: John (m. Florence Morgan) Jones
2 CONT *John Jones of Lanarth Court, Treowen, and Penllwyn, Co. Monmouth, Efq.; = Florence, fifter and heir of Henry Morgan of Penllwyn, Efq. ob. Dec. 1765; ch: Philip (m. Catherine Weyborne), Edmund, John, William (m. Elizabeth Morgan) 
2 CONC Jones
2 CONT *William Jones of Clytha Houfe, Co. Monmouth, Efq. now living, and a Widower; = Elizabeth, daughter of Sir William Morgan, of Tredegar, Knight of the Bath, by Lady Rachel Cavendifh; and fifter and heir of her brother William Morga
2 CONC n, Efq. ob. S.P.
2 CONT *________________________
