1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1. John Webbe (c1630-d.29 Oct 1700) Second Baronet, married Mary Blomer (d.1709)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT http://jliptrap.us/gen/webbe.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT # John Webbe (c1630-d.29 Oct 1700) Second Baronet, married Mary Blomer (d.1709)
2 CONT ##Mary Webbe (c1666) married Charles Gerrard, Lord Gerrard of Bronley
2 CONT ##John Webbe (c1670-17 Oct1745) Third Baronet, married Barbara Belasyse (c1670-28 Mar1740) .m(2) Helena Moore (c1680-19 Jun 1771)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT General Sir John Webbe (c1597-c1680) married Mary Carryl (c1609-c1661) youngest child of John Carryl and Mary Dormer (married 2 Jun 1599) of Warnham, Sussex.  They lived in Odstock, Wiltshire.  He was made a Baronet of Oldstocke a
2 CONC nd Great Canford 2 Apr 1644 "as a reward of his family having both shed their blood in the King's cause and contributed, as far as they were able, with their purses, in his defence."  They were Roman Catholic.  In 1646, his manor,
2 CONC  rents, and demesne lands were sequestered, value £300 per annum.  Their children's christenings were not recorded in the Anglican Parish Register in Odstock or Salisbury.  John's will refers only to his heir, John, youngest daugh
2 CONC ter Marina, and granddaughter Mary daughter of John.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://jliptrap.us/gen/webbe.htm
