1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Charles Dormer, 2nd Earl of Carnarvon''' was born on 25 October 1632 the son of Robert Dormer, 1st Earl of Carnarvon and Lady Anna Sophia Herbert.
2 CONT
2 CONT * He was baptised on 26 November 1632 at St. Benet's, Paul's Wharf, London, England.
2 CONT * He married, firstly, Elizabeth Capell, daughter of Arthur Capell, 1st Baron Capell of Hadham and Elizabeth Morrison, before 1653. [four surviving children]
2 CONT * He married, secondly, Lady Mary Bertie, daughter of Montagu Bertie, 2nd Earl of Lindsey and Bridget Wray, Baroness Norris, before 1675. [no surviving issue]
2 CONT * He died on 29 November 1709 at age 77 at Ascott House, Wing, Buckinghamshire, England, without surviving male issue.
2 CONT * He was buried on 18 December 1709 at Wing, Buckinghamshire, England.
2 CONT * He was Herediatary Chief Avenor and keeper of the King's Hawks on 20 September 1643.
2 CONT * He succeeded to the title of  3rd Baronet Dormer, of Wyng, co. Buckingham [E., 1615] on 20 September 1643.
2 CONT * He succeeded to the title of  3rd Baron Dormer of Wyng, co. Buckingham [E., 1615] on 20 September 1643.
2 CONT * He succeeded to the title of  2nd Earl of Carnarvon [E., 1628] on 20 September 1643.
2 CONT * He succeeded to the title of  2nd Viscount Ascott, co. Bucks [E., 1628] on 20 September 1643.
2 CONT * He graduated from Oxford University, Oxford, Oxfordshire, England, on 12 April 1648 with a Master of Arts (M.A.).1 His last will was dated 20 July 1709. 
2 CONT * On his death, his Earldom and Viscountancy became extinct.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Charles Dormer, 2nd Earl of Carnarvon and Elizabeth Capell
2 CONT * Lady Isabella Dormer
2 CONT * Lady Anna Sophia Dormer
2 CONT * Charles Dormer, Viscount Ascott b. 25 Jun 1652, d. b 1673
2 CONT * Lady Elizabeth Dormer b. 1653, d. c 24 Oct 1677
2 CONT * Hon. William Dormer b. 25 Sep 1666, d. c Apr 1668
2 CONT * Hon. Robert Dormer b. 14 Jan 1667/68, d. c Feb 1668/69
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations: ''G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, 
2 CONC Extinct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume III, page 45.''
2 CONT
