1 NAME Charles Dormer, 5th Baron Dormer of Wyng
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 22 APR 1668
1 DEAT
2 DATE 2 JUL 1728
1 OCCU 5th Baron Dormer of Wenge
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He succeeded to the title of 5th Baron Dormer of Wyng, co. Buckingham [E., 1615] on 17 September 1712.
2 CONT
2 CONT Debrett's Peerage of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland, 15th Ed. (1825) on page 354: "By his 2d wife, he had issue 7 sons, who all died s.p. except James, the 6th, who settled at Antwerp; and 5 das. who all d. unm. e
2 CONC xcept Frances, the 3rd, who m. William Plowden, of Plowden.  By his first wife he had two sons, Charles and John, successively barons Dormer.  His lordship d. 2 July 1728, and was succeeded by his eldest son, Charles."
