1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1638
1 DEAT
2 DATE 9 AUG 1712
1 OCCU of Dunleckney & Newry
1 TITL Col
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.thepeerage.com/p26495.htm#i264943
2 CONT
2 CONT Colonel Dudley Bagenal was born circa 1638.2 He was the son of Colonel Walter Bagenal and Elizabeth Roper.1 He married, firstly, Ann Butler, daughter of Edward Butler, there were no children of this marriage.2 He married, secondly
2 CONC , Ann Mathew, daughter of George Mathew, in 1668.2 He died on 9 August 1712.2
2 CONT
2 CONT Colonel Dudley Bagenal was educated at St. John's College, Oxford University, Oxford, Oxfordshire, England.2 He was admitted to Middle Temple in 1658.2 He lived at Dunleckney, Bagenalstown, County Carlow, Ireland.2 He was restored
2 CONC  to his Carlow estates by King Charles I circa 1660.2 He held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.) for Old Leighlin in 1668.2 He held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.) for Carlow in 1689.2 He fought in the Battle of t
2 CONC he Boyne in 1690, as a Colonel of an Infantry Regiment.2 He was subsequently attainted with his estates forfeit.2 He held the office of Gentleman Usher to King James II at the Court of St. Germains.2
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Colonel Dudley Bagenal and Ann Mathew
2 CONT * George Bagenal2
2 CONT * Nicholas Bagenal2 d. 1737
2 CONT * Dudley Bagenal2 d. 1757
2 CONT * Mary Bagenal2 d. 1691
2 CONT * Margaret Bagenal2
2 CONT * Katherine Bagenal2 d. 1736
2 CONT * Ann Bagenal2 d. 1734
2 CONT * Walter Bagenal+2 b. c 1670, d. 1745
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Citations''
2 CONT * [S47] Hugh Montgomery-Massingberd, editor, Burke's Irish Family Records (London, U.K.: Burkes Peerage Ltd, 1976), Bagenal, page 45. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Irish Family Records.
2 CONT * [S47] Hugh Montgomery-Massingberd, Burke's Irish Family Records, Bagenal, page 46.
