1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_O%27Brien,_7th_Earl_of_Thomond O'Brien] was the son of Barnabas O'Brien, 6th Earl of Thomond and Anne Fermor. '''In 1641, he married his first cousin Anne O'Brien (d. September 
2 CONC 1645), daughter of Henry O'Brien, 5th Earl of Thomond, by whom he had one son:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Henry, Lord Ibrackan (c. 1642 – 1678)
2 CONT
2 CONT After Anne's death, he married '''Sarah Russell, daughter of Sir Francis Russell, and widow of Sir John Reynolds.''' This made O'Brian a brother-in-law of Henry Cromwell, who had married Sarah's sister Elizabeth.[1] O'Brian and Sa
2 CONC rah had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Henry, died in infancy
2 CONT * Henry Horatio, Lord Ibrackan (d. 1690), who was father of Henry O'Brien, 8th Earl of Thomond (1688–1741)
2 CONT * Elizabeth (d. 3 June 1688), without issue
2 CONT * '''Auberie Anne Penelope, married Henry Howard, 6th Earl of Suffolk,''' and had issue
2 CONT * Mary, married Sir Matthew Dudley, 2nd Baronet
