1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT ''Last updated 19 July 2025''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Hon. Helen Butler''' was the daughter of Edmund Butler, 2nd Viscount Mountgarret and Grizel FitzPatrick.1,2 She died on 28 January 1631/32.3  She was buried at St. Canice Cathedral, Kilkenny, County Kilkenny, IrelandG.4  
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Walter Butler, 11th Earl of Ormonde, son of Hon. John Butler and Katherine MacCartie.3 
2 CONT
2 CONT After her marriage, Hon. Helen Butler was styled as Countess of Ormond on 22 November 1614.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walter_Butler,_11th_Earl_of_Ormond
2 CONT
2 CONT About 1584 Butler married a second cousin, Helen Butler (also known as Ellen), eldest daughter of Edmund Butler, 2nd Viscount Mountgarret and his wife Grizel FitzPatrick.[12][13] Their common great-grandfather was Piers Butler, 8t
2 CONC h Earl of Ormond.
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter and Helen had two sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Thomas Butler, Viscount Thurles (1594–1619), married Elizabeth, daughter of Sir John Pointz, and had issue, including James Butler, 1st Duke of Ormond[14]
2 CONT # James, died young in France[15]
2 CONT —and nine daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Margaret, married Barnaby Fitzpatrick, 5th Baron Upper Ossory[16]
2 CONT # Catherine, married Piers Power of Monalargie, 2nd son of Richard Power, 2nd Baron Power of Curraghmore[17][18][19]
2 CONT # Ellen (died 1663), married Pierce Butler, 1st Viscount Ikerrin[20]
2 CONT # Helena, married James Butler of Grellagh, 5th son of James Butler, 2nd Baron Dunboyne[21]
2 CONT # Joan, married 1st George Bagenal,[22] 2ndly Theobald Purcell, and 3rdly Sir Thomas Esmond, 1st Baronet.
2 CONT # Mary, married George Hamilton of Greenlaw and Roscrea[23]
2 CONT # Elizabeth, married 1st Sir Edmond Blanchville and 2ndly Richard Burke, 6th Earl of Clanricarde[24]
2 CONT # Eleanor (died 1633), died unmarried[25]
2 CONT # Ellis Butler (died 1625), who married Sir Terence O'Brien-Arragh, 1st Baronet of Arragh[26]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral Entry for Helen Butler, Countess of Ormond, 1631.
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000220094497854&size=large}}
2 CONT >Source: From Funeral Entries Vol.17, published online by the National Library of Ireland.
2 CONT http://catalogue.nli.ie/Record/vtls000529291#page/171/mode/1up
2 CONT ----
