2 CONC er)%20Bryan&pg=PA429#v=onepage&q&f=false GoogleBooks]
2 CONT # WikiTree contributors, "Helen Butler (bef.1570-1631)," WikiTree: The Free Family Tree, (https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Butler-11331 : accessed 19 July 2025).
2 CONT # https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walter_Butler,_11th_Earl_of_Ormond
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Helen Butler (bad link) 
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Helen Butler, also known as the Honorable Helen Butler (died 1631), was the wife of Walter Butler, 11th Earl of Ormond. She was the daughter of Edmund Butler, 2nd Viscount Montgarret and Grizel FitzPatrick. Through her son Thomas,
2 CONC  she is an ancestor of Queen Elizabeth II.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Her children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Elizabeth Butler, who married Richard Bourke, 6th Earl of Clanricarde, son of Sir William Bourke and Joan O'Shaughnessy
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Butler, Viscount Thurles (d. 15 Dec 1619), who married Elizabeth Poyntz, daughter of Sir John Poyntz and Elizabeth Sydenham
2 CONT
2 CONT Ellis Butler (d. 19 Feb 1625), who married Sir Terence Arragh, son of Mortogh MacBrian-Arragh and Slaney Butler
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Ellen Butler (d. 16 Jun 1663), who married Pierce Butler, 1st Viscount of Ikerrin, son of Sir James Butler
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]References
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ "Lady Elizabeth Butler", The Peerage, Retrieved 1 oct 2009.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Butlers of County Clare by Sir Henry Blackall
2 CONT
2 CONT Appendices
2 CONT
2 CONT Appendix VI: Office of Arms, Dublin Castle
2 CONT
2 CONT (I)
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral Entries[165]
2 CONT
2 CONT (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1632 
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor, Countess of Ormond.[166]
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Abbreviations
2 CONT
2 CONT ADD. MSS - Additional MSS. British Museum
2 CONT
2 CONT C.S.P. - Calender, State Papers
2 CONT
2 CONT G.O. - Genealogical Office, Dublin (formerly Ulster Office)
2 CONT
2 CONT H.M.C. - Historical Manuscripts Commission
2 CONT
2 CONT I.G.R.S. - Irish Genealogical Research Society
2 CONT
2 CONT Ir. Gen - Irish Genealogist (Journal of I.G.R.S.)
2 CONT
2 CONT P.R.O. - Formerly in Public Record Office, Dublin
2 CONT
2 CONT S.P.Ire. - State Papers, Ireland
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. The chiefs of the house of Butler bore the title “the Butler of Ireland” simpliciter (cf. the Earls Marischal in Scotland) until Edmond, the 6th Butler, was given the name and honour of Earl of Carrick in 1315. His s. James was
2 CONC  cr. Earl of Ormonde in 1328.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. J. P. Prendergast, author of The Cromwellian Settlement of Ireland.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. These have since been acquired by Rev. W. Clare, F.I.G.R.S., who published wills and administrations ante 1800 in Butler Testamentary Records and has loaned his Chanc. Bills to the I.G.R.S. Library.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Ir. Gen. Vol. 2, Nos.3, 4, 5, 6.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Abbreviated to “barony by writ” or “barony by summons”.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Only dau. & heiress of William le Petyt, 6th Baron of Dunboyne.
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. J. H. Round, Ency. Britt.11th Ed. Vol 3, p. 422, article on “Baron”.
2 CONT
2 CONT 8. There were actually six generations of James Butlers, but as the last d.v.p unmar, the succession did not go through him, but through his bro. Henry, who succeeded their father, Cornet Butler. This James was B.A. (T.C.D.) and a
2 CONC  barrister. He died 2 Sept, 1791.
