2 CONT 80. The Lamberts are one of the comparatively few Cromwellian settlers among the Galway gentry. They descend from the Lamberts of Calton, Yorks, one of whom was Gen. John Lambert, the celebrated Commonwealth leader. Ellen Lambert’
2 CONC s mother was a dau. of Thos Seymour of Ballymore Castle, Co. Galway. The late Archdeacon St. John D. Seymour, the antiquary, was a member of this family. Ballymore is said to be the oldest inhabited castle in Galway. It was besieg
2 CONC ed by Ginkell in June, 1690 (Macaulay Hist. of Engl., chapter XVII).
