2 FORM jpg
2 NOTE http://www.historum.com/european-history/18989-irish-confederate-wars-1641-1653-a-5.html
3 CONT
3 CONT This map shows the country after the Gaelic rally which gradually occured after the Bruce Invasion and the Black Death. The areas in blue were the parts which were most intensively settled and so managed to hang on the longest.
3 CONT The complete feudal system had been established in these blue areas replacing the Gaelic system and ordinary people down to the lowest level would have been affected by this. In these blue areas we are talking about baronies, mano
3 CONC rs, serfs, intensive tillage based agriculture, large numbers of lower order English and Welsh settlers living in villages and towns. In parts of eastern Ireland the settlers even outnumbered the natives, for example in the area m
3 CONC arked Wexford Lordship, Gaelic was replaced by Yola, an archaic English language which was still spoken there into modern times.
3 CONT the blue areas would slowly turn green as they were under cultural attack from the edges and from within but they would never entirely revert to what had existed before and instead became a sort of hybrid culture.
