1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Wikipedia contributors. "<em>[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_Nugent,_2nd_Earl_of_Westmeath Richard Nugent, 2nd Earl of Westmeath]</em>." Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia. Photo: By Peter Gavigan - Prakica D
2 CONC CZ 6.2, CC BY-SA 3.0, https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=3821077
2 CONT
2 CONT While attempting to make his way back to Ireland in December 1641 upon the outbreak of the 1641 Rebellion, Nugent was arrested on suspecion of complicty in the rising. He subsequently served as a cavalry commander during the Irish
2 CONC  Confederate Wars, seeing action at the Battle of Dungan's Hill in August 1647, where he was captured. He later served as General of the Forces of Leinster from 1650-52. During Oliver Cromwell's campaign in Ireland, Clonyn Castle,
2 CONC  the main Nugent residence, was burnt: according to one account Lord Westmeath burnt it himself to prevent it falling into his enemies hands. He submitted to the Parliamentary forces in the latter year but was excluded from the Ac
2 CONC t of Settlement 1652 and transplanted to Connaught. After the Restoration of Charles II, he received a large pension as a reward for his loyalty to the Crown.
