2 CONT
2 CONT Generation 5:
2 CONT
2 CONT THOMAS VAUGHAN of Dunraven and Pembrey Court, Pembrey, Carmarthenshire, Wales.. Born abt. 1540.  He married Catherine Johnes.
2 CONT
2 CONT More about Thomas Vaughan:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Thomas Vaughan, the elder son and heir held the manor of Pembrey and the
2 CONT
2 CONT Glamorgan and Breconshire properties, the whole being of the yearly value
2 CONT
2 CONT of One thousand Five hundred pounds to which he later added by the purchase
2 CONT
2 CONT of Fallersdon in Wiltshire.  He became a justice of the peace for
2 CONT
2 CONT Carmarthenshire, and served as High Sheriff of the county on two occasions,
2 CONT
2 CONT 1566 and 1570.  His will was proved in 1584.  His wife, Catherine Jones,
2 CONT
2 CONT was daughter of "yr hen Sir Thomas Sions o Abermarlais" as Dwnn describes
2 CONT
2 CONT him, by Mary Berkeley.  After her husband's death, Catherine married
2 CONT
2 CONT secondly Robert Thomas, and thirdly William Bassett.
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation 6:
2 CONT
2 CONT WALTER VAUGHAN of Bredwardine, Dunraven and Pembrey was born abt. 1516.
2 CONT
2 CONT Was High Sheriff of Carmarthenshire, 1557. He married Blanch Rydall. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Was the Mayor of Pembrey in 1574, 1580 and 1595, where he died in office.
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter Vaughan of Pembrey Court was High Sheriff in 1557, and his son Thomas served the same office in 1566 and 1570. The Vaughans in due course ended without male heirs and the mansion and estate came to Bridget Vaughan, sole hei
2 CONC ress, who married John Ashburnham of Sussex in 1677, and thereafter remained in her Ashburnham descendants.
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation 7:
2 CONT
2 CONT SIR RICHARD VAUGHAN of Bredwardine was born about 1460 and was sheriff of Herefortshire in 1530-31. He married Ann Butler.
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation 8:
2 CONT
2 CONT SIR THOMAS VAUGHAN of Bredwardine, Hefortshire, England was born about 1435. Died 1483 at Hergest Court, Kington, Herefordshire, England. He married Elinor Whitney. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Now a farm, Hergest Court was for centuries the home of the Vaughan Family and it is here that Sir Thomas Vaughan, popularly known as "Black Vaughan" was taken prisoner and decapitated in 1483. It is said that at the time of his d
2 CONC eath his head fell to the ground, to be seized by his bloodhound dog, who then ran off with it in the direction of Kington Church, some two miles away. The head has been seen many times hovering above the moat and both Black Vaugh
2 CONC an and his bloodhound have been witnessed walking together in the direction of the church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation 9:
2 CONT
2 CONT WATKIN VAUGHAN of Bredwardine was born about 1414 at Bredwardine, Herefordshire, England. He married Ellen or Elizabeth Wogen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation 10:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Roger Vaughan was born about 1385 in Bredwardine, Herefordshire, England. He died during the battle of  Agincourt, France in 1415. He married Gwladus Verch Dafydd.
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation 11:
2 CONT
2 CONT Rosser Roger Vaughan, Hen-The Aged was born about 1352 in Bredwardine, Herefordshire, England.
2 CONT
