1 NAME John /Oxenbridge/
2 GIVN John
2 _MARNM Oxenbridge
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Kings Chapel Burying Ground
2 ADDR
3 ADR1 58 Tremont Street
3 CITY Boston
3 STAE Massachusetts
3 POST 02108
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 30 JAN 1609
2 ADDR
3 CITY Daventry
3 STAE England
3 POST NN11
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 DEAT
2 DATE 28 DEC 1674
2 ADDR
3 CITY Boston
3 STAE Massachusetts
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Reverend
1 TITL Rev
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rev John Oxenbridge BIRTH	30 Jan 1609, Daventry, Daventry District, Northamptonshire, England DEATH	28 Dec 1674 (aged 65), Boston, Suffolk County, Massachusetts, USA BURIAL	Kings Chapel Burying Ground, Boston, Suff
2 CONC olk County, Massachusetts, USA, MEMORIAL ID 18700092
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Daniel Oxenbridge M.D. of Christ Church, Oxford, so of Rev John of Coventry, scholar and divine, and Katherine Harby, daughter of Thomas Harby and Katherine Throckmorton. Descendant of Henry II King of England through Thoma
2 CONC s de Throckmorton. Brother of Elizabeth who married Oliver Saint John. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Jane Butler, and had one daughter, Bathshua, who married Richard Scott of Jamaica. Jane was a scholar of theology and John would often ask her opinion of his preachings. Jane died 25 April 1655, aged 37 years. Andrew Ma
2 CONC rvell, who was their friend, wrote an epitaph Janae Oxenbrigiae Epitaphium for her tomb at Eton, which was defaced terribly during the Restoration. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Secondly, husband of Frances Woodward, daughter of Hezekiah Woodward of Botscombe, Gloucestershire, ejected vicar of Bray. They married in 1656, and had one daughter, Theodora, who married Rev Peter Thatcher. Frances died July 165
2 CONC 9 in her childbed in the first year of their marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thirdly, husband of Mary Hackshaw, married by licence dated 26 Feb 1661. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Fourthly, husband of Susanna, widow of John Parris, meeting in Barbados and they were married after 1660. Susanna died in 1696. Some records state she is his third wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT John was a pensioner of Emmanuel College, Cambridge in 1626, then transferred to Magdalen Hall, Oxford where he earned his B.A. degree in 1628 and his M.D. in 1631. He tutored at Magdalen until deprived of the position in 1634 by 
2 CONC Archbishop Laud after he drew up a new code of articles regarding the government of the college no one approved of.
2 CONT
2 CONT John resided in Bermuda from 1634 to 1641, then returned to England in where he helped negotiate the surrender of Scarborough Castle during the Civil War, appointed a fellowship of Eaton College and served as a lecturer at Berwick
2 CONC -upon-Tweed until 1651. He was ejected from Eaton for Puritanism in 1660, and expelled from Berwick by the Act of Uniformity in 1662. He resided at the Dutch republic of Surinam 1662 to 1667, then Barbados until 1669. He then sett
2 CONC led in Boston by 1670 where he and Susanna joined the First Church of Boston. John was soon vote unanimously to become their pastor. John died near the end of one of his sermons and was buried in the King's Chapel Burying Ground i
2 CONC n Boston.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bio by: Anne Shurtleff Stevens
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse Photo Susana Oxenbridge 1616–1696
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Theodora Oxenbridge Thacher 1659–1697
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription 66yrs. 6th minister - 1st Church.
