2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Oxenbridge-4#_note-2
2 CONT
2 CONT >Several years ago I visited the SAR library in Los Angeles, and copied some pages from the NEH&G, Vol. 44, pgs. 84-85, and 194-195, in which are printed the wills of Daniel Oxenbridge, and his wife, Katherine Oxenbridge.
2 CONT >>Daniel's will states: "To son Daniel all my part and share in the Tyune Farm, he to pay and discharge the sum of three hundred pounds for which I stand bound unto my son-in-law Mr. Edmond Hunt for his wife's portion," (p. 84).
2 CONT >>Katherine's will, proved 5 November 1651, states: "I give to the Plantation of New England Ten pounds for to buy books for the Indians to learn to read. ... To my daughter Hunt my ring that is set with pearls and all my own wear
2 CONC ing clothes,"(p. 85).[3]
2 CONT
