1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Cheney Hales, esq. of the Dungeon, who died early in life in 1594, and was buried in St. Mary Bredin church. He married Mary, daughter of Richard Hardres, of Hardres, who afterwards remarried William Ashenden, and 
2 CONC lastly George Walter, esq. 
2 CONT
2 CONT By her first husband she had an only son Sir James Hales, of the Dungeon, who dying in 1665,  was buried by his wife, daughter and heir of Sir Thomas Norton, who died in 1659, in St. Mary Bredin church. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They left an only daughter and heir Elizabeth, married first to Sir Stephen Hales, K. B. of Snetterfield, in Warwickshire, who died in 1668 without issue; on which she married secondly, George, third son of William Sheldon, esq. o
2 CONC f Beoly, in Worcestershire, as abovementioned; they both lie buried in St. Mary Bredin church. This branch of the Hales's bore for their arms the same as those of St. Stephen's. There are pedigrees of them in the two heraldic visi
2 CONC tations of the co. Kent, of 1574, 1619, and in MSS. No. 2230, to the year 1664, in the British Museum. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.british-history.ac.uk/survey-kent/vol11/pp147-164
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT See pedigree of Elizabeth Hales, "da. & heire" of Sir James Hales, in Visitation of Kent 1663-1668 p 69, and under Sources.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Historic Canterbury ~ ST. MARY BREDIN (BREDING) ~
2 CONT
2 CONT Little Lady Dungil, St. Mary Breden
2 CONT
2 CONT ROSE LANE, CANTERBURY
2 CONT
2 CONT Among the monuments and inscriptions are the following....A plain altar tomb on the south side of the altar rails, and round the verge an inscription for Humphrey Hales, esq. son of Sir James Hales, deceased 1555. The same father 
2 CONC Sir James Hales. A mural tablet over the above, for George Sheldon, third son of William Sheldon, esq. of Beoly, in Worcestershire, who first married Frances, daughter of Thomas More, esq. of Gobbins in Hertfordshire, and afterwar
2 CONC ds Elizabeth, only daughter and heir of Sir James Hales, of the Dungeon, the widow of Sir Stephen Hales, K.B. of Sntierfield, in Warwickshire, which George died without issue in 1679, and lies buried here, as does Elizabeth his se
2 CONC cond wife, who died afterwards that same year; arms, Sheldon, a fess, between three martlets.
2 CONT
