1 TITL Major
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Among the royalists who fled to Virginia after the death of King Charles I, were Grey/Graye Skipwith (later Sir Grey)  and his future brother in law Edward Dale. Grey/Graye was the fourth son and sixth child of Sir Henry Skipwith,
2 CONC  Knight, and first Baronet of Prestwold, Leicestershire, whose ancestry goes back to the time of William the Conqueror. Diana was Sir Henry's second daughter and fifth child youngest child. Though Edward may have served in the Roy
2 CONC alist Army, there there is no record of him having the title 'Major' when he left England. It seems likely that he gained the title while serving in the Lancaster County Militia. Edward settled on the north side of Rappahannock Ri
2 CONC ver in Lancaster Co. and Grey.Graye settled on the south side in what is now Middlesex Co. Edward Dale soon became active in Lancaster Co. Affairs, serving as Clerk from 1655-1674: he was Justice of the County Court for 14 years; 
2 CONC High Sheriff for four years; and a member of the House of Burgesses for 2 years. He and Lady Diana had 2 children: Katherine, who married Capt. Thomas Carter of Lancaster Co.; and Elizabeth, who married Capt. John Rodgers of North
2 CONC umberland co. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The epitaph for Edward Dale's tomb is recorded in the Carter Prayer Book, now in the Virginia Historical Society. Of interest is the following excerpt: 
2 CONT
2 CONT As Nieghbor--Father--Husband he excelled and in early years crowned his other accomplishments by a felicitous marriage with Diana ye daughter of Sir Henry Skypwith of Preswold in ye county of Leicester Bart who is left a little wh
2 CONC ile to mourn him. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Major Dale's will has disappeared, but his son in law Thomas Carter sealed his will in 1700 with the seal of the Dales. The crest on the seal identifies Edward as one of the Dales of Northampton, County of Chester and of London. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Major Dale had extensive land holding, 3400 acres. In 1674 he added 500 acres to daughter, Katharine Carter. In 1677 he added 600 acres to daughter Elizabeth Rodgers. He left his home plantation in St. Mary's White Chapel Parish (
2 CONC Lancaser co., near Barford) to grandsons Peter and Joseph Carter, who divided it in 1712. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Some of his extensive colleciton of books on law, medicine, history, religion, poetry and natural science are said to have been preserved by Carter descendants. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Major Dale left 12 pounds to daughter Elizabeth and the remainder of his estate to his Carter grandchildren. Daughter Katharine was named executrix. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a Major in the Lancaster County Militia. Records indicate that he had been a Major in the royal army. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Edward Dale and Diana Skipwith are: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Dale, married William Rogers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Katherine Dale, born Abt. 1652 in Lancaster County, Virgina; died May 10, 1703 in Barford, Lancaster County Virginia; married Thomas Carter , Sr May 04, 1670 in Barford, Lancaster County, Virginia.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Major Edward Dale was living at Rappahannock River, Lancaster, VA, US, having sought refuge in Virginia after the death of Charles I with Sir Grey Skipwith, his brother in law and fellow royalist.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Diana Skipwith, daughter of Sir Henry Skipwith and Amy Kemp.
2 CONT
2 CONT Major Edward Dale held the several offices. From 1655 to 1674 he was Clerk of the County; from 1699 to 1684 was a Commissioner of the County Court; High Sheriff in 1670, 1671, 1679, and 1680; member of the House of Burgesses in 16
2 CONC 77 and 1682-3. In 1655 at Lancaster, VA, US.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/GMVK-PJ7 FamilySearch Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 3 2019, 7:23:25 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Edward Dale was a Royal Refugee who emigrated to America and became a Justice of Virginia; high Sheriff 1670-1680; A Burgess 1677-1683; married Diana, daughter of Sir Henry Skipwith. Their daughter,Katherine, married Captain Thoma
2 CONC s Carter, a Burgess and land owner of Virginia,
