2 CONT Gamaliel Taylor was born in Ottumwa, Iowa on October 13, 1845. He was married November 26, 1874, to Laura Caroline Wright. Gamaliel Taylor was the son of Eber Taylor, born in New York State September 6,1811, died in Junction City,
2 CONC  Oregon, July 20,1861 and Clarissa Stout. They were married in Iowa on April 4, 1841.
2 CONT
2 CONT Clarissa Stout was the daughter of John Stout who was born in West Virginia on December 21, 1795, died in Ottumwa, Iowa, on may 6, 1858, married in Randolph County, West Virginia, 1815 to Mary Barbara Castner (Kestner- Kessner) wh
2 CONC o was born in West Virginia June 28, 1799, died at Albia, Iowa on May 20, 1876.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Stout was the son of St. Ledger Stout who was born in Amwell Township, Hunterdon County, New Jersey, died in Beverly, West Virginia, 1806 and Anna Barcalo (Buckalow) born in New Jersey, died in West Virginia after 1806.
2 CONT
2 CONT St. Leger Stout was the son of St. Leger Codd Stout who was born in Hunterdon County, New
2 CONT
2 CONT Jersey, 1736, died in New Jersey and married in New Jersey to Susannah who died in 1770.
2 CONT
2 CONT St. Leger Codd Stout was the son of James Stout who was born in New Jersey, married between April 28, 1731-1733 to Lady Mary Ann Codd, who was born in Maryland, the daughter of Captain St. Leger Codd, who was born in Northumberlan
2 CONC d County, Virginia, about 1676, died about 1731, married in Virginia to Mary Hansen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain St.Leger Codd was the son of Col. St. Leger Codd, who was born in Virginia, died in Maryland 1707, married in Virginia to Anna (Bennett) Bland, widow of Governor Bland and daughter of Governor Richard Bennett of Virginia, 
2 CONC who married Mary Ann Utie, daughter of Captain John Utie.
2 CONT
2 CONT Col. St. Leger Codd was the son of William Codd, born in England, died in Ulcombe, Kent, England, 1653, married in England to Mary St. Leger.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary St. Leger was the daughter of Sir Warham St. Leger who was born in England, died in England hi 1631, married in England to Mary, daughter of Sir Rowland Hayward, Lord Mayor of London.... On down to Royalty in Italy, France, e
2 CONC tc.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://www.shirleyassociation.com/NewShirleySite/NonMembers/Surnames/SwanSurname.html
2 CONT
2 CONT >Colonel Swann married, as his second wife, on 13 January 1649/50, Sarah Codd, daughter of Samuel and Susannah Codd, and a member of an old Kentish family.  She died on 13 January 1654/5 "Having been married that day just five yea
2 CONC rs", and was buried at Swann's Point. 
