2 CONT
2 CONT '''DOCUMENTATION OF 3RD MARRIAGE TO TRISTRAM THOMAS JR. (indicated in his will, where she is referenced as widow, as well as maiden name and previous married names)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Accounting in Queen Anne's County, Maryland on the estate of Thomas Eubanks filed on 15 October 1725 by Trustram [Tristram] Thomas and Jane, his wife executrix of the Last Will and Testament of Thomas Eubanks.
2 CONT Source Date
2 CONT 1725
2 CONT Where The Record Is Found (Citation)
2 CONT Prerogative Court Accounts, Liber 7, pages 166-167, Queen Anne's County, Maryland
2 CONT Describe The Record (Notes)
2 CONT This source proves that Tristram Thomas (about 1664-11 February 1745/1746) and his third wife, Jane Kemp Clothier Eubanks Thomas were married before 15 October 1725. Thomas Eubanks (jane Kemp's second husband) died in Queen Anne's
2 CONC  County, Maryland. His will was dated 23 April 1723 and was proven on 4 July 1723.
