1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *''''''Anne Glemham1
2 CONT *''''''F, #6342, d. 10 January 1638/39
2 CONT *Last Edited=28 Mar 2004
2 CONT *''''''     Anne Glemham was the daughter of Sir Henry Glemham and Lady Anne Sackville.1,2 She married, firstly, Paul Bayning, 1st Viscount Bayning of Sudbury, son of Paul Bayning and Susanna Norden, before 1613.2 She married, sec
2 CONC ondly, Dudley Carleton, 1st and last Viscount Dorchester, son of Anthony Carleton, on 14 June 1630.2 She died on 10 January 1638/39 at Westminster, London, England.2 She was buried on 31 January 1638/39 at Gosfield, Essex, England
2 CONC .2 Her will (dated 1 and 3 September 1638) was probated on 15 January 1638/39.2
2 CONT *''''''      From before 1613, her married name became Bayning.2 As a result of her marriage, Anne Glemham was styled as Baroness Bayning of Horkesley on 27 February 1627/28. As a result of her marriage, Anne Glemham was styled as
2 CONC  Viscountess Bayning of Sudbury on 8 March 1627/28. From 14 June 1630, her married name became Carleton.2
2 CONT *''''''Children of Anne Glemham and Paul Bayning, 1st Viscount Bayning of Sudbury
2 CONT **1.Elizabeth Bayning, Countess of Shepey+3
2 CONT **2.Hon. Cicelia Bayning3
2 CONT **3.Paul Bayning, 2nd Viscount Bayning of Sudbury+2 b. c 1616, d. 11 Jun 1638
2 CONT **4.Anne Bayning, Viscountess Bayning of Foxley+4 b. 23 Apr 1619, d. Oct 1678
2 CONT **5.Hon. Mary Bayning+1 b. c 1623, d. b 20 Jan 1671/72
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extin
2 CONC ct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 133. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *2.[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume II, page 37.
2 CONT *3.[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume II, page 38.
2 CONT *4.[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume II, page 35.
2 CONT *http://thepeerage.com/p635.htm#i6342
2 CONT *__________________
