3 CONT ROBERT PEAKE (LINCOLNSHIRE 1551-1619 LONDON)
3 CONT Portrait of Cecilia Neville (b.c.1604), full-length, in an arcadian landscape
3 CONT oil on canvas
3 CONT 83 x 47 in. (211.8 x 119.4 cm.)
3 CONT Provenance
3 CONT By descent at Hampton Court Castle, Herefordshire to the following,
3 CONT George Capel-Coningsby, 5th Earl of Essex (1757-1839), until 1810, when sold with the house to the following,
3 CONT Richard Arkwright (1755-1843), Hampton Court Castle, Herefordshire, and by descent until 1912, when sold with the house to the following,
3 CONT Mrs Nancy Burrell, Hampton Court Castle, Herefordshire; her sale, Knight, Frank and Rutley, on the premises, 15 March 1925, lot 550.
3 CONT Vesey Grange, Sutton Coldfield; Slater, Dann & Co, on the premises, 28 September 1960, lot 239.
3 CONT Mr Southall, Grimshaw Hall, Knowle; Christie's, South Kensington, 8 March 2000, lot 283, as 'Attributed to Robert Peake', with a later inscription lower right.
3 CONT with The Weiss Gallery, London, April 2001, where acquired by the present owner [Jasper Conran].
3 CONT Literature
3 CONT 'Paintings At Hampton Court, co. Hereford', The Gentleman's Magazine, XCV, July 1825, p. 20.
3 CONT J. Sherwood, ‘Baby Grand’, World of Interiors, March 2002, p. 135, illustrated in Jasper Conran's London home.
