1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Book of the Lockes: A genealogical and historical record of the descendants ... By John Goodwin Locke
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=2twUAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA358&lpg=PA358&dq=Matthew+Michael+Locke+1550&source=bl&ots=dd3fJR-MCD&sig=mWoBIujyABMkQ7CMo5siY7b88Y0&hl=en&ei=nqcrTYa9L4zSsAPq0ZWmBw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=1&ved=0C
2 CONC BkQ6AEwADgU#v=onepage&q=Matthew%20Michael%20Locke%201550&f=false
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/bookoflockesgene00lock
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/bookoflockesgene00lock#page/342/mode/1up
2 CONT *John Locke, sheriff of London, 1460. ch: Thomas d. 1507
2 CONT *Thomas Locke d. anno 1507 m. Joan Wilcock d.1512 ch: 1. John d.1519 (a), 2. Sir William d. 1550 m. 2 wives (b) 1st Elizabeth Spencer, 2nd Catharine, daughter of Wm. Cook, 3. Michael.
2 CONT **	(a) I am of opinion, after an examination of Stow's "Survey of London," that the "arms in the window" were those of Sir William Locke, who was buried in Mercer's Chapel in 1550; yet a doubt remains.
2 CONT **	(b) He had four wives.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/bookoflockesgene00lock#page/343/mode/1up
2 CONT *3. Michael Locke, younger brother (a) of Sir William, children: 1. Matthew
2 CONT *1. Mathew Locke, ch: 1. Richard d.1617 and 2. Christopher
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/bookoflockesgene00lock#page/344/mode/1up
2 CONT *2. Christopher Locke, the youngest son children: 1. Christopher, 2. John, 3. Honour, 4. Christian, '''5. Lewis. 
2 CONT *'''5. Lewis Locke, baptized 13th July 1606; was buried at Taunton Saint Mary Magdalen, March 27, 1692. By four wives he had thirty-five children, most of whom lived to be men and women; and what is more remarkable, his eldest son
2 CONC ''' John, born 1625, was fifty-nine years of age, when '''his youngest son''' Christopher was born at Taunton, anno 1684. It is reported in the family that John had a great-grandson as old as his younger brother; which is, perhaps
2 CONC , '''the chief reason why this branch of the family cannot truly ascertain their respective degrees of kindred. It is, however, generally believed, that all the Lockes of Somersetshire and Devonshire derive themselves from this Le
2 CONC wis; but whether so or not''', we know that Allen, '''one of the younger sons by the last wife''', was father of another Allen who was father of the present Mr. Thomas Locke of Taunton, Maltster, who has six sons, three of whom ar
2 CONC e settled in London and three in Taunton, the youngest being a Master of Arts of the University of Oxford, also one daughter not yet married.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/bookoflockesgene00lock#page/358/mode/2up
2 CONT **	The following Pedigree is principally compiled from the Herald's Visitations and the Gentleman's Magazine.
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *Sir WILLIAM, Knt. and Alderman, b. 1480, d. 1550. He was knighted by Hen. VIII. for going over to Dunkirk and pulling down the Pope's bull; was sheriff of London 1548. Sir William was Gent. of the Privy Chamber. His 3d wf. was El
2 CONC eanor, wid. of Walter Marshe. She d. 1546. His 4th wf. was Elizabeth, widow of Robert Meredith. = 1st  Alice Spencer or Elizabeth Spencer, of London, who died 1522, buried at Mercer's Chapel, London; ch:  William (b.1511 d.1517), 
2 CONC Philip (d.1524), Jane (m. Robt. Meredith), Peter (d.1517), William (b.1517 d.1519), Richard (d.1516), Edmund (d.1545), Thomas (m. Mary Louge), Matthew (m. Elizabeh Baker) Locke; = 2d. Katherine, dau. of William, and sister  and co
2 CONC -heir of Sir Thos Cook of Wiltshire, Knt. She was buried at Merton Abbey, Surrey. She d. Oct. 14, 1537. ; ch: Dorothy (m. Otwell Hill & Jno. Cosworth), Katherine (m. Thomas Stacey & William Matthew), Rose (m. _ Throgmorton, Esq. &
2 CONC  Anthony Hickman), John (d. France), Alice (d.1537), Thomasin (d.1530), Henry (m. Anne Vaughan), Michael (m. Jane Wilkinson & Margery Peryn), Elizabeth (m. Richard Hill & Nicholas Bullingham), John (d.1537) Locke
2 CONT *In a note on page 343, I commented on the statement made in the Gentleman's Magazine, that Michael Locke, the Father of Mathew of Pensford, was a younger Brother of Sir William, while other authorities had spoken of him as a son 
2 CONC of Sir William. The principal reason that has influenced my opinion in favor the the statement in the Gent. Mag. is that the Michael Locke who was son of Sir William had three sons, Zachary, Benjamin, and Eleazer, and several daus
2 CONC ., and that although these three sons speak of each other and their sisters in their wills, no mention is made of a bro. Matthew. On this Hypothesis, the descent of Matthew is represented by the dotted line.
2 CONT **MICHAEL, of London, merchant. 2. m. Margery Peryn, wid. of Caesar Dalmarias, fa. of Sir Julius Caesar, Knt. = Jane, dau. of William Wilkinson, mercer, and shf. of London. ; ch: Matthew (See note p. 358), Eleaser, Benjamin, Zacha
2 CONC ry, dau. (m.Wm. Sanson), dau. (m. _ Jenney)
2 CONT ***MATTHEW, of Pensford, in Somersetshire. (see note p. 358); ch: Richard (d.1617), Christopher
2 CONT ****CHRISTOPHER, of Pilrow, near Lockestown.  ch: Perhaps Sarah (m. Nicholas Davies), Christopher (bap.1593), John (m. Miss Keen or Ken), Honour (m. Francis Shepard), Christian (bap.1601), '''Lewis (bap.1606)''',  William (Probabl
2 CONC y) (m. Elisabeth _ ) Locke
2 CONT *****'''Lewis, bap. July 13, 1606, buried at Taunton, St. Mary Magdalen, Mch. 27, 1692, by 4 wives had 35 chil., most of whom lived to be men and women. ; = : ch:''' John (b.1625), Allen, William (m. Dorothy Cooksley), Christopher
2 CONC  (b.1684), Richard? (was a writer) Locke
2 CONT ******John, eldest son, b. 1625.
2 CONT ******Allen, a younger son by 4th wf.
2 CONT ******William, of Pitminster, son of 4th wife, died Jan'y 25, 1719, a 49. = Dorothy, dau. of Richard Cooksley, of Dunstar, Gent. ; ch: Richard (m. Hannah Dod) Locke
2 CONT ******Christopher, youngest son, b. at Taunton, 1684.
2 CONT ******(Richard?) of Pitminster, son or gr. son of Lewis; was a writer. ___________________
2 CONT *'''A history and genealogy of Captain John Locke (1627-1696) of Portsmouth and Rye, N.H., and his descendants; also of Nathaniel Locke of Portsmouth, and a short account of the history of the Lockes in England (1916?]) 
2 CONT *http://archive.org/details/historygenealogy00lock 
2 CONT *http://archive.org/stream/historygenealogy00lock#page/571/mode/1up 
2 CONT *Pg. 571
2 CONT *SAME TEXT AS IN "Book of the Lockes : ...." ______________________________
