1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sailed on the Mary & John, landed in Ipswitch MA 1634, Moved to Newbury, MA 1635
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: Henry (Immigrant, 1634 "Mary and John") Lunt Birth: ABT 1610 in England Death: 1662 Religion: Newbury church
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendants: Sen. John Kerry, Alice Hathaway Lee, first wife of Teddy Roosevelt, GREAT GREAT GRANDFATHER OF REVOLUTIONARY WAR COL. TIMOTHY PICKERING
2 CONT
2 CONT FREEMAN AT NEWBURY, 1638
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry immigrated on the "Mary and John" in 1634. He lived in Ipswich and Newbury. His will was dated 8 July 1662 and proved 30 September 1662.
2 CONT
2 CONT "History tells us that Henry Lunt and his wife, Ann, came from England in the ship, Mary and John, and that they first landed at Agawam, now Ipswich, MA, and came to what is now called Newbury, MA, in the spring of 1634-5." --Hist
2 CONC ory of the Lunt Family, p.114 Marriage 1 Ann (Immigrant) b: ABT 1618 in probably England Married: ABT 1638 Children
2 CONT  Cornet Daniel Lunt b: 17 MAY 1641 in Newbury, Essex Co, MA
2 CONT  Henry Lunt b: 20 FEB 1653 in Newbury, Essex Co., MA
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: 1) The Ancestors of Senator John Forbes Kerry (b. 1943), by William Addams Reitwiesner, WReitwiesn@aol.com, Website, 2004 http://members.aol.com/_ht_a/wreitwiesn/candidates2004/kerry.html 2) Judith Mae Field Stuntz Databa
2 CONC se, 6 Oct 2004 http://worldconnect.rootsweb.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=jud&id
2 CONT =I19064
2 CONT 3) Ancestry of Northeastern Pennsylvania
2 CONT http://www.dsdata.com.au/cgi-bin/ind_scr.cgi?478 4) Ancestors of Russell Edward Spooner II, 2003 http://www.spoonergen.com/res/resg71.htm 5) Patrick McDonald Database, 14 Sep 2005 http://wc.rootsweb.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=p
2 CONC jmpjm&id=I5076 6) Thomas S. Lunt, A History of the Lunt Family in America (Salem, MA: The Salem Press Company, 1914) _UID: F19EBAA6A6574EAE91C9393237D813905F0C
2 CONT =-=-=-=-=-=-=-==-
2 CONT
2 CONT "He held the rank of Lieutenant-colonel [in the army of Charles I.] in Sir Thomas's regiment at York in 1640, and was at Nottingham at the raising of the standard in July 1642. He was engaged in the action near Cherborne Castle, a
2 CONC nd subsequently at the battle of Edgehilll in the same year, and was killed at the siege of Bristol, 25 July 1643."
2 CONT
2 CONT "He was referred to as being of "great sobriety, wisdom and courage." He was killed leading a charge at the capture of Bristol.
