1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jonet (Janet) Sanders (later Turner) was an English-born woman who lived from 1590 to 1658 during the late Tudor and Stuart eras. Her biographical records are primarily preserved through digital genealogical databa
2 CONC ses like YourRoots.
2 CONT
2 CONT -Vital Statistics-
2 CONT Birth: 1590 in Charleswood, Surrey, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 1658 in Alloa, Clackmannanshire, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT -Family Background-
2 CONT Parents: She was the daughter of Thomas Saunders of Surrey and Elizabeth Bathurst of Kent.
2 CONT Ancestry:
2 CONT Her maternal lineage includes Lancelot Bathurst, an Alderman of London. Her paternal lineage traces back to Bedfordshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage:
2 CONT She married Robert Turner, who was originally from Alloa, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT The couple had multiple children, including a son named Adam Cornelius Turner who later settled in Lancashire, England.
