2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Edward HUNGERFORD.....1596-1648, inherited the estates of his kinsman Sir Edward HUNGERFORD in 1607. He was a member of both the Short and Long Parliaments in 1640. During the Civil War he attached himself to the parliamentary
2 CONC  party, fighting at Lansdowne and at Roundway Down.
2 CONT
2 CONT * parents: Anthony Hungerford & Lucy St John
2 CONT
2 CONT Married
2 CONT # Margaret Hallyday d 19.07.1629, dau of William Hallyday, Lord Mayor of London
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT * He obtained a license, dated 26 February 1620, to marry Margaret, daughter and coheiress of William Holliday , alderman and lord mayor of London  She had no issue by him, and survived him till 1672, when she was also buried at F
2 CONC arleigh.
2 CONT * In 1653 Margaret petitioned the Council of State  to pay her £500, a small part of the sum borrowed from her husband by the parliament. Parliament had ordered repayment in 1649.
2 CONT * Oliver Cromwell  appears to have interested himself in her case. Sir Edward's reversionary interest ithe Farleigh estates passed to his royalist half-brother Anthony Hungerford (d. 1657)
2 CONT ===============================================
2 CONT
