1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Bridget Hungerford 
2 CONT * Born: before 1598 at Great Bedwyn, England
2 CONT * Father: Sir Anthony Hungerford of Black Bourton 
2 CONT * Mother: Lucy Hungerford [relict of John St John ]
2 CONT
2 CONT Bridget Hungerford was the 1st daughter of Sir Anthony Hungerford of Black Bourton, Oxfordshire and Lucy Hungerford. On 5 Oct 1612 at Great Bedwyn, Wiltshire she married Alexander Chocke son of Francis Chocke of Yatton, Somerset a
2 CONC nd Mary, daughter of Thomas Swift of London, nephew of Alexander Chocke. [1] (s.p.)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anthony_Hungerford_of_Black_Bourton
2 CONT
2 CONT Anthony Hungerford married twice.  Firstly to Lucy Hungerford, a daughter of Sir Walter Hungerford (died c.1596) of Farleigh Castle in Wiltshire, by whom he had children including
2 CONT
2 CONT >'''Bridget Hungerford''', who married three times, firstly to Alexander Chocke (1594–1625) of Shalbourne,[8] secondly to John Rudhale and thirdly to John Vaughan, of Herefordshire, a Roman Catholic.[9] NO. “Mary Pitt was said to 
2 CONC have had a dowry of £2500 when she became the second wife of Sir Alexander Choke.[1]. Mary was a young widow and married two more times, to John Rudhale and then to John Vaughn.”
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT >The sources vary as to the number of children. Henry Lancaster states in the ODNB (published in 2009) "The couple had one son, Edward Hungerford (1596–1648) and two daughters before Lucy died on 4 June 1598", but in The History o
2 CONC f Parliament (published 2010) he states "Bridget, Hungerford’s only daughter from his first marriage, married Alexander Chocke".
2 CONT
2 CONT N.B.  We have Lucy Hungerford’s Monumental Inscription listing her Hungerford children as Edward, Bridget and Jane.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/HUNGERFORD.htm#Bridget%20HUNGERFORD3
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Hungerford-345
2 CONT * Wiltshire Family History Society. Marriage Register, Great Bedwyn, Wiltshire. V1.2 Jun 2015 citing:Alexander Chocke and Bridget Hungerford 5 Oct 1612 accessed:27 Nov 2019
2 CONT *=
2 CONT * The Visitation of the County of Somerset 1623, Chalke (Choke) Family Pedigree. < [https://archive.org/details/visitationofcoun00byustge/page/n35/mode/2up Archive.Org] >
2 CONT * https://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1604-1629/member/chocke-alexander-ii-15934-1625
