1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Jane Hungerford 
2 CONT * Born: 1598 Farleigh, Hungerford, Somersetshire, England
2 CONT * Father: Sir Anthony Hungerford of Black Bourton 
2 CONT * Mother: Lucy Hungerford, relict of John St John
2 CONT * Died: 14 Jun 1659
2 CONT
2 CONT There is no evidence this Lucy Hungerford married https://www.geni.com/people/Fabyan-Farley/6000000000970074038?through=6000000002447068619
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT on 22 April 1617 Jane married Robert Strange. Their marriage took place at Great Bedwyn, Wiltshire. [1] Robert was mentioned as "son in law" in the will of Jane's father Anthony. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Lucy bap 22 Jul 1619
2 CONT # Elizabeth bap 11 Oct 1620
2 CONT # Margaret bap 1 Nov 1622
2 CONT # Ann bap 27 May 1623
2 CONT # Katherine bap 14 Apr 1626
2 CONT # Jane bap 3 Feb 1628
2 CONT # Robert bap 1 Jun 1631
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert and Jane's coheiress Jane Strange m. Sir Robert Jocelyn 1st Bt. of Hyde Hall, Sawbridgewoth, Herts.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT Lucy Hungerford married Anthony Hungerford in 1595 [after the death of her first husband John St John] on the 20 September 1594. Lucy herself died on 4th June 1598 having had three children in quick succesion with her second husba
2 CONC nd. According to her MI they were Edward, Bridget & Jane. Jane therefor must have been born in 1597 or 1598 & certainly no earlier. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Heere lieth the body of Sir John St John, Knight who maried Lucy daughter & co heire of Sir Walter Hungerford of Farley, Knight by whom he had issue Walter that died young Sir John St John Knight & Baronet, Oliver that died youn
2 CONC g Katherine Anne Jane Elinor Barbara Lucy & Martha that died a child. He deceased the 20 of September 1594. She was secondly maried to Sir Anthony Hungerford Knight by whom she had Edward Bridget and Jane & then died the 4 of June
2 CONC  1598 This was erected by Sir John St John Knight & Baronet in the year of our Lord 1615 the 20 of Jul"
2 CONT
2 CONT In his will [Anthony Hungerford] bequeaths property and money to his sons Sir Edward, Anthony, Giles and John. He also leaves bequests to his daughters Sarah and Cecilia; his sons in law '''Robert Strange''' and John Southby and h
2 CONC is brother Sir John Hungerford. He also refers to his recently deceased wife "Dame Sarah". outside of family bequests he leaves money for poor apprentices in the parish of Great Bedwyn and especially mentions "Edward, the plough b
2 CONC oy who I brought out of Wiltshire"! [8]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Farley Hungerford Castle, Farleigh, Somerset, England is correct address
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources Collectanea Topographica Et Genealogica, Volume 5 page 29
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Afterwards Sir Anthony Hungerford of Black Bourton, co. Oxford, and the ancestor of the branch of the family which continued for four subsequent generations at that place. He was M.P. for Marlborough 35 Eliz. and for Bedwyn 39, 
2 CONC 43 Eliz. 1 and 12 Jac. I.; and was knighted at Whitehall Dec. 11, 1606. <BR>
2 CONT
2 CONT >He married first Lucy, daughter of Sir Walter Hungerford, of Farley Castle, and widow of Sir John St John, and by her had issue Sir Edward Hungerford, to whom his great-uncle Sir Edward Hungerford, of Farley Castle (second son of
2 CONC  Walter Lord Hungerford) on his death in 1607, "for the preservation of his name, settled his estate." (Epitaph at Farley.)"
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
