1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Anthony Hungerford was born 1607 in Black Bourton, Oxfordshire, England and died Aug. 17, 1657, Black Bourton, Oxfordshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Brief Biography==
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Anthony Hungerford was an English Member of Parliament who supported the Royalist cause during the English Civil War. He was born 1607/08 in England and died 17 Aug 1657 in Black Bourton, Oxfordshire, England. Anthony was elec
2 CONC ted in 1640 to both the Short and Long parliaments as member for Malmesbury. As a royalist he sat in the king's Oxford Parliament during its first session December 1643 to March 1644. He was fined for his delinquency by the Long P
2 CONC arliament, and was committed to the Tower of London in 1644, He was apparently at liberty in Oct. 1644. According to a statement which he drew up in 1644, to excuse himself from paying the fine imposed on him, ‘he never took up ar
2 CONC ms for the king' went after the battle of Edgehill to his house in Black Bourton, Oxfordshire; was carried thence by a troop of the king's horse to the ‘assembly' at Oxford, where he gave no vote against the parliament, and soon a
2 CONC fter returning home, purposely rode to the parliamentary camp at Burford, where he was taken prisoner. His fine was reduced, but he was still unable to pay it, and in 1648 orders were given for the seizure of his estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anthony succeeded to Farleigh Castle in 1653 as heir of his half-brother Edward. There he died on 18 August 1657, and he was buried in Black Bourton Church on 15 September following.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Family==
2 CONT Sir Anthony Hungerford was the son of Sir Anthony Hungerford of Black Bourton and his second wife Sarah Crouch. Anthony married Rachel Jones, daughter of Rice Jones of Astall, Oxfordshire, by whom he had twelve children. His heir 
2 CONC was his son Edward. A second son, called Colonel Anthony Hungerford, entered Nicolas's service as a secret agent in England, in the royalist interest, in 1655, in the hope, it is said, of obtaining his elder brother's estate. Rach
2 CONC el, a daughter, married Henry Cary, 4th Viscount Falkland, at Black Bourton on 14 April 1653. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1627 In the name of God Amen, in the three and twentieth day of June in the year of our Lord, one thousand five hundred Twentie and seven, I Sir Anthonie Hungerford of Black Bourton in the countie of Oxon... Sir John Hungerford my
2 CONC  brother, my son Anthonie Hungerford, Dame Sara my late wife, Gyles Hungerford my son, John Hungerford my son, my son Sir Edward Hungerford, Knight, my loving son in Lawe Robert Strange, Esquier, daughters Sarah & Sicilea [Cecilia
2 CONC ?], my three sons John, Henrie & Giles Hungerford, my sone Edward being my eldest son, John Hungerford my servant, Symon Croker my children's school master, Edward the plough boy, Mistress Bridget Strainge sister to my son in law 
2 CONC Robert Strainge, Executors Edward Hungerford [son] , loving son in lawe John Southby.
2 CONT
2 CONT
