2 CONT *'''Notes: also a royalist died at Farleigh in 1657. His son, Sir Edward - said to have entertained Charles II at Farleigh in Sep 1683. Edward was known as 'The Spendthrift' it is said he wasted £80,000 in capital and spent around
2 CONC  £14,000 a year. He was forced to sell Farleigh in 1686 and died in 1711. At this time, Farleigh was described as virtually unchanged from the time of the great English Barons, but by 1701, a long process of decay had begun to tak
2 CONC e its toll.
