1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *Thepeerage.com entry:  "Sarah Shelton was born at Wootton Hall, Norfolk, England. She was the daughter of Maurice Shelton and Elizabeth Kemp. She married Robert Suckling, son of Robert Suckling and Anne Wodehouse,
2 CONC  on 16 November 1669 at Barningham, Suffolk, England. She died on 5 November 1695 at Wooton [sic], Norfolk, England. From 16 November 1669, her married name became Suckling.  http://www.thepeerage.com/p53998.htm#i539973
2 CONT *Note information about Wootton Hall, alternatively spelt Woodton, and the Sucklings here: https://woodton.wordpress.com/our-community/woodton-in-history/
2 CONT *There is a Sarah Suckling buried 16 Sep 1711 at Woodton (?): "England, Norfolk, Parish Registers (County Record Office), 1510-1997," database with images, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/pal:/MM9.3.1/TH-267-12124-33576-75?
2 CONC cc=1416598 : accessed 11 April 2016), Woodton > Baptisms, Marriages, Burials > 1538-1739 > image 38 of 54; Record Office, Norwich.
2 CONT *Grave: http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=37657496 "She was the wife of Robert Suckling Esq. of Woodton. They had issue eight sons and seven daughters. She was the daughter of Maurice Shelton Esq. of Shelton, N
2 CONC orfolk and his wife Elizabeth (Kemp) Shelton."
