1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://sallysfamilyplace.com/maple-lawn/james-sampson-elizabeth-barcroft-2/
2 CONT
2 CONT James Sampson ca 1625 – 1689 & ca 1648 Elizabeth Barcroft ca 1633 – bef 1689 of Stepney, London, England & Surry County, VA
2 CONT
2 CONT James Sampson and Elizabeth Barcroft were married ca 1648 in Stepney, County Middlesex. the old parish church
2 CONT
2 CONT 1664 Isle of Wight records: signed as “James Sampson of Stevenheath Parish in County Middlesex, Shipwright.” D&W#1 p21
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 Dec 1666 Elizabeth and James Sampson sign receipt for George Moore for her share of the estate of her father, Charles Barcroft. D&W#1 p9 84
2 CONT
2 CONT 15 March 1669/70 Elizabeth Sampson witnessed will of Thomas Wooten.
2 CONT
2 CONT Chapman Wills 1, 14
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth had died before her husband wrote his will 4 Feb 1688/89;
2 CONT
2 CONT James Sampson’s will was probated 9 April 1689. Legatees were
2 CONT * – daughter Margaret, wife of Nicholas Wilson
2 CONT * – Mr George Moore and his wife
2 CONT * – son James Sampson
2 CONT * – “my daughter Clarke”
2 CONT * – John Browne
2 CONT * In codicil he mentions his deceased wife on her death bed requested that he take notice that she left her two daughters, Margaret and Elizabeth 300 acres apiece of the land [ obviously the 1200 acres granted Elizabeth Barcroft i
2 CONC n 1647. [JamesSampson still owned the 1200 acres in 1704.
2 CONT
2 CONT Information based on research
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of James Sampson & Elizabeth Barcroft:
2 CONT *1. Elizabeth Sampson ca 1648 – married 1st ca 1665 Edward Browne II ca 1640-bef 1675 married 2nd Thomas Clarke II ca 1650 – 1698/1701 Dr. Holtzclaw
2 CONT *2. Margaret Sampson ca 1650 – 1698 in her nuncupative will mentioned her son James; then stated that Mr. Moore and James Sampson should have nothing to do with her estate and appointed as her executors Thomas Clarke and John Brow
2 CONC ne. Chapman I 54 married ca 1687 Nicholas Wilson died 1696 he married 1st 1678 Elizabeth, the widow of Wm Cooker
2 CONT *4. James Sampson ca 1657 – 1728 Isle of Wight married Mary Maddera
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disputed child
2 CONT
2 CONT Geni does not accept https://www.geni.com/people/Sarah-Bracewell/6000000002980001396 as their daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Sarah Sampson ca 1648 – 1735 Isle of Wight wrote her will 20 March 1733/34 – prob 26 May 1735 married by 1670 Richard Braswell ca 1648 – 1725 Isle of Wight wrote will 28 July 1724 – prob 1725 son of the Rev Robert Bracewell
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT SARAH IS NOT A SAMPSON
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah, wife of Richard the 1st (in America) is not a Sampson! 1st of all, James Sampson, her supposed father, had a will dated 1688, and he did not name Sarah, at all. Now if he had omitted her (which he didn't), she did not name 
2 CONC a son James. That far back in time, people were pretty good about naming sons after fathers. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Per Braswell Genealogy website: 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT See more at https://braswellgenealogy.blogspot.com/2007/10/james-sampson-will-isle-of-wight-co-va.html
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE: James Sampson (wife Elizabeth Barcroft) is often referred to as the father of Sarah, wife of Richard Braswell the 1st, yet there is no mention of a Sarah Braswell in this will. Richard & Sarah followed Braswell naming patter
2 CONC ns yet it is evident by their wills they did not name children James, Sampson, or Elizabeth. There are no records to indicate that Sarah's surname was Sampson. It is another Braswell Myth.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Barcroft married 1st Dorothy Crosbie on 20 Feb 1632/33 at St. Olave's of Southwark in London. She was the daughter of John Crosbie of St. Albans in Hertfordshire. She apparently died a short time after the birth of her dau
2 CONC ghter Elizabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT 17 June 1647 - Elizabeth Barcroft granted 1200 acres IoW Co. this was his daughter
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
