1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Philip Greely BIRTH	21 Sep 1644, Salisbury, Essex County, Massachusetts, USA DEATH	17 Mar 1718 (aged 73), Salisbury, Essex County, Massachusetts, USA BURIAL	Salisbury Colonial Burying Ground, Salisbury, Essex Count
2 CONC y, Massachusetts, USA, MEMORIAL ID 163137569
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1711 Phillip Grele of Salisbury, administrator of the estate of his father, Andrew Grele, formerly of Haverhill, claimed that injustice had been done him in regard to the common lands. He sent a messenger from Salisbury with a 
2 CONC summons for the commoners of Haverhill, but the messenger went no farther than the house of Joseph Peaslee, with whom the summons was left, and by him taken to the town meeting, where he delivered it with his explanation to the "C
2 CONC lerk of the Commons." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouce Sarah Ilsley, 1644–1710
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Jonathan Greeley 1672–1750
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription HERE LYES Y BODY OF MR PHILIP GREELY WHO DIED MARCH Y 17 1718 IN Y 74 YEARE OF HIS AGE
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/163137569/philip-greely
