2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas being the oldest son of William Ward and Phebe Fenner received a double portion of the will. The fulling mill was held jointly by Thomas and his brother William. Thomas took an active part in public affairs. He was a select
2 CONC man, lieutenant fo the South Company, 1699 and was made Captain of it before 1712. He was appointed by the General Court to be Justice of the Peaces for Hartford County in 1712 and continued to hold it to 1729. He was Deputy to th
2 CONC e General Court in 1706, 1711-12. Thomas Ward died 2 JUNE 1728 in his sixty eighth year, buried in Riverside Burial ground, Middletown. A large table monument marks his resting place. The will of Thomas Sr. reveals that he owned n
2 CONC egro man Peter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
