1 NAME Phebe /Lee/
2 GIVN Phebe
2 SURN Lee
2 _MARNM Large
1 SEX F
1 DEAT
2 ADDR
3 CTRY Colonial America
1 BIRT
2 DATE BEF 20 MAY 1642
2 PLAC Rusper, Sussex, England
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *Phebe has no documented marriage or children.
2 CONT ===Biographical Summary===
2 CONT Phoebe Lee was a daughter of the immigrant Thomas Lee and his wife, Phoebe Browne. She is best known for her migration to the American colonies as an infant following the death of her father at sea during the 1645 crossing. Her li
2 CONC fe is documented within the records of the early Connecticut River Valley settlements.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Parentage===
2 CONT Father: Thomas Lee (c. 1614–1645)
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Phoebe Browne (1620–1664)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Vital Statistics===
2 CONT Birth: May 20, 1642, Rusper, Sussex, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: Date and location unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage and Issue===
2 CONT Spouse: Unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: None documented
2 CONT (Note: Genealogical consensus indicates that the various claims of a marriage between this Phoebe Lee and a "John Large" or similar individuals are unsupported by primary evidence and originate from speculative, unverified seconda
2 CONC ry sources.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Documented Facts===
2 CONT Migration: Arrived in the American colonies in 1645 as an infant with her mother, Phoebe (Browne) Lee, following the death of her father at sea.
2 CONT
2 CONT Settlement: Raised within the community of Saybrook (later Lyme), Connecticut, where her mother’s later marriages to Greenfield Larrabee and James Cornish placed the family among the established settlers of the region.
2 CONT
2 CONT Primary Documentation: Her birth is recorded in the parish register of Rusper, England. Beyond her childhood in Connecticut, contemporary records provide no further verifiable details regarding her adult life, marriage, or death.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Legitimate Sources===
2 CONT The American Genealogist (TAG), Parish Registers of Rusper, Sussex, England, and the Genealogical Dictionary of the First Settlers of New England by James Savage.
2 CONT
2 CONT —-
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Lee born ?, Married before 1640, '''Phebe Brown''' In Rusper, England.  He died on their ship to New England in 1645 of smallpox. Phebe m. (2) Greenfleld Larrabee, (3) James Cornish.   Phebe was the daughter of William & Ja
2 CONC ne Mills, who traveled with them to New England. Phebe’s mother also died of smallpox on that voyage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children  of Thomas Lee and Phebe Brown, baptized at Rusper, England: (Hartford Times 4/22/1959) 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Jane Lee Baptized 9/12/1640, Rusper, England Married (1) Samuel Hyde of Norwich, Conn,, (2) John Birchard. 
2 CONT # Phoebe Lee Baptized 5/20/1642, Rusper, England, married John Large of Long Island 
2 CONT # Lieut.  Thomas Lee E.A.,, Baptized 9/29/1644, married (1) Sarah Kirkland, (2) Mary De Wolf (1676)
