1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Tillinghast-39
2 CONT
2 CONT Mercy (Tillinghast) Power
2 CONT Born about 9 Sep 1680 [uncertain] in Providence, Rhode Island 
2 CONT Died about 13 Nov 1769 [uncertain] at about age 89 in Providence, Providence, Rhode Island 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Mercy "Mary, Marcy" [uncertain] Power formerly Tillinghast edit===
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Pardon Tillinghast II  and Lydia (Tabor) Mason  edit
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister of Sarah (Tillinghast) Harrington [half], John Tillinghast [half], Mary (Tillinghast) Carpenter [half], Lydia (Tillinghast) Odlin, Pardon Tillinghast, Phillip Tillinghast, Benjamin Tillinghast, Abigail (Tillinghast) Sheldon
2 CONC , Joseph Tillinghast, Hannah (Tillinghast) Haile and Elizabeth (Tillinghast) Taber add sibling
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Nicholas Power III — married before 1701 in Rhode Island map icon at age 20 add/edit spouses
2 CONT Mother of Hope (Power) Brown , John Power Sr  , Joseph Power , Anne Power , Nicholas Power IV and Mary Lydia (Power) Sabin  add/edit children
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Mercy Tillinghast, daughter of Pardon and Lydia (Taber) Tillinghast was born c 1680. [1] [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Nicholas Power III, as his second wife by 1701, as their daughter Hope was born in January 1701/2. Nicholas was born in 1673, son of Nicholas II and Rebecca (Rhodes) Power. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas died on May 18, 1734. [1] [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marcy Power, widow of Colonel Nicholas, died on November 13, 1769, in her 91st year. [4] [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Power Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Hope born on January 4, 1701; married James Brown on December 21, 1722 [1] [3]; Hope died June 8, 1792. [2]
2 CONT John born on April 7, 1702; married Martha ___. He died on February 18, 1772 at North Providence. [1]
2 CONT Joseph born ___; married Jane Diana ___. He was a mariner of Newport in 1741, later of Boston. [1]
2 CONT Anne born on December 12, 1707; married first John Stewart on May 25, 1724 [3]; married second George Laws. [1]
2 CONT Sarah born ___; married William Burrough on April 1, 1729. [1] [3] [2]
2 CONT Nicholas Power IV born ___; married his cousin Anne Tillinghast, daughter of Philip and Martha (Holmes) Tillinghast on [2] He died at Saramaribo, Surinam, c January 27, 1743/4. [3] His wife was born April 13, 1713, and died after 
2 CONC 1744. [1]
2 CONT Lydia born ___; married ___ Carr of Newport. [1]
2 CONT Mercy born ___; married Hezekiah Sabin. [1]
2 CONT Sources
