2 CONT ------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From Molyneux Family History, Pg. 93:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.archive.org/stream/historygenealog00unkngoog#page/n101/mode/1up/search/Caryll
2 CONT
2 CONT (3 Vis.) 285. Caryll; b. 1621, d. Feb 2, 1699, buried in Sefton.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was outlawed by parliament for his exertion in the Royalist cause. his estate was sequestrated by the Commonwealth, but after the restoration, he lived in great splendor at Croxteth Hall near Liverpol. He was arrested in 1694 f
2 CONC or treason and acquitted; m. Mary, daughter of Alexander Barlow.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Moore, son of the Governor of Liverpool, mentions that at the siege and taking Liverpool in June 1644 by Prince Rupert, "Carill, who is now Lord Mullinex, killed 7 or 8 pore men with his owne hands," adding, "Good Lord deli
2 CONC ver us from ye cruelty of ye blud-thirsty Papests. Amen."
2 CONT
2 CONT Caryll Molyneux died at Croxteth in 1698.
2 CONT
2 CONT *286. Phillip.
2 CONT *287. Francis, died young.
2 CONT *288. Charlotte; m. Sir William Stanley of Hooton in Cheshire.
2 CONT *289. Mary; m. 1st George Selby of Whitehouse, in the North of the Bishopric of Durham; m. 2nd Edward Mostyn of Talacre in Flintshire, Bart. to whom she was 3rd wife.
2 CONT *290. (4 Vis.) William Molyneux; b. 1636; d. 1717 (Viscount of Germouston); m. Bridget, daughter of Robert Lucy.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 104:
2 CONT
2 CONT 22. - 285. Caryll Molyneux was constituted Lord Lieutenant and Custus Rotulorum of County Lancaster; also made Admiral of the Narrow Seas; m. Mary, daughter of Alexander Barlow of Barlow in said County. His Lordship d. 1697; burie
2 CONC d at Sefton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT 23. 
2 CONT *316. Richard Molyneux; m. Mary, eldest daughter of William, Marquis of Powis, who was by James II after his abdication created Duke of Powis.
2 CONT *317. Caryll; died infant.
2 CONT *318. Mary; m. Thomas Preston of Furniss, County Lancaster.
2 CONT *319. Frances; m. 1677, Sir Neil O'Neil of County Antrim, Bart.
2 CONT *320. Margaret; m. 1st, Jnico, the 7th Viscount of Gormanson; m. 2nd, Robert Cassey, Esq., Counsellor at Law; m. 3rd, Colonel James Butler of Kelveloigher, County Tipperary, Esq., page of honor to King Charles II, d. 1711
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Caryll Molyneux, 3rd Viscount Molyneux (1624 – 2 February 1699) was an Irish peer. He was the younger son of Richard Molyneux, 1st Viscount Molyneux and inherited the title from his elder brother in 1654. He married Mary Barlow, d
2 CONC aughter of Sir Alexander Barlow of Barlow.
2 CONT
2 CONT He joined the Royalist army at the outbreak of the English Civil War, and served with his brother, Richard Molyneux, 2nd Viscount Molyneux, in the Lancashire Regiment, which was mostly Catholic, through almost all the fighting fro
2 CONC m Manchester (1642) to Worcester (1651). After the death of this brother in 1654, he succeeded to the viscounty and the constableship of Liverpool Castle. As a well-known Catholic Cavalier, he experienced very harsh treatment from
2 CONC  the victors; and the family estates suffered severely.
2 CONT
2 CONT It was not until the reign of James II that Molyneux's fortunes improved. He was then made Lord Lieutenant of Lancashire (1687–1688) and Admiral of the Narrow Seas, and was one of the few who fought with any success on James's sid
2 CONC e against the Prince of Orange, for he seized and held the town of Chester, until all further resistance was in vain. After using the castle to store arms, he was arrested on a fictitious charge of treason for a suspected Jacobite
2 CONC  rebellion called The Lancashire plot. Along with other Catholics, he was imprisoned in the Tower but was victoriously acquitted in 1694. He did not however recover the hereditary constableship and the castle was leased to the bur
2 CONC gesses who in 1704 were authorised by the Crown to destroy it.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his death at Croxteth in 1699 his title passed to his only surviving son, William Molyneux, 4th Viscount Molyneux.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Caryll Molymeux:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p22103.htm#i221022
