1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Tufton,_4th_Earl_of_Thanet
2 CONT
2 CONT John Tufton, 4th Earl of Thanet (7 August 1638 – 27 April 1680), styled The Honourable John Tufton until 1679, was an English politician and nobleman.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tufton was the second son of John Tufton, 2nd Earl of Thanet, by Lady Margaret, daughter of Richard Sackville, 3rd Earl of Dorset and Lady Anne Clifford. Through his father he was a great-great-grandson of William Cecil, 1st Baron
2 CONC  Burghley.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was educated at Eton and Queen's College, Oxford. He sat as Member of Parliament for Steyning from August 1679 to November 1679, when he succeeded his elder brother Nicholas Tufton, 3rd Earl of Thanet in the earldom and entered
2 CONC  the House of Lords.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Thanet died unmarried in April 1680, aged 41. He was succeeded in the earldom by his younger brother, Richard.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was also the hereditary High Sheriff of Westmorland from 1679 to 1680.
