1 NOTE {geni:about_me} See "The Great Migration Begins."  Came to Salem in 1633.  Married Widow Bridget Verry, by 6 Oct 1635.  Died between 17 Dec 1649 and 10 Dec 1656.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT See other entry for more information.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Yeoman- (a free man who owned his own farm).May 14, 1634, admitted freeman, so probably arrived in Salem in 1633. In 1636 he received a grant of 120 acres, both sides of Goldwaite's brook. He and his wife were members of the First
2 CONC  Church Of Salem.
2 CONT
2 CONT Visit '''The Giles Memorial''' by John Adams Vinton on the web.Google it. 
