1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Samuel Ware
2 CONT * Birth:	Sep 30 1657 - Dedham, Norfolk, Massachusetts
2 CONT * Parents:	Robert Ware, Margaret Hunting
2 CONT * Married: Elizabeth Rice, Sarah Fuller
2 CONT * Death:	Mar 1730 - Dedham, Norfolk, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Samuel Ware and Elizabeth Rice:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Joseph Ware, born June 23, 1691; died April 30, 1710.
2 CONT # Samuel Ware, born July 20, 1694; died July 30, 1722.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT John Carpenter (d. 1713) married (2) prob. Dedham, between 29 Dec. 1702 and 7 March 1705/6, SARAH (FULLER) DAY, widow of Ralph Day of Dedham. Widow Sarah m. (3) Dedham 27 July 1721, Samuel Ware (not Ward)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT # http://www.warefamilyassociation.com/html/MA_RWgrandch.htm
2 CONT # http://www.pcez.com/~bigshoe/du/Rice/eastman.html#2312
2 CONT #https://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Samuel_Ware_%288%29 cites
2 CONT ## Dedham (Massachusetts). Town Clerk; Julius Herbert Tuttle; Benjamin Fisher; and Don Gleason Hill. The early records of the town of Dedham, Massachusetts. (Dedham, Massachusetts: Dedham Transcript Press, 1886-1936) Vol. 1, p. 7.
2 CONC  1657 Samuell, the Son of Robert & Margarett Ware, was borne the 30 of ye 7 m'o.  [Note: In old-styles dates, the seventh month is September. More info may be found here.]
2 CONT ##Massachusetts. Probate Court (Suffolk County). Probate records, 1636-1899. (Salt Lake City, Utah: Genealogical Society of Utah, 1969-1971) Case 6074. Vol. 28, p. 489 Will of "Samuel Ware of Dedham ... Weaver being weak in Body",
2 CONC  dated 6 Mar 1730/31, proved 22 Mar 1730[/31], names wife Sarah Ware; Mary Day "who hath Lived with me and been helpfull to me", heirs of my brother John Ware Deceased; heirs of my brother Nathaniel Ware deceased; heirs of my brot
2 CONC her Robert Ware deceased; sister Hester Man; brother Ephraim Ware; brother Ebenezer Ware; whole estate to Nathaniel Man my Kinsman "who hath at the Date hereof doth Dwell with me and hath for a Considerable Number of years past be
2 CONC en helpfull to me" he paying above legacies. Friends Jeremiah Fuller of Stoughton and John Gay of Dedham Taylor to be executors. Vol. 29, p. 94 14 Jun 1731: Letter testamentary on estate of Samuel Ware jun'r late of Dedham Weaver 
2 CONC deceased issued to Jeremiah Fuller of Stoughton Husbandman and John Gay of Dedham Tailer. Vol. 29, p. 261 11 May 1731: Inventory of personal estate of Samuel Ware late of Dedham Deceased: not totaled, by Noah Kingsbery, Amos Fulle
2 CONC r, William Eaton. Added 15 Sep 1731: additional inventory, mostly real estate: £90, by Jabez Pond, David Fuller, William Eaton.
