1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.djsmith.us/wade.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT EDWARD WADE b. abt 1640, York Co., VA, EDWARD died abt 1682, York Co., VA.
2 CONT m. 1670, in Wilmington Parish, James City, VA, MARY HAMPTON, b. 1652, Wilmington Parish, York Co., VA, (daughter of THOMAS HAMPTON) d. abt 1700, New Kent Co., VA.  
2 CONT
2 CONT >Comment: Mary Hampton was Edward Wade’s 2nd wife, married after 1670.  Edward Wade had sons Edward b. 1660 & James b abt 1665; they must have been children of an earlier wife. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children included:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sixth Generation
2 CONT
2 CONT 8.	'''JAMES WADE b. abt 1665''', New Kent, VA, m. abt 1685, in VA, Margaret Mosby, b. 1665, New Kent, VA, (daughter of JOHN HAMPTON and MARY MANN). JAMES died 1740, Hanover Co., VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT * 	 	  	i	William WADE b. 20 Oct 1685, St. Peters arish, New Kent Co., VA.
2 CONT * 	 	  	ii	Henry WADE b. 30 Jan 1689, St. Peters arish, New Kent Co., VA.
2 CONT * 	 	  	iii	Edward WADE b. 1690, St. Peters arish, New Kent Co., VA.
2 CONT * 	 	  	iv	Margaret WADE b. 1 May 1694.
2 CONT * 	  	9.	v	JAMES Jr. WADE b. abt 1697.
2 CONT * 	 	  	vi	Robert WADE b. abt 1700, james City, VA.
2 CONT * 	 	  	vii	Richard WADE b. abt 1700, Henrico, VA, d. 15 Nov 1757, Tuckahoe Creek, Goochland, VA.
2 CONT * 	 	  	viii	Andrew WADE b. abt 1700, York, VA.
2 CONT * 	 	  	ix	Sarah WADE b. 24 Nov 1700, St. Peters arish, New Kent Co., VA.
2 CONT * 	  	10.	x	John George WADE b. 1704 .
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCE: http://kueber.us/p110.htm#i2198
2 CONT
2 CONT First Located: 1680-1700, St Peters Parish, New Kent County, VA
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Located: 1704, New Kent County, VA
2 CONT
2 CONT Quit Rents of Virginia, 1704
2 CONT
2 CONT James Wade was taxed for 150 acres in New Kent County in 1704
2 CONT
2 CONT Cavaliers and Pioneers, Volume III, Patent Book 12, Page 356
2 CONT
2 CONT Neil Marion Nugent, Virginia State Library, Richmond, 1979
2 CONT
2 CONT On 24 March 1725, for 35 shillings, James Wade received a patent for 350 acres in Hanover County, Virginia, on both sides of Hollowing Camp Creek.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hanover County, Virginia, Patent Book 12, Page 246
2 CONT
2 CONT Neighboring land owners were Alexander Snead, George Sims, Benjamin Brown, Charles Snelson, William Pulliam and John Hill. They and James Wade had land adjoining 400 acres in Hanover County that were patented to John Clements on 1
2 CONC 7 August 1725.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hanover County, Virginia, Patent Book 14, Page 219
2 CONT
2 CONT A patent was issued to Richard Bullock, Jr. on 25 August 1731 for 400 acres adjacent to James Wade.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hanover County, Virginia, Patent Book 14, Page 480
2 CONT
2 CONT On 28 September 1732 a patent for 400 acres of lapsed land, previously granted to Nathaniel Dickenson on 28 September 1728, was granted to Joseph Moutray. The tract bounded by Wade's line and the land of John Clement.
2 CONT
2 CONT Virginia County Records, Volume VI
2 CONT
2 CONT Edited by William Armstrong Crozier, Published 1909
2 CONT
2 CONT Hanover County Wills
2 CONT
2 CONT Order Book for 1733
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 21
2 CONT
2 CONT Penix, Edward, St. Paul's Parish, 24 December 1734 - 6 March 1735. Sons George, John and Joseph, the child my wife now goes with; wife Esther and friend William Winston to be executors; Witnesses V. Cobbs, Thomas Standley, James W
2 CONC ade.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation		James Wade was Farmer.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT James Wade, Jr., who was born in 1697, could have been a brother of Henry Wade,
2 CONT who was born in New Kent County on 30 June 1689 and married Judith Via. Henry
2 CONT Wade was a son of James Wade of New Kent County, Virginia, who was born about
2 CONT 1665-1667 and had, at least, five children, son Henry Wade, who was born in New Kent
2 CONT County on 30 June 1689 and married Judith Via, who was born in New Kent County on
2 CONT 11 April 1699; son Anthony Wade; daughter Margaret Wade; daughter Mary Wade; and
2 CONT daughter Sarah Wade. Henry Wade and Judith Via had a son Henry Wade, Jr. who was
2 CONT born in Hanover County, Virginia, in 1740 and married Lucy Turner of Hanover County
2 CONT on 30 August 1761. Lucy Turner Wade was born in 1744, probably in Hanover County.
2 CONT (THE WADE QUARTERLY, Volume 6, Issue 1, June 1979, query by Irene Lovell Wade,
2 CONT St. Louis, MO; and Volume 4, Issue 1, June 1977, data of Barbara Gates, Seattle, WA,
2 CONT including excerpt from a Bible possessed by Florence Wade Becker, Bluefield, WV.)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT
