3 NOTE Thomas White of Somerset:
4 CONT
4 CONT * has NO CONNECTION to Swanbourne, Hampshire
4 CONT * is NOT the son of Elizabeth Inglefield and Sir Robert White
4 CONT * did NOT marry Agnes/Agneta White of Farnham
4 CONT * is NOT related to any of the Swanbourne Whites
4 CONT * is NOT related to any of the Farnham Whites
4 CONT
4 CONT * Has NO reason to appear in ANY of the Visitations, as he has NO highborn or gentry connections - he's a simple, but successful, yeoman farmer of Somersetshire, no more and no less. 
3 NOTE Or else there's ANOTHER generation missing, which is not at all unlikely.
3 NOTE There are, unquestionably, errors of both omission and commission in this published version. Robert III White of Swanborne is conspicuous by his absence, and Agnes (Agneta) wife of Sir Thomas White is completely misrepresented.
3 NOTE This page appears to be based on the 1612 Visitation, with possible later annotations (up to c. 1615). The ubiquitous Richard Mundy, who collected and illustrated many of the Visitation mss, appears to have fl. mid-17th century an
4 CONC d to have been personally involved only with the last few rounds of such.
