1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Robert Blennerhassett m. Elizabeth Conway; b.est.c1575 dau. of Capt. Jenkin (Jenkyn) Conway; of Castle Conway, Killorglin, Co.Kerry, & Mary Herbert; 
2 CONT Jenkin Conway was one of the original planters in Co.Kerry with Sir Edward Denny, being granted the lordship of Killorglin, later called Castle Conway, in 1614; he descended from Conway of Bodrhyddran, Pembrokeshire, Wales 
2 CONT Like Robert Blennerhassett, Jenkin Conway was an Undertaker or Planter in the "Plantation of the Province of 
2 CONT Munster" and was granted Seigniory (Lordship) of Killorglin in 1614 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Conway was 16th in descent from King Henry I of England
