1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Isaac Stearns (1633 - 1676)''', fourth child of Isaac Stearns and Mary Barker, was born 6 January 1633 Watertown, Middlesex County, Massachusetts; he died 29 August 1676 Watertown, Middlesex County, Massachusett
2 CONC s. He married '''Sarah Beers (1639 - 1823)''', daughter of Richard Beers (c1613 - 1675) and Elizabeth Firman (c1615 - 1706); with whom he had six children.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Marriages and Children==
2 CONT # Sarah Stearns (born 14 January 1661 Cambridge, Middlesex, Massachusetts), married her stepbrother John Wheeler, the son of Thomas Wheeler and his first wife
2 CONT # Mary Stearns (born 8 October 1663 Watertown, Middlesex County, Massachusetts)
2 CONT # Isaac Stearns (born 26 August 1665 Watertown, Middlesex County, Massachusetts)
2 CONT # Samuel Stearns (born 11 January 1667 Concord, Middlesex  County, Massachusetts)
2 CONT # Abigail Stearns (born 1670 Cambridge, Middlesex County, Massachusetts)
2 CONT # John Stearns (born 1675 Concord, Middlesex  County, Massachusetts)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources==
2 CONT * The history and vital records of Watertown, Massachusetts
2 CONT * Savage's Genealogical Dictionary
2 CONT * John Brooks Threlfall. "Fifty Great Migration Colonists to New England and Their Origins".
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT son of Isaac and Mary (Barker) Stearns, of Watertown, Mass.; d., Aug. 29, 1676. Inventory, £300: six children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac Stearns II was the son of Isaac Stearns and Mary Barker, who were said to travel to Massachusetts Bay Colony on the Arbella with the Winthrop fleet. Isaac Sr was a tailor and settled near Mt Auburn in Watertown. Isaac II was
2 CONC  admitted freeman in 1665. On 24 June 1660 he married Sarah Beers, daughter of Capt. Richard and Elizabeth Beers. They lived in Cambridge Farms (Lexington) until his death on 29 August 1676. A writing in the files of the court dat
2 CONC ed 19 June 1677 says he left 3 sons and 3 daughters. His widow, Sarah, then married Sgt. Thomas Wheeler of Concord, on 23 July 1677.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Isaac and Sarah (Beers) Stearns: Sarah, b. 14 Jan 1661, m. John Wheeler of Concord Mary, b. 8 Oct 1663, m. John Cutler Isaac, b. 26 Aug 1665, m. Elizabeth Stone Samuel, b. 11 Jan 1667, m. Phebe -- Abigail, m. Samuel Ha
2 CONC rtwell of Concord John, b. 1675, m. Mercy Davis Source: Bond's Genealogies and History of Watertown Descendents of Isaac Stearns by Avis Stearns Van Wagenen
2 CONT * Reference: [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=101385291 Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 12 2016, 18:28:38 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac Stearns II was the son of Isaac Stearns and Mary Barker, who were said to travel to Massachusetts Bay Colony on the Arbella with the Winthrop fleet. Isaac Sr was a tailor and settled near Mt Auburn in Watertown. Isaac II was
2 CONC  admitted freeman in 1665. On 24 June 1660 he married Sarah Beers, daughter of Capt. Richard and Elizabeth Beers. They lived in Cambridge Farms (Lexington) until his death on 29 August 1676. A writing in the files of the court dat
2 CONC ed 19 June 1677 says he left 3 sons and 3 daughters. His widow, Sarah, then married Sgt. Thomas Wheeler of Concord, on 23 July 1677.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Isaac and Sarah (Beers) Stearns: Sarah, b. 14 Jan 1661, m. John Wheeler of Concord Mary, b. 8 Oct 1663, m. John Cutler Isaac, b. 26 Aug 1665, m. Elizabeth Stone Samuel, b. 11 Jan 1667, m. Phebe -- Abigail, m. Samuel Ha
2 CONC rtwell of Concord John, b. 1675, m. Mercy Davis Source: Bond's Genealogies and History of Watertown Descendents of Isaac Stearns by Avis Stearns Van Wagenen
