0 @I6000000002043279412@ INDI
1 NAME Samuel /Stearns/ I
2 GIVN Samuel
2 NSFX I
2 _MARNM Stearns
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 24 APR 1638
2 ADDR
3 CITY Watertown
3 STAE Massachusetts
3 CTRY United States
1 BURI
2 DATE 1683
1 DEAT
2 DATE 3 AUG 1683
2 ADDR
3 CITY Watertown
3 STAE Massachusetts
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 TITL Corporal
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Was he really born in Massachusetts??  His father is listed as having been born & died in England.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT [https://archive.org/stream/bemishistorygene00drap#page/n5/mode/2up THE BEMIS HISTORY AND GENEALOGY] being an account, in greater part of the descendants of Joseph Bemis, of Watertown, Mass. ... By Colonel Thomas Waln-Morgan Drape
2 CONC r ... Published 1900, San Francisco, California, p. 58
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * Reference: [http://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Stearns-56 WikiTree Genealogy] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 16 2017, 1:50:55 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel married Hannah Manning, eldest daughter of William and Dorothy Manning of Cambridge, and sister to Samuel Manning, who married Elizabeth Stearns, sister to Samuel. He settled on a farm at the northwest corner of the cross-r
2 CONC oads made by the roads from Cambridge to Waltham and by that going north to Lexington.[2/4545]
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel died at a young age but nonetheless held many offices of trust in Watertown. He was chosen surveyor of highways in 1666;[4/1:86] surveyor of cattle, fences, and hogs 1669;[4/1:93] constable in 1670;[4/1:96] selectmen in 167
2 CONC 3,[4/1:112] 1675,[4/1:121] 1676,[4/1:125] 1678,[4/1:132] 1679,[4/1:136] 1682,[4/2:10] and 1683;[4/2:13] town appraiser 1676[4/1:125] and 1678.[4/1:132] He was first referred to as "corporal" in 1683.[4/2:13] On July 10, 1694 Phill
2 CONC ip Shattuck was ordered to "take care of the Widdow Relict of Samll Sternes with her Children and provide for them from this Day for one month (they being Represented Poor and in necessity of Reliefe)"[4/2:76]
2 CONT
2 CONT Watertown records list the date of death of Corporal Samuel Stearns as the last of August 1682,[5/1:54] but the inventory of the estate has the death date as August 21. Inventory of his estate was taken Sept. 28, 1683 by Samuel St
2 CONC one, John Mose (probably Morse), William Bond, Sr., and John Biscoe and totaled 481.04.00.[3/6:136]
2 CONT
2 CONT REFERENCE:
2 CONT # Genealogy and Memoirs of Isaac Stearns and his Descendants - Mrs. Avis Stearns Van Wagenen, 1901
2 CONT # History of Watertown - Henry Bond, 1860 (pgs.454-455)
2 CONT # Middlesex County Probate (First Series Docket 21324)
2 CONT # Watertown Records, 1894
2 CONT # Watertown Records, 1894 (Birth, Marriage, and Death Register)
2 CONT
