2 CONT # [https://archive.org/details/genealogicaldic03savarich/page/238/mode/2up  A genealogical dictionary of the first settlers of New England] showing three generations of those who came before May, 1692, on the basis of Farmer's Reg
2 CONC ister by Savage, James, 1784-1873 p.239
2 CONT
2 CONT # [http://books.google.com/books?id=SvAUAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA24&lpg=PA24&dq=Elizabeth+sawtel+1669+Joseph+morse&source=bl&ots=Z6t-8-yB1W&sig=-909ArUMpTYO6_iyRWIpB3xvVqs&hl=en&sa=X&ei=d71hUs3dNIS0ygHGj4G4Cg&ved=0CDEQ6AEwAQ#v=onepage&q=Eliz
2 CONC abeth%20sawtel%201669%20Joseph%20morse&f=false Stearns Genealogy and Memoirs,] Volume 1 By Avis Stearns Van Wagenen.  Page 24.  "Abigail Stearns, b.,__;md., Apr. 27, 1666, Dea. John Morse, b., Feb. 28, 1639. She d., Oct. 16, 1690,
2 CONC  and was the mother of nine children."
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Abigail  is the six or seventh child of Isaac Stearns and Mary Barker. She was united in marriage on 27 Apr 1666 in Watertown to John Morse and they are the parents of nine children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * John Morse-15 Mar 1667-bef 1669
2 CONT * James Morse-25 Nov 1668-26 Apr 1718
2 CONT * John Morse-15 Mar 1669/1670-Aft 1718
2 CONT * Joseph Morse-25 Aug 1671-24 Jun 1709
2 CONT * Abigail Morse-23 Dec 1673-Few weeks old in 1674
2 CONT * Abigail Morse-6 Aug 1677-3 May 1758
2 CONT * Isaac Morse-7 Jan 1678/1679-25 Nov 1694
2 CONT * Samuel Morse-21 Jun 1682
2 CONT * Nathanial Morse-Abt 29 Jan 1687/1688
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT LInks:
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/123899757/abigail-morse#add-to-vc Find A Grave Memorial #123899757]
2 CONT
