1 NAME Charles /Stearns/
2 GIVN Charles
2 _MARNM Stearns
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1640
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://bigelowsociety.com/rod2011/stearns11.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Subject: Stearns
2 CONT Source:  Genealogies of the Families and Descendants of the Early Settlers of Watertown, Massachusetts, Includes Waltham and Weston - by Henry Bond, M.D. Boston, 1860.
2 CONT
2 CONT                                  Part 3
2 CONT
2 CONT p.453
2 CONT
2 CONT The Children of Isaac Stearns and Mary Stearns
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Mary Stearns born in England; m. in Woburn July 9, 1646, Isaac Learned,
2 CONT [Learned, a fruitful branch]
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Hannah Stearns m. in Watertown Dec 25, 1650, Henry Freeman and was buried,
2 CONT June 17, 1656.  The Record says she m. Samuel Freeman but there is good reason
2 CONT to believe that it is an error.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. John Stearns who settled in Billerica where he died March 5, 1668/9.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Isaac Stearns b. Jan 6, 1632/3; admitted freeman 1665; died Aug 29, 1676.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Sarah Stearns b. Sept 22, 1635; d. Oct 6, 1700; m. June 7, 1655, Samuel
2 CONT Stone of Cambridge; six children.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Samuel Stearns b. April 24, 1638; died Aug 3, 1683.
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Elizabeth Stearns who m. April 13, 1664, Samuel Manning of Cambridge
2 CONT afterwards of Billerica.  She died early leaving two sons, Samuel & John
2 CONT Manning.
2 CONT
2 CONT 8. Abigail Stearns who m. April 27, 1666, Deacon John Morse; 8 children
2 CONT (see also, Memorial of the Morses, p. 74.
2 CONT                                    ---
2 CONT John Stearns was one of the first settlers of Billerica.  He m. (1) Sarah,
2 CONT the only dau. of Isaac and Sarah Mixer of Watertown.  She died June 14, 1656
2 CONT and he m. (2) in Barnstable December 1656, by Thomas Hinckley, Esq., Mary
2 CONT Lothrop b. oct 4, 1640; dau of Thomas Lothrop by wife Mary.  This Thomas
2 CONT Lorthrop who died 1701, aged 80 was the elest son of Rev. John Lothrop of
2 CONT Scituate and Barnstable; by his first wife Mary.  John Stearns died March 5,
2 CONT 1668/9 and his widow, Mary m. May 6, 1669, Capt. William French, Esq. of
2 CONT Billerica, by whom she had 4 children**  Capt. French died Nov 20, 1681 aged
2 CONT 78 and she m. (3) 1684, Isaac Mixer, Jr. of Watertown as his 3d wife.  She
2 CONT was living in 1735, "very aged"  Inventory March 23, 1668/9 by William French
2 CONT and Jonathan Danforth and another but name not listed.  ?390. 18. 4.
2 CONT Children of John Stearns & wife, Sarah Mixer:
