1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Graves-580
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of William Graves and Elizabeth (Bean)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 2nd Lieutenant Crispus Graves was a Revolutionary War veteran, who was commissioned 6 Sept. 1770
2 CONT
2 CONT On 24 April, 1775, heserved in Capt. John Withley's Company, 31st Massachusetts Regiment, under Col. Edmund Phinney,
2 CONT
2 CONT Crispus is buried in the Old Cemetery off Presumpscot St. neart G.T.R.R. in Portland, Me. He has a government stone, located left center of cemetery.
2 CONT
