1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Thomas Savage, 3rd Earl Rivers (c. 1628 – 14 September 1694) was an English peer.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the first son of John Savage, 2nd Earl Rivers by his wife Catherine, daughter of William Parker, 13th Baron Morley.[1] His father was closely involved in the English Civil War on the Royalist side from 1641. Consequently he
2 CONC  lost his castles at Halton and Rocksavage and their contents were confiscated.
2 CONT
2 CONT About 1647, he married firstly Elizabeth, illegitimate daughter of Emanuel Scrope, 1st Earl of Sunderland by his mistress Martha Jeanes. Their children included: Thomas, who married Charlotte, daughter of Charles Stanley, 8th Earl
2 CONC  of Derby; Richard, who succeeded as 4th Earl Rivers; Elizabeth; and Annabella. They also had other children who died young.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT About 1684, he married secondly Arabella, daughter of Robert Bertie, 3rd Earl of Lindsey. They had no issue.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He died at his house in Great Queen Street in the Parish of St Giles in the Fields, Middlesex. A memorial to him by William Stanton was installed in St Michaels Church, Macclesfield.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
