1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lady Catherine Savage, mar. as his first wife her sister's brother-in-law Sir Charles Sidley, 5th Bt., of Ailesford, co. Kent (b. 1639; d. 20 Aug 1701), and had issue (2)
2 CONT
2 CONT >Charles Sedley inherited the title (5th baronet) in 1656 when his brother William died. By his first wife '''Lady Katherine Savage''', daughter of John, 2nd Earl Rivers he had only one legitimate child, Catherine, Countess of Dor
2 CONC chester, mistress of James II. The couple lived in Great Queen Street. After his first wife had been sent to a convent in Ghent on account of a serious mental condition, Sedley in vain tried to obtain a divorce. (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT >>Catherine's mother, also named Catherine, was the daughter of Earl Rivers. When Catherine was a child, her mother went mad, imagining that she was the Queen of England, and having to be addressed as 'Her Majesty.' She was confin
2 CONC ed to a Catholic convent abroad (Lady Catherine was Catholic while her husband and daughter were not) while her husband continued his carousing with his friends, 'the Merry Gang' in between his duties in Parliament. (3)
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT # http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sir_Charles_Sedley,_5th_Baronet_
2 CONT # http://www.cracroftspeerage.co.uk/online/content/Rivers1626.htm
2 CONT # http://scandalouswoman.blogspot.com/2008/08/royal-mistresses-catherine-sedley.html
