1 NOTE {geni:about_me} CRANFEILD, Edward of B[arba]dos, taking a voyage to sea.
2 CONT 9 Feb 16'3 [? 1633/? 1639] (sic), RB6/13, p. 301.
2 CONT Wf Elizabeth Cranfeild; eldest son Francis Cranfeild & younger son William Cranfeild, both under age; mo Mary Peasley in London; uncle William Goodman of Compton in the Hole, Warwickshire & friend John Harny ...
2 CONT
2 CONT CRANFIELD, FRANCIS, Gent of Barbados, at present resolved on a voyage with the fleet to the Indies.
2 CONT 7 February 1654, RB6/13, p. 130
2 CONT Wf Dorothy Cranfield now residing in England & to her ch. if she hath any; mo Elizabeth Canfield (sic); bro Edward Cranfeild; friends Ensign John Wise & Middleton Cooper - Xtrs in trust. signed Francis Cranfield
2 CONT Wit: Robert (x) Sanderson, John (x) Reece
2 CONT Proved 26 Mar 1656
2 CONT
2 CONT 1656 PCC will of Francis Cranfield,In the name of God amen, I Francis Cranfield,  Eldest sonne and haire to Edward Cranfield of London, Esq, deceased, being in now perfect health and memorie and undertaking a great voyage by sea t
2 CONC o the Island of Barbados ( where I have a plantation bequeathed mee by my deceased father and where most part of mine estate lyes. Knowinge my selfe to bee mortall, and not knowing how it may please God to deale with mee, Doe orda
2 CONC ine my last will and testament in manner and form following... namely I give and bequeath untoDorothy Cranfield my lawfull and wedded and welbeloved wife (, now living in Chiswell Street in Cripplegate parish, London) all my goode
2 CONC s and estate..or after my arrival in Barbados. Signed 8th day of May in the year of our Lord six hundred and fifftie four. Francis Cranfield. will proved 1656 England PCC
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife Dorothy's will mentions brethen Edward Cranfield
