1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Gertrude Bamfylde'''1
2 CONT F, #204231
2 CONT Last Edited=17 Nov 2023
2 CONT '''     Gertrude Bamfylde is the daughter of''' Sir John Bamfylde, 1st Bt. and Gertrude Coplestone.1 '''She married Sir William Morice, 1st Bt.''', son of Sir William Morice and Elizabeth Prideaux.
2 CONT '''     Her married name became Morice.'''1
2 CONT '''Children of Gertrude Bamfylde and Sir William Morice, 1st Bt.'''
2 CONT 1. Mary Morice+1 d. c Jun 1698
2 CONT 2. Gertrude Morice2 b. c 1645, d. Jan 1679
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT 1.[S15] George Edward Cokayne, editor, The Complete Baronetage, 5 volumes (no date (c. 1900); reprint, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 1983), volume II, page 126. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Baronetage.
2 CONT 2.[S5792] Robin Dening, "re: Rochfort Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger LUNDY (101053), 2 January 2012. Hereinafter cited as "re: Rochfort Family."
2 CONT From: https://www.thepeerage.com/p20424.htm#i204231
2 CONT ______________________
2 CONT '''Sir William Morice, 1st Baronet''' (c. 1628 – 7 February 1690), of Werrington (then in Devon but now in Cornwall), was an English Member of Parliament.
2 CONT Origins
2 CONT '''Morice''' was the eldest son of Sir William Morice, a Member of Parliament who assisted in the Restoration of King Charles II, and was knighted and appointed Secretary of State for the Northern Department in 1660.
2 CONT Career
2 CONT '''The younger William was created a baronet''' on 20 April 1661. In 1689, he entered the House of Commons as Member of Parliament (MP) for Newport, in Cornwall, but died a year later.
2 CONT Marriages and children
2 CONT He married twice:
2 CONT *'''Firstly to Gertrude Bampfylde''', daughter of Sir John Bampfylde, 1st Baronet of Poltimore and North Molton in Devon, '''by whom he had three children''':
2 CONT **William Morice (1660–1688) who married Anne Lower, and predeceased his father without issue.
2 CONT **Mary Morice, who married (as his 3rd wife) Sir John Carew, 3rd Baronet (1635–1692) of Antony, Cornwall.
2 CONT **Gertrude Morice (d. 1679), who married Sir Walter Yonge, 3rd Baronet
2 CONT *Secondly he married in 1676 Elizabeth Reynell, 4th daughter of Thomas Reynell (d. 1698) of East Ogwell, Devon, MP for Devon in 1656 and MP for Ashburton 1658 and Sheriff of Devon 1677.[2] By her he was the father of:
2 CONT **Sir Nicholas Morice, 2nd Baronet (1690–1715).
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sir_William_Morice,_1st_Baronet
2 CONT _________
