1 NOTE {geni:about_me} B-91 Henry Peyton inherited the landed estate of his father. The brothers Henry, Valentine and Philip Peyton were all situated on Aquia Creek and its branches. Aquia Creek is located in Stafford County, Virginia. F
2 CONC rom "Peytons Along the Aquia" page 26.
2 CONT
2 CONT =---------------------------=
2 CONT ''Curator note: The following from John B. Fox is not about this Henry Peyton but perhaps refers to a younger generation, his descendant or a (grand) nephew.''
2 CONT
2 CONT My Edward Boswell ancestor, born 1749, who resided in Prince William County, Va., had a neighbor, friend, perhaps relative Valentine Peyton. An older fellow named Henry Peyton was in the same region. When Henry Peyton died, Edward
2 CONC  and Valentine validated Henry's signature on his last will and testament. These two men had sons named Craven. Edward had a brother, Hezekiah Boswell who also had a son named Craven. The Boswells moved to North Carolina. Since th
2 CONC e two Boswells named sons Craven, it seems more likely that their mother was a Peyton. Have a feeling that Valentine Peyton is the uncle of Edward and Hezekiah Boswell.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 8/9 Aug 1765 Robert Peyton and Ann his wife sold to John Semple for 94 pounds current money of Va. all the undivided share of 230 A. which was devised by the Last Will and Testament of his father Valentine Peyton, Gent. decease
2 CONC d, to be equally divided between Francis Peyton, Craven Peyton, and Robert Peyton on Occoquan R. in Pr. WmCo.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 9 Aug 1765 Robert Peyton and Ann his wife sold to Thomas Gibson for 150 pounds 284 A. on Little R. or Hunger Run in LoudounCo granted to Charles Green who transferred it to Valentine Peyton who devised it to Robert Peyton.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 11 May 1767, Francis Peyton and Frances his wife, Craven Peyton and Ann his wife sold John Semple 230 A. [280 A.?] at the Falls of the Occoquan devised to them and to their brother, Robert Peyton, by their father, Valentine Pey
2 CONC ton by his last Will and Testament in writing duly proved and recorded among the Records of County Court of Prince William.
2 CONT
2 CONT I would like to know the source of the Craven name in the Peyton family. It is often the case that if a woman marries into a family, and she does not have males to carry forth the family name, the family into which she married use
2 CONC s her family name as a given name.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sincerely,
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/John-B-Fox/6000000076940932976 John B. Fox]
2 CONT
