1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Cocke-296
2 CONT
2 CONT "Genealogies of Virginia Families" from The Virginia Magazine of History and Biography shows: THOMAS COCKE, (JR.)(3) (Captain), (son of Thomas Cocke) born c. 1662; died 1707 (at age 45); married first, about 1687 Mary Brazier (Bra
2 CONC zure, Brashear, Brasier, Brassieux, Brashure) of Nansemond; married second Frances -[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Death & Legacy
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of Thomas Cocke. Henrico Co., VA, DB/WB 1706-1709, pp. 24-28, w. 16 Jan 1706 (o.s.), codicil w. 14 Feb 1706 (o.s.), p. Apr Court 1707. Digital image at Ancestry.com - [4] [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Cocke's will was admitted to probate 1707. He appointed his son Thomas his executor, and his "beloved friends Thomas Farrar, Littlebury Epes and Sam'l Harwood (his brother-in-law), Gent., overseers of his last will and test
2 CONC ament". He left six children: Thomas, James Powell, Henry, Brassuir, Mary, Elizabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife (Frances) had a separate estate settled on her by her father, which she retains intact.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT *http://roglo.eu/roglo?lang=en;i=2401102
2 CONT *James P. C. Southall. (1929). Origins of the Cocke Families of Virginia. The William and Mary Quarterly, 9(1), 49–59. https://doi.org/10.2307/1920377
