1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Stephen Cocke (son of Thomas S. Cocke and Agnes Powell?) was born Bet. 1666 - 1668.  Stephen had died by 1704, as an acknowledgment regarding the debt of her late husband Stephen Cocke at a local store was presente
2 CONC d by Martha Cocke, administratrix, and recorded on August 14, 1711.14
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 
2 CONT * (1) Mistress Sarah Marston on Bet. 1688 - October 1689.
2 CONT *  (2) Martha (Batte) Jones-Bannister on May 26, 1694, daughter of Thomas Batte, Captain.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Stephen Cocke:
2 CONT
2 CONT First wife:Mistress Sarah Marston. Second wife: Martha Batte - Stephen was Martha's third husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Stephen Cocke and Mistress Sarah Marston: Marriage: Bet. 1688 - October 1689
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Stephen Cocke and Martha (Batte) Jones-Bannister: Marriage: May 26, 1694
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Stephen Cocke and Mistress Sarah Marston are:
2 CONT # +Abraham Cocke, b., Henrico County, Virginia, d. May 10, 1760, Amelia County, Virginia.  Perhaps son of 2nd marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Stephen Cocke and Martha (Batte) Jones-Bannister are:
2 CONT # Agnes Cocke, d. date unknown.
2 CONT # Batte Cocke, d.y., d. date unknown.
2 CONT # Charles Cocke, d.y., d. date unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * http://www.genealogy.com/ftm/b/e/n/John-R-Bennett-FL/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-1124.html
2 CONT * Extracted from “Peter Jones of Peter’s Point” by Nancy Heuser.   [https://petersburgpreservationtaskforce.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/08/Peter-Jones-of-Peter-Point-Heuser.pdf PDF] 
2 CONT ** 13 The marriage to Stephen Cocke is proven by an order in the same court in 1694 (Folder 22, p. 535) that “Stephen Cocke & wife, Martha, administrators of John Bannister, decd.”, as well as a second entry on p. 545 that “Martha
2 CONC , relict of Abraham Jones & John Bannister, married Stephen Cocke.”
2 CONT ** 14 Prince George Wills and Deeds 1710-1713, p. 66. Also see Boddie, John Bennett, Southside Virginia Families, Vol. 1. Genealogical Publishing Company, Baltimore, Maryland, 1966, pp 221-222
2 CONT
