1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Children of Richard Cocke (d 1706) and Elizabeth  are:l
2 CONT
2 CONT John Cocke, born 1673; died 1699. He married Obedience Branch November 1696 in Henrico Co., VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Cocke-67
2 CONT
2 CONT John was the son of Richard and Elizabeth Cocke. He married Obedience Branch on November 24, 1696 in St Johns Church, Henrico County, Virginia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They were the parents of:
2 CONT
2 CONT *Martha (1697-1769) married Arthur III Moseley
2 CONT *Elizabeth (unknown-unknown)
2 CONT *John ( 1698-July 15, 1759)
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1697 Thomas Branch, eldest son of Thomas Branch, who was eldest son of Christopher Branch, sold 100 acres at Kingsland to John Cocke and his then wife, Obedience Branch. The deed recited that Obedience was daughter and co-heir 
2 CONC of John Branch and that Christopher Branch had given the tract to William Branch and his wife, Jane, grandmother of Obedience
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT *Henrico Records, Vol. 1688-97, p. 710
2 CONT *The William and Mary Quarterly, Volume 25 http://books.google.com/books?pg=PA108&lpg=PA108&dq=John+Cocke+and+Obedience+Branch&sig=PBOsjBMvMJLA7yFsFiS5MgNb3aM&ei=BFvoU7GSI5OXyASVuICIAQ&id=gSsjAQAAIAAJ&ots=yyf2O2auIg&output=text
2 CONT *THOMAS AND WILLIAM BRANCH OF HENRICO AND SOME OF THEIR DESCENDANTS By Williaam Clayton Torrence
2 CONT *"Pedigree Resource File," database, FamilySearch (http://familysearch.org/pal:/MM9.2.1/3SP1-KH9 : accessed 2014-08-11), entry for John /Cocke/.
2 CONT
