1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Elizabeth Cocke
2 CONT *Born: 1675 at “Bremo” in  Henrico Co., Virginia
2 CONT *Death: 19 Sep 1726 (aged 50–51) in Warwick County, Virginia
2 CONT *Parents: Richard Cocke (10 Dec 1639 - 1706) &  Elizabeth 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth married Miles Cary, Jr. (1671 - 1724) Aug 1695 at St John’s Episcopal Church in Richmond.  Issued marriage license 22.  He was the son of Thomas Cary and Ann Milner.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children: 
2 CONT *  	1. Richard Cary,   b. Abt 1696,   d. 1721  (Age ~ 25 years)
2 CONT *  	2. Thomas Cary,   b. Abt 1698,   d. Bef Oct 1775, Chesterfield Co., Virginia (Age ~ 77 years)
2 CONT *  	3. Miles Cary,   b. 1701
2 CONT *  	4. Nathaniel Cary,   b. Abt 1703,   d. Bef 1761  (Age ~ 57 years)
2 CONT *  	5. Anne Cary,   b. Abt 1707
2 CONT *  	6. Elizabeth Cary,   b. Abt 1709
2 CONT *  	7. Bridget Cary,   b. Abt 1711
2 CONT *  	8. Dorothy Cary,   b. Abt 1712
2 CONT *  	9. Martha Cary,   b. Abt 1714
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT >"In his will dated November i8, 1706, Rich- ard Cocke, of Bremo, leaves legacies to each of his grandchildren then in existence, Cockes, Carys and Pleasants, boys and girls, naming them. The children of his daughter Elizabeth Gar
2 CONC y he enumerates as follows: "Richard Cary, JE20; Thomas Gary, JEio; Miles Gary, JEio; Nathaniel Gary, £10." It would seem to follow that that was the order of their birth (Richard was updovibtedly the eldest, receiving a double po
2 CONC rtion), and that none of the daugh- ters of Miles Gary3 was born prior to 1706. We have accordingly followed that order in our enumeration. The question is now of interest, as upon it depends the seniority of the extant Ghesterfie
2 CONC ld and Peartree Hall lines."
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * [https://archive.org/stream/jstor-4241922/4241922#page/n5/mode/2up page 410-412] of "Genealogy of the Cocke Family of America"
2 CONT * "Richard Cocke of Bremo and His Children" by James P. C. Southall
2 CONT *http://wrenacres.com/genealogy/getperson.php?personID=I1443&tree=ScottDickson cites
2 CONT *Genealogy of the Cocke Family in Virginia 
2 CONT *Adventurers of Purse and Person, Vol. 1.
2 CONT *https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/82033573/elizabeth-cary
2 CONT *https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Cocke-65 cites
2 CONT *The Virginia Carys; an essay in genealogy by [Harrison, Fairfax], 1869-1938. [from old catalog]. Publication date 1919 Cary family (Miles Cary, 1623-1667) [from old catalog] Henrico records for marriage license, August 22, 1695, 
2 CONC and Register, St. John's Church, Church Hill, Richmond, for his marriage, August 25, 1695.  Page 49 [https://archive.org/details/virginiacarysan01harrgoog/page/n97 Archive.Org]
2 CONT *(2) Eggleston Notes for record of his will proved 1724 in Warwick Will Book, I, 313; 
2 CONT *(3) Will of Richard Cocke, of Bremo, dated November 18, 1706, from Henrico records
