2 TITL St. John's Episcopal Church in Richmond 
2 _PRIM Y
2 NOTE Elizabeth and Miles Cary were married here August 25th, 1695. St. John's Episcopal Church is the oldest church in Richmond, built by Col. Richard Randolph in 1741 and gives the name to Richmond's oldest neighborhood, Church Hill. 
3 CONC It was the site of two important conventions in the period leading to the American Revolutionary War, and is most famous as the location where Patrick Henry gave his closing speech at the Second Virginia Convention with the famous
3 CONC  quotation "Give me liberty or give me death!" The churchyard cemetery is the resting place of Elizabeth Arnold Poe who was the mother of the famous poet Edgar Allan Poe, and George Wythe, one of the signers of our nation's Declar
3 CONC ation of Independence.
3 CONT
3 CONT http://historicstjohnschurch.org/explore-the-history
