1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Martha Cocke was born ABT 1676 in Bremo, Henrico Co., Virginia, and died AFT 1726 in prob. Henrico Co., Virginia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://wc.rootsweb.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=jhmjr&id=I40858
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of  Richard Cocke the elder and  Elizabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married 
2 CONT #Joseph Pleasants 15 MAY 1699 in St. John's Church, Henrico Co., Virginia, son of John Pleasants and Jane Larcombe. He was born ABT 1674 in Bremo, Henrico Co., Virginia, and died BET 09 SEP 1725 AND 07 FEB 1726 in Henrico Co., Vir
2 CONC ginia. He was buried in Friends Burial Ground near Henrico Co., Virginia. 
2 CONT # Edward Bennett 05 FEB 1727 in Henrico Co. (Curles Meeting House), Virginia. He was born ABT 1675 in guesstimate.
2 CONT
2 CONT From VII. DESCENDANTS OF MARTHA (COCKE)(3) PLEASANTS (FOURTH GENERATION)
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Richard Cocke (2) and wife of Joseph Pleasants(2). 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had issue: 
2 CONT * 1. Joseph Pleasants; 
2 CONT * 2. John Pleasants m. Susanna Woodson; 
2 CONT * 3 . Richard Pleasants; 
2 CONT * 4. Thomas Pleasants; 
2 CONT * 5. Robert Pleasants; 
2 CONT * 6. Jane Pleasants; 
2 CONT * 7. Martha Pleasants m. Nathaniel Vandewall; 
2 CONT * Elizabeth Pleasants.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 25th day, fifth month 1700, Martha's name is first mentioned at the Henrico Monthly Meeting, when she signed a marriage certificate.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married 2nd to Edward Bennett b: ABT 1675 in guesstimate Married: 05 FEB 1727 in Henrico Co. (Curles Meeting House), Virginia 4
2 CONT
