1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 9 Mary Cocke must have been born around 1680. She married Obadiah Smith around 1700 or a little later. I have eight children listed for them, although there seems to be some doubt about whether one or two of them w
2 CONC ere children or younger siblings of Obadiah Smith. She died on her husband's plantation on Turkey Creek, in southeastern Henrico County, in 1754.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT > "4. William Cocke born 1655; died 1693. He married first, Jane Clarke, in 1678; and second, Sarah Flower, about 1689. He left 3 children, William, Mary and Elizabeth. This William Cocke was no doubt the William Cocke, whose daug
2 CONC hter Sarah in 1723 married Capt. Henry Wood." "Genealogy of the Cocke Family of Virginia" The Magazine of History and Biography 3, no. 4 (1896): 405-414. ( p 411). Retrieved from http://www.jstor.org/stable/4241922
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=draper1&id=I65458
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Cocke (William Cocke5, Richard Cocke4, John Cocke3, Thomas Cocke2, Robert Cocke1) was born ABT 1676 in Henrico Co., Virginia, and died BEF APR 1754 in Bellevue, Henrico Co., Virginia. She married Obadiah Smith ABT 1695 in Hen
2 CONC rico Co.,Virginia, son of John Smith and Hannah Daft. He was born ABT 1665 in Charles City Co., Virginia, and died MAY 1746 in Henrico Co., Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 8 children of Mary Cocke and Obadiah Smith, named in his 1746 Will, were: “ … Seven Children Viz; John, Obadiah, Jacob, Luke, Elizabeth, Ann & Molly. …” … and William “ Item. my Will further is that my son William Smith shall 
2 CONC pay Seven pounds & ten Shillings for his brothers & sisters, Viz; John, Obadiah, Jacob, Luke, Eliz'th, Ann, Mary….”
2 CONT
2 CONT * 	2	  i.	Jacob Smith was born BET 1695 AND 1730 in Henrico Co., Virginia, and died ABT 1791 in Hanover Co., Virginia. He married Anne UNKNOWN ABT 1744 in Henrico Co., Virginia. She was born ABT 1724 in Henrico Co., Virginia. 1746
2 CONC  Will of Obadiah Smith: “ I give and bequeath unto my beloved son Jacob Smith & his heirs three hundred acres of land be the same more or less being the remainder of the head of land above the Brook Road lying and Binding as follo
2 CONC ws. Begining on John Cannons line on the Brook Road down the said line to Coll. Byrds line up the same to Johns Branch down the branch to John Prices line so to Thomas Williamsons line & along the same to Mr. Richardson line to th
2 CONC e Road and down the Road to the place begun. Item. I give to my aforesaid son Jacob Smith two Negro slaves called Doll & Rachel to him & his heirs.”
2 CONT *	3	  ii.	Elizabeth Smith was born BET 1695 AND 1730 in Henrico Co., Virginia, and died AFT 1760.  Married _ Ellis.  1746 Will of Obadiah Smith: “Item. I give and bequeath unto my Daughter Elizabeth Ellis & her heirs forever one t
2 CONC ract of land containing four hundred acres more or less being the uppermost part of a branch called Long & hungary. Item. I give unto my aforesaid Daughter Elizabeth Ellis two Negro slaves called Magen & Will a sucking child to he
2 CONC r and her heirs.”
2 CONT *	4	  iii.	Luke Smith was born ABT 1692 in Henrico Co., Virginia, and died ABT MAR 1758 in Halifax Co., Virginia.  Note: Luke Smith Was born in 1710 and died before 1783. His father was Obadiah Smith, son of John Smith who wrote h
2 CONC is will in 1689 in Charles City County Virginia. John Smith and Hannah Daft had two sons: Obadiah, and Luke who married Arabella GROMARRIN.  1746 Will of Obadiah Smith:  “ I give and bequeath unto my beloved son Jacob Smith & his 
2 CONC heirs three hundred acres of land be the same more or less being the remainder of the head of land above the Brook Road lying and Binding as follows. Begining on John Cannons line on the Brook Road down the said line to Coll. Byrd
2 CONC s line up the same to Johns Branch down the branch to John Prices line so to Thomas Williamsons line & along the same to Mr. Richardson line to the Road and down the Road to the place begun. Item. I give to my aforesaid son Jacob 
2 CONC Smith two Negro slaves called Doll & Rachel to him & his heirs.”
2 CONT * 	5	  iv.	Anne Smith was born BET 1695 AND 1730 in Henrico Co., Virginia. 1746 Will of Obadiah Smith: “Item. I give & bequeath unto my loving Daughter Ann Smith one Negro slave Named Jane a sucking child to her & her heirs.”
2 CONT * 	6	  v.	Mary ‘Molly’ Smith was born 06 OCT 1726 in Henrico Co., Virginia, and died 15 NOV 1804 in "Montrose", Powhatan Co., Virginia. She married William Smith 18 FEB 1742, son of Robert Smith and Mary Ann UNKNOWN. He was born 1
2 CONC 8 NOV 1720 in Powhatan, Co., Virginia, and died 16 JAN 1790 in "Montrose", Powhatan Co., Virginia. 1746 Will of Obadiah Smith:  “Item. I give and bequeath unto my Daughter Mary Smith & her heirs forever one tract of land containin
2 CONC g four hundred acres more or less being part of the aforesaid tract adjoyning to Rawlin Blackborne. Item. I give unto my aforesaid Daughter Mary Smith two Negro slaves called Peter and Jeremy to her & her heirs.”
2 CONT *	7	  vi.	William Smith was born BET 1710 AND 1730 in Henrico Co., Virginia, and died AFT 1753 in Virginia. 1746 Will of Obadiah Smith: “Item. I give and bequeath unto my loving son William Smith and his heirs three hundred acres 
2 CONC of land be the same more or less begining on horse Swamp on the Brook Road up the said road to Mr. Richardsons line thence to Mr Masseys line and thence to William Ferriss's line to horse Swamp & up the same the the place begun. “
2 CONC Item. I give to my aforesd son William Smith & his heirs the land I bought of William Ferris being by Estimation forty acres be the same more or less. “Item. I give and bequeath unto my afors'd Son William Smith and his heirs all 
2 CONC the remainder of the afores'd tract of land and likewise the Plantation whereon I now live with all the appurtenances there unto belonging. “Item. I give unto my aforesaid Son William Smith three Negro Slaves called Toby, Frank & 
2 CONC her child called Denise to him and his heirs.” Item: “my Will further is that my loving Son William Smith shall be whole and Sole Executor of this my last will and Testament October the Twenty sixth MDCCXLIV 1744.”   Also executor
2 CONC  of his mother Mary’s Will in 1753.
2 CONT * 	8	  vii.	John Smith was born BET 1710 AND 1730 in Henrico Co., Virginia, and died AFT 1753.  1746 Will of Obadiah Smith: “IMPRIMIS. I give & bequeath unto my beloved son John Smith and his heirs Three Hundred Acres of Land be t
2 CONC he same more or less begining on John Pleasants line on Miry Branch & up the branch to the Hundred Farm the same with in a hundred yards or thereabouts of John Cannons line and leaving that distance to Joseph Pleasants line & Henc
2 CONC e to the place begun and likewise I give twenty acres of Meadowland lying and joyning to the Cattail branch & likewise I give to my said son John Smith a Water mill with two acres of land adjoyning one acre of each side the afore 
2 CONC said Mill. Item. I give to my aforesaid son John Smith two Negro slaves called Raimer and Sarah to to him and his heirs.”
2 CONT * 	9	  viii.	Obadiah Smith was born ABT 1720 in Henrico Co., Virginia, and died 1765 in Hanover Co., Virginia.  1746 Will of Obadiah Smith:  “Item. I give and bequeath unto my beloved son Obadiah Smith & his heirs three hundred ac
2 CONC res of land more or less beginning on John Pleasants line on Miry branch & up the same to Jacob's path so up the same to Jacobs path so up the same on the South side of the white oak slash to the Brook Road & up the same road to t
2 CONC he horse swamps & Down horse Swamp to John Sharps line & thence to the place begun. Item. I give unto my aforesaid son Obadiah Smith one Negro slave called Joe to him & his heirs.“
2 CONT
