1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Son of	Richard "the Younger" Cocke and Elizabeth (.) Cocke
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/cocke/722/ GENEALOGY OF THE COCKE FAMILY OF VIRGINIA] Prepared by James C. Southall.  Published in Genealogies of Virginia Families from the Virginia Magazine of History and Bio
2 CONC graphy, Volume II
2 CONT
2 CONT RICHARD COCKE’S (4) BRANCH
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Cocke (4), (born 1707; died 1772) married Elizabeth Hartwell (4) of Swan’s Point, Surry, and raised the following named children, viz:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Hartwell Cocke (5), 
2 CONT * Benjamin Cocke (5), 
2 CONT * Elizabeth Hartwell Cocke (5) and 
2 CONT * Rebecca Cocke (5).
2 CONT
2 CONT In a second marriage with Elizabeth Ruffin, relict of Mr. Kinchin, he raised 
2 CONT * Nancy Cocke (5), 
2 CONT * Richard Cocke (5) (the author of this narrative), 
2 CONT * Lucy Cocke (5), 
2 CONT * Nathaniel Cocke (5) and 
2 CONT * John Cocke (5).
2 CONT
2 CONT ==parents==
2 CONT
2 CONT RICHARD COCKE (2) of Bremo, born 1672; died 1720; married first Anne Bowler.We don’t know the name of his second wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne Bowler was the daughter of Thomas Bowler of the county of Rappahannock (now Essex and Richmond); member of the Governor’s Council in 1670.She was born in 1695 and died 1705.There appear to have been three children by this mar
2 CONC riage, one of them Bowler Cocke (4) of Bremo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Among the children of the second marriage was '''Richard (4)''' the ancestor of Col. Richard Cocke of Bacon’s Castle, of Hartwell Cocke (5), General John Hartwell Cocke (7) &c.(In the Revolutionary period there was a Bowler’s Whar
2 CONC f on the Rappahannock.The name now is spelled also Boulware.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
