3 STAE England
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 DEAT
2 DATE 9 FEB 1697
2 ADDR
3 CITY Playford
3 STAE England
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Family and Education b. aft. 1637, 1st surv. s. of Sir Henry Felton, 2nd Bt.†, of Shotley, Suff. and Playford by Susanna, da. of Sir Lionel Tollemache, 2nd Bt.†, of Helmingham, Suff.; bro. of Thomas Felton*.  m. by
2 CONC  1676, Elizabeth, da. of Sir George Reresby of Thrybergh, Yorks., wid. of Sir Francis Foljambe, 1st Bt.†, of Walton, Derbys., Edward Horner of Mells, Som. and William, Visct. Monson of Castlemaine [I]†, 1da.  suc. fa. as 3rd Bt. O
2 CONC ct. 1690.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Offices Held
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography Felton stood with Sir Joseph Williamson on the Tory interest at Thetford in 1690, but after a double return they were declared not elected. Although he originally had no intention of standing at Orford, in 1695 he joined
2 CONC  his Whig brother Thomas as a candidate at the eleventh hour, in order to prevent an outsider being brought in and to settle the ‘differences’ in the borough. Thomas was quite ‘cold in the matter and told him he durst not propose 
2 CONC him to his party for they looked on him [to be] as great a Jacobite as Sir Edward Turnor*’, but Felton ‘proposed himself’ at a meeting of the local Whig ‘cabal’ and was accepted. Afterwards, some Whigs expressed strong reservation
2 CONC s about the arrangement. Their fears, however, were not borne out. Forecast as likely to support the Court in the divisions of 31 Jan. 1696 on the proposed council of trade, Felton signed the Association promptly and in his dealin
2 CONC gs with the corporation he did little to satisfy Tories in Orford: in October 1696 one Tory wrote, ‘I have reason to believe he is more for them [the Whigs] than us’.2
2 CONT
2 CONT Reported on 27 Jan. 1697 to be ‘very sick and not like to recover’, he died on 9 Feb.3
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref Volumes: 1690-1715 Author: D. W. Hayton Notes 1. Procs. Suff. Inst. Arch. iv. 33, 55; Add. 19125, ff. 127–9.  2. W. Suss. RO, Shillinglee mss Ac.454/1009, 968, Theophilus Hooke to Sir Edward Turnor, 4 Nov. 1695, Nathaniel Good
2 CONC ing to same, 26 Oct. 1696.  3. Ibid. Ac.454/969, Gooding to Turnor, 27 Jan. 1696[–7]; Hervey Diary, 26.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/collection-1/myheritage-family-trees?itemId=314936721-1-501227&action=showRecord&indId=externalindividual-b9949136d0f04f260097133f58d6b305&mrid=d8deedf28d6e0934d05428ba867cb221 MyH
2 CONC eritage Family Trees] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 11 2016, 1:52:11 UTC''
