1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *''''''Catherine Russell1
2 CONT *''''''F, #12065, b. 23 August 1676, d. 30 October 1711
2 CONT *Last Edited=1 Feb 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.01%
2 CONT *''''''   Catherine Russell was born on 23 August 1676.1 She was the daughter of Rt. Hon. William Russell, Lord Russell and Lady Rachel Wriothesley.1 She married John Manners, 2nd Duke of Rutland, son of John Manners, 1st Duke of 
2 CONC Rutland and Hon. Catherine Noel, on 23 August 1693.1 She died on 30 October 1711 at age 35.1
2 CONT *''''''      Her married name became Manners.
2 CONT *''''''Children of Catherine Russell and John Manners, 2nd Duke of Rutland
2 CONT **1.Lady Catherine Manners+ d. 18 Feb 1780
2 CONT **2.Frances Manners
2 CONT **3.Lord William Manners+ b. bt 1696 - 1711, d. 1772
2 CONT **4.John Manners, 3rd Duke of Rutland+ b. 21 Oct 1696, d. 29 May 1779
2 CONT **5.Lady Elizabeth Manners+ b. c 1709, d. 22 Mar 1730
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 319. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Pe
2 CONC erage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *2.[S3409] Caroline Maubois, "re: Penancoet Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger Lundy, 2 December 2008. Hereinafter cited as "re: Penancoet Family."
2 CONT *From: http://thepeerage.com/p1207.htm#i12065
2 CONT *___________
2 CONT *''''''John Manners, 2nd Duke of Rutland KG (18 September 1676 – 22 February 1721) was the son of John Manners, 1st Duke of Rutland and his third wife Catherine Wriothesley Noel, daughter of Baptist Noel, 3rd Viscount Campden. He 
2 CONC was styled Lord Roos from 1679 until 1703 and Marquess of Granby from 1703 until 1711.
2 CONT *''''''He married, firstly, Catherine Russell, daughter of William Russell, Lord Russell and Lady Rachel Wriothesley, on 23 August 1693. They had nine children:
2 CONT **John Manners, 3rd Duke of Rutland (1696–1779)
2 CONT **Lord William Manners (1697–1772)
2 CONT **Lord Edward Manners
2 CONT **Lord Thomas Manners (d. 1723)
2 CONT **Lord Wriothesley Manners
2 CONT **Lady Catherine Manners (d. 18 February 1780), married on 29 October 1726 Henry Pelham and had issue.
2 CONT **Lady Elizabeth Manners (1709 – 22 March 1730), married John Monckton, 1st Viscount Galway and had issue.
2 CONT **Lady Rachel Manners (d. c. 1723)
2 CONT **Lady Frances Manners, married Hon. Richard Arundell, son of John Arundell, 2nd Baron Arundell of Trerice.
2 CONT *He married, secondly, Lucy Sherard, daughter of Bennet Sherard, 2nd Baron Sherard, on 1 January 1713. They had eight children:
2 CONT **Lord Sherard Manners (c. 1713 – 13 January 1742)
2 CONT **Lord James Manners (1720 – 1 November 1790)
2 CONT **Lord George Manners (d. December 1721)
2 CONT **Lady Caroline Manners (d. 10 November 1769), married on 2 October 1734 Sir Henry Harpur, 5th Baronet (d. 1748), married on 17 July 1753 Sir Robert Burdett, 4th Baronet (d. 1797).
2 CONT **Lady Lucy Manners (c. 1717 – 18 June 1788), married on 28 October 1742, in London, William Graham, 2nd Duke of Montrose and had issue.
2 CONT **Lord Robert Manners (c. 1721 – 31 May 1782), married on 1 January 1756 Mary Digges and had issue
2 CONT **Lord Henry Manners (d. 1745)
2 CONT **Lord Charles Manners (d. 1761)
2 CONT *External links
