1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =='''William Stourton, 12th Baron Stourton==
2 CONT '''William Stourton, 12th Baron Stourton (died 1685) was the grandson and successor of William Stourton. He was the son of Edward Stourton (1617-January 1644) and Mary Petre (c. 1624-1672), daughter of the 3rd Baron Petre
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He married Elizabeth Preston (died April 1688), daughter of Sir John Preston, in 1665. The couple had at least four sons;
2 CONT * Edward (1665–1720), became Baron in 1685.
2 CONT * Thomas (1667–1743), became Baron in 1720.
2 CONT * Capt. Charles Stourton (1669-18 Sept 1739), father of:
2 CONT ** Charles Stourton, who became Baron in 1743.
2 CONT ** William Stourton, who became Baron in 1754.
2 CONT *John Stourton (1673-3 October 1748)
2 CONT
2 CONT From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Stourton,_12th_Baron_Stourton
2 CONT *______________________
2 CONT *'''William Stourton, 12th Baron Stourton
2 CONT *'''M, #60872, b. circa 1644, d. 7 August 1685
2 CONT *Last Edited=21 Nov 2004
2 CONT *'''     William Stourton, 12th Baron Stourton was born circa 1644. He was the son of Edward Stourton and Mary Petre. He married Elizabeth Preston, daughter of Sir John Preston, Bt., in 1665. He died on 7 August 1685.
2 CONT *'''     He gained the title of 12th Baron Stourton.
2 CONT *'''Children of William Stourton, 12th Baron Stourton and Elizabeth Preston
2 CONT ** 1.Edward Stourton, 13th Baron Stourton b. 1665, d. Oct 1720
2 CONT ** 2.Thomas Stourton, 14th Baron Stourton b. 1667, d. 24 Mar 1743/44
2 CONT ** 3.Captain Charles Stourton+ b. 1669, d. 18 Sep 1739
2 CONT ** 4.John Stourton b. 1673, d. 3 Oct 1748
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p6088.htm#i60872
2 CONT *_____________________
2 CONT *'''William STOURTON (12º B. Stourton of Stourton)
2 CONT *'''Born: ABT 1644
2 CONT *'''Died: 7 Aug 1685
2 CONT *'''Buried: Stourton
2 CONT *Father: Edward STOURTON
2 CONT *Mother: Mary PETRE
2 CONT *'''Married: Elizabeth PRESTON (B. Stourton of Stourton) ABT 1665
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Edward STOURTON (13º B. Stourton of Stourton)
2 CONT **2. Thomas STOURTON (14º B. Stourton of Stourton)
2 CONT **3. Charles STOURTON
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/STOURTON.htm#William STOURTON (12º B. Stourton of Stourton)
2 CONT *_______________________
2 CONT *William [Stourton], 11th Baron Stourton
2 CONT *born   in or bef. 1594
2 CONT *mar.   2 Jul 1615 Frances Moore (d. 5 Jan 1662/3; bur. at Dorking, co. Surrey), dau. of Sir Edward Moore, of Odiham, co. Hampshire, by his second wife Hon Frances Stourton, widow of his uncle John [Stourton], 9th Baron Stourton, 
2 CONC and 2nd dau. by his second wife of William [Brooke], 10th Lord Cobham of Kent
2 CONT *children
2 CONT **	1. Hon Edward Stourton, a strong supporter of King Charles I (b. c. 1617; dvp. Jan 1643/4), mar. after 28 Oct 1638 Hon Mary Petre (mar. (2) bef. 20 Sep 1650 Sir Thomas Longueville, of Bradwell; bur. 27 Sep 1672 at Stourton, co.
2 CONC  Wiltshire), 1st dau. of Robert [Petre], 3rd Baron Petre, by his wife Hon Mary Browne, 6th dau. of Anthony Maria [Browne], 2nd Viscount Montagu, and had issue:
2 CONT ***'''		1a. William Stourton, later 12th Baron Stourton
2 CONT ***		1a. Mary Stourton (d. unm.)
2 CONT **	2. Hon John Stourton (dvp. unm.)
2 CONT **	3. Hon William Stourton (dsp.), mar. Margaret Morgan, dau. of George Morgan, of Penrith, co. Cumberland
2 CONT **	4. Hon Thomas Stourton, a monk (d. 1684)
2 CONT **	1. Hon Mary Stourton (d. 1650), mar. 1649 Sir John Weld, of Lulworth Castle, co. Dorset, and Compton Bassett, co. Wiltshire (d. 11 Jul 1674), 3rd son of Sir John Weld, of Arnold's Court, co. Middlesex, by his wife Frances Whitm
2 CONC ore, dau. of William Whitmore, and had issue
2 CONT **	2. Hon Frances Stourton, a nun at Cambrai
2 CONT *died   died 25 Apr 1672 (bur. at Stourton, co. Wiltshire)
2 CONT *suc. by   grandson
2 CONT *note   Knight of the Bath on the creation of Prince Charles as Prince of Wales 1616; he gave £300 for the war against the Scots 1638/9; in the Civil War he was not militarily active in his support for King Charles, but he still s
2 CONC uffered as a Catholic at the hands of the Parliamentarians, having his estate sequestered in 1645 ; he was in Oxford when it surrendered to the Parliamentary Army in 1646 ; between 1649 and 1654 he was fined several times for bein
2 CONC g a recusant
2 CONT *
2 CONT *'''William [Stourton], 12th Baron Stourton
2 CONT *'''born   c. 1644
2 CONT *'''mar.   after 20 Aug 1664 Elizabeth Preston (d. Apr 1688), dau. of Sir John Preston, 1st Bt., of Furness Abbey, co. Lancaster, and Preston Patrick and Never Levens, co. Westmorland, by his wife Jane Morgan, dau. and cohrss. of 
2 CONC Thomas Morgan, of Heyford, co. Northampton
2 CONT *children
2 CONT **	1. Hon Edward Stourton, later 13th Baron Stourton
2 CONT **	2. Hon Thomas Stourton (dvp. an infant)
2 CONT **	3. Hon Thomas Stourton, later 14th Baron Stourton
2 CONT **	4. Hon William Stourton (dvp. an infant)
2 CONT **	5. Capt Hon Charles Stourton (b. 1669; d. 1739), mar. 1699 Katherine Frampton (d. 1736), dau. and cohrss. of Richard Frampton, of Bitson, co. Dorset, and had issue:
2 CONT ***		1a. Charles Stourton, later 15th Baron Stourton
2 CONT ***		2a. William Stourton (b. 1703; dvp. an infant)
2 CONT ***		3a. Hon William Stourton, later 16th Baron Stourton
2 CONT ***		4a. Richard Stourton (dvp. an infant)
2 CONT ***		5a. Thomas Stourton (dvp. an infant)
2 CONT ***		6a. Thomas Stourton (dvp. young 1713)
2 CONT ***		7a. James Stourton (b. 1715; d. unm.)
2 CONT ***		1a. Hon Mary Stourton (d. 21 Nov 1764), mar. bef. 1721 Jordan Langdale, of Cliffe, co. York, and had issue
2 CONT ***		2a. Hon Katherine Stourton, a nun in the English convent at Liège (d. 29 Jul 1777)
2 CONT ***		3a. Hon Jane Stourton (b. 7 Jan 1708; dsp. 21 Dec 1769), mar. Anthony Kemp, of Slyndon, co. Sussex
2 CONT ***		4a. Elizabeth Stourton, a nun at Liège (b. May 1711; d. 7 Apr 1741)
2 CONT ***		5a. Dorothy Stourton (dvp. an infant)
2 CONT **	6. Hon Botolph Stourton (b. 1672; dsp.)
2 CONT **	7. Hon William Stourton (b. 1673; dsp. 1728)
2 CONT **	8. Hon John Stourton, a priest, Prior of Winchester (b. 1673; d. 1748)
2 CONT **	9. Hon Peter Stourton (dvp. an infant)
2 CONT *'''died   7 Aug 1685 (bur. at Stourton, co. Wiltshire)
2 CONT *'''suc. by   son
2 CONT *'''note   Although he had been summoned to Parliament in 1673 and taken his seat, he was excluded from the House of Lords under the Act of 1678 - his successors remained excluded until the Catholic Emancipation Act was passed in 
2 CONC 1829
2 CONT *From: http://www.cracroftspeerage.co.uk/online/content/stourton1448.htm 
2 CONT *_______________________________
2 CONT *'''History of the noble house of Stourton, of Stourton, in the county of Wilts; (1899)
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/historyofnobleho01mowb
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/historyofnobleho01mowb#page/167/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.167
2 CONT *   The Right Honourable Sir John Stourton, knight, P.C., Treasurer of the Royal Household, created Baron and Lord Stourton, of Stourton, Co. Wilts., in the Peerage of England, only son and heir of Sir William Stourton, knight, Sp
2 CONC eaker of the House of Commons, knight in Parliament for the shires of Somerset, Wilts., and Dorset, and Lord of Stourton, Co. Wilts., Great Easton, Co. Essex, Sopley, Co. Hants and of several other Manors, by Elizabeth, his wife, 
2 CONC daughter and coheir (or sole heir) of Sir John Moigne, knight, by Catherine (Belvale,) his wife. He was born in 1399 and was aged 14 years on the death of his father in 1413. .... etc.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/historyofnobleho01mowb#page/206/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.206
2 CONT *   Lord Stourton, by Margery, his only wife (who was under age in 1411), daughter of Sir John Wadham,(*) knight, of Merefield, Co. Somerset, one of the Puisne Justices of the Court of Common Pleas, 1388-1397, by Joan Wrottesley, 
2 CONC his wife, had issue :(f) .... etc.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/historyofnobleho01mowb#page/211/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.211
2 CONT *   John, Lord Stourton, died on St. Catherine's day, the 25th day of November, 1462, and the Inquisitions taken after his death shew he died seized of considerable manors, advowsons, lands, tenements and hereditaments in the Coun
2 CONC ties of Devon, Somerset, Dorset, Gloucester, Southampton, Essex, London, Middlesex and Wilts, leaving William Stourton, his son and next heir, aged 32 years, who succeeded his father in the peerage as William, 2nd Lord Stourton. 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/historyofnobleho01mowb#page/226/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.226
2 CONT *   The Right Honourable William, Lord Stourton, 2nd Baron of Stourton, Co. Wilts, in the peerage of England, son and heir of Sir John Stourton, knight, of Stourton aforesaid, who had been created Baron of Stourton by Letters Pate
2 CONC nt on the 13th May, 1448, by Margaret, (or Margery) his only wife, daughter of Sir John Wadham, knight, of Merryfield, Co. Somerset, one of the Puisne Judges of the Court of Common Pleas. 
2 CONT *   Lord Stourton succeeded his father in the Stourton peerage on St. Catherine's day, 25th November, 1462(*). He inherited the vast estates which his father succeeded to, some of which descended paternally, as coming from Sir Wil
2 CONC liam Stourton, and some through his wife, Elizabeth Moigne ; and those which John, Lord Stourton, inherited under the charter of John Hame, and by purchase, as well as by favour of Henry VI. He was born about 1432, and was aged 30
2 CONC  years on the 25th November, 1462, and in the same year he had livery of his fathers estates, but his homage was respited, .... etc.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/historyofnobleho01mowb#page/227/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.227
2 CONT *   This estate was settled as the jointure of Margaret, Lady Stourton, who after the death of her first husband, William, 2nd Lord Stourton, presented with her second husband. Sir John Cheyne or Cheyney, knight. Lord Cheyney, K.G
2 CONC ., who died sine prole on the 30th May, 1499. .... etc.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/historyofnobleho01mowb#page/228/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.228
2 CONT *   He married Margaret, eldest daughter and coheir of Sir John Chidiock, knight, of Chidiock and Caundle, Co. Dorset, .... etc.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/historyofnobleho01mowb#page/242/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.242
2 CONT *   William, Lord Stourton, died on the 18th February, 1477-8, 17 Edward IV., and was buried in the parish church of Mere, dedicated to the honour of St. Michael the Archangel, probably in the Chantry Chapel of the blessed Virgin 
2 CONC Mary, .... etc.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/historyofnobleho01mowb#page/251/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.251
2 CONT *   The Right Honourable John, Lord Stourton, eldest son and heir of William, 2nd Lord Stourton, by Margaret (Chidiock,) Lady Stourton. his only wife. He succeeded his father on the 18th February, 1477-8, as the 3rd Baron of Stour
2 CONC ton, Co. Wilts, in the peerage of England, when of the age of 24 years. 
2 CONT *   He was born circa 1453-4, was of Stourton, Co. Wilts, and Fulham, Co. Middlesex, was as the Lord Sturtons son and heir among those who were inhanced to the honour of knighthood, as knight a of the Bath, by Edward IV., on Whit-
2 CONC sunday, the 18th April, after the custom of England in the time of peace, 1475, and had livery and seizen of his father's possessions the year following his father's death, but his homage was then respited. 
2 CONT *   Lord Stourton married Katherine(*), only daughter of Sir Maurice Berkeley, (who died in 1474(t),) of Beverston, Co. Gloucester, knight of the body of Edward IV., by Ann, his wife, daughter of Reginald West, Lord de la Warr, an
2 CONC cestor of the Earls Delawarr. 
2 CONT *   Lady Stourton, after Lord Stourton's death, remarried to Sir John Brereton, knight, and as sole sister .... etc.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/historyofnobleho01mowb#page/273/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.273
2 CONT *   The Right Honourable William, 5th Baron and Lord Stourton of Stourton, Co. Wilts, in the peerage of England, was the second son of William, second Lord Stourton, by Margaret (Chidiock) Lady Stourton, his wife. He succeeded as 
2 CONC fifth Lord Stourton at the death (February iSth, 14S7,) of his nephew Francis, fourth Lord Stourton, whose uncle and heir he was then found to be. 
2 CONT *   William, 5th Lord Stourton, must have been born about the year 1457, being described as "aged 30 years and upwards" in the inquisitions taken after the death of his infant nephew. 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/historyofnobleho01mowb#page/274/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.274
2 CONT *   William, 5th Lord Stourton, married (firstly) Katherine, eldest daughter of John de la Pole(*), Duke of Suffolk, K.G., by Lady Elizabeth Plantagenet, his wife, second daughter of Richard Plantagenet, Duke of York, and sister o
2 CONC f Edward IV. and Richard III(f). The Duke was made Constable of Wallingford Castle 1
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/historyofnobleho01mowb#page/275/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.275
2 CONT *Henry VII. He died in 1491 and was buried(*), with his Duchess, under a table monument in the Collegiate Church of St. Andrew in Wingfield, Co. Suffolk, of which he was lord and owner by inheritance from his ancestor. Sir John Wi
2 CONC ngfield, of Wingfield Castle. ....
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/historyofnobleho01mowb#page/276/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.276
2 CONT *   Lord Stourton married (secondly) Thomasine, daughter of Sir Walter Wrottesley, knight, who adhered to the Earl of Warwick, the King Maker, and was proclaimed a traitor in 1470, when a price was set on his head. He escaped with
2 CONC  Warwick to Calais(*). Sir Walter Wrottesley was Lord of Perton 9 Edward IV., was buried in the Grey Friars Church, now Christ Church, London, in 1471. He came of an ancient family long seated at Wrottesley, co. Stafford, (where t
2 CONC he present Lord Wrottesley, his descendant, now resides,) by Jane, his wife, daughter and heir of William Baron, Esquire, of Reading, Co. Berks, one of the Tellers of the Court of Exchequer temp. Henry VI. and Edward IV. This Will
2 CONC iam Baron (or his father), is mentioned in Fullers Worthies as one of those bearing arms from their ancestors. ....
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/historyofnobleho01mowb#page/279/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.279
2 CONT *   The exact date of the death of this Lord Stourton is stated to be February 17th in the various Inquisitions taken after his death. His will was proved in March, 1523. He left no issue whatever and consequently his lands and ho
2 CONC nours passed to his brother Edward, who thereupon succeeded as 6th Lord Stourton.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/historyofnobleho01mowb#page/292/mode/1up
