1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====Wikitree ''(4 Aug 2025)'' [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Earle-83 John Earle (abt. 1660–bef. 1728)]
2 CONT * '''b.''' about 1660 [uncertain] in Portsmouth, Colony of Rhode Island and Providence Plantations
2 CONT * '''d.''' before 2 Feb 1728 before about age 68 in Tiverton, Bristol, Province of Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT * '''Husband of''' Mary (Wilcox) Earle — married 1686 in Dartmouth, Bristol, Plymouth Colony
2 CONT * '''Father of''' John Earle, Daniel Earle, Benjamin Earle, Mary Earle, Rebecca Earle and Elizabeth (Earle) Westgate
2 CONT * '''The will of John Earle of Tiverton,''' yeoman, was dated 12 February 1718-9 and proved on 19 March 1727/28 in Bristol.[11] "In his will, ... he mentions his wife Mary; sons John, Daniel and Benjamin; and daughters Mary, Rebec
2 CONC ca, and Elizabeth."[12][13] '''The inventory''' for his estate, for £251. 6s. 1d, was taken on 2 Feb 1727-8 in Tiverton.[13] Based on this information, John would have died sometime between 1719 and 1728.
2 CONT * '''Unsourced claim:''' "JOHN EARLE was born 16 October 1659, at Portsmouth, Aquidneck Island, Rhode Island."
2 CONT * '''Unsourced claim:''' "John Earle died 2 February 1728, age 68, at Tiverton, Bristol, Massachusetts."
2 CONT * '''Land Transactions'''
2 CONT ** '''1686:''' "Before this removal and in October, 1686," according to one commentator, "John Sprague, son of John and grandson of Francis Sprague, and Lydia, his wife, conveyed to [John Earle] all right, or claim of inheritance,
2 CONC  in 'one half of a purchase of Land Lying In ye township of Dartmouth, In the county of Bristol, where my Uncle Ralf Earl now lives.' This was the land which Francis Sprague gave to his son-in-law, Ralph Earle."[8]
2 CONT ** '''1688:''' John's father, "Ralph Earle of Dartmouth" gifted to John's son (Ralph's grandson) John, 7 May 1688, "one hundred acres of land which [Ralph] purchased from [Ralph's] Brother William Earle of Dartmouth ... being in .
2 CONC .. Dartmouth ... at a place commonly called and known by the name of Nanquid Neck," to vest in his "grandson ... after his father's decease and not before."[9]
2 CONT ** '''1693:''' Retaining for himself and John's mother for their lives the rights to the profits, John's father gifted to John "of Dartmouth," 28 Feb 1692-3, a life estate in two hundred and fifty acres in Dartmouth, and, at John'
2 CONC s death, left one hundred of the acres in fee to John's son John, one hundred of the acres in fee to John's son Daniel and the remaining fifty acres in fee to John's son Benjamin.[10]
2 CONT
2 CONT ====From ''The Earle Family: Ralph Earle and His Descendants'': [https://archive.org/stream/earlefamilyralph00inearl#page/26/search/Sprague Archive]
2 CONT
2 CONT John Earle (Ralph [2], Ralph [1]), son of Ralph and Dorcas (Sprague) Earle; m. Mary (d. 1735), dau. of Daniel and Elizabeth (Cook) Wilcox, and d. in 1728.
2 CONT
2 CONT John had taken the oath of fidelity, or Freeman's oath, in Dartmouth before Mar. 24, 1686, but he afterwards removed to Tiverton. Before this removal, and in October 1686, John Sprague, son of John and grandson of Francis Sprague,
2 CONC  and Lydia, his wife, conveyed to him all right, or claim of inheritance, in "one half of a purchase of Land Lying In ye township of Dartmouth, In ye county of Bristoll, where my Uncle Ralf Earl now lives." This was the land which
2 CONC  Francis Sprague gave to his son-in-law, Ralph Earle [2-1].
2 CONT
2 CONT In his will, which was executed Feb. 12, 1719, he mentions his wife Mary; sons John, Daniel, and Benjamin; and daughters Mary, Rebecca, and Elizabeth. The inventory was 251 pounds, 6 s., 1 d.
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of John and Mary (Wilcox) Earle were:
2 CONT * [47-1] John Earle, b. Aug. 7, 1687.
2 CONT * [48-2] Daniel Earle, b. Oct. 8, 1688; m. Grace Wicks, 1716.
2 CONT * [49-3] Benjamin Earle, b. May 25, 1691; m. Rebecca Westgate
2 CONT * [50-4] Mary Earle, b. June 1, 1693; living, unmarried, in 1769
2 CONT * [51-5] Rebecca Earle, b. Dec. 17, 1695.
2 CONT * [52-6] Elizabeth Earle, b. Sept. 6, 1699; m. 1st George Westgate; 2d, Capt. John Adams, of Warren, RI
