2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT
2 CONT Earle page 31
2 CONT took freeman oath in Dartmouth prior to March 24 1686.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1688 his father gave to him and his wife the land “adjoining the Fall River” at Pocasset, in Freetown. the top of the left ear off.
2 CONT
2 CONT His dwelling house was about one and one half miles north-easterly from the central village of Leicester on Mulbery street.  It was a gambrel one-story dwelling. Which was taken down in 1846.  
2 CONT
2 CONT March 5, 1721 Ralph was “Voted  that Ralph Earl” should have a certain “pew spot” in the meeting-house, he paying the town ten shillings. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In the next twelve years the Quakers were established in Leicester.  Ralph joined the group. In 1732 Ralph and his sons William and Robert and four other men, asked to be released from paying “ any part of the Tax for the Seport o
2 CONC f the minister or ministers established by the Laws of the province” because they were alleged they were Quakers.   Ralph went to Philadelphia to visit William Penn.  
2 CONT
2 CONT At a town meeting March 22, 1735 “ voted to allow Mr Ralph Earl four shillings to meet worcester men to perambulate ye line between worcester and lester.”
2 CONT
2 CONT Society of Friends organized in Leicester in 1735.  as early as 1732 Ralph and sons William, Robert and Benjamin declared themselves Quakers and asked to be excused from the payment of parish taxes for the support of the Congregat
2 CONC ional minister. on account of conscientious scruples. pg 95 meeting  house of Quakers was built on Earle family property
2 CONT
2 CONT Will executed May 25 1750.  Among the bequests to his wife is his “negro boy Sharp”; and he directs that if the negro be faithful and well=behaved, he shall have his freedom at her decease.  If he be not faithful, he may be sold. 
2 CONC  Before Ralph died he manumitted the slave, and on April 6th 1756 gave him 30 acres of land on the southern declivity of Asnebumskit.  In the dee he state “In consideration of Love, good will and faithful service to me performed b
2 CONC y my negro servant Sharp” he make this gift.  Sharp would assume the name Freeborn” as his surname.  Ralph deed recorded Worcester Registry Book 38 p 85
2 CONT Nathaniel son of Nathaniel grandson of Thomas was another to have been given property. lot 141 on map and 297
