1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William Cory was born about 1659 in Portsmouth, Newport Co, RI. He died on 14 May 1704 in Portsmouth, Newport Co, RI. 
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: In 1684, William was made a freeman. 1687 served on Grand Jury. July 2, 1695 He was appointed by assembly, on a committee to propose a
2 CONT
2 CONT method of making tax rate.. Will Dated 14 May 1704. Proved 4 June 1704.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Ex. Honored Mother and my brother-in-law, Joseph Cook. To son Michael, 12 acres, at age, and if he die without issue, to son Thomas. To second son William, all other lands, housing and orchard to me belonging, except 15 acres. To
2 CONC  third son Thomas 5 acres. To son
2 CONT
2 CONT Michael 10 acres. To daughter Patience Cory, 5 pounds (paid by her brother William), a cow and a feather bed. To daughter Mary Cory a cow. To daughter Amey Cory a Cow, 5 pounds and a bed. To Four daughters, the rest of movables, w
2 CONC hen they are eighteen or married."
2 CONT
