2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary was born about 1664 at Dartmouth in Plymouth Colony, the daughter of William and Martha (Earle) Wood. She m. (1) Samuel Wilcox; m. (2) Thomas Mallet; m. (3) John Sanford. She died at Newport 15 Dec 1721 in the 57th year of he
2 CONC r age. Mary is buried in the Common Burial Ground (Newport). Her headstone has the Sanford Arms thereon. More information in source.[1] Children with Samuel Wilcox:
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeremiah b. 24 September 1683
2 CONT William b. 2 February 1685
2 CONT Mary b. 14 February 1688; m. Thomas Brooks
2 CONT An action of trespass, writ dated 18 July 1723, has Jeremiah Wilcox of Dartmouth, yeoman, son and heir to Mary Sandford, deceased, formerly wife to Thomas Mallett of Newport, deceased, and then wife ot John Sanford of Newport, but
2 CONC cher, vs. James Akin of Newport, innholder.[2] The defendant claimed
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Mallett's will devised his remaining estate to his wife Mary but did not say the house and land were part of that remainder.
2 CONT Mary entered the premises and died about 15 January 1721, leaving the plaintiff her oldest son and heir then surviving.
2 CONT [Plaintiff's claim] did not recognize that Mary Mallett left a daughter Mary then married to Capt. Thomas Brooks of Newport, who [Mary] is lately dead and hath left behind her severall children
2 CONT Mary was born in 1664.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Wood-10427
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary (Wood) Sanford (abt. 1665 - abt. 1721)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Mary Sanford formerly Wood aka Wilcox, Mallett===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 1665 in Dartmouth, Bristol, Massachusetts Bay Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of William Wood Sr. and Martha (Earle) Wood
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister of William Wood Jr., George Wood, Joseph Wood, Margaret (Wood) Taber, Daniel Wood 1st and Rebecca (Wood) Sanford
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Samuel Wilcox — married 1683 in Massachusetts Bay Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Thomas Mallett — married before Apr 1697 [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of John Sanford — married about 1714 [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of Jeremiah Wilcox
2 CONT
2 CONT Died about 15 Dec 1721 at about age 56 in Newport, Rhode Island
2 CONT
