1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sarah Cornell===
2 CONT *Born about 1668 in Little Compton, Newport, Rhode Island
2 CONT * Died 16 Jan 1748 at about age 80 in Warren, Bristol County, Rhode Island
2 CONT *Daughter of Thomas Cornell II and Sarah (Earle) Lake
2 CONT *Wife of Zaccheus Butts — married 1690 (to 1700) [location unknown]
2 CONT *Wife of John Cole — married 25 Aug 1712 in Swansea, Bristol, Massachusetts. He was Susannah Briggs’s widower.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 
2 CONT # Sarah Butts
2 CONT # John Butts
2 CONT #  Abigail (Butts) Cole
2 CONT #  Mary (Butts) Brayton 
2 CONT # Elizabeth (Butts) Cundall
2 CONT
2 CONT The American Genealogist July 1935, p24. In a footnote it is mentioned that Zaccheus deserted his wife, Sarah, and put their daughter, Mary, in the family of Joseph Palmer “which family were not suitable to bring her up” The court
2 CONC  ordered Mary to be put in the family of David Lake, “whose wife is the child's grandmother.”
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Cornell-412
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 22 Apr 2021 | Created 26 Sep 2012 | Last significant change: 22 Apr 2021
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah was the daughter of Thomas Cornell, Jr. and Sarah Earle (Thomas's 2nd wife). She married Zaccheus Butts in 1689 in Little Compton, Rhode Island. They had 4 other children: Sarah, John, Abigail and Elizabeth. Zaccheus deserte
2 CONC d Sarah. When that happened their daughter, Mary was put in family of Joseph Palmer but was deemed "...not suitable to bring her up" so ordered her to be put in family of David Lake "whose wife is childs grandmother." After Zacche
2 CONC us died, Sarah married John Cole on August 15, 1712 in Swansea, Massachusetts. It was his 2nd marriage as well. Her father, Thomas Cornell, Jr. was executed for murdering his mother, Rebecca (Rebecka) Briggs Cornell. It is an inte
2 CONC resting mystery, to read more about it: "Killed Strangely: The story of Rebecca Cornell" by Elaine Forham Craine.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah died on January 16, 1748 in Warren, Bristol, Rhode Island [2] Buried in Kickemuit Cemetery, Near Warren, Rhode Island [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Husband Zaccheus Butts. Wife Sarah Cornell. Marriage 1691 Little Compton, Newport, Rhode Island, United States. [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Fact: http://familysearch.org/v1/LifeSketch Zaccheus Butts abandoned her Fact: Burial Kickemuit Cemetery, Warren, Bristol, Rhode Island, British Colonial America
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/9258410/sarah-cole
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Cornell Cole
2 CONT
2 CONT BIRTH	1668
2 CONT
2 CONT DEATH	16 Jan 1748 (aged 79–80) Warren, Bristol County, Rhode Island, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT BURIAL	 Kickemuit Cemetery Warren, Bristol County, Rhode Island, USA MEMORIAL ID	9258410
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah was a daughter of Sarah (Earle) & Thomas Cornell. She had a brother, John and a sister, Innocent.
2 CONT
2 CONT She first married Zaccheus Butts about 1692. They had 2 children, John and Mary.
2 CONT
2 CONT She then married John Cole, August 25, 1712 in Swansea, MA. They had 3 children, Mary, Hannah and John. (See will on husband John Cole's memorial.)
2 CONT
