1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Innocent Cornell. Born ca 1673 in Portsmouth, RI. Innocent died aft 15 Nov 1720.
2 CONT
2 CONT The wife of Richard Borden was the daughter of Thomas and Sarah (Earle) Cornell. The names of Richard and Innocent’s children are given as follows: eldest daughter Sarah named after Innocent’s mother, eldest son John named after R
2 CONC ichard’s father, next eldest son Thomas named after Sarah’s father, next eldest daughter Mary named after Richard’s mother. Also, a later daughter Rebecca is named after Sarah’s grandmother Rebecca, whom her father Thomas was exec
2 CONC uted for murdering. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Innocent married Richard Borden (9733) , son of John Borden (2853) (Sep 1640-4 Jun 1716) & Mary Earle (12880) (ca 1655-Jun 1734). Born on 25 Oct 1671 in Newport, RI.2 Richard died in Bristol, RI, on 12 Jul 1732; he was 60.136
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children include:
2 CONT
2 CONT 21932	i.	Sarah Borden (Died soon) (31 Jul 1694-Aug 1694)
2 CONT
2 CONT 21933	ii.	John Borden (10 Dec 1695-)
2 CONT
2 CONT 21934	iii.	Thomas Borden (8 Dec 1697-Apr 1740)
2 CONT
2 CONT 21935	iv.	Richard Borden (ca 1699-ca 1740)
2 CONT
2 CONT 21936	v.	Mary Borden (29 Jan 1701-23 Jul 1786)
2 CONT
2 CONT 21937	vi.	Joseph Borden (4 Nov 1702-Dec 1736)
2 CONT
2 CONT 21938	vii.	Samuel Borden (25 Oct 1705-1 Sep 1778)
2 CONT
2 CONT 21939	viii.	Rebecca Borden (18 Jul 1712-30 Apr 1750)
