1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Mary Herbert:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p42763.htm#i427624
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Mary Herbert [1]
2 CONT *F, #427624, 
2 CONT *d. 30 October 1744
2 CONT *Last Edited=23 Sep 2010
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Mary Herbert married, firstly, Richard Molyneux, son of Caryll Molyneux, 3rd Viscount Molyneux.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, secondly, Francis Browne, 4th Viscount Montagu, son of Francis Browne, 3rd Viscount Montagu, circa 1690.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, thirdly, George Maxwell of Orchardtoun, 3rd Bt. on 22 August 1716.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 30 October 1744.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of William Herbert, 1st Marquess of Powis and Lady Elizabeth Somerset.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Her married name became Molyneux.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT From circa 1690, her married name became Browne.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT From 22 August 1716, her married name became Maxwell.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
