1 NAME James, Esq. /Hussey of Westown and of Courtown/
2 GIVN James, Esq.
2 _MARNM Hussey of Westown and of Courtown
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1759
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =CONSULT THE SOURCES PROVIDED=
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://books.google.com/books?id=RtsWAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA323&lpg=PA323&dq=Mary+Hussey+of+Westown+%281729-%29&source=bl&ots=DSW-sJqVIC&sig=-ceFFb3vm7kjpfTkI5KjGGvZpqs&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0CB8Q6AEwAGoVChMIr9yW3_7jxwIVSHUeCh0C7gsv#v=onepage&q
2 CONC =Mary%20Hussey%20of%20Westown%20%281729-%29&f=false The Peerage of England, Scotland, and Ireland: The peerage of England]
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Genealogical History of the Dormant, Forfeited and Extinct Peerages of the British Empire by Sir Bernard Burke, Ulster King of Arms''
2 CONT
2 CONT Hussey -- Baron and Earl of Beaulieu. Barony by Letters Patent, dated 11 May 1762. Earldom by Letters Patent, dated 6 July 1784.
2 CONT
2 CONT SIR HUGH HUSSEY, who went to Ireland, 17 HENRY II., married the sister of Theobald Fitz-Walter, the first Butler of that kindom, and d. seized of large possessions in the co. Meath, from the grant of Hugh de Lacie. His son '''Walt
2 CONC er Hussey''', was father, by Agnes his wife (dau and heir of Hugh de Lacei, Sen., Earl of Ulster) of '''Hugh Hussey''', who married a daughter of Adam de Hereford, and had a son, William Hussey, who, by Catherine Fitzgerald his wi
2 CONC fe, a daughter of the house of Kildare, was father of Sir John Hussey, Knt, 1st Baron of Galtrim, summoned to parliament 25 Mar and 22 Nov 1374 and 22 Jan 1377. From him descended the great house of HUSSEY, '''Barons of Galtrim'''
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT PETER HUSSEY, Esq., 2nd son of James Hussey, Baron of Galtrim, by Mary, his wife, daughter of Richard Aylmer, sq., of Lyons, married Mary, only daughter and heir of Bartholomew Bellew, Esq., of Westown, co. Dublin, and had a son.
2 CONT
2 CONT LUKE HUSSEY, Esq., of Westown, whose will bears date 17 April 1671. He married Elizabeth Barnewall, and was father of a daughter Katharine who married first to Christopher D'Arcy, Esq. of Stidall and secondly to Thomas D'Arcy; and
2 CONC  of a son, COL. EDWARD HUSSEY, of Westown, whose will was proved 25 Nov 1742; he married Mabel Barnewell and had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. James, his heir
2 CONT 2. George, d. unm. 3. Luke, d. unm 4. Nicholas, who d. unm 5. Mabel, mar. to Batthias Barnewall, Esq. of Castletown, co Meath
2 CONT
2 CONT =The eldest son JAMES HUSSEY, Esq. of Westown,co. Dublin and of Courtown, co. Kildare, m 1705 (M.L. dated 6 July) '''Catherine, daughter of Richard Parson, Viscount Rosse, and by her who died in March 1, 1766''', had issue (with f
2 CONC our daughters, Frances, Elizabeth, Mable, and Mary, wife of James Hussey, Esq. of Galtrim), three sons, EDWARD, his heir; Richard, d.s.p.; James, d.s.p. Mr. Hussey died in 1759 and was survived by his eldest son.=
2 CONT
2 CONT EDWARD HUSSEY, Esq. of Westown, who married in 1743, Isabella, eldest daughter and co-heir of John, Duke of Montague, and relict of William Montague, Duke of Manchester, and assumed at the decease of his father-in-law, thename and
2 CONC  arms of Montague. In 1753, he was installed a knight of the Bath; in 1762, created a peer of Great Britain as Baron Beaulier, of Beaulier; and in 1784, advanced to be EARL BEAULIEU. By the co-heiress of Montague, his lordship had
2 CONC  an only son. John, who died unmarried and one daughter, Isabella, who also died unmarried in 1772. He died in 1802 (when the peerage expired), and was survived in the Irish estates by his brother, RICHARD HUSSEY, Esq of Westown, 
2 CONC who died unmarried, having devised h is property to his cousin (the grandson of Catherine Hussey, by her husband, Sir Andrew Aylmer, Bart.) GERALD STRONG, Esq., who assumed, in consequence, the name and arms of HUSSEY. Owing, howe
2 CONC ver, to the will of Lord Beaulieu, who had bequeathed the estates to Lord Sidney Osborne, youngest son of the Duke of Lees, litigation ensued, and was at length termined by a compromise and division of the prperty under an act of 
2 CONC parliament, 51st GEORGE III. Mr. Strong-Hussey married in 1781, Mary, daughter of Anthony Lynch, Esq., of La Vally, co. Galway, and had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Anthony, his heir
2 CONT 2. Margaret 3. Isabella |
2 CONT Mr. Strong-Hussey, Esq., of Westown was born 24 August 1782, and married 19 Aug 1811 Mable, eldest daughter of Malachi Donelan, Esq, of Ballydoneian, co. Galway, and dying 12 July 1859, left, with other isue, a son and heir, the l
2 CONC ate Malachi Strong-Hussey, Esq. of Westown.
2 CONT
