1 NAME William /O'Brien/ 7th Baron Inchiquin, 2nd Baron O'Brien & 2nd Earl of Inchiquin
2 GIVN William
2 SURN O'Brien
2 NSFX 7th Baron Inchiquin, 2nd Baron O'Brien & 2nd Earl of Inchiquin
2 _MARNM O'Brien
2 NICK Gov. of Jamaica
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1638
2 ADDR
3 CITY Inchiquin
3 CTRY Ireland
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT JAN 1692
2 ADDR
3 CITY Spanish Town
3 STAE Saint Catherine Parish
3 CTRY Jamaica
1 OCCU Governor of Jamaica   also Vice Admiral of the Caribbean Seas 1690 -1692
1 TITL Col.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Burke, Bernard, Sir. [http://archive.org/stream/genealogicalhera00inburk#page/614/mode/2up A genealogical and heraldic dictionary of the peerage and baronetage of the British Empire]. London : Harrison 1869. page
2 CONC  615<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''William O'Brien''' 
2 CONT * son of Murrough O'Brien, 1st Earl of Inchiquin and Elisabeth St. Leger.
2 CONT * Served under his father in various military activities in France and Spain but was captured with his father by the Turks in 1660 and imprisoned in Algiers until the English Parliament had paid a ransom of 7,500 dollars. 
2 CONT * He was a Privy Councillor from 1671 to 1685. 
2 CONT * Captain General of the Forces at Tangier from 1674 to 1680 
2 CONT * Colonel of the '''2nd Tangier Regiment of Foot''' from 1675 to 1680. <br/>
2 CONT He was attainted in his absence by the Irish Parliament of King James II in 1689.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the first Governor of Jamaica and Vice-Admiral of the Caribbean Seas from 1690 to 1692. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in Jamaica in 1692 and his Irish estate and titles were inherited by his son William. His younger son James inherited the Earl's trading interests.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_O%27Brien,_2nd_Earl_of_Inchiquin
