2 CONT Honora Boyle (d. c. November 1710, bur. 14 November 1710 Saint Patrick's Church, Dublin, County Dublin), sister and co-heiress of Murrough (Boyle), 1st Viscount Blesington, daughter of The Most Rev. Michael Boyle, DD, Archbishop o
2 CONC f Armagh and Lord Chancellor of Ireland, and his second wife the Hon. Mary O'Brien.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 1st, Thomas Cromwell, 3rd Earl of Ardglass (Strensham, Worcestershire, 29 November 1653 – 11 April 1682) - no issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT His widow married secondly bef. 1687 Francis Cuffe (12 September 1656 - 26 December 1694), Member of Parliament for County Mayo in the Parliament of Ireland, son of Sir James Cuffe of Ballinrobe, County Mayo - had issue - 
2 CONT
2 CONT married thirdly c. 1700 as his first wife Captain Sir Thomas Burdett, 1st Baronet, of Garahill, County Carlow (14 September 1668 - 14 April 1727), without issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Cuffe
