1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Murragh Boyle, 1st Viscount Blesington (c.1645–1718) was an Irish peer and member of the House of Lords.
2 CONT
2 CONT * from http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Murrough_Boyle,_1st_Viscount_Blesington_
2 CONT
2 CONT Murrough (or Murragh) Boyle was born in Cork, Ireland, the son of The Most Reverend Michael Boyle, Archbishop Bishop of Armagh. He married twice; firstly Mary Parker, daughter of Dr. John Parker, Archbishop of Dublin and secondly 
2 CONC Lady Mary or Ann Coote, daughter of Charles Coote, 2nd Earl of Montrath.   By his first wife he had a daughter Mary and by his second a son and heir, Charles and two daughters Amelia and Anne.
2 CONT
2 CONT Murrough was author of a tragedy, entitled "The Lost Princess". Baker, a contemporary dramatic critic, characterised this production as "truly contemptible", and added that the "genius and abilities of the writer did no credit to 
2 CONC the name of Boyle". (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT On his death in Dublin on April 26, 1718 he was buried at St Patrick's Cathedral, Dublin. His title was inherited by his son Charles Boyle, 2nd Viscount Blesington
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT * Burke's (below) says his mother was Margaret; Wikipedia & the peerage.com have Mary, the 2nd wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://www.thepeerage.com/p1933.htm#i19326
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------
2 CONT # [http://books.google.com/books?id=DRmxFzmHXDUC&vq=BLESINTON&pg=PA262#v=onepage&q=BLESINTON&f=false A Catalogue of the Royal and Noble Authors of England, Scotland] ..., Volume 5.   By Horace Walpole, Thomas Park.  Page 262. 
2 CONT # [http://books.google.com/books?id=1ysWkXKSrpIC&pg=PA70#v=onepage&q&f=false A Genealogical History of the Dormant: Abeyant, Forfeited, and Extinct] ... By Sir Bernard Burke.  Page 70.  "BOYLE-VISCOUNTS BLESINTON."
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Wikipedia contributors. "<em>[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Murrough_Boyle,_1st_Viscount_Blesington Murrough Boyle, 1st Viscount Blesington]</em>." Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia.
