1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Langhorne-80
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Langhorne
2 CONT * Born about 1629 in St Gabriel Fenchurch, London, England
2 CONT * Daughter of William Langhorne Bt. and Mary (Oxenbridge) Langhorne
2 CONT * Sister of William Langhorne Bt, Daniel Langhorne and Thomas Langhorne	
2 CONT * Wife of Christopher Conyers — married 1643 [location unknown]
2 CONT * Mother of John Conyers 3rd Bt
2 CONT * Died 27 Apr 1654 at about age 25
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Langhorne, baptised on 1 December 1629 at St Gabriel Fenchurch, London, was the eldest child of William Langhorne and his wife Mary Oxenbridge, and sister of Sir William Langhorn, 1st Bt. an East India Merchant. [1] [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT On 28 September 1648, she married by license Christopher Conyers [3] at Long Ditton, Surrey. [4] She died in childbed on 27 April 1654, giving birth to her only son John. [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Christopher Conyers succeeded to the family baronetcy as 2nd Baronet in December 1664, and Sir John Conyers became 3rd Baronet in 1693. Elizabeth Conyers had been the heiress of her brother Sir William Langhorne, and Sir John 
2 CONC Conyers inherited his uncle's estate at Charlton, Kent at his death in February 1714.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p63878.htm#i638776
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Langhorne
2 CONT * F, #638776, b. circa 1624
2 CONT * Elizabeth Langhorne was born circa 1624. She was the daughter of William Langhorne and Mary Oxenbridge. She married Sir Christopher Conyers, 2nd Bt., son of Sir John Conyers, 1st Bt. and Frances Groves, in 1643.
2 CONT * From 1643, her married name became Conyers.
2 CONT * Child of Elizabeth Langhorne and Sir Christopher Conyers, 2nd Bt.
2 CONT * Sir John Conyers, 3rd Bt.+ b. 1649, d. 1719
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
