1 NOTE !BIRTH, SEE "HERRING HERITAGE"
2 CONT BY JAMES MAURICE GRIMWOOD OF HOUSTON
2 CONT TEXAS
2 CONT __________
2 CONT Herring Highlights 1642-1984
2 CONT by James Maurice Grimwood &
2 CONT Lola Herring Kennedy pg. 2-3
2 CONT US/CAN 929.273  H435g
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of John Herring
2 CONT (Note: Original & facsimile thereof difficult to read.)
2 CONT
2 CONT In the name of God Amen
2 CONT
2 CONT I being in good & perfectt memorie   first I committ my body to the
2 CONT Earth & into the hands of the Almighty God & my Savior Jesus Christ.
2 CONT
2 CONT Give unto my sonne Anthony Herring  two steers of four years old a
2 CONT piece and one Cow of three years called Brantie (?), and  one heiffer of
2 CONT two years old with a whitely face    one small flock bed,       with a . . .
2 CONT & a flock pillor for it one Iron pott of three or four gallions     one  smale
2 CONT (small)  fowling piece  (a lightweight gun designed for shooting birds, firing
2 CONT small pellets instead of a small bullet),    three dishes & one pewter bason
2 CONT one candlestick     one pewter flaggon pott  &  three pewter spoons one
2 CONT white earthern salseller   and one other boll  . . . & one Sow of three quarters
2 CONT of a year old.
2 CONT
2 CONT And I give unto my Sonne Anthony  three barrels of Tar After the debts
2 CONT are paid I give unto my Sonne Anthony Herring half the cropp of tobacco,
2 CONT small chest to put his clothes in:
2 CONT
2 CONT And I bequeath all the rest of my whole Estate both in and removeables,
2 CONT within doors  &  or without   that is or shall be called or knowne to be
2 CONT mine, unto my well beloved  wife Margorie Herring.
2 CONT
2 CONT I give unto the child John Whitfield, one heiffer of one year old with a
2 CONT motley face.
2 CONT
2 CONT                                                                               John (his mark) Herring
2 CONT
2 CONT      John Herring appointed Margorie (or Margerie), his relict, executrix of
2 CONT his will. Apparently, she qualified in November 1672, with Thomas Pooles
2 CONT and Thomas Grosse listed as "Security" which simply meant they guarantee
2 CONT the execution of the document's provisions. Margorie, by nuncuperative will
2 CONT (an oral will spoken out in court by those who heard the testator speak, and
2 CONT then written into the records) bequeathed her estate to John Whitfield,
2 CONT orphan, with no mention being made of Anthony Herring.
2 CONT     Clement Creswell, listed as John Whitfield's father-in-law, qualified 17
2 CONT February 1675 as the executor of Margorie Herring's estate, and her will was
2 CONT written into the records 15 March 1675.
2 CONT    Creswell's will, made in the Isle of Wight Country, was dated 12 March
2 CONT 1682 and recorded 9 November 1683. Among items included in the document
2 CONT was:  ". . .John Whitfield, legacy which Margery Herring left him." Creswell
2 CONT had 2 sons, John and Clement (Jr.) who were ages 17 and 15, respectively, in
2 CONT April 1683. Also, there was a married daughter. Jennet Macon--but there is
2 CONT no indication of a daughter being married to John Whitfield.
2 CONT    Child of John Herring:
2 CONT 1. Anthony Herring
2 CONT Born:  ca     1648   Isle of Wight Co. VA
2 CONT Mar:   ca     1677
2 CONT Died:  ca     1715   Isle of Wight Co. VA
2 CONT __________
2 CONT Cavaliers and Pioneers, Patent Book 1, Part II, Page 129
2 CONT Robert Eyres, 200 acs. Low. Norf Co., May 22, 1642, Page 780.
2 CONT About 8 mi. up a Southern br. of Eliza. River. Trans. of 4 pers:
2 CONT Robert Eyres, Francis Poythres, William Brown, John Herring.
