1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Isabella Carr:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p3749.htm#i37490
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabella Carr [1]
2 CONT *F, #37490, 
2 CONT *b. 20 January 1669/70, 
2 CONT *d. 7 March 1692/93
2 CONT *Last Edited=5 Feb 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabella Carr was born on 20 January 1669/70.[1] She was the daughter of Rt. Hon. Sir Robert Carr, 3rd Bt. and Elizabeth Bennet.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married John Hervey, 1st Earl of Bristol, son of Sir Thomas Hervey and Isabella May, on 1 November 1688 at St. Martin-in-the-Fields, Covent Garden, London, England.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 7 March 1692/93 at age 23, in childbed.[1] She was buried on 16 March 1692/93 at Ickworth, Suffolk, England.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Her married name became Hervey.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Isabella Carr and John Hervey, 1st Earl of Bristol
2 CONT *1. unknown daughter Hervey [2]
2 CONT *2. Carr Hervey, Lord Hervey [3] b. 17 Sep 1691, d. 15 Nov 1723
2 CONT *3. unknown daughter Hervey [2] b. c 7 Mar 1693
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume II, page 323. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *2. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 507. Hereinafter cited as Burke's P
2 CONC eerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *3. [S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume II, page 324.
