1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Digges-2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ann Digges''' was born about 1685 to William Digges and Elizabeth (Sewall) Wharton. Her father was a politician in Colonial Virginia and a councillor in Colonial Maryland in the late seventeenth and early eighteenth centuries.[
2 CONC 1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Her father, William Digges, died on 24 July 1697, leaving a will which mentioned several large Maryland plantations "and directed that his plantation on the York River be used most advantageously for his daughters." However, the Y
2 CONC ork River plantation was inherited by William's eldest son Edward, who on 21 Sept 1699 sold it to his uncle Dudley, William's younger brother.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Ann Digges who married Henry Damall (1682-1759), son of Henry Darnall (ca. 1645-1711), and Mary[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT # Henry Darnall III b. 1703,   d. Aft 1788, Prince George's County, Maryland. Married Anne Talbot.
2 CONT # Eleanor Brooke (Darnall) Carroll b. 1704, Anne Arundel County, Maryland  d. 1796, Upper Marlboro, Prince George’s County, Maryland.  Married Daniel Carroll.   
2 CONT #  John Darnall,   b. 1708,   d. 9 Feb 1768, Frederick County, Maryland - probate. Married ? 
2 CONT # Ann (Darnall) Bradford b. Abt 1712, Prince George's County, Maryland d. Aft 1733, Prince George’s, Maryland.  Married John Bradford.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT She was mentioned in the will of her father.[6]
2 CONT
