1 NAME Henry Skipwith /Carter/
2 GIVN Henry Skipwith
2 _MARNM Carter
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1676
2 PLAC Barford Plantation
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY Colonial America
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1743
2 PLAC Barford Plantation
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY Colonial America
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biographical Summary===
2 CONT Henry Skipwith Carter was a documented landholder and planter in Lancaster County, Virginia. He was a member of the established Carter family of the Northern Neck, specifically the line descending from Captain Thomas Carter of "Ba
2 CONC rford." He served as a vestryman and functioned within the socio-political framework of colonial Lancaster County. While frequently identified in secondary sources as the father of various individuals—including the John Carter bor
2 CONC n in 1708—his own estate records offer only a partial view of his issue, creating the "genealogical gaps" often filled by later, unverified speculation.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Vital Statistics===
2 CONT Born: 1676, "Barford," Lancaster County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Died: 1743, Lancaster County, Virginia.
2 CONT -Will Proved: October 14, 1743, Lancaster County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Unknown
2 CONT The "Christ Church" Attribution: You will often see "Christ Church, Lancaster, Virginia" listed in online family trees (like WikiTree) as his burial site. This is a common assumption, not a confirmed fact.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Parentage===
2 CONT Father: Captain Thomas Carter (1630–1700)
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Katherine Dale (1652–1703)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage and Issue===
2 CONT Spouse: Anne Harris (m. c. 1698, Lancaster County).
2 CONT Issue (Documented)
2 CONT -Primary Probate Evidence: The will of Henry Skipwith Carter (Lancaster County Will Book 13, Page 324) identifies his children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Verified Children:
2 CONT 1. Thomas Carter
2 CONT 2. Joseph Carter
2 CONT 3. Henry Carter
2 CONT 4. Edward Carter
2 CONT 5. Peter Carter
2 CONT 6. Elizabeth Carter
2 CONT
2 CONT Researcher’s Note: The individual John Carter (c. 1708–1782) is not named in the probate documents of Henry Skipwith Carter. The absence of his name in his purported father’s will is the primary reason the parentage claim remains 
2 CONC unverified.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence Inventory & Record Analysis===
2 CONT 1. Primary Document (The Last Will and Testament)
2 CONT Document: Will of Henry Skipwith Carter, Lancaster County Will Book 13, Page 324.
2 CONT Significance: This is the legal instrument used to settle his estate. Its silence regarding a "John" is the primary evidentiary conflict for researchers attempting to link him to the Stafford County John Carter.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. The Attribution Problem
2 CONT Analysis: The assertion that John Carter (1708–1782) was his son is an external attribution. It appears to have originated from later genealogical research attempting to place "orphaned" or undocumented individuals of the same nam
2 CONC e into known, prestigious families. Without a naming clause in the 1743 will or a supporting deed of gift, this relationship fails the standard of documentary proof.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Verifiable Sources===
2 CONT 1. Lancaster County, Virginia Will Book 13, Page 324. (Will of Henry Skipwith Carter, 1743).
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Miller, Joseph Lyon. The Descendants of Capt. Thomas Carter of "Barford," Lancaster County, Virginia. (A primary genealogical reference, though it should be cross-referenced against the actual probate record for accuracy).
2 CONT
2 CONT  Updated 07/06/2026
2 CONT
2 CONT —-
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	Jun. 7, 1676 Death: 	1743 Lancaster County Virginia, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry Skipworth Carter, son of Capt Thomas Carter and Katherine Dale Carter, was born on their Barford Plantation. oral family history says he was buried in Christ Church Cemetery, however no headstone survives. - Blanche Keating 
2 CONC Collie, family researcher 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Parents:
2 CONT   Capt. Thomas Carter (1630 - 1700)
2 CONT   Katherine Skipwith Dale Carter (1652 - 1703)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Siblings:
2 CONT   Edward Carter (1671 - 1743)*
2 CONT   Thomas Carter (1672 - 1733)*
2 CONT   John Carter (1674 - 1750)*
2 CONT   Henry Skipwith Carter (1676 - 1743)
2 CONT   Diane Carter (1678 - 1680)*
2 CONT   Joseph Carter (1690 - 1765)*
2 CONT
2 CONT *Calculated relationship
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Body lost or destroyed Specifically: Burial site unk
2 CONT
2 CONT Edit Virtual Cemetery info [?]
2 CONT
2 CONT Created by: Blanche Keating Collie Record added: Jun 05, 2014  Find A Grave Memorial# 130910755 http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=carter&GSfn=henry&GSmn=skipwith&GSbyrel=all&GSdyrel=all&GSob=n&GRid=130910755&df
2 CONC =all&
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT "4th son Thos. and Kath. Carter born of a Wensdy the 7th June and was baptzed at Home by Rev Mr. Dogette on sunday after Service ye 18th Capn Wm Ball, Capn David Fox, and Mrs. Srah Fleet standing."  I bid p. 8. He died in Lancaste
2 CONC r in 1743    "At the time of his father's death in 1700 Henry Carter was in England.  He returned to Virginia, where he was married on May 6, 1704 to Anne Harris--old Prayer Book.  Her parentage is shown by a leas e for 200 acres 
2 CONC of land on Nov. 9, 1704, from Henry Carter and wife Anne, "who was daughter  Gainey Harris, loate of the county, Gent, who by his will dated 14th April, 1693, left the above mentione d premises to his daughter Ann."  Ibid, p.303. 
2 CONC    In a deposition made April 8, 1743, Henry Carter stated that he was about sixty-seven years of age.  Ibid, p. 303    March 21, 1732, "Henry Carter, of the County of Lancaster, Gent.," made his will which was probated Oct, 10, 1
2 CONC 743.  He left home plantation and negro man, Courtney, to son, Gainey Carter.  Ibid, p. 30 3
