2 CONT Jeff Carter writes on 13 Jun 2016 - The Thomas Carter who patented 220 acres in 1661 was Capt. Thomas Carter, the son of William Carter of Surry. This 220 acres was the Vintner's Company's land, part of Epaphroditus Lawson's holdi
2 CONC ngs that John Carter and Bartholomew Hoskins put together back in the 1640s (Nugent, Vol. 1, pp. 135, 151, 387); and this was a re-patent set up by John Carter. After Capt. Thomas Carter of Surry temporarily moved to Lancaster to 
2 CONC serve as Judge, John Carter had the land declared deserted and re-patented it again in 1665 to Edward Carter (Nugent, Vol. 1, p. 480). None of these lands could have been the original Barford plantation.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.palmspringsbum.org/genealogy/getperson.php?personID=I53617
