2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fulwar_Skipwith
2 CONT
2 CONT Fulwar Skipwith (February 21, 1765 — January 7, 1839) was an American diplomat and politician, who served as a U.S. Consul in Martinique, and later as the U.S. Consul-General in France. He was instrumental in negotiating the Louis
2 CONC iana Purchase in 1803 and was president of the Republic of West Florida in 1810 for 74 days; later, becoming Congressman for La.
2 CONT
2 CONT Early life
2 CONT
2 CONT Skipwith was born in Dinwiddie County, Virginia, and was a distant cousin of U.S. President Thomas Jefferson. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
