1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Col. St. Leger Codd  1635, admitted Grays Inn May 1, 1656, emigrated to Virginia by 1670, removed to Cecil Co. Maryland, died 1706. He married 1st Anne (Mottrom) Wright Fox, 2nd Anne (Bennett) Bland. She died in N
2 CONC ovember 1687 at Wharton’s Creek, Kent County, Maryland. He m. 3rd Anne (Hynson) Randall Wickes. Colonel St. Leger Codd left a will dated 7 November 1706 and proved in Maryland on 9 February 1707/8, and in Lancaster, Virginia, on 8
2 CONC  April 1708."
2 CONT [https://www.shirleyassociation.com/NewShirleySite/NonMembers/Surnames/St.%20LegerSurname.html]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/98714716/st_leger-codd
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial Feb.9, 1706/1707 in St. Paul's Churchyard, Kent Co., MD from St. Paul's register, page 252.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of William Codd and Mary St. Leger. 
2 CONT
2 CONT # 1st marriage to Anne (Mottram) [Wright] Fox
2 CONT # 2nd marriage to Ann (Bennett) Bland
2 CONT # 3rd marriage to Ann (Hyson) [Randall] Wickes.  Assumes  Codd married by next year after Anne Bennett's death in 1687.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT "Col. St. Ledger Codd, born in England 1635 died in Maryland Nov. 7, 1706; came to Virginia prior to 1670; a member of the House of Burgess & Maryland legislature for Cecil Co. He married (2) Ann Bennett, widow of Theodrick land, 
2 CONC and daughter of Colonial Governor Richard Bennett and his wife Ann Utie the daughter of John Utie who had a plantation on the James River 1622. Capt. St. Leger Codd only child of above marriage born 1676, died abt. 1731; married M
2 CONC ary Hanon daugher of Col. Hans Hanson."
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Will
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I44621&tree=Tree1
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1653-1800 Lancaster County, Virginia Wills [Ida J. Lee];
2 CONT * CODD, St. Leger, of Cecil County, Md. Will. 9 July 1706. Rec 8 Sept. 1708.
2 CONT * Wife (no name) 
2 CONT * Sons: James (all lands in county of Kent); Berkely, (all lands in Corrotoman); St. Leger (land in Cecil Co. bought of Jno. Salisbury); 
2 CONT * Daughters: Beatrix, and '''Mary Paddison'''. 
2 CONT * Extrs. Sons Berkeley and St. Leger Codd and Thos. Smythe. 
2 CONT * Wits. Henry Anderson, Thos. Simson, Locklau Orchall and Rebecca Simson. W.B. 9, p. 264.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Anne Mottrom, daughter of John and Lucy Mottrom, married 1) Richard Wright 2) David Fox 3) by 11 May 1670 to  St. Leger Codd (1st wife)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) Anne Bennett (1642 - Nov 1687), daughter of Richard and Mary Ann Bennet, married 1) Theodorick Bland 2) Aft 23 Apr 1672 to St. Leger Codd (2nd wife) 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3) Ann Hynson, daughter of Thomas Hynson and Grace , who married first, Benjamin Randall, second, Joseph Wickes (ca. 1620-1692), and third, assumes Codd married by next year after Anne Bennett's death in 1687, to St. Leger Codd (c
2 CONC a. 1634-ca. 1707/8) (3rd wife)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=98714716
2 CONT
2 CONT TAYLOR STOUT
2 CONT
2 CONT Gamaliel Taylor was born in Ottumwa, Iowa on October 13, 1845. He was married November 26, 1874, to Laura Caroline Wright. Gamaliel Taylor was the son of Eber Taylor, born in New York State September 6,1811, died in Junction City,
2 CONC  Oregon, July 20,1861 and Clarissa Stout. They were married in Iowa on April 4, 1841.
2 CONT
2 CONT Clarissa Stout was the daughter of John Stout who was born in West Virginia on December 21, 1795, died in Ottumwa, Iowa, on may 6, 1858, married in Randolph County, West Virginia, 1815 to Mary Barbara Castner (Kestner- Kessner) wh
2 CONC o was born in West Virginia June 28, 1799, died at Albia, Iowa on May 20, 1876.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Stout was the son of St. Ledger Stout who was born in Amwell Township, Hunterdon County, New Jersey, died in Beverly, West Virginia, 1806 and Anna Barcalo (Buckalow) born in New Jersey, died in West Virginia after 1806.
2 CONT
2 CONT St. Leger Stout was the son of St. Leger Codd Stout who was born in Hunterdon County, New
2 CONT
2 CONT Jersey, 1736, died in New Jersey and married in New Jersey to Susannah who died in 1770.
2 CONT
2 CONT St. Leger Codd Stout was the son of James Stout who was born in New Jersey, married between April 28, 1731-1733 to Lady Mary Ann Codd, who was born in Maryland, the daughter of Captain St. Leger Codd, who was born in Northumberlan
2 CONC d County, Virginia, about 1676, died about 1731, married in Virginia to Mary Hansen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain St.Leger Codd was the son of Col. St. Leger Codd, who was born in Virginia, died in Maryland 1707, married in Virginia to Anna (Bennett) Bland, widow of Governor Bland and daughter of Governor Richard Bennett of Virginia, 
2 CONC who married Mary Ann Utie, "daughter" (widow) of Captain John Utie.
2 CONT
2 CONT Col. St. Leger Codd was the son of William Codd, born in England, died in Ulcombe, Kent, England, 1653, married in England to Mary St. Leger.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary St. Leger was the daughter of Sir Warham St. Leger who was born in England, died in England hi 1631, married in England to Mary, daughter of Sir Rowland Hayward, Lord Mayor of London.... On down to Royalty in Italy, France, e
2 CONC tc.
2 CONT
2 CONT Exerpt from "Some Colonial Familes" by Eliose Anna May Roberts
2 CONT
