1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From "Martha's Extended Family" family tree page on Richard Kemp:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://martisgenes.info/p266.htm#i3366
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Kemp[1],[2]
2 CONT *M, d. 9 April 1782
2 CONT *Birth* Richard was born.  
2 CONT *Marriage* He married Susannah Piggott on 29 November 1745 in Fairfax, Loudoun County, Virginia.[3],[4]
2 CONT *Death* Richard died on 9 April 1782 in North Carolina .[3]
2 CONT *Burial* He was buried in April 1782 in Cane Creek, Orange County, North Carolina.[3]  
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Susannah Piggott b. 13 Mar 1724, d. 11 Sep 1781
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 
2 CONT *Prudence Kemp b. s 1746, d. 7 Apr 1787
2 CONT *Joseph Kemp+ b. s 1749
2 CONT *Margery Kemp b. 31 Oct 1759, d. 21 Mar 1798
2 CONT *Richard Kemp b. s 1761
2 CONT *Susannah Kemp b. s 1763
2 CONT *Rachel Kemp b. s 1768
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations:
2 CONT *1.[S177] William Wade Hinshaw, Encyclopedia of American Quaker Genealogy, p. 358.
2 CONT *2.[S187] Warren E Pickett, John Piggott Sr. (1680 ?- 1738) of Susquehannah Hundred in Cecil County MD. Together with some account of the Browne and Clayton families from whom his wife Margarey Brown Piggott descended, p. 5.
2 CONT *3.[S177] William Wade Hinshaw, Encyclopedia of American Quaker Genealogy.
2 CONT *4.[S187] Warren E Pickett, John Piggott Sr. (1680 ?- 1738) of Susquehannah Hundred in Cecil County MD. Together with some account of the Browne and Clayton families from whom his wife Margarey Brown Piggott descended.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------
