1 NOTE {geni:about_me} When Mary Jane Clothier was born on 5 January 1710, in Queen Anne's, Maryland, British Colonial America, her father, Robert Knapp Clothier, was 29 and her mother, Jane Kemp, was 24. She married Stephen Thomas on 5 
2 CONC January 1731, in Talbot, Maryland, British Colonial America. They were the parents of at least 12 sons and 5 daughters. She died before 2 October 1767, in Queen Anne's, Maryland, British Colonial America, at the age of 57, and was
2 CONC  buried in Queen Anne's, Maryland, British Colonial America.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/L5TT-S1P/mary-jane-clothier-1710-1767
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/105725233/mary-thomas#add-to-vc
2 CONT
2 CONT BIO: Mary was the daughter of Robert Clothier and Jane Kemp Clothier.  She married Stephen Thomas and he became a Quaker when he married into her Quaker family.  They married 5 Jan 1731 in Third Haven Meeting House in Maryland.  M
2 CONC ary died circ 1760.
2 CONT
2 CONT Stephen & Mary Clothier Thomas had 13 Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1) Sarah (Thomas) Lambdin (1731-1810)
2 CONT * 2) Rev. Robert Thomas (1733-1817)
2 CONT * 3) Stephen Thomas (Jr.) (1736-1808)
2 CONT * 4) Mary (Thomas)Primrose (1738-1774)
2 CONT * 5) William 'Ram Billy' Thomas (1741-1800
2 CONT * 6) John Thomas (1743-1814)
2 CONT * 7) Susan (Thomas) Matthews (1745-1826)
2 CONT * 8) Elizabeth (Thomas) Harry (1747-1790)
2 CONT * 9) Lewis Thomas (1750-1817)
2 CONT * 10) Brig. Gen. Tristram Thomas (1752-1817)
2 CONT * 11) Philemon Thomas (1756-1833)
2 CONT * 12) Edgar Benjamin Thomas (1756-1833)
2 CONT * 13) James Clothier Thomas (1758-1790)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Brief Life History of Mary Jane
2 CONT When Mary Jane Clothier was born on 5 January 1710, in Queen Anne's, Maryland, British Colonial America, her father, Robert Knapp Clothier, was 29 and her mother, Jane Kemp, was 24. She married Stephen Thomas on 5 January 1731, in
2 CONC  Talbot, Maryland, British Colonial America. They were the parents of at least 11 sons and 5 daughters. She died before 2 October 1767, in Queen Anne's, Maryland, British Colonial America, at the age of 57, and was buried in Queen
2 CONC  Anne's, Maryland, British Colonial America.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/LT2F-NX5/stephen-thomas-1705-1774
2 CONT
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/L5TT-S1P/mary-jane-clothier-1710-1767
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Mary a Quaker. Findagrave says Stephen became a Quaker when they married. 
