2 CONT Henry COMPTON
2 CONT Born: ABT 1584, Brambletye, East Grinstead, Sussex, England
2 CONT Died: ABT 1649
2 CONT Notes: Educated Christ Church Oxf. 1599; L. Inn 1602. Associate bencher, L. Inn 1604; custos brevium, court of common pleas C.1630; ranger, Ashdown forest; j.p. Suss. dep. lt. by 1624. It was his connexion with the Sackville famil
2 CONC y that secured Compton his parliamentary seat at East Grinstead, though his own residence was close by. His association with the Sackvilles began in boyhood, when, in 1592, his mother made a second and disastrous marriage to Rober
2 CONC t Sackville, second Earl of Dorset, then a widower. His own marriage naturally strengthened the connexion. Compton died in or before Jul 1649, when the committee for compounding ordered that the heirs to his estate should pay the 
2 CONC balance of his fine. No will has been found. Have no confirmation as of yet that Henry was indeed son of Henry Compton and Cecily Sackville. History of Parliament simply states that Henry and Cecily had ?3 sons and 3 daughters. It
2 CONC  seems highly likely however given the ties to the Sackville family between the Comptons and Bridges families.
2 CONT Father: Henry COMPTON (1º B. Compton)
2 CONT Mother: Anne SPENCER (B. Mounteagle/B. Compton/C. Dorset)
2 CONT Married: Cecily SACKVILLE
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT 1. Henry COMPTON (d. 13 May 1652, in a duel with George Brydges)
2 CONT 2. Mary COMPTON (m. John Lumley)
2 CONT 3. '''Cicely COMPTON (B. Arundell of Wardour) (m.1 Henry Arundel, B. Arundell of Wardour - m.2 John Fermor)'''
2 CONT 4. Son COMPTON
2 CONT 5. Dau. COMPTON
2 CONT 6. Son COMPTON
2 CONT Married 2: Mary BROWNE
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT 7. John COMPTON
2 CONT 8. George COMPTON
2 CONT 9. Peter COMPTON
2 CONT 10. Francis COMPTON
2 CONT 11. Son COMPTON
2 CONT 12. Son COMPTON
2 CONT http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/COMPTON.htm#Henry%20COMPTON2
