1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *''''''Elizabeth Bayning, Countess of Shepey1
2 CONT *F, #29982
2 CONT *Last Edited=21 Feb 2011
2 CONT *''''''     Elizabeth Bayning, Countess of Shepey was the daughter of Paul Bayning, 1st Viscount Bayning of Sudbury and Anne Glemham.1 She married, secondly, Lt.-Gen. David Walter.2 She married, firstly, Francis Lennard, 14th Lord
2 CONC  Dacre, son of Richard Lennard, 13th Lord Dacre and Elizabeth Throckmorton, in 1641.1
2 CONT *''''''      Her married name became Walter.2 From 1641, her married name became Lennard.1 She was created Countess of Shepey [Engalnd] on 6 September 1680, for life.2
2 CONT *''''''Children of Elizabeth Bayning, Countess of Shepey and Francis Lennard, 14th Lord Dacre
2 CONT **1.Elizabeth Lennard+3 d. 28 Dec 1701
2 CONT **2.unknown daughter Lennard2
2 CONT **3.Philadelphia Lennard+4 b. 29 Jan 1643/44
2 CONT **4.Thomas Lennard, 1st and last Earl of Essex+2 b. 13 May 1654, d. 30 Oct 1715
2 CONT **5.unknown son Lennard2 b. a 1655
2 CONT **6.unknown son Lennard2 b. a 1655
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extin
2 CONC ct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume II, page 38. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *2.[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 1014. Hereinafter cited as Burke's P
2 CONC eerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *3.[S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 2, page 2659.
2 CONT *4.[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume III, page 252.
2 CONT *From: http://thepeerage.com/p2999.htm#i29982
2 CONT *_______________
2 CONT *Viscount Bayning, of Sudbury in the County of Suffolk, was a title in the Peerage of England. It was created on 8 March 1628 for Paul Bayning, 1st Baron Bayning. He had already been created a Baronet, of Bentley Parva in the Coun
2 CONC ty of Essex, in the Baronetage of England on 24 September 1611,[1] and Baron Bayning, of Horkesley in the County of Essex, on 27 February 1628, also in the Peerage of England. He was succeeded by his son, the second Viscount. On h
2 CONC is early death in 1638 the titles became extinct.
2 CONT *The substantial Bayning estates in Essex and Sussex devolved on the Honourable Anne Bayning, daughter of the first Viscount. In 1674 the viscountcy was revived in favour when she was made Viscountess Bayning, of Foxley in the Cou
2 CONC nty of Berkshire, for life, in the Peerage of England. She was the wife of firstly Henry Murray, Groom of the Bedchamber to Charles I, and secondly of Sir John Baber. The life peerage became extinct on her death in 1678. The Bayni
2 CONC ng title was revived once again in 1797 in favour of the Viscountess Bayning's great-great-grandson Charles Townshend, who was made Baron Bayning in the Peerage of Great Britain. See this title for more information.
2 CONT *''''''The Honourable Elizabeth Bayning, daughter of the first Viscount, married Francis Lennard, 14th Baron Dacre, and was created Countess of Sheppey for life in 1680''''''. The Honourable Mary Bayning, daughter of the first Vis
2 CONC count, married William Villiers, 2nd Viscount Grandison, and was the mother of Barbara, Duchess of Cleveland, mistress of Charles II.
2 CONT *Viscount Bayning (1628)
2 CONT *Paul Bayning, 1st Viscount Bayning (1588–1629)
2 CONT *Paul Bayning, 2nd Viscount Bayning (1616–1638)
2 CONT *Viscountess Bayning (1674)
2 CONT *Anne Baber, Viscountess Bayning (1619–1678)
2 CONT *See also
2 CONT *Baron Bayning
2 CONT *Duke of Cleveland
2 CONT *References
2 CONT *1.^ George Edward Cockayne Complete baronetage Volume 1 1900
2 CONT *Leigh Rayment's Peerage Pages [self-published source?][better source needed]
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viscount_Bayning
2 CONT *See also http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baron_Dacre
2 CONT *______________
