2 CONT From Wikipedia:
2 CONT
2 CONT Humphrey Coningsby (born ca. 1623) was an English politician who sat in the House of Commons from 1641 to 1644. He supported the Royalist side in the English Civil War.
2 CONT
2 CONT Coningsby was the eldest son of Fitzwilliam Conningsby, of Hampton Court, Herefordshire. He matriculated at Lincoln College, Oxford on 23 February 1638, aged 15. He was of the Middle Temple in 1639.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT In November 1641, Coningsby was elected Member of Parliament for Herefordshire in the Long Parliament, replacing his father who had been expelled as a monopolist.[2] He supported the King and was disabled from sitting in parliamen
2 CONC t on 22 January 1644.
2 CONT
2 CONT Coningsby married Lettice Loftus, eldest daughter of Sir Arthur Loftus of Rathfarnham, Ireland. Their son Thomas became Earl Coningsby
