2 CONT *'''   FRANCIS HOWARD II., brother of Thomas I.: Earl of Effingham, & Baron Howard of Effingham. B. after 1681; st. Hon. Francis Howard, Esq., [1696]-1725; Captain & Lieut-Colonel, 3rd Regt. of Foot Guards, July 26, 1722; succ. as
2 CONC  8th Baron Howard of Effingham, July 10, 1725; Lieutenant, & Lieut-Colonel, 1st Troop of Horse Grenadier Guards, July 15, 1731; cr. Earl of Effingham, Dec. 8, 1731; Deputy Earl Marshal of England, Dec. 13, 1731; Colonel, (20th) Re
2 CONC gt. of Foot, July 22, 1732; Captain & Colonel, 2nd Troop of Horse Grenadier Guards, June 21, 1737; Colonel of Horse, June 21, 1737; Brigadier-General, July 2, 1739; Captain & Colonel, 4th Troop of Horse Guards, Dec. 22, 1740; m. (
2 CONC 1) Digna, d. of Major-General O'Ferrel; m. (2) Anne, sister of Robert Bristow, Esq., July, 1728; d. Feb. 12, 1743. __________________
2 CONT *'''The Lords Effingham and the American colonies (1976)
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/details/lordseffinghamam00feld
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/lordseffinghamam00feld#page/3/mode/1up
2 CONT *Francis, 5th Baron Howard of Effingham (1643-1695), of Great Bookham, Surrey, was the great-grandson of Sir William Howard of Linfeld, who was the second son of William, first Lord Howard of Effingham. Since Lord Francis Howard p
2 CONC layed a role in pre-revolutionary days as Governor of Virginia, he is dealt with at length in the following chapter.
2 CONT *He was succeeded by his second but eldest surviving son, Thomas, as 6th Baron Howard of Effingham (1682-1725). Lord Thomas had no sons, and the Barony devolved upon his brother
2 CONT *'''Francis, 1st Earl of Effingham and 7th Baron Howard (1683- 1742). His Lordship was a military officer of high rank. Succeeded by his only son
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/lordseffinghamam00feld#page/4/mode/1up
2 CONT *   Thomas, 2nd Earl of Effingham and 8th Baron Howard (1714-1763), also a military officer of rank. he was succeeded by his elder son.
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/lordseffinghamam00feld#page/6/mode/1up
2 CONT *Lord Francis Howard, 5th Baron of Effingham, of Great Bookham, Surrey was baptized September 17, 1643. His first wife was Philadelphia, daughter of Sir Thomas Pelham, Bt., whom he married July 8, 1673, and by whom he had three so
2 CONC ns and three daughters. She died August 13, 1685. On January 20, 1689, he married Susan, widow of Philip Harbord, of Stanninghall, Norfolk, and daughter of Sir Henry Felton, Bt., after he had returned to England.
2 CONT *This second marriage was to last a little more than six years, since Lord Effingham died March 30, 1695. She survived him thirty-one years. The title passed to his second but eldest surviving son, Thomas. _____________________
