2 CONT *''''''Thomas Pelham, 1st Baron Pelham of Laughton1
2 CONT *''''''M, #28048, b. circa 1653, d. 23 February 1711/12
2 CONT *Last Edited=13 Feb 2011
2 CONT *'''''' Thomas Pelham, 1st Baron Pelham of Laughton was born circa 1653.4 He was the son of Sir John Pelham, 3rd Bt. and Lady Lucy Sydney.3 He married, firstly, Elizabeth Jones, daughter of Sir William Jones, on 26 November 1679.4
2 CONC  He married, secondly, Lady Grace Holles, daughter of Gilbert Holles, 3rd Earl of Clare and Grace Pierrepont, on 21 May 1686.1 He died on 23 February 1711/12.4
2 CONT *''''''     Thomas Pelham, 1st Baron Pelham of Laughton held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.) (Whig) for East Grinstead from 1678 to 1679.4 He held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.) (Whig) for Sussex between 1679 
2 CONC and 1702.4 He was Commissioner of Customs between 1689 and 1691.4 He held the office of Lord of the Treasury from March 1689/90 to March 1690/91.4 He held the office of Lord of the Treasury from 1698 to 1699.4 He held the office o
2 CONC f Lord of the Treasury from 1701 to 1702.4 He succeeded to the title of 4th Baronet Pelham, of Laughton, co. Sussex [E., 1611] circa January 1702/3.4 He was created 1st Baron Pelham of Laughton, co. Sussex [England] on 16 December
2 CONC  1706.4
