1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LHNW-85T
2 CONT
2 CONT There appears to be little documentation on this William Lunsford, other than he arrived in Virginia with his father, Sir Thomas Lunsford. Some biographers mistakenly claim he was the son of Thomas Lunsford's first wife, Ann (or M
2 CONC ary) Hudson. He was, in fact, the son of Sir Thomas's second wife, Katherine Neville. (see the proof at www.genealogybyvirgil.com) No sources definitively affirm his wife. Some mention a Blackwell, while others suggest a Griffin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT As the eldest son of a knight, he automatically inherited the title of Esquire. Lunsford is the correct spelling of the surname as evidenced by his father's signature on letters
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:
2 CONT Sir Thomas Lunsford 1604–1653  •  LZLS-P1H ​​
2 CONT Marriage: 1 June 1640 Binfield, Berkshire, England
2 CONT Katherine Neville 1612–1649  •  2HXS-MYT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT The Lunsfords had been in Sussex England for at least 500 years. William Sr. was the first to emigrate to Virginia where the next several generations would settle in the New World.
2 CONT  The Stuarts returned to the restored throne in 1660, though continued questions over religion and power resulted in the deposition of another Stuart king, James II, in the Glorious Revolution (1688). 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://indirectlyconnected.wordpress.com/2018/03/12/the-lunsford-immigrant-and-the-three-musketeers/
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-65328531-2-4196/william-lunsford-in-myheritage-family-trees
2 CONT
