1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Edmund Thomas (1633–1677) was a Welsh politician who sat in the House of Commons in 1654 and 1656 and sat in Cromwell's Upper House. He supported the Parliamentary cause during the English Civil War and the Interre
2 CONC gnum.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT From https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edmund_Thomas_(Parliamentarian)_
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas came from family that were for many years seated at Wenvoe. The original name was Harpwaye, of Tresimont, in Herefordshire: they took the name of Thomas, as a result of a marriage with Catherine, daughter and sole heir of T
2 CONC homas ap Thomas, of Wenvoe Castle.[4] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas married firstly Elizabeth Morgan, daughter of Sir Lewis Morgan of Rhiwperra and sister of Thomas Morgan. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married secondly Mary Lewis, daughter of Sir Thomas Lewis of Penmark Place at Wenvoe on 1 August 1671. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His son and heir William Thomas married the daughter of Philip, Lord Wharton.
