1 NAME Edward /Hungerford/ KB, MP
2 GIVN Edward
2 SURN Hungerford
2 NSFX KB, MP
2 _MARNM Hungerford
1 NAME Sir Edward Hungerford, KB, MP
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Trafalgar Square
2 ADDR
3 CITY London
3 STAE Greater London
3 CTRY UK
1 BIRT
2 DATE 20 OCT 1632
2 PLAC Farleigh Castle
2 ADDR
3 CTRY England
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1711
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1690-1715/member/hungerford-sir-edward-1632-1711
2 CONT
2 CONT b. 20 Oct. 1632, 1st s. of (Sir) Anthony Hungerford† of Farleigh Castle, Som. and Blackbourton, Oxon. by Rachel, da. of Rice Jones of Asthall, Oxon.  educ. Queen’s, Oxf. 1649.  m. (1) Dec. 1657 (with £4,000), Jane (d. 1664), da. a
2 CONC nd h. of Sir John Hele of Clifton Maybank, Dorset, and Wembury, Devon, 1s. (d.v.p.) 3da. (2 d.v.p.); (2) 3 Feb. 1666 (with £1,000), Jane (d. 1674), da. of Hugh Culme of Burlescombe, Devon, 2s. (1 d.v.p.); (3) by 1682, Jane (d. 170
2 CONC 3), da. and h. of George Digby of Sandon, Staffs., wid. of Charles, 4th Baron Gerard of Gerard’s Bromley, Staffs. 1s.  suc. fa. 1657; KB 23 Apr. 1661.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 287 [http://archive.org/stream/dormantextinctba02bankuoft#page/n7/mode/2up  Dormant and Extinct Baronage of England]
2 CONT
2 CONT http://openlibrary.org/books/OL7022374M
2 CONT
2 CONT "This family, it feems, had feats at Farley, in Somerfetfhire ; Black - Bourton, in Oxfordlliire; Down-Amney, and Winrufli, in Gloucefterfhire; Cadenham, in Wiltfhire, &c. The Hungerfords of Farley, became extinct in the direct li
2 CONC ne, in the perfon of Sir Edward Hungerford; who having fold the Farley eftate, died in 1711, at the very great age of 115: his fon and grandfon dying before him without iflue. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Peach Hungerford, Efquire, now of Dinglcy-Hall, in Northamptonfhire, fome time one of the reprefentativcs in parliament for the county of Leicefler, is lineally defcended from the Hungerfords of Down-Amncy ; and retains polTc
2 CONC flion of the family vaults in Farley caftle and Salifbury cathedral".
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Allegedly ended his days living on charity as a Kt of Windsor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dissipated his family's once vast landed wealth, selling 30 manors, plus the manor of Farleigh, together with Farleigh Castle itself (the last two for £56,000 – roughly £4,000,000 in late-1990s terms).
2 CONT
2 CONT He was Member of Parliament (M.P.) Chippenham , 1678, 1679 and 1681, New Shoreham 1685, 1688 and 1690 and Steyning 1695, 1698, 1700 and 1702 in 1660.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was Knight, Order of the Bath (K.B.) in 1661.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was resided when in London at Hungerford Ho, on the site of the present Charing Cross Station (and the northern bank of the Thames end of Hungerford Bridge, hence its name) until this was burnt down , Lieutenant-Colonel Regimen
2 CONC t of Archers 1661 and Co in 1669.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 23 November 1692 married 3rd Jane Digby (died ) and was buried 8 July 1711 further issue(?).
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1748 a s of Sir Edward's either by his 2nd or 3rd wife died at Black Bourton, Oxon, when according to some sources the male representation of the Hungerfords died out, although a branch seems to have settled in Ireland around t
2 CONC he mid-17th century and.
