1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A second son, called Colonel Anthony Hungerford, entered Nicolas's service as a secret agent in England, in the royalist interest, in 1655, in the hope, it is said, of obtaining his elder brother's estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/177934973/anthony-hungerford
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription
2 CONT Near this place lyeth the body of Colel. Anthony Hungerford of Blackbourton of this County, second son of Anthony Hungerford of Farleigh Castle in the County of Somerset, Esq. He married Mary Saintbarbe of Whiteparish in the Count
2 CONC y of Wilts, widdow. He departed this life on the seaventh day of June in the year of our Lord 1703 and in the 69th year of his age.
2 CONT Gravesite Details
2 CONT North Chapel contains marble wall cartouche to Anthony Hungerford, 1703, with richly carved military trophies.
