1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [ http://www.cracroftspeerage.co.uk/online/content/shelleyb1611.htm?zoom_highlight=Sir+John+Shelley+3rd+Bt Sir John Shelley, 3rd Bt. was born: after 1662 Ref: Cracrofts]
2 CONT
2 CONT mar. (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT Hon Winifred Neville (bur. spm. 24 May 1687 at Clapham, co. Sussex), only dau. of George [Neville], 1st Baron Bergavenny, by his wife Mary Gifford, dau. of Dr Thomas Gifford, of Dunton Waylett, co. Essex, by his wife Anne Brooksby
2 CONC , dau. and hrss. of Gregory Brooksby, of Burstall, co. Leicester
2 CONT
2 CONT only child by first wife
2 CONT * Frances Shelley, later de jure suo jure Baroness Bergavenny
2 CONT
2 CONT mar. (2)
2 CONT
2 CONT c. 1690 Mary Gage (mar. (2) George Mathew, of Thurles, co. Tipperary; d. between Apr 1717 and 1722), dau. and eventually cohrss. of Sir John Gage, 4th Bt., of Firle, co. Sussex, by his first wife Mary Middlemore, dau. of Robert Mi
2 CONC ddlemore, of Edgbaston, co. Warwick
2 CONT
2 CONT children by second wife:
2 CONT * Sir John Shelley, 4th Bt.
2 CONT * Richard Shelley, Commissioner of the Stamp Office, mar. ..... Fleetwood, and had issue
2 CONT * Mary Shelley, mar. in or before 1712 Sir John Lawson, 3rd Bt., of Brough-in-Catterick, co. York, and had issue
2 CONT * Elizabeth Shelley, mar. Edward Sheldon
2 CONT * Catherine Shelley, mad. George Mathew, and had issue died: 25 Apr 1703 (bur. at Clapham, co. Sussex) suc. by: son by second wife
2 CONT
