1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Mary Betts is mentioned in the The memorial history of Hartford County, Connecticut, 1633-1884, Volume 1 edited by James Hammond Trumbull as having been the School Dame. This [https://www.geni.com/people/Mary-Bet
2 CONC ts/6000000072249013151 Mary Betts] died in 1647 which is not consistent with other sates I've seen. Specifically, the will of Thomas Betts from 1688 still refers to his wife, Mary.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/Grace-Morris/5678779172790103812 Is not a known daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Betts-of-Norwalk/6000000006802928410?through=5678779172790103812 & Mary his wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Name also seen as Mary Bridge with no supporting evidence, nor is there an indication Thomas Betts had more than one wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT from: http://www.onegreatfamily.com/fh/Grace-Betts/603764231<br/>
2 CONT Looks like Mary was born Redmond and perhaps married a Bridge, since several of Grace's siblings have a last name of Bridge.
