1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Originally known as William Rayment.
2 CONT
2 CONT Genealogies of the Raymond Families of New England, 1650-1 to 1886', compiled by Samuel Raymond and published in 1886, reports at page 121:
2 CONT >The Court records of Salem, Dec. 28, 1697, say:
2 CONT >>"The testimony of William Raymond, aged 60 years or thereabouts. Testifieth and saith that I, said Raymond, came to New England about the year '52"
2 CONT >He was a prominent citizen of the town he was in the Narragansett fight, 1765; was appointed to the General Court in 1683, Lieut. Commander of Beverly and Wenham troop; he commanded a company in the Canada Expedition, 1690 and wa
2 CONC s a Deputy for Beverly, 1685 and 6.
2 CONT
