1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *From http://www.thepeerage.com/p3425.htm#i34242   Reverend Maurice Suckling was born in 1676 at Woodton, Norfolk, England. He was the son of Robert Suckling and Sarah Shelton. He married Mary Turner, daughter of S
2 CONC ir Charles Turner, 1st Bt. and Mary Walpole, in 1723. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 21 September 1730.1 He was buried on 23 September 1730 at Barsham, Suffolk, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT He graduated from Trinity College, Cambridge University, Cambridge, Cambridgeshire, England, in 1696 with a Bachelor of Arts (B.A.). He graduated from Trinity College, Cambridge University, Cambridge, Cambridgeshire, England, in 1
2 CONC 699 with a Master of Arts (M.A.). He was the Rector between 1701 and 1730 at Woodton, Norfolk, England. He was the Rector between 1714 and 1730 at Barsham, Norfolk, England. He held the office of Prebendary of Westminster between 
2 CONC 1725 and 1730. He graduated from Trinity College, Cambridge University, Cambridge, Cambridgeshire, England, in 1728 with a Doctor of Divinity (D.D.).
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Reverend Maurice Suckling and Mary Anne Turner:     Robert Suckling b. 2 Jun 1724, d. 16 Mar 1724/25;     Catherine Suckling+ b. 9 Mar 1725, d. 26 Dec 1767;     Captain Maurice Suckling b. 4 May 1726, d. 17 Jul 1778;  
2 CONC    Robert Suckling b. 9 Jun 1727, d. 19 Aug 1727;     John Suckling b. 9 Feb 1728, d. 18 Feb 1728;     William Suckling b. 15 Jul 1730
