1 NAME James /Browne/
2 GIVN James
2 SURN Browne
2 _MARNM Browne
2 NICK James Browne (Quaker Minister)
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC East Nottingham Friends Meeting
2 ADDR
3 CITY Calvert
3 STAE Maryland
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1656
2 ADDR
3 CITY Sywell Parish, Wellsborough
3 STAE England
1 BAPM
2 DATE 27 MAR 1656
2 ADDR
3 CITY Sywell Parish, Wellsborough
3 STAE England
1 DEAT
2 DATE 2 JUN 1715
2 PLAC East Nottingham Friends Meeting
2 ADDR
3 CITY Calvert
3 STAE Province of Maryland
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 OCCU Weaver
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} (Ben M. Angel notes: East Nottingham is the name of the [http://www.mht.maryland.gov/nr/NRDetail.aspx?NRID=427&COUNTY=Cecil&FROM=NRCountyList.aspx '''Friends Meeting''' ], or Quaker Congregation/Community, that Jam
2 CONC es Brown helped to found in Cecil County, Maryland - not to be confused with Nottingham Township in adjacent Chester County, Pennsylvania, which he and others were trying to extend south into present Maryland):
2 CONT
2 CONT Unattributed information on James Brown[e] 
2 CONT
2 CONT James Browne, born 27 Mar 1656 in Boarsworth, Wellingsboro, Northampton, England;  died Bet. 1715 - 1716 in Nottingham Twp., Chester County, PA. He was the son of . Richard Browne and Mary Master. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Honour Clayton 08 Aug 1679 in Marcus Hook, Delaware County, PA. ( Honour Clayton, born 18 Mar 1661/62 in Rumboldswyke, Sussex, England; died in Chester County, PA. She was the daughter of  William Clayton and Prudence M
2 CONC ickel.)
2 CONT
2 CONT More About James Browne: Burial: Bet. 1715 - 1716, East Nottingham Twp., Chester County, PA
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Honour Clayton: Alternate Dates: 29 Nov 1662, May be date of birth
2 CONT
2 CONT More About James Browne and Honour Clayton: Alternate dates: 08 Jun 1679, May be date of marriage Marriage: 08 Aug 1679, Marcus Hook, Delaware County, PA
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Because of the intermarriage of Quakers, James and Honour are the 8th great-grandparents three times over for Frances' generation and 9th great-grandparents twice over. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From "Martha's Extended Family" family tree page on James Brown: 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://martisgenes.info/p80.htm#i951
2 CONT
2 CONT James Brown[1],[2],[3]
2 CONT *M, b. 27 March 1656, d. 1715
2 CONT *Father* Richard Browne b. s 1625, d. 9 Aug 1662 
2 CONT *Mother* Mary (?) b. 1632 
2 CONT *Birth* James was born on 27 March 1656 in Poddington, Northampton, England.[4],[5] He was the son of Richard Browne and Mary (?).  
2 CONT *Marriage* He married Honour Clayton on 8 August 1679 in Burlington, Burlington County, New Jersey.,[6],[5]
2 CONT *Death* James died in 1715 in Chester County, Pennsylvania, .[4],[7]  
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Honour Clayton b. 18 Mar 1662 
2 CONT *Children 
2 CONT **1. James Brown b. 17 Mar 1681
2 CONT **2. William Brown+ b. 13 Mar 1682, d. 1716
2 CONT **3. Clayton Brown b. 1 Oct 1685
2 CONT **4. Jeremiah Brown+ b. c 1687, d. 7 May 1767
2 CONT **5. Margery Brown+ b. c 1691, d. 24 Feb 1738
2 CONT **6. Daniel Brown+ b. s 1695
2 CONT **7. Mary Brown b. s 1701
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.[S184] James E. Bellarts, The Quaker Yeoman, A Genealogy of Clayton,m Reynolds, Beals, Brown and Descended and Related Lines, p. 42.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.[S180] William Wade Hinshaw, Encyclopedia of American Quaker Genealogy, p. 200.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.[S187] Warren E Pickett, John Piggott Sr. (1680 ?- 1738) of Susquehannah Hundred in Cecil County MD. Together with some account of the Browne and Clayton families from whom his wife Margarey Brown Piggott descended, p. 15.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.[S184] James E. Bellarts, The Quaker Yeoman, A Genealogy of Clayton,m Reynolds, Beals, Brown and Descended and Related Lines.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.[S187] Warren E Pickett, John Piggott Sr. (1680 ?- 1738) of Susquehannah Hundred in Cecil County MD. Together with some account of the Browne and Clayton families from whom his wife Margarey Brown Piggott descended.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.[S180] William Wade Hinshaw, Encyclopedia of American Quaker Genealogy.
2 CONT
2 CONT 7.[S2952] Pennsylvania Chester County, Wills 1713-1825.
2 CONT
