1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Sarah-Carr/6000000042152748027
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah GREELEY 1, 2 was born 21 Mar 1676 in Salisbury, Essex, Massachusetts. She married Captain Richard CARR on 10 Aug 1727 in Salisbury, Essex, Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT This source seems to mix up Richard Carr, Sr. and Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Carr Sr. married Sarah Greeley as his 3rd wife.  The children listed below were his son’s.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Genealogy of the Greely-Greeley Family''. Page 29.  < [https://archive.org/details/genealogyofgreel00gree/page/28/mode/2up?q=Francis+hook Archive.Org] > 
2 CONT
2 CONT 10.   '''SARAH GREELE''' 3( Philip2, Andrew1) , b. at Salisbury, Mass., March 21, 1675-6; m. at Salisbury, Mass., by Rev. Caleb Gushing, Aug. 10, 1727, Capt. Richard Carr, b. at Salisbury, Mass., son of Richard Carr. He was drowne
2 CONC d at Salisbury, Mass., at about nine o'clock at night, March 4, 1733-4. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She m. 2d, at Salisbury, Mass., May 17, 1738, William Hook.* He d., Salisbury, Mass., Dec. 26, 1743. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children : —
2 CONT # 59. James Carr, b. Salisbury, Mass., Oct. 3, 1728.
2 CONT # 60. Mary Carr, b. Salisbury, Mass., July 6, 1730.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT William Hook, son of William Hook and Elizabeth, married 2nd on 17 May 1738 in Salisbury, Massachusetts Bay Colony to Sarah Greeley (1675 - 1750), daughter of Philip Greeley and Sarah Mary Ilsley.  She was the widow of Richard Car
2 CONC r (1659-1727).  No children by second marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT # Greeley, George Hiram. ''Genealogy of the Greely-Greeley Family''. Boston, MA: Frank Wood Printer, 1905. Page 29.  < [https://archive.org/details/genealogyofgreel00gree/page/28/mode/2up?q=Francis+hook Archive.Org] > William Hook
2 CONC  was twice married. His first wife was Mary, who died at Salisbury, Mass., Oct. 25, 1736. By this marriage there were several children, but none by the second.
2 CONT # “''Humphrey Hooke of Bristol and his family and descendants in England and America during the seventeenth century''.” by Todd, Frederick W. (Frederick William), 1842-1902 Publication date 1938.  Page 132.  < [https://archive.org
2 CONC /details/humphreyhookeofb00todd/page/132/mode/1up Archive.Org] >
2 CONT #https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Greeley-705
