1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Hannah Winsley
2 CONT * Birth	Mar 23 1689
2 CONT * Parents: Ephraim Winsley and Mary Greeley
2 CONT * Spouses: 1) Thomas Philbrook - Marriage	1710 2) Andrew Greele - Marriage	Jan 22 1743
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From ''Genealogy of the Greely-Greeley family'', Page 47.
2 CONT
2 CONT 40. ANDREW GREELE3 (Benjamin 2, Andrew 1), b. at Haverhill, Mass., March 17, 1683-3; m. Salisbury, Mass. (published Dec. 19, 1703), Eleanor Hook, b. at Salisbury, Mass., Feb. 20, 1673, dau. of William and Elizabeth Hook. She d. Sa
2 CONC lisbury, Mass., Nov. 23, 1727. He m. 2d, at Salisbury, Mass., Jan. 23, 1743, Hannah Winsley, b. at Salisbury, Mass., March 23, 1688-9, dau. of Ephraim and Mary (Greele) Winsley (No. 29). He d. Salisbury, Mass., Nov. 9, 1747.
2 CONT
2 CONT Administration on his estate was granted his widow, Hannah, but by reason of bodily infirmity and age, she refused the trust, and asked that Francis Hook, husband of Edith Greele, be ap- pointed, which request was granted May 2, 1
2 CONC 748.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Winsley-19
2 CONT
2 CONT Ephraim Winsley was born April 14, 1681 in Salisbury, Massachusetts. He married Mary Greeley there on Jan 26, 1668[1] and they had at least eight children.[2] He died in Salisbury on October 8, 1709.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT 7.  Hannah b Mar 23, 1688/9; married Andrew Greeley
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
