1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LZBQ-JMJ
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/69614650/samuel-greele
2 CONT ----
2 CONT aka Greeley
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Greeley-97
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The revered.. Deacon Samuel Greele, was born on December 22nd of 1695, to Joseph Greele and Martha Wilford of Haverhill, Essex, Massachusetts Bay (of British Colonial America).
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel was the first born of his 8 other Siblings.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Surname Greele changed to Greeley"
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the Greely-Greeley Genealogy.. Samuel was a bricklayer, a husband of Three Wives, by which he fathered several Children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel married 1st, Rachel Robenson/ Robinson abt 1719 in Haverhill, Essex, Massachusetts Bay (or Hudson New Hampshire ?). Rachel passed away on September 19th of 1758 in Hudson, Hillsborough, New Hampshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Greeley, May 10, 1721 in New Hampshire. Birth & Christening record-[1]
2 CONT Meriam Greeley, October 8, 1722 in New Hampshire. Birth & Christening record-[2]
2 CONT Mehitable Greeley, October 1, 1724 in New Hampshire. Birth & Christening record-[3]
2 CONT Martha Greeley, September 26, 1726 in New Hampshire. Birth & Christening record-[4]
2 CONT Rachel Greeley, October 15, 1729 in New Hampshire. Birth & Christening record-[5]
2 CONT Jonathan Greeley, February 26, 1732 in New Hampshire. Birth & Christening record-[6]
2 CONT Mary Greeley, March 1, 1734 in New Hampshire. Birth & Christening record-[7]
2 CONT Hannah Greeley, November 22, 1736 in New Hampshire. Birth &Christening record-[8]
2 CONT Nathaniel Greeley, March 14, 1739 in New Hampshire. Birth & Christening record-[9]
2 CONT Samuel at some point in his time, become known as Deacon Samuel Greele
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel married his 2nd wife, Jane French on April 19th of 1759 until her passing in June of 1762, in New Hampshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married his 3rd wife, Susanah Merrill on January 9th of 1764 in New Hampshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Kendall Mellem
2 CONT
2 CONT -1)South End (or Ford Cemetery) in Hudson: Susanah Greele, Wid. of Dea. Samuel Greele, died Nov. 15, 1784. Age 72 yrs. 
2 CONT -2)The Early Church Records of Hudson, NH as kept by Rev. Nathaniel Merrill and published separately and later by the NEHGS, give the following items listed under Marriages by Rev.Nathaniel Merrill: 
2 CONT -1759 Apr. 19 Samuel Grele & ____ French. (Note: there is a definite blank space where the first name should appear) 
2 CONT -1764 Jan 9 Samuel Grele & Susanna Merrill 
2 CONT -3) The Hudson VR's gives the following death: Greeley, Susanna AGE: 73 05 Nov 1784 Hudson, NH 
2 CONT Deacon Samuel Greele had passed away on May 25th of 1771 in Hudson, Hillsborough, New Hampshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Blodgett Cemetery in Hudson, Hillsborough County, New Hampshire, United States. [10]
2 CONT
2 CONT
