1 TITL Capt.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Robert Denison, b. Sept. 7, 1673, was married, in 1696, to Joanna Stanton, dau. of Robert and Joanna (Gardner) Stanton. He settled in the North Society of New London, (then called Mohegan, now Montville.) In 1710, 
2 CONC he bought of Owaneco, chief sachem of the Mohegans, 500 acres of land in Mohegan, on the east side of Gardner's Lake, for which he paid £20. At that time he was "Capt. Robert Denison of Stonington ;" but soon afterwards, he settle
2 CONC d on the land he had bought of Owaneco. In 1716, he bought of the Mohegans another tract of land.
2 CONT
2 CONT DENISON GENEALOGY, ANCESTORS AND DESCENDANTS OF CAPTAIN GEORGE DENISON, Of Stonington Connecticut, by John Denison Baldwin and William Clift, Worcester, MA, 1881, p 17, 60
2 CONT ----
2 CONT HISTORY OF THE TOWN OF STONINGTON, county of New London, Connecticut, from its first settlement in 1649 to 1900, by Richard Anson Wheeler, New London, CT, 1900, p. 339, 341, 592
2 CONT ----
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~nanc/denison/aqwg04.htm#392
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert DENISON (John Borodell , George ) was born 17 Sep 1673 in Roxbury, Suffolk Co., Massachusetts and was christened 14 Oct 1677. He died 1737.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert married (1) Joanna STANTON, daughter of Robert STANTON and Joanna GARDINER, about 1696 in Stonington, New London Co., Connecticut. Joanna was born 5 Jun 1679 in Stonington, New London Co., Connecticut. She died about 1717 i
2 CONC n Montville, New London Co., Connecticut.
2 CONT
2 CONT     m. Robert Denison
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     + 	138 	M 	i 	Robert DENISON was christened 27 Mar 1697 and died 1766.
2 CONT
2 CONT     + 	139 	M 	ii 	John DENISON was christened 8 May 1698 and died 28 Nov 1776.
2 CONT
2 CONT     + 	140 	F 	iii 	Joanna DENISON was christened 27 Aug 1699 and died Nov 1733.
2 CONT
2 CONT       	141 	M 	iv 	
2 CONT
2 CONT     	Nathaniel DENISON was christened 19 Apr 1702 in 1st Church of Stonington, Stonington, New London Co., Connecticut. He died 1722.
2 CONT
2 CONT     DENISON GENEALOGY, by E. Glenn Denison, Josephine Middleton Peck, Donald L.
2 CONT
2 CONT         Jacobus, The Pequot Press, Inc. Stonington, CT, 1963. Page 4.
2 CONT
2 CONT       	142 	M 	v 	
2 CONT
2 CONT     	Andrew DENISON was christened 23 Apr 1704 in Stonington, New London Co., Connecticut. He died 1727.
2 CONT
2 CONT     DENISON GENEALOGY, by E. Glenn Denison, Josephine Middleton Peck, Donald L.
2 CONT
2 CONT         Jacobus, The Pequot Press, Inc. Stonington, CT, 1963. Page 4.
2 CONT
2 CONT       	143 	F 	vi 	
2 CONT
2 CONT     	Sarah DENISON was christened 14 Apr 1706 in 1st Church of New London, New London, New London Co., Connecticut. She died 1714.
2 CONT
2 CONT     DENISON GENEALOGY, by E. Glenn Denison, Josephine Middleton Peck, Donald L.
2 CONT
2 CONT         Jacobus, The Pequot Press, Inc. Stonington, CT, 1963. Page 4.
2 CONT
2 CONT     + 	144 	F 	vii 	Ann DENISON was christened 21 Mar 1708 and died 1792.
2 CONT
2 CONT     + 	145 	M 	viii 	Thomas DENISON was christened 4 Dec 1709 and died 24 Oct 1787.
2 CONT
2 CONT     + 	146 	F 	ix 	Lucy DENISON was christened 12 Aug 1711.
2 CONT
2 CONT       	147 	F 	x 	
2 CONT
2 CONT     	Elizabeth DENISON was born about 1713 in Stonington, New London Co., Connecticut. She died in his youth.
2 CONT
2 CONT     + 	148 	F 	xi 	Abigail DENISON was christened 6 Nov 1715.
2 CONT
2 CONT       	149 	M 	xii 	
2 CONT
2 CONT     	George DENISON was christened 13 Oct 1717 in 1st Church of Stonington, Stonington, New London Co., Connecticut. He died in his youth.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert also married (2) Dorothy STANTON, daughter of Thomas STANTON Jr. and Sarah DENISON, about 1718. Dorothy was christened 24 Apr 1681.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     + 	150 	M 	xiii 	George DENISON is printed as #87.
2 CONT
2 CONT     + 	151 	F 	xiv 	Dorothy DENISON is printed as #88.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Capt. Robert Denison, the first of the name that settled in the North Parish of New London, now Montville, was son of John Denison and Phebe Lay, and a grandson of Capt. George Denison, the first of Stonington. This Capt. George D
2 CONC enison was born in England in 1618. He came to this country with his father and two brothers about1631, and settled at Roxbury, Mass.  In 1640 he married Bridget Thompson of Stonington, by whom he had two daughters. Upon her death
2 CONC , in 1643, Capt. Denison returned to England and engaged in the civil war, which was then going on there. And the tradition in the family is that in an engagement in Ireland he was dangerously wounded, and in this situation was ca
2 CONC st upon the hospitality of Mr. John Brodil of Cork, a gentleman of wealth who had an only daughter, Anne Brodil, who became a ministering angel to him in his critical condition and great need. That he recovered and persuaded her t
2 CONC o marry him and to share his fortunes in this new world the sequel of events clearly prove. He had by her seven children, John, George, William, Anne, Margaret, Brodil, and Mary. The two daughters by his first wife were Sarah, bor
2 CONC n 20 March, 1641; married ___Stanton; and Hannah, born 20 May, 1643; married ___Saxton. Capt. George Denison was the first representative of Stonington in the General Assembly at Hartford. He died 23 Oct., 1694, while attending th
2 CONC e assembly at Hartford, at the age of 76. His widow died 26 Sept., 1712, aged 97.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Denison, their eldest son, born 1646, at Roxbury; married in 1667 Phebo Lay of Saybrook, daughter of Robert Lay. Their son, Robert, born 17 Oct., 1673, married Joanna Stanton, born 5 Jan., 1679. He is known to the records as 
2 CONC Capt. Robert Denison of the North Parish. In January, 1709, Owaneco, the sachem of the Mohegans, convoyed by deed to Capt. Robert Denison, then of Stonington, a tract of 500 acres of land " on the southmost side of the little pond
2 CONC  called ' Opsoboxuk' and adjoining land of Oliver Manwaring in the North Parish of New London." He moved on to this land within two or three years thereafter, and built his house. This house is still standing, though it may have b
2 CONC een several times remodeled since. This house was afterwards occupied by Erastus Gardner, and now by Mr. Theodore Lehman. Capt. Robert Denison died about 1737.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children by Joanna. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Robert, bap. 21 March, 16U7; m. Deborah Oriswold. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. John, b. 28 Nov., 16US; in. Patience Griawold. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Johanna, b. ; m. Thomas Morehouse. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Mary, b. ; died young. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Nathaniel, b. ; died about 30 years old, unm. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Sarah, b. ; died about 11 years' old. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 8. Andrew, b. ; died in the West Indies at 23. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 10. Thomas, b. ; m. Elizabeth Baile.y in 1709. 9. Anna, b. ; m. Capt. James Fitch. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 11. Lucy, b. ; m. Samuel Rogers. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 12. Elizabeth, b. ; died young. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 13. George, b. ; died in infancy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 14. Abigail, b. ; m. Wm. Wattles of Lebanon. His 
2 CONT
2 CONT first wife died and ho married for his second, Widow 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorothy Frink. Her maiden name was Stanton. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children by Dorothy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 15. George, b. ; m. Hannah Dodgo. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 16. Dorothy, Imp. 30 Dec., 1722; in. 1st, Ebonezor Rogers; 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2d, Dea. David Copp; 3d, Jonathan Avery
2 CONT
