2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT [[Category: Stonington_Connecticut-Study]]
2 CONT [[Category: Stonington, Connecticut]] [[ Category: New London County, Connecticut Colony]]
2 CONT == Biography == 
2 CONT Phebe Denison, the ninth child of [[Denison-15|John  Borodell Denison]] and [[Lay-294|Phoebe Lay]], was born and Christened on 6 April 1690 <ref name="CS-Mounsey">Rev. Creighton Spencer-Mounsey. '' The BillingsFamily of Connecticu
2 CONC t'', Register (April 1927).  p. 164. Avail at NEHG.</ref> at Stonington, Connecticut.
2 CONT This Phebe Denison was a namesake for her earlier born (1668) sister who died young. She married Ebenezer Billings, son of Ensign Ebenezer Billings and Anne Comstock, on 2 Apr 1706. <ref name="CS-Mounsey"/> They had 11 children du
2 CONC ring the timespan through April 1732, all born at or near Stonington, Connecticut. Phebe (Denison) Billings died on 30 Dec. 1775 at age 85 <ref name="CS-Mounsey"/>, in or near Stonington, Connecticut.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT <references />
2 CONT *Richard Anson Wheeler. ''History of the Town of Stonington, County ofNew London, Connecticut, From Its First Settlement in 1649 to 1900''.New London, CT: Press of the Day Publishing Co., Jan. 1900; p. 237, no. 22: https://archive
2 CONC .org/stream/historyoftownofs00whee_1#page/n259/mode/1up; p. 339, p. 58: https://archive.org/stream/historyoftownofs00whee_1#page/n361/mode/1up
