2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Mehitable Fenner, d/o Lt. Gov. Thomas and Dinah (Borden) Fenner of R.I. She married (1) Timothy Starkweather; (2) Samuel Sterry; 3d Dr. Wm. Blodgett.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Named as a married daughter in her father's will: Maj. Fenner died Feb. 27, 1718, ae. 65 years and 5 months, his will having been made Feb, 19, of same year. In this document he made, due provision for his wife Dinah, and his "poo
2 CONC r helpless child Eleazar, bestowed £5 apiece on his three daughters Freelove Westcotte, Mehitable Starkweather, and Mary Abbott, and divided his remaining property between his five sons Thomas, Richard, Joseph, Arthur and John.[2]
2 CONT Mehitable Fenner m. Timothy Starkweather 18 Oct 1705 in Preston, Connecticut.[3] Timothy Starkweather of Stonington died about 1717. His wife Mehitable administered his estate. Samuel Sterry and Samuel Prentes took the inventory[4
2 CONC ]
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Sterry m. his 2d w. Mehitable [ ...] 8 Feb 1724/5.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT William, m. Mehetable Steevens*. Mar. 31, 1737 (*note at bottom of page of original manuscript states: "Wm. Blodgett's widow is referred to as widow of Samuel Sterry in probate files of Blodgett estate")[6] When William died about
2 CONC  1739, Mehitable the widow refused to administer his estate leaving it to William's eldest son William.[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Mehitable and Timothy Starkweather.[1][8]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Mehitabel b. Preston 12 Jan 1706/7 m. 1745 John Birket
2 CONT 2. Joseph b. Preston 8 Oct 1709 m. Anna Starkweather
2 CONT 3. Arthur, killed by lightning b. Preston 1 Jun 1712; living in Prston 1734
2 CONT 4. Mary b. Preston 6 March 1714/5 m. William Blodgett, s/o Dr. William Blodget
2 CONT . Samuel name in the Fenner Genealogy is probably an error according to the Starkweather Genealogy.
2 CONT Child of Mehitabel and Samuel Sterry
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Roger Sterry, town clerk of Preston, Connecticut
2 CONT Probate of Mehitabel Blogget.
2 CONT
2 CONT Will dated 29 Sept 1744. Inventory 10 Oct 1744. Son in law William Blogget, executor. Bequests to
2 CONT Mehitable Burkit, daughter, £30
2 CONT Mary Bloggit, daughter, looking glass and other goods
2 CONT Stephen Starkwether, grandson, biggest pewter platter and 20s
2 CONT Arter Starkwether, grandson, next biggest pewter platter and 20s
2 CONT Huldah Starkwether, granddaughter, next biggest pewter platter , grid irons and 20s
2 CONT Timothy Starkwether, grandson, next biggest pewter platter and 20s
2 CONT Roger Sterry all the rest of her estate, except apparel to be divided by two daughters
2 CONT Debts were paid to Saml Starkweather, Ebenezer Leonard, David Randale, Theo Stnton, Jn Starkweather, Jo William, Roger Billings, Will Denison, Gidion Safford, Benj Blodgett, Marther Park, James Frink jr, Nath Stanton, Moses Tyler,
2 CONC  Ephraim Smith, Joseph Kinnie, Ephraim Herrick, Saml Prentice, Cypryan Sterry, Jn Cook, Saml Harrington for Cyprian Sterry (this is his inherited goods), Joseph Bowdish, Jn Boardman, Nathan Leonard, John Denison. [9]
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
