1 NOTE
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: The Fenner Family
2 CONT Fourth Edition
2 CONT Alfred Fenner Isham
2 CONT Los Angeles, California
2 CONT February 15, 1929 - Page 14
2 CONT 127 HON. RICHARD FENNER AND 1,SHELDON 2,THORNTON
2 CONT [b 1695;d 6 Feb. 1773] Richard m 1st Abigail Sheldon [b 1695;d 1744], daughter of Nicholas Sheldon and Abigail Tillinghast, on 11 Jan. 1716, by Justice Richard Brown. He m 2nd Mrs. Abigail Thornton, daughter of Richard Clemence. W
2 CONC ill in Johnston records Vol. 1, p 87 mentions a homestead in Johnston, lands in Pawtuxet given to Arthur; to Lydia 100L and furniture; to John the right of his brother Joseph and himself in tract in Glocester; to Richard and Jerem
2 CONC iah a right in tract in Scituate near Chaupauseakock hill. His personalty amounted to 
2 CONT 330L 4s. Richard was a justice of the peace. He lived probably for a time in the homestead of his father, Major Thomas, and then built a home nearby and on the opposite side of the Plainfield pike, which divides Cranston and Johns
2 CONC ton. The site is probably close to the Simmons mansion in Johnston, which was occupied in 1826. Richard served as a judge from 1732 to 1737, and was a member of the Governor's Council in 1740.
