1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hyde Genealogy #8 Jabez Hyde  b at Norwich Conn in May 1677 the youngest son of Samuel Hyde 2 and Jane Lee was a grandson of William Hyde the first of Norwich, He m 29 Dec 1709 a sister of his brother William's wif
2 CONC e Elizabeth Bushnell b 31 Jan 1686 the youngest daughter of Richard Bushnell Esq and Elizabeth Adgate of Norwich. They settled at Norwich West Farms now Franklin where he had a large tract of land He was a wealthy farmer and was a
2 CONC  justice of the peace of Norwich and a representative in the general court eight sessions He d 5 Sept 1702 His wife survived him, and d 21 August 1768. He is in some of the records called Capt. Jabez Hyde. He was appointed clerk o
2 CONC f the Franklin church in 1716 and was such clerk many years. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children were 
2 CONT # Jabez b 16 Sept 1713 at Norwich m Lydia Abel
2 CONT # Phinehas b 2 Feb 1720 at Norwich m Anne Rogers
2 CONT # Joseph b 23 Aug 1724 at Norwich He d 10 July 1754 at Norwich unm
2 CONT # Elizabeth b 9 July 1711 at Norwich m Simon Tracy
2 CONT # Abigail b 17 Nov 1715 at Norwich m Jonathan Barstow 
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Genealogical and personal memorial of Mercer County, New Jersey By Francis Bazley Lee, 
2 CONT
2 CONT "He was an extensive land holder and justice of the peace, and in some of the old records he is called Captain Jabez Hyde. He married Elizabeth Bushnell, daughter of Richard Bushnell, Esq., and they had a number of children."
2 CONT ----
2 CONT HISTORY OF THE TOWN OF STONINGTON, County of New London, Connecticut, from its first settlement in 1649 to 1900, by Richard Anson Wheeler, New London, CT, 1900, p. 445
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT See "Genealogical and personal memorial of Mercer County, New Jersey, Volume 2 edited by Francis Bazley Lee" at http://books.google.com/books?id=dNgMAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA614&lpg=PA614&dq=jabez+hyde+1677&source=bl&ots=OYXMaSofnt&sig=P830Z
2 CONC KfMJKqPskhNnuFcQR1PHEo&hl=en&ei=gyPASaDhDILuMtHEwKEN&sa=X&oi=book_result&resnum=2&ct=result#v=onepage&q=jabez%20hyde%201677&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://books.google.com/books?id=rIKhN5aMelcC&dq=Elizabeth%20Bushnell%20Jabez%20Hyde&pg=PA8#v=onepage&q=Elizabeth%20Bushnell&f=false  Hyde Geneaology by Reuben Hyde Walworth]
2 CONT Husband of Elizabeth Bushnell.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Norwich Probate District records - Will:
2 CONT I Jabez Hide of Norwich in the County of New London and Colony of Connecticut in New England ... this ninth day of February AD 1756 ... my wife Elizabeth, my son Jabez, ... my son Phenehas ... my daughter Abagial ..., my beloved g
2 CONC rand children Elizebeth Jabez & Mary the only children of my beloved daughter Elizabeth deceased the wife of Simon Tracy...
2 CONT Will submitted for probate September 20th 1762
2 CONT
