2 CONT ===John Lee
2 CONT * Birth: 21 Sep 1670 • Lyme, New London, Connecticut
2 CONT * Death: 17 Jan 1715 • Lyme, New London, Connecticut
2 CONT * Father: Thomas (Lt) Lee II (1644–1705)
2 CONT * Mother: Sarah "Ann" Kirkland (Kirtland) (1645–1676)
2 CONT * John was born on 21 September 1670 in Lyme, Connecticut.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage & Family
2 CONT
2 CONT John Lee married Elizabeth Smith (1670-1761) on 8 February 1692 in Lyme, Connecticut.[2] [3][4]. She was the daughter of Richard Smith and Joanna (Quarles).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT Sarah Lee (1693–1732)
2 CONT # Elizabeth Lee (1695–1720)
2 CONT # Phebe Lee (1696–1785)
2 CONT # Lucy Lee (1699–1757)
2 CONT # Jane (Jeane) Lee (1701–1739)
2 CONT # John Lee (1703–1745)
2 CONT # Joseph Lee (1705–1779)
2 CONT # Mary Lee (1708–1722)
2 CONT # Hepzibah Lee (Sill) (1710–1783)
2 CONT # Benjamin Lee (1712–1777)
2 CONT # Joanna Lee (1715– )
2 CONT
2 CONT John and Elizabeth Smith Lee
2 CONT
2 CONT John Lee and Elizabeth Smith were married Feb. 8, 1692. Sarah, born Nov. 12, 1693. Elizabeth, April 30, 1695. Phebe, March 2, 1696. Luce, June 20, 1699. Jeane, May 20, 1701. John, May 17, 1703. Joseph, Nov. 26 1705. Mary, Jan. 20,
2 CONC  1707-8. Hepsibah, May 16, 1710. Benjamin, Sept. 4, 1712. Joannah, April 28, 1715.
2 CONT
