1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Peck was the son of Joseph Peck and Sarah Parker.  He was born 29 Jul 1678 in Lyme, New London, Connecticut and died there on 28 Jan 1734.  He was buried in the Duck River Cemetery in Old Lyme.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 28 December 1699, Samuel Peck married to '''Elizabeth Lee''', daughter of Thomas Lee and Mary DeWolf.  She was born 20 Oct 1681 in Lyme, New London, Connecticut and died in Old Lyme on 29 Aug 1731, where she was buried.
2 CONT
2 CONT On about 25 Jan 1732, Samuel Peck married to Martha Nettleton, daughter of John Nettleton and Sarah Woodmansee.  She was born 1 December 1692 in Killingsworth, Middlesex, Connecticut, and died 27 January 1770 in Lyme.  Martha was 
2 CONC William Barber’s widow.  She survived Samuel and married thirdly to Peter Pearson.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Elizabeth Lee and Samuel Peck were:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Elizabeth (1) b. 26 APR 1702 d. 15 JAN 1704/5
2 CONT # Elizabeth (2) b. 14 MAY 1705 d.  8 OCT 1730  m. Dea. Richard Ely
2 CONT # Samuel Jr    b. 12 JUL 1707 d.  7 NOV 1782
2 CONT # William      b. 31 AUG 1709 d. 25 NOV 1739
2 CONT # Benjamin      b.  6 Mar 1711 d. 12 Feb 1784  m. Sarah Champion
2 CONT # Elijah        b. 29 Oct 1713 d.  6 Aug 1771  m. Hepsibah Pearson
2 CONT # Jedediah      b.  1 JUN 1717 d.  1744 @sea,
2 CONT # Daniel        b.  4 MAR 1721 d.  1 MAR 1751 
2 CONT # Silas        b.  2 OCT 1724 d.    JUN 1808
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT #Peck, Darius, ''A Genealogical Account Of The Descendants In The Male Line Of William Peck, One Of The Founders In 1638 Of The Colony Of New Haven, Conn''. Hudson, N.Y.: Bryan & Goeltz, Steam Book Printers, 1877; pp. 18-19.  < [h
2 CONC ttps://books.google.com/books?id=eGdJAAAAMAAJ&vq=Nettleton&pg=PA19#v=onepage&q&f=false GoogleBooks] > 
