1 NAME John /Larrabee/
2 GIVN John
2 SURN Larrabee
2 _MARNM Larrabee
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 16 JAN 1689
2 ADDR
3 CITY Windham
3 STAE Connecticut
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE MAR 1746
2 ADDR
3 CITY Louisbourg
3 STAE Nova Scotia
3 CTRY Canada
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Children Of John, Of Windham:
2 CONT
2 CONT From Sacco Valley Settlements:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. John,6 whose wife d. in Windham, Conn., Aug. 15, 1756, aged 60 years. He may have d. at Louisburg in 1746. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Hannah Williams, a dau. of Capt. Adam Larrabee, writes: "My father always spoke of his great-grandfather as John Larrabee, and of his wife Hannah who he said sat up nights and spun to earn money to buy the communion service f
2 CONC or the old Congregational church in Windham." 
2 CONT
2 CONT This statement, associated with the grave-stone of Hannah from which the foregoing dates were copied, establishes the connection between Greenfield Larrabee, the i st, of Saybrook, and the family of which Ex-Gov. William Larrabee 
2 CONC is a living representative, as will further appear.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes 
2 CONT * On a monument in Windham, Conn., the following inscriptions appear: "In Memory Of   MRS. HANNAH, WIFE OF MK. JOHN LARRABEE. She died August ye 15, A. D. 1756, aged 00 years, beloved of all."  "JOHN LARRABEE, HUSBAND OF HANNAH, D
2 CONC ied in battle at Louisburg, March, 1746." 
2 CONT * [http://genforum.genealogy.com/larrabee/messages/231.html 3. Mary HATCH-] (b.1691;d.1716) sp: John LARABEE- (b.1690;m.1711;d.1746) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources  
2 CONT # [http://books.google.com/books?pg=PA790&lpg=PA790&dq=John+larrabee+Rebecca+park&sig=E9ov_vME56hyolPAMwdGD59modg&ei=t6PkUa2uPIvYigKNn4GwCw&id=CfQgAQAAMAAJ&ots=a5P6kE41Af&output=text Saco Valley settlements and families:]  histori
2 CONC cal, biographical ..., Volume 2.  By Gideon Tibbetts Ridlon.  Page 790-792
