1 NOTE
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: New England Ancestry of Susan Alma Cook (1866 - 1934)
2 CONT Researched  and Compiled by Philip R. Bunnelle
2 CONT Santa Clara, California 1998
2 CONT Page 64
2 CONT 112 Nicholas Sheldon, Jr. son of Nicholas and Abigail (Tillinghast) Sheldon.
2 CONT    Nicholas was born in Providence, RI, in 1694. Evidence indicates he married his first cousin Penelope Arnold. He probably lived in that part of Providence which was set off as Cranston in 1754.
2 CONT    The 1774 Rhode Island census shows a Nicholas Sheldon heading a household of 3 in Cranston. He is shown in 1777 Military census as aged 60+ and in the 1782 state census is the Nicholas Sheldon heading a household of six.
2 CONT    He died at Cranston 9 March 1787, aged 93. His will dated 3 March 1787 was proved 24 March 1787. Calling him of Cranston, yeoman, far advanced in years, it mentions: son Nicholas and Stephen, both of whom have unnamed children.
2 CONC  Daughters Sarah Waterman, wife of Benjamin, Hannah Henry, wife of Caleb, Mary Colvin, wife of George, & ____Congdon, first wife of Ephraim Congdon. Grandchildren of Ephraim Congdon by his first wife my daughter. Witnesses: Thomas
2 CONC  Hazard, Thomas Sarle, Nehemiah Knight.
