2 CONT John Power Sr
2 CONT Born about 1703 [uncertain] in Providence, Rhode Island 
2 CONT Died 18 Feb 1772 at about age 69 in Providence, Providence, Rhode Island 
2 CONT
2 CONT Capt. John Power Sr edit
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Nicholas Power III and Mercy (Tillinghast) Power  edit
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Mary (Power) Cooke [half], Hope (Power) Brown, Joseph Power, Anne Power, Nicholas Power IV and Mary Lydia (Power) Sabin add sibling
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Lydia (Winsor) Angell — married 1728 (to 1731) in Providence, Providence, Rhode Island map icon at age 25
2 CONT Husband of Mary (Holloway) Power — married 25 Dec 1735 in Holy Trinity Church in Wilmington, New Castle, Delaware Colony map icon at age 32 add/edit spouses
2 CONT Father of John Power Jr.  , Holloway Thomas Power Sr. , Son Power , Unknown (Power) Perkins , James Power , Jeremiah Power , Mary Margaret (Power) Sinclair and Thomas Power add/edit children
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Capt John Power, the son of Nicholas Power and Mercy Tillinghast was born about 1702/1703 in Providence, Rhode Island. [1] He died 18 Feb 1772 (aged 68–69) in Providence, Rhode Island and is buried at North Burial Ground in Provid
2 CONC ence, Providence County, Rhode Island.[2][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Known children of John Power include but not all:
2 CONT
2 CONT John Power (1729–1786)
2 CONT Anne Power Knowles (1732–1811)
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT John Power Sr is listed in the U.S., Sons of the American Revolution Membership Applications, 1889-1970 as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth Date Apr 1703
2 CONT Birth Place Providence, Rhode Island
2 CONT Death Date 18 Feb 1772
2 CONT Death Place Providence, Rhode Island
2 CONT SAR Membership 99400
2 CONT Role Ancestor
2 CONT Application Date 24 Jan 1970
2 CONT Father: Nicholas Power
2 CONT Mother: Marcy Power
2 CONT Spouse: Lydia Power
2 CONT Children: John Power [4]
2 CONT He married Lydia (Winsor) Angell around 1728. [5]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a ship’s captain. He left his son and wife in Rhode Island. Both he and his wife remarried and had children with their next spouse.
2 CONT
2 CONT FamilySearch has [Power] listed as a child in this family. More research needs to be conducted.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
