2 CONT ''The Haile/Hail/Hale Family: The Descendants of Richard Haile of Swansea (1640-1729)'' compiled by William Jonathan Hale (1866-1936), edited, revised & extended by Lyman Mower, 1997 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth:  Sep. 15, 1709 Swansea Bristol County Massachusetts, USA  Death:  Apr. 14, 1738 Swansea Bristol County Massachusetts, USA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Some records show the surname as Hale. The burial site for Barnard could not be found and it's assumed it was in Swansea.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barnard is the son of John & Hannah Tillinghast Haile/Hale.
2 CONT
2 CONT ***** "History of Swansea Massachusetts 1667-1917" by Otis Olney Wright Page 167
2 CONT
2 CONT "Barnard Haile (1709-38) inherited sixty-eight acres in the division of his father's estate including two ten acre lots...He married Hannah, daughter of Samuel and Experience Wheaton born 1719 Sept. 12." ...
2 CONT
2 CONT ***** "The Haile/Hail/Hale Family - The Descendants of Richard Haile of Swansea (1640-1729)" By William Jonathan Hale (1866-1936) Page 47
2 CONT
2 CONT "Barnard Haile married Hannah Wheaton, the daughter of Samuel and Experience (Pierce) Wheaton before 1728. He built a house on the land laid out to him by the commissioners who divided his father's estate. [On the cellar of that h
2 CONC ouse a small house was recently built for Mrs. Julia W. Sherman (prior to 1936), who told the workmen to excavate until they found the old cellar wall, for she wished the house to stand upon part of the foundation of the old house
2 CONC  in which her grandmother was born. She was a descendant of Hannah Wheaton from her second marriage to John Wood, Jr., whom Hannah married in 1739.]"
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 55
2 CONT
2 CONT "Children of Barnard Haile (1709-1738) and Hannah Wheaton (1712-1749+):
2 CONT  i. Freelove Haile. Born, 11 February 1727/8(?), in Swansea, Massachusetts, she married Nathaniel Bourn, 2 March 1748/9, in Swansea.
2 CONT  ii. Hannah Haile, Born, 1732; m. 1751 Samson Mason.
2 CONT  iii. Coomer Haile. Born, 5 November 1734, in Swansea, Massachusetts, he died, October 1782, in Providence, Rhode Island. Comer married Margaret Ingraham on 13 November 1757...
2 CONT  iv. Amos Haile. Born, 1736; m. 1758, Ruth Easterbrooke."
2 CONT
