1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Freelove Hale 
2 CONT *Birth:  Apr. 3, 1712 Rehoboth Bristol County Massachusetts, USA  
2 CONT *Death:  Jan. 30, 1803 Providence County Rhode Island, USA 
2 CONT *Daughter of John Hale and Hannah Tillinghast
2 CONT *Married 1)  Oliver Kingsley 
2 CONT * Married 2)  Jotham Carpenter Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: Freelove Hale was born April 3, 1712, in Rehoboth, Rhode Island Colony or Swansea, Bristol, Massachusetts Bay, daughter of John Hale and Hannah Tillinghast. "Freelove the Daughter of John Haile and Hannah his Wife was Born 
2 CONC april ye 3 1712"[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: She died in Providence County, Rhode Island, between 12 OCT 1801 and 30 Jan 1803.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Oliver Kingsley was born in 1705, the son of Nathaniel and Christian (Cole) Kingsley.[1]. He married Freelove Hale on 31 December, 1729, in Swansea.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children were 
2 CONT # Pardon
2 CONT # Lydia
2 CONT #  Peleg
2 CONT # James
2 CONT # Ann
2 CONT # Freelove.
2 CONT
2 CONT He passed away in 1739.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Lydia Kingsley was the widow of Oliver Kingsley,[1] with whom she had 5 children, when she married Jotham Carpenter, widower of Mehitable Thompson, with whom he had eight children in 1748.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Freelove Hale and Jotham Carpenter  had an additional four children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Freelove, born 1749, married Job Whipple; 
2 CONT # Jotham III, born 28 Nov 1750, married Hannah Gulley;
2 CONT #  Oliver, born 15 Nov 1753, married Joanna Ballou; and, 
2 CONT # Desire, born 26 Oct 1755, married William Lang.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 1803 CARPENTER Mrs. Freelove, widow of Deacon Jotham, at Cumberland, in 91st year. Gazette of Feb. 26, 1803 Death Providence 
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Carpenter, Freelove, of Cumberland, widow, far advanced in years. Will dated 12 Oct 1801, proved 28 Feb 1803, pgs 62-63. Mentions: Sons Jotham Carpenter & Oliver Carpenter. Daughters Freelove Whipple, Desire Ballou, Lydia Blake,
2 CONC  & Anna Bliss." 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
