1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === Priscilla Hazen
2 CONT *Gender: Female
2 CONT *Birth: Nov 25 1664  Rowley, Essex, Massachusetts Bay Colony
2 CONT *Marriage: July 21 1681 Rowley, Essec, Massachusetts Bay Colony
2 CONT *Death: Apr 25 1752  Newbury, Essex, Province of Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT *Parents:  Edward Hazen and Hannah Grant
2 CONT * Husband: Jeremiah Pearson (son of 	Dea. John Pearson and Dorcas)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://mathcs.clarku.edu/~djoyce/gen/report/rr04/rr04_004.html#P10361
2 CONT
2 CONT 6409. Jeremiah Pearson. Born on 25 Oct 1653 in Rowley, MA.85 Jeremiah died in Newbury, MA 23 Feb 1736/7.85 
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation: Caprenter, Miller, Farmer.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 21 Jul 1681 when Jeremiah was 27, he married Priscilla Hazen, daughter of Edward Hazen (ca 1614-Jul 1683) & Hannah Grant (ca 1631-Feb 1715/6), in Rowley, MA.85 Born on 25 Nov 1664 in Rowley, MA.419 Priscilla died in Rowley, MA,
2 CONC  on 25 Apr 1752; she was 87.85
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeremiah and Priscilla were dismissed 15 Jan 1710 from the Rowley Church to the Newbury Church. Priscilla returned to Rowley sometime after Jeremiah’s death.85
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children include:
2 CONT # Priscilla Pearson (3 Dec 1682-26 Feb 1776). Married Capt. Nathaniel Mighill
2 CONT # Miriam Pearson (Died young) (ca Jul 1685-Dec 1689)
2 CONT # Hannah Pearson (Died soon) (22 Apr 1688-18 Jul 1690)
2 CONT # Capt. John Pearson (10 Apr 1690-26 Feb 1781). Married 1) Elizabeth Mix 2) 	Lydia Ilsley.
2 CONT # Hepzibah Pearson (10 Dec 1692-bef 16 Nov 1726).  Married 	Richard Knight.
2 CONT # Miriam Pearson (8 Feb 1694/5-15 Jan 1782).  Married Ebenezer Burpee.
2 CONT # Moses Pearson (26 Mar 1697-1778). Married 	Sarah Titcomb. 
2 CONT # Capt. Jeremiah Pearson (ca 1699-3 Jan 1768) Married Mary Titcomb.
2 CONT # Amos Pearson (5 Jan 1701/2-Sep 1779) Married Mary Morse.
2 CONT # Hannah Pearson (12 May 1704-6 Mar 1797).  Married John Downer.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * '''Residence''': Massachusetts, United States - 1664
