1 NAME John /Giles/
2 GIVN John
2 SURN Giles
2 _MARNM Giles
1 NAME John Giles, of Salem
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 15 APR 1645
2 ADDR
3 CITY Salem
3 STAE Massachusetts Bay Colony
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 BAPM
2 DATE 11 MAY 1645
2 PLAC Salem, Essex co., MA
2 ADDR
1 BURI
2 DATE 6 DEC 1715
1 DEAT
2 DATE BEF 6 DEC 1715
2 ADDR
3 CITY Beverly
3 STAE Massachusetts
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Giles was one of the men who participated in the "physical examination" of John Proctor and John Willard during the Salem Witch Hysteria. The "examination" turned up no devil's marks.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT *BIRTH	John was born on 15 April 1645 in Salem, Essex co., MA[1,39,44] and baptized in Salem, Essex co., MA on 11 May 1645[2,45]. John's birth record reads: "Giles, John, s. Edward [Edmond in C.R.1] and Bridgett."
2 CONT *DEATH	According to Torrey, John died possibly in 1730; he would have been 84[1].  Died intestate.
2 CONT *MARRIAGE #1	Before 1671 when John was 25, he first married Elizabeth TIDD daughter of Samuel TIDD, in Salem, Essex co., MA[1,20,48,49,50,51]. Elizabeth was born in May of 1642[1].
2 CONT *MARRIAGE #2	On 5 May 1679 when John was 34, he second married Elizabeth GALLEY in Beverly, Essex co., MA by Major Dennison[1,2,52,53,20,46,54]. Elizabeth was the widow of Osmand TRASK. John & Elizabeth's Salem Marriage record rea
2 CONC ds: "Gyells, John, widr. and Elisabeth Trask, wid., of Beverly, at Salem." [46] Torrey has him under "Gyells"[1]. Their Marriage record in Beverly reads "Gyels, John, widr., of Salem, and Elis[abeth] Trask, wid., May 5, 1679"[47].
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT From "Giles Memorial," page 13, viewer page 25.  < [https://sail1620.org/images/downloads/Published_Family_Genealogies/the_giles_memorial._genealogical_memoirs_of_the_families_bearing_the_names_of_giles__gould__holmes__jennison__l
2 CONC eonard__lindall__curwen__marshall__robinson__sampson__and_webb___j._vinton__1864_.pdf PDF] >
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of John Giles were
2 CONT
2 CONT by first wife, b. in Salem, (now South Danvers,)
2 CONT
2 CONT *36. John,3 b. about 1671 ; m. 1, Abigail Raymond; 2, Esther Swinnerton. 
2 CONT
2 CONT By second wife, b. in Beverly
2 CONT
2 CONT * 37. Eleazar, 3 b. March 19, 1679-80 ; m. Lydia Grover.
2 CONT * 38. Mary, 3 b. Feb. 28, 1681 ; m. John Wheeler.
2 CONT * 39. Bridget,3 b. Jan. 1, 1683; d. Feb. 10, 1689.
2 CONT * 40. Return, 3 b. ; m. Samuel Wardwell of Andover, Dec. 20, 1716. The last named. Return Giles, is not recorded as a dau. of John Giles, but it is recorded that Samuel Wardwell of Andover m. Return Giles of Beverly as above ; and
2 CONC  there was no other Giles in Beverly who could be her father. We shall have frequent occasion to note the imperfection of the early records.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also seen:
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Giles, born 1671 at Salem, married Jonathan Bacon
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage record in Salem VRs is “Gyells, John, widr., and Elis[abeth] Trask, wid., of Beverly, at Beverly.”  
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage record in Beverly VRs is “Gyels, John, widr., of Salem, and Elis[abeth] Trask, wid., May 5, 1679”
2 CONT
2 CONT John was one of the people who participated in the physical examination of John proctor & John Willard during the Salem Witch Hysteria
2 CONT
2 CONT Physical Examination of John Proctor and John Willard
2 CONT
2 CONT We whose names under written having searched the bodyes of John procter sev’r & John Williard now in the Goale & doe not find any thing to farther suspect them
2 CONT
2 CONT Dated June 2, 1692
2 CONT Rondel ap’re testis
2 CONT *John Rogers
2 CONT *Joshua Rea Jun’r
2 CONT *John Cooke
2 CONT *J. Barton Chyrg’n
2 CONT *Jno Gyles
2 CONT *William Hine
2 CONT *Ezekiel Cheever
2 CONT (Reverse) Return of Doctor Barton & other men that Search’t Willard & Procter
2 CONT
2 CONT [Essex County Archives, Salem -- Witchcraft Vol. 1 Page 15]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT On 24 November 1685, "Florence Gally" was presented at Salem Court "for abusing John Giles in scratching him in the face so that the blood appeared... Mr. Jno. Gyles appeared in behalf of Florence Galley, she being sick and not ab
2 CONC le to come"  Three may be two men by the name of John Giles represented here, the first being the grandson of Florence and the second being the son-in-law.
2 CONT Source Link: https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000144050493823label=@S110@
2 CONT Source Link: https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000144050493825label=@S322@
2 CONT Source Link: https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000144051348826label=@S6@
2 CONT Source Link: https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000205517131860label=@S1061@
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT From "The Giles Memorial", page 11.  Viewer page 25.  < [https://sail1620.org/images/downloads/Published_Family_Genealogies/the_giles_memorial._genealogical_memoirs_of_the_families_bearing_the_names_of_giles__gould__holmes__jennis
2 CONC on__leonard__lindall__curwen__marshall__robinson__sampson__and_webb___j._vinton__1864_.pdf PDF] >
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. JOHN GILES,' second son of Edward' and Bridget Giles ; b. in Salem, [South Dauvers,] April 15, 1645; m. 1st, before 1671, ___ Giles, dau. of John Giles. 2, in 1679, Elizabeth (Galley) Trask, dau. of John Galley of Beverly, and 
2 CONC widow of Osmund [Osmyn ?] Trask of Beverly.J
2 CONT
2 CONT The proof of the first marriage is found in a Deed, dated Feb. 8, 1708-9, in which John Giles of Beverly, in the County of Essex, yeoman, and Elizabeth his wife, "for that love, good will, and natural affec- tion which I bear to m
2 CONC y loving son Eleazar Giles, carpenter, and my loving son-in-law John Wheeler, cooper, both of Beverly, convey a certain parcel of land in Beverly formerly belonging to my father-in-law John Giles of the town and county aforesaid ;
2 CONC " also another parcel of 7^ acres of land m Beverly. [Essex Deeds, 21 : 30.]* Moreover,
2 CONT John Giles, in the record of his second marriage in 1679, is called a "widower." We know that he had a wife in 1671. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The proof of the second marriage is three-fold: 1. John Gallee of Salem, aged 78 in 1683, made his willin 1683, in which he mentions John Giles who m. his dau. Elizabeth. 2. John Giles of Beverly, and Elizabeth his wife, dau. of J
2 CONC ohn Galley of BeverJy, deceased, convey land, Jan. 27, 1706-7, to John Wheeler and Mary his wife, their daughter. [Essex Deeds, 32 : 80.] 3. Elizabeth Gyles, now wife of John Giles of Beverly, formerly wife of Osmund Trask, late o
2 CONC f Beverly, deceased, administratrix of his estate, conveys land. In this deed, dated Feb. 18, 1687-8, she mentions her sons by her former husband, viz., Samuel, Benjamin, Joseph, William, and Edward Trask. [EssexDeeds, 36 : 45. Jo
2 CONC hn Giles resided in Salem, i. e. in South Danvers, until his second marriage in 1679, as will appear from the deeds now to be quoted: 1671, Dec. 7. John Giles of Salem, husbandman, sells to AVilliam Trask and his bi'other John Tra
2 CONC sk, both of Salem, a "ten acre lot" of upland in Salem, bounded on lands of John Southwick and Samuel Very. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In this deed his wife is said to give consent, but her name does not appear. [Essex Deeds, Salem, 3 : 155. 1679, April 18. John Giles of Salem, yeoman, for .£150 conveys to Vzall Wardall [Uzal Wardwell] of Ipswich, house carpenter
2 CONC , my dwelling-house, with all the out-houses, Barne, &c., with all the land they stand u])on, and all my land adjoyning and belonging thereto, being by estimation 9 or 10 acres, more or less, which is situate, lying and being with
2 CONC in the township of Salem, and now in the possession and occupation of me the said John Giles, bounded S. W. on the comon land, W. on land of Samuel Very, N. on John King, and E. on land of EleazarGiles. Bridget Giles, mother of th
2 CONC e said John Giles, and executrix or administratrix of Edward Giles, deceased, gives her free consent to the above conveyance. No wife is mentioned. [Ibid, 6 : 120. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1679, on his second marriage, he removed to Beverly, and resided there till his death. He lived there till his death. He lived in the immediate vicinity of the easterly end of Beverly Common, as we learn from the following deed
2 CONC  :
2 CONT
2 CONT 1705-6, March 13. John Giles, Eliezer Giles, "carpenter," and John Wheeler, " cooper," all of Beverly, convey to the town of Beverly,
2 CONT ----
