1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Dea Samuel Ware BIRTH	8 Feb 1717, Wrentham, Norfolk County, Massachusetts, USA DEATH	5 Jan 1806 (aged 88), Conway, Franklin County, Massachusetts, USA BURIAL	Howland Cemetery, Conway, Franklin County, Massachusetts
2 CONC , USA, PLOT 2nd sec, 10th row, MEMORIAL ID 82761867
2 CONT
2 CONT son of Nathaniel Ware & __________
2 CONT
2 CONT m. 1) Anna Goodale on 24 July 1745 Anna b. 1710 d. 7 May 1756 aged 45
2 CONT
2 CONT m. 2) Hannah (Billings) Belding on 3 Nov 1757 at New Braintree Hannah had married first on 2 Jan 1745/6 Silas Belding (d.1756) Hannah b. 23 Sept 1724 in Hardwick d. 1814 in Conway in her 90th year
2 CONT
2 CONT children all with first wife Anna: Samuel b. 9 May 1746 d. 5 Dec 1829 Jonathan b. 1747 d. 9 Feb 1829 Timothy b. 23 Jan 1748/9 d. 11 June 1769 Jesse b. 31 July 1750 d. Oct 1829 m. Anna Woods Mary b. 25 Dec 1751 d. 13 Aug 1785 m. Th
2 CONC omas Fletcher Elizabeth b. 14 April 1755 d. 26 March 1831 m. Maj. Aaron Fisher
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel was born in Wrentham, removed to Braintree then to Conway in 1771. Was a farmer and a deacon. Was received into the church in New Braintree with wife Hannah in June 1781
2 CONT
2 CONT DIED – At Conway, on the fifth inst. Deacon Samuel Ware, aged 88. After __ ing finished the course assigned him, he serenely composed, through the curtain death, into the arms of his favor. Early awakened from the death like flee 
2 CONC __sin, it has been his preserving endea__ through a long course of years, “to have ways a conscience void of offence toward God and man.” 
2 CONT
2 CONT His religion was not like Sunday suit, but he was watchful, and prayerful that in all his thoughts words and actions God might be honored and obeyed. In you_ he was discreet, fond of instruction, and active in the cause of truth; 
2 CONC in middle age, diligent and laborious in his occupation, and indesa__gable in his exertions to build up Zion, both by precept and example particularly, in his own house – and when age gradually benumb___ his faculties, and dissolv
2 CONC ed the powers of life his patience and resignation shone in humble, cheerful and affectionate demeanor; __ his studiousness still to be useful with the ren__nat of his capacity, although in the humble employments, and in the peace
2 CONC ful serenity __ entire reliance on Christ’s free grace, with which he met the King of terrors. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was ever, through life, watchful over, and jealous of the remaining corrupt propensities of his nature, and ever rejoiced with trembling.  He delighted to do good to all as he had opportunity, and in turn, was loved and respect
2 CONC ed by all his acquaintance. “Go thou and do likewise.” [published on January 22, 1806 in The Hampshire Gazette, Northampton, Mass.]
2 CONT
2 CONT [father and birth details from FAG contributor 47561076; Ware genealogy : Robert Ware of Dedham, Massachusetts, 1642-1699, and his lineal descendants by Emma Forbes Ware, (1838-1898) published 1901 page 55-56; thanks for assist fr
2 CONC om FAG contributor 48022670 ]
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents	 Nathaniel Ware 1648–1724
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouses Anna Hinds Walker Goodale Ware 1710–1756 (m. 1745)	 Hannah Billings Ware 1724–1814 (m. 1757)
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings	 Nathaniel Ware 1697–1781 Betty Ware Grant 1699–1726 Beriah Ware 1704–1756
2 CONT
2 CONT Children	 Samuel Ware 1746–1829	 Jonathan Ware 1747–1829
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription
2 CONT
2 CONT Dea Samuel Ware  died 5 Jan 1806  in the 89 year of his age  Mrs Hannah Ware  Relict of Dea Samuel Ware  died 25 Feb 1814 aged 90
2 CONT
