1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Full Context of Genealogical and Family History of the State of Connecticut, Vol. I-IV  III) Nathaniel , son of Rev. Samuel Mann , was born in Milton , about 1677 ; died in Wrentham , May 11, 1756 . He married, December 19, 1704 ,
2 CONC  Elizabeth George . His will was dated October 19, 1754 . Children, born at Wrentham : 1. George , September 29, 1705 . 2. John , August 12, 1707 . 3. Nathaniel , August 6, 1709 . 4. Mary , July 24, 1711 . 5. Robert , April 11, 17
2 CONC 13 . 6. Jeremiah , May 26, 1715 . 7. Joseph , August 13, 1717 . 8. Ezra , October 13, 1719 . 9. Timothy , mentioned below. 10. Richard , August 17, 1723 .
2 CONT
2 CONT Connecticut Puritan Settlers, 1633-1845   Catalogue of the Names of the First Puritan Settlers of Connecticut. (Continued.) [Mann Family.] Nathaniel Mann, who m. Elizabeth George in 1704, came from Massachusetts to what is now Man
2 CONC sfield when it was a wilderness, and being the first settler in the place, it was honored by the name of Mansfield, in memory of its first settler, about 1720. He removed to Hebron, where he purchased another farm, and settled upo
2 CONC n it for life--but he died at his son's in Colchester, at an advanced age. Among his children he had a son John, who lived, and died in old age, upon the farm purchased by his father in 1720. Baldwin says that they died in Wrentha
2 CONC m, Vital Records of Wrentham, MA, 1910, pages 471 & 472.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel's death date is found in the "Vital Records of Wrentham, Norfolk Co., MA", to 1850, Vol. 2, page 472.
2 CONT
2 CONT Catalogue of the Names of the First Puritan Settlers of Connecticut. (Continued.) [Mann Family.] Nathaniel, son of Rev. Samuel, m. Elizabeth George, Dec. 1704, and had children, George, John, Nathaniel, Mary, Robert, Jeremiah, Jos
2 CONC eph, Ezra, Richard and Timothy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Listed in "The Mann Family Tree Chart", held by NEHGS. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Tombstone inscription, viewed and photographed on 17 July 2004 by Benjamin Kinsey at Wrentham Centre Cemetery. " In memory of Mr Nathaniel Mann who died May 11th 1756 in ye 80th year of his life"
2 CONT
2 CONT American Genealogical-Biographical Index (AGBI) Record  about Nathaniel MANN  Name: Nathaniel MANN  Birth Date: 167?   Birthplace: Massachusetts   Volume: 109   Page Number: 340   Reference: A genealogical dict. of the first settl
2 CONC ers of New England, showing three generations of those who came before May, 1692. By James Savage. Boston. 1861. (4v.)v.3:146  
2 CONT
2 CONT NEHGS-REGISTER, Vol. 13, 1859, p. 326. Submitted by George W. Messinger  NATHANIEL MAN who married Elizabeth George had 10 children. He died May 11th, 1756, aged 80. Ch.:  1. George-b. Sept. 29, 1705.  2. John-b. Aug. 12, 1707.  3
2 CONC . Nathaniel-b. Aug. 6, 1709.  4. Mary-b.July 24, 1711.  5. Robert-b. April 11, 1713.  6. Jeremiah-b. May 26, 1715.  7. Joseph-b. Aug. 13, 1717.  8. Ezra-b. Oct. 13, 1719.  9. Timothy-b. May 3, 1722.  10. Richard-b. Aug 17, 1723.  
2 CONC From cousin Barbara Wyatt
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel Man in the Massachusetts, Town and Vital Records, 1620-1988 Name:Nathaniel Man Event Type:Death Birth Date:abt 1676 Death Date:11 May 1756 Death Place:Wrentham, Massachusetts Death Age:80
2 CONT
