1 OCCU Minister of Religion & Harvard Graduate
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=26957094 '''Rev Nathaniel Huntting'''] Find A Grave Memorial# 26957094
2 CONT * [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=cr&GRid=33956735&CRid=1435258& '''South End Cemetery, East Hampton, Suffolk County, New York, USA''']
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://books.google.com/books?id=lxARAQAAMAAJ&lpg=RA1-PA48&ots=KkmMkO7fAD&dq=Edward%20Mitchelson%20marshal%20general%20biography&pg=RA1-PA48#v=onepage&q=Edward%20Mitchelson%20marshal%20general%20biography&f=true The Heroes o
2 CONC f the American Revolution and Their Descendants:] Battle of Long Island (Google eBook) Henry Whittemore Heroes of the Revolution Publishing Company, 1897 - Long Island, Battle of, New York, N.Y., 1776 - 505 pages.  Page 48:
2 CONT
2 CONT >Rev. Nathaniel Huntting, son of John (2) and Elizabeth (Paine) Huntting, was born in Dedham, Mass" 1675; graduated at Harvard, 1693; removed to East Hampton, L. I., where he died, 1753. He married Mary, daughter of John and Ruth 
2 CONC Green, of Boston, Mass. Nathaniel Huntting (1) was the second minister of the church at East Hampton, where he preached from 1696 to 1746. John Green, born in Cambridge, Mass., 1636, was the son of Percival and Ellen Green, of Eng
2 CONC land, who came to New England on the ship " Susan and Ellen," in 1635. John Green was Marshal-General or High Sheriff of Massachusetts colony in 1681, succeeding his father-in-law, Edward Mitchelson, who had held the office since 
2 CONC 1657. Ruth, a sister of Mary Green, married another ancestor of Teunis D. Huntting, thus forming a direct relationship on the maternal as well as the paternal side.
2 CONT
2 CONT >By his marriage with Mary Green, daughter of John Green, Nathaniel Huntting (1) had a son, Nathaniel ( 2).
