2 CONT Will:
2 CONT
2 CONT "In the name of God, Amen. I, John Wade, of the County of Amherst and State of Virginia in reasonable state of health of body and sound of mind and memory thanks be given to God calling to mind the mortality of my body and knowing
2 CONC  it is appointed for all men once to die. I do make and ordain this my last will and testiament, that is to say principally and first of all I give and recommend my soul into the hands of almighty God that gave it and my body I re
2 CONC commend to the earth to be buried ina decent manner at the directions of my executors; never dobting but at the general resurrection I shall receive the same again by the power of God and as toughing such sorldly estate where with
2 CONC  it has pleased God to bless me with in this life, I give, demise and dispose of those in the follwing manner and form.
2 CONT
2 CONT First, after the decease of self I bequeath to my son, Dawson, an English shilling. Likewise I bequeath to my beloved wife, Elizabeth, during her life all my estate both land, stoak, household stuff, and eberything I possiss to he
2 CONC r use and after her decease to my son and daughter, Jesse Shasteen (son-in-lar) and Eleanor Shasteen whatever shall be then remaining. And I do hereby utterly disallow, remove and disanul (sic) all and every other former testament
2 CONC s, will, legees (sic), bequests and Escc (could be executors) by me in any ways before named wills and bequeaths, ratifying and confirming this and no other Elizabeth. In witness whereof I have hereunto set my hand and seal this f
2 CONC ifteenth day of February one thousand seven hundred and eighty five."
