2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT The will of Richard Wade, Sr. was dated 21 August 1755 and proved in Goochland
2 CONT County Court on 15 November 1757. Sons John and Joseph Wade received the land on
2 CONT which their father lived for equal division. The legacies of sons William and
2 CONT Richard Wade were the lands and goods that were in their possession. Daughters
2 CONT Elizabeth Boatwright (Elisabeth Bootwright) and Joanna Tyler (Tilor) were
2 CONT bequeathed the pewter which they already had. Daughter Lucy Barnett got a cow and
2 CONT two sows. The rest of the estate was to be divided between the two youngest sons,
2 CONT John and Joseph, and two youngest daughters, Frances and Martha, after his wife
2 CONT had taken her dower right. He named his wife as executrix. He signed his will
2 CONT before Robert Willis, Richard Barnett and Edward Barnett and it was proved by
2 CONT Robert Willis and Edward Barnett. (Goochland County, Virginia, Deed Book 7, page
2 CONT 214, abstract, Mrs. Louis C. Hill.)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Goochland County, Virginia, Deed Book 1, Page 446 On 15 January 1733
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Wade of St James Parish, Goochland County, sold to William Maynard, for 40 pounds, 200 acres on the north side of the James River in the Parish and County of Goochland. The tract was bounded by lands of Robert Willis and L
2 CONC aForce, as well as that of Richard Wade, where the boundary crossed Hazle Branch. Signed by Richard Wade, the ded was witnessed by Anthony Hoggatt, Joseph Dabbs, John Phelps, Peter Ware and Thomas Hinton. 
2 CONT Goochland County, Virginia, Deed Book 2, Pages 65-66 On 17 March 1734
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Wade of Goochland County, planter, conveyed to Leonard Henley of Blissland Parish, James City County, for one year, for 5 shillings sterling, 202 acres on Little Tuckahoe Creek and lying in both Goochland and Henrico Count
2 CONC ies. The boundaries were in a flat valley near the hed of Little Drinkinghole Creek, a small branch on the west side of Little Tuckahoe Creek in Goochalnd County, next to Thomas Hardin, on the north side of the same branch in Henr
2 CONC ico County and on the west side of Little Tuckahoe Creek in Goochland County. On the following day a subsequent deed for the same purpose involved another payment of 10 pounds, 10 shillings. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Goochland County, Virginia, Deed Book 2, Pages 264 and 272 On 15 November 1736
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Wade deeded to James Wade, both of St James Parish, Goochland County, 240 acres in that count in the fork of Tuckahoe Creek, where James Wade was living. It ws the remainder of a tract, granted to Richard Wade by patent da
2 CONC ted 28 Sepember 1728, from which Richard Wade had previously conveyed a portion to William Maynard. Signed by Richard Wade, the deed was witnessed by William Street and John Utley. Richard Wade acknowledged it in court on 16 Novem
2 CONC ber 1736. Griselle Wade, wife of Richard, relinquished her dower right in court in March 1746. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Goochland County, Virginia, Deed Book 4, Pages 196 and 272 On 18 June 1743
2 CONT Goochland County, Virginia, Deed Book 4, Pages 196 and 272 On 18 June 1743 Richard Wade bought 200 acres for 25 pounds fro William Gray and his wife Elizabeth, who was the executrix fo the will of William Chamberlayne, deceased. T
2 CONC he tract, adjoining Leonard Henley, Richard Wade, John Price, Rene LaForce, Giles Letcher and James Wade, had been occupied formerly by William Maynard, who had mortgaged it to William Chamberlayne. William Gray was described as a
2 CONC  gentleman of New Kent County, Virginia, when Richard Wade sold part of this tract to William Wildey on 15 November 1743.
2 CONT
2 CONT Goochland County, Virginia, Deed Book 5, Page 436 09 July 1748
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Wade of Goochland County gave 45 acres of land to his son William Wade, for love and affection, on 09 July 1748. William was already residing on the tract, which was on Little Tuckahoe Creek adjoining land of Price, Willis
2 CONC  and Henley. The deed, which was signed by Richard Wade and marked by Griselle Wade was witnessed by Daniel Price, Rene Laforce and Samuel Shepard. It was acknowledged by Richard Wade and his wife Griselle on 19 July 1748. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Goochland County, Virginia, Deed Book 6, Page 163 On 19 August 1751
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Wade, Sr., of St James Northam, Goochland County, conveyed for love and affection to his son Richard Wade, Jr., 75 acres on Deep Branch of Little Tuckahoe Creek in the same parish and county. The tract on which Richard, Jr
2 CONC ., was then living was adjacent to the land of Rene LaForce, Giles Letcher and Dan Price. The deed was signed by Richard Wade and Griselle Wade, who made her mark.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
