2 DATE 4 DEC 1677
2 PLAC Probably Ballycarty Castle
2 ADDR
3 CITY Ballycarty
3 STAE Munster
3 CTRY Ireland
1 TITL Capt.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Captain John Blennerhassett held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.) for Kerry.
2 CONT
2 CONT alias John "Jack" Hassett  High Sheriff of Kerry 1640-1;  | Capt. of Regt. of Foot 1643;   MP ("Knight of the Shire") for Kerry 1661-66 (when he unseated Richard Chute)                 
2 CONT
2 CONT He gained the rank of Captain in 1643 in the service of the Foot.
2 CONT
2 CONT He acquired the forfeited McElligott lands of East and West Ballymacelligott, Ballygrelah, and East and West Gortanleas in 1661.
2 CONT
2 CONT He lived at Ballycarty Castle, Ballyseedy, County Kerry, Ireland.
