2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 10 MAY 1654
2 ADDR
3 CITY Barnstable
3 STAE Plymouth Colony
1 DEAT
2 DATE 26 OCT 1728
2 ADDR
3 CITY Billerica
3 STAE Province of Massachusetts
1 OCCU
1 TITL Lt.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Was the first recorded birth in Billerica, Massachusetts. " His long continuance in several offices, of a civil and military kind, affords a proof of the confidence reposed in him by his fellow citizens." from Gene
2 CONC alogies of the Families and Descendants of the Early Settlers of Watertown, MA (1855; 2nd ed., Boston 1860, 450-522) by Henry Bond.
2 CONT
2 CONT History of the Andrews Family, published 1890
2 CONT
2 CONT Buried in the Old South Cemetary, Billerica, Mass.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Only''' child of John  Stearns and Sarah Mixer
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/2HKB-DHY/capt-john-stearns-ii-1654-1728
2 CONT
2 CONT Capt John Stearns II
2 CONT Male
2 CONT 10 May 1654–26 October 1728
2 CONT •
2 CONT 2HKB-DHY
2 CONT
2 CONT Brief Life History of John
2 CONT
2 CONT When Capt John Stearns II was born on 10 May 1654, in Billerica, Middlesex, Massachusetts Bay Colony, British Colonial America, his father, John Stearns, was 31 and his mother, Sarah Mixer, was 19. He married Elizabeth Bigelow on 
2 CONC 6 September 1676, in Watertown, Middlesex, Massachusetts Bay Colony, British Colonial America. They were the parents of at least 6 sons and 6 daughters. He died on 26 October 1728, in Billerica, Middlesex, Massachusetts Bay Colony
2 CONC , British Colonial America, at the age of 74, and was buried in Old South Burying Ground, Billerica, Middlesex, Massachusetts, United States.
2 CONT
