1 NAME Isaac /Stearns/ III
2 GIVN Isaac
2 SURN Stearns
2 NSFX III
2 _MARNM Stearns
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 26 AUG 1665
2 ADDR
3 CITY Lexington
3 STAE Massachusetts
3 CTRY Colonial America
1 BURI
2 DATE 1741
1 DEAT
2 DATE 22 MAY 1741
2 ADDR
3 CITY Stoughton
3 STAE Massachusetts
3 CTRY Colonial America
1 OCCU
1 TITL Deacon
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Isaac Stearns III was the son of Isaac Stearns II and Sarah Beers. His wife, Elizabeth Stone, was the daughter of Simon Stone of Watertown and Mary Whipple of Ipswich. Isaac Stearns III and his family lived in Lexi
2 CONC ngton and then moved to Stoughton about 1716, where they built the first house in Stoughton. The house no longer stands but a memorial marks the site (the marker is pictured). It is not known where Isaac or Elizabeth are buried. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Isaac III and Elizabeth were:
2 CONT *Isaac IV, b. 19 Oct 1697 (twin)
2 CONT *Simon, b. 19 Oct 1697 (twin)
2 CONT *Jabesh, b. 27 Jan 1700
2 CONT *Jonathan, b. 20 Nov 1791
2 CONT *Hannah, b. 26 Jan 1704, m. Capt Ezekiel Upham of Sturbridge
2 CONT *Mary, b. 14 Nov 1706, m. Dr. Edward Esty of Stoughton
2 CONT *Martha, b. 14 Nov 1709, m. Daniel Talbot of Stoughton
2 CONT *Ebenezer, bapt. 8 July 1711, m. Thankful Clap of Walpole
2 CONT *Abigail, b. 12 Nov 1713
2 CONT
2 CONT From Isaac Stearns Genealogy by Avis Stearns VanWagenen, p. 23-24.
2 CONT * Reference: [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=104309165 Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 12 2016, 18:28:38 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT Actual text from Genealogy and memoirs of Isaac Stearns and his descendants, by Avis Stearns Van Wagenen (Generation Three):
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.ebooksread.com/authors-eng/avis-stearns-van-wagenen/genealogy-and-memoirs-of-isaac-stearns-and-his-descendants-wna/page-3-genealogy-and-memoirs-of-isaac-stearns-and-his-descendants-wna.shtml
2 CONT
2 CONT 56— ISAAC STEARNS 3d (20), b., Aug. 26, 1665, son of Isaac Jr., and Sarah (Beers) Stearns, of Lexington, Mass.; md., , 1696, Elizabeth Stone, b., Oct. 9, 1670. The births of his first four chil. are recorded in Cambridge, and the 
2 CONC rest in Lexington, Mass. He removed to Stoughton, Mass., about 1716. Administration of the estate of "Isaac Stearnes, of Stoughton" was granted to his sons, Simon and Jonathan Stearns, May 22, 1741. His inventory, £585, 2sh., 6d.,
2 CONC  was dated June 25, 1741; nine children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Cambridge:
2 CONT *1. 57— ISAAC STEARNS, 4th (159), b., Oct. 19, 1697. 
2 CONT *2. 58— SIMON STEARNS (163), b., Oct. 19, 1697. 
2 CONT *3. 59— JABESH STEARNS, b., Jan. 27, 1700; d., Apr. 30, 1700. 
2 CONT *4. 60— JONATHAN STEARNS (167), b., Nov. 20, 1701 ; of Stoughton. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children born in Lexington
2 CONT *5. 61— HANNAH STEARNS, b., Jan. 26, 1704; md., Nov. 17, 1726, Capt. Ezekiel Upham, of Sturbridge, Mass., b., 1700; d., Jan. 10, 1788. 
2 CONT **(a) — Ezekiel Upham Jr., b., Nov. 30, 1727. 
2 CONT **(b) — Hannah Upham, b., Dec. 4, 1729. 
2 CONT **(c) — Abigail Upham, b., Feb. 22, 1732; md., Dec. 21, 1752, Ephraim White; d., Jan. 6, 1759. 
2 CONT **(d) — John Upham, b., Apr. 6, 1734. 
2 CONT **(e) — Asa Upham, b., May 18, 1736. 
2 CONT **(f) — William Upham, b., Oct. 29, 1738. 
2 CONT **(g) — Isaac Upham, b., Oct. 3, 1741. 
2 CONT **(h) — Nathaniel Upham, b., July 25, 1745. 
2 CONT *6. 62— MARY STEARNS, bapt. Nov. 10, 1706; md., about 1729, Dr. Edward Esty, of Stoughton, who lived to be 100 yrs. old. They had fourteen chil, who all d., without families, except the two following: 
2 CONT **a) — Solomon Esty, who had one son, Solomon Esty Jr., who md. and d., early, leaving a son, Solomon Esty and a dau., Mary or Mercy Esty, both of whom lived in Newton, Mass. 
2 CONT **(b) — Mercy Esty, b., Nov. 14, 1730; d., Dec. 25. 1824; md., Nov. 21, 1776. David Sumner, of Milton, Mass., and had one daughter, Mercy Sumner. 
2 CONT *7. 63— MARTHA STEARNS, bapt., Feb. 7, 1709-10; md., Nov. 1, 1734, Daniel Talbot, of Stoughton, Mass., who d., Mar. 9, 1778. 
2 CONT **(a) — Amaziah Talbot, b., Sept. 7, 1837; d., aged 17 yrs., near Crown Point or Ticonderoga. 
2 CONT **(b)— Daniel Talbot Jr., b., Sept., 1740; d., Nov. 2, 1820. 
2 CONT **(c) — Martha Talbot, b., Aug. 14, 1742; md., June 29, 1762, Seth Johnson, of Stoughton. 
2 CONT **(d) — Isaac Talbot, b., June 21, 1744; nid., Nov., 1769, Susan Turner, of Walpole. 
2 CONT **(e) — George Talbot, b., June i, 1746; d., Feb. 25, 1827. 
2 CONT **(f)— Sarah Talbot, b., Dec. 13, 1751. 
2 CONT **(g) — Benjamin Talbot, b., Dec. 13, 1751.
2 CONT ***Benjamin Talbot d., soon. 
2 CONT ***Sarah Talbot md., July 10, 1783, Amos Guild; d., Aug. 10, 1829. 
2 CONT **(h) — Benjamin Talbot, b., 1753; a Lieutenant; d., 1778, Chesterfield, N. H., on his way home from the Revolutionary Army. 
2 CONT *8. 64— EBENEZER STEARNS (174), bapt, July 8, 1711. 
2 CONT *9. 65— ABIGAIL STEARNS, bapt., Nov. 12, 1713; intention of marriage with Samuel Brackett pub., Aug. 24, 1737. 
2 CONT
