2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Sternes, the son of Isaac Jr. and Sarah Beers, was born on December 20, 1667, at Cambridge, Middlesex, Massachusetts,[1] A merged profile showed that he was born at Lexington,[2] [3]but I can find no record of his birth in 
2 CONC the Lexington VRs.Watt-266 00:45, 1 April 2014 (EDT)
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Phoebe Waite before 1697. [4] It is said that he died as the result of the falling of a tree on November 19, 1721.[5] The Lexington records show that Samuel died on December 19, 1721.[2] Samuel had eleven children.[5][6
2 CONC ]
2 CONT
2 CONT 66— SAMUEL STEARNS (21), b., Jan. 11, 1667-8, son of Isaac Jr. and Sarah (Beers) Stearns, of Lexington. Mass.; md., Phoebe —. He was tithing man and assessor in Lexington for several years, and was killed by a casualty, said to ha
2 CONC ve been the falling of a tree, Nov. 19, 1721. His widow administered his estate, John Stearns of Concord (78), being her surety. She moved to Littleton. Mass., in 1730. with some of her children. There was a "Caution of Chelmsford
2 CONC , July 24, 1750, against settlement of Phoebe Stearns from Littleton." Samuel Stearns had eleven children.[5]
2 CONT
