1 OCCU Deacon, soldier in King Philip's War
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} On 19 Dec 1675 he was a soldier in King Philip's War and wounded at the Great Swamp Fight in Rhode Island. On 24 May 1682 he became a freeman in Massachusetts. In 1711 he invested 6 pounds in the establishment of t
2 CONC he town of Lexington, Massachusetts. At some point he invested 1 Pound in the new meeting house in Cambridge, Massachusetts. In 1714, 1715 and 1723 he was a Selectmen of Lexington, Massachusetts. On 17 Nov 1715 he was elected Deac
2 CONC on of the Church of Lexington, Massachusetts; the same church where his father was Deacon and held that office for 20 years, until his death. At some point he served in Capt. Thomas Prentincs troop of horse in the Narraganset Expe
2 CONC dition.
2 CONT
