2 CONT 16 Dec 1714: Articles of agreement relating to the estate of Samuel Converse (Senior, d. 1699). "Articles of Agreement made between Sarah Converse relict and the children and heirs of the said deceased, for the settlement of the d
2 CONC ecedent's estate, which was valued at 130 pounds, that our honored mother, Sarah Converse shall have for her use 50 pounds, during her life, to wit, that she shall have half use of the house and cellar; that JOSEPH Converse shall 
2 CONC provide her certain things, and shall have 11 pounds, 18s, besides what he has purchased of his eldest brother SAMUEL. It is agreed that JOSEPH shall have the whole of the estate of the deceased, he to pay the rest of their severa
2 CONC l parts as above.
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed SARAH Converse <mother>, JOSEPH Converse <son>, MARY Converse (daughter), HANNAH Converse <daughter>, and David Roberts Jr, guardian to JOSIAH Converse <son>.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Dutton-418
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Dutton, son of Thomas Dutton and Susannah Palmer Dutton, was born in Reading, Massachusetts, September 14, 1648. He married Rebecca Draper (widow of Adam Draper of Concord) on January 10, 1678-79. He married second, Novembe
2 CONC r 1721, Sarah Converse. He bought or had land of his father in Billerica in 1670. He was in Sergeant Hill's garrison in 1675 and in the center squadron in 1707. In 1677 he served and was wounded by Indians in the ill-starred exped
2 CONC ition to Kennebec country. Children: 1. Rebecca, born 1679, married Daniel Shed; 2. Thomas, born 1681, 3. John, born 1683-4, 3, Susannah, born 1687, 5, Susan born 1687. All born at Billerica.[1] Thomas apparently died in 1728.
2 CONT
