2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Shepard-161
2 CONT
2 CONT Rachel was born about 1665 in Concord, Massachusetts to John and Sarah Goble Shepard.[1] She married John Stone in Lexington on April 27, 1687[2] and they had at least six children born there.[1] Rachel died in Lexington on March 
2 CONC 17, 1724 and is buried at the Old Burying Ground.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT # Rachel b 12 Mar 1687; died young
2 CONT # John b 15 Dec 1689
2 CONT # Mary b 26 Sep 1692
2 CONT # Anna b 27 Nov 1694
2 CONT # Rachel b 06 Jun 1697
2 CONT # Ruth b 27 Aug 1700
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT *Bartlett, J. Gardner. Gregory Stone Genealogy: Ancestry and Descendants of Dea. Gregory Stone of Cambridge, Mass., 1320-1917. (Boston, Massachusetts: Stone Family Association, 1918) 80, . “Children of Dea. Samuel Stone and Sarah 
2 CONC Stearns: John, b. Cambridge Farms [Lexington] 12 May 1663, d. 3 Feb 1711/12, m. Cambridge 27 Apr 1687 Rachel Shepard. Will of John Stone Jr. of Cambridge, husbandman, dated 19 Jan 1711/12, proved 10 Mar 1711/12, mentions wife Rach
2 CONC el; daughters Mary Stone, Anna, Rachel and Ruth [last three underage, Ruth "youngest"]; sons John [sole executor]; Joseph Watkins [apparently apprentice?]; brother Samuel Stone and Dea. John Miriam overseers.”
2 CONT * https://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:John_Stone_%28129%29
