2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Stone-4325
2 CONT
2 CONT Lydia Stone was born on November 11, 1665, and baptized on December 31, 1665, both in Lexington, Middlesex, Massachusetts[1]. She was the daughter of Samuel and Sarah (Stearns) Stone. Lydia married Francis Bowman on July 26, 1684,
2 CONC  in Lexington. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had 7 children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Francis
2 CONT * Mary
2 CONT * Lydia
2 CONT * John
2 CONT * Sarah
2 CONT * Isaac
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial Inscription: Here Lyes Buried the Body of Mrs Lydia Bowman wife to Lieut Francis Bowman Who Decd Decembr ye 10 1719 in ye 55 Year of Her Age
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Old Burying Ground Lexington Middlesex County Massachusetts, USA Plot: B.22[2]
2 CONT
