1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Samuel Manning Jr.=
2 CONT BIRTH	1665, Cambridge, Middlesex County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT DEATH	20 Feb 1755 (aged 89–90), Windham, Windham County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT BURIAL	Palmertown Cemetery, Scotland, Windham County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID 42876119, Photos by Sara & C D Bird
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT Samuel Manning, Jr, eldest son of Samuel Manning by his first wife Elizabeth Stearns (Isaac,1), was b. circa 1665 prob. at Cambridge, Mass. before his parents moved to Billerica, Mass. He d. Feb. 20, 1755 at Windham, Conn., not in
2 CONC  the year 1775 purportedly inscribed on his gravestone.  In circa 1696 Samuel m. Deborah Spalding (q.v. Spaulding), dau. of Edward Spalding (q.v.) and Priscilla Underwood, b. Sept. 12, 1667 at Chelmsford, Mass. She d. Aug 8, 1725 
2 CONC at Windham, Conn., Æ 63. They had nine children who will outlined later.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Manning came back in early life to Cambridge, Mass., to live, when his father in 1698 gave him a deed of the real estate which his great-grandfather purchased there in 1638. For reasons not now fully understood he did not e
2 CONC njoy the ancestral home in Cambridge as well as he anticipated, which unrest caused him to seek a home for himself and family where they could enlarge their possessions and live more agreeably to their taste and comfort. So, in or
2 CONC der to consummate his plans, he sold nearly all of his real estate in Cambridge, Mass., between the years of 1720 and 1724, and during this interval he removed his family to that part of the town of Windham known now as Scotland, 
2 CONC Conn., where he spent the remainder of his life, dying Feb. 24. 1755. His wife departed this life before him, dying June 30, 1723.  Samuel Manning m. Deborah , unknown.  They had eight children. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Graveyard Detail'''
2 CONT According to the Manning Genealogy (1902), p. 60, Samuel's almost unreadable gravestone, misread by a Manning family descendant prior to 1900, says:
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Inscription'''
2 CONT Here Lies the Body of
2 CONT Mr. Samuel Manning
2 CONT Who Departed this Life
2 CONT Febr 20th 1775 [sic 1755] in
2 CONT The 93d year of his Age
2 CONT
2 CONT ''The sweet Remembrance
2 CONT of the Just
2 CONT Shall Flourish when
2 CONT He sleeps in dust.''
2 CONT
