2 CONT Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob Pennington had their beginnings in Cecil County, Maryland, according to several researchers including Group Leader Patricia Dear of California, who stated in her article in Pennington Pedigrees 14-1, pp. 
2 CONC 4-5, that she had documented that Abraham Pennington of early Cecil County, Maryland, was the same Abraham who moved to Virginia and later on to South Carolina where he d.. Abraham was listed as yeoman, planter, and Indian trader 
2 CONC in the records.
