1 NOTE {geni:about_me} widower of Sarah Jaques who died 4/6/1816
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.maineulsterscots.com/docs/THE_BATH_DAILY_TIMES.pdf Johnson Graves and Sarah (Staples, sister of Stephen and Samuel Staples) left  children as follows: Daniel, who died of measles at Falmouth, 20 months old. Elizabeth, b
2 CONC orn April 19, 1759, who married Benj. Jaquith of Bowdoin. John, born July 4, 1762 in Falmouth, resided in Litchfield, Maine. William, born, Aug. 4, 1765 in Topsham, married 1st, Sarah Jacques of Bowdoin, a sister  of Benj. Jacques
2 CONC , above mentioned. She died Apr. 6, 1816, aged 44, being 44 the 4th of June  next. His second wife was widow Catherine Dunham, of Bowdoinham. She was born in  Topsham, her first husband being Capt. Thos. Dunham. Her maiden name wa
2 CONC s Potter, a  daughter of Elder Potter, Jr., formerly of Topsham. Crispus Graves, born Oct 20, 1767, married Betsey Jacques, Dec. 13, 1792
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT William GRAVES  
2 CONT Birth: estimated between 1737 and 1797
2 CONT Son of Charles Johnson GRAVES and Sarah (Staples) GRAVES 
2 CONT Brother of Daniel GRAVES; Elizabeth (Graves) JAQUES; John GRAVES and Crispus GRAVES 
2 CONT Donald Bronson GRAVES	
