1 TITL Capt.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Capt. Ebenezer Graves (381) was born 10 Jan. 1771 in Marblehead, Mass., was baptized 13 Jan. 1771, and died 21 Dec. 1850.  He first married Rebecca Cash, daughter of Moses Cash, on 30 Nov. 1794 in Marblehead.  She 
2 CONC died 16 May 1806.  He secondly married Ruth Barker, sister of Capt. George Barker.  Ebenezer was a sea captain, and for many years commanded vessels trading between Marblehead and foreign ports.  His last voyage was to Bilboa, Spa
2 CONC in in 1823.  He lived in Marblehead, Mass.  His widow died 8 March 1868 at the age of 91 years, 9 months and one day. They adopted Emeline Reed, niece of his first wife.  (R‑20)
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT * Graves, Ebenezer  Born Jan. 10, 1770.
2 CONT * Selectman 1797-1799, 1800-1804 to 1810. 
2 CONT * 1798 Schooner "Saratoga." (C. P.) (Jr.) 
2 CONT * 1803 Brigantine "Polly." (Condemned G. C.) (Jr.) 
2 CONT * 1804 and 1805 Representative to General Court. 1816 Barque "Increase." 
2 CONT * ____ Brigantine "Czarina." (Mate). 
2 CONT * 1818 Schooner "Caesar," 9lT. (S. P.) 
2 CONT * 1819 Schooner "Caesar," 109T. 
2 CONT * 1820 Schooner "President." 
2 CONT * Schooner "Tom." 
2 CONT * Barque "Panama."
