1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =LT Jonathan Frye=
2 CONT * BIRTH 4 Dec 1742 Andover, Essex County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT * DEATH 12 Jul 1793 (aged 50) Bucksport, Hancock County, Maine, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL Frye Family Cemetery, Bucksport, Hancock County, Maine, USA
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID 193950394 Photos by Veteran Guy
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan Frye, b. Andover, graduated Harvard College, 1761; served four years Lieutenant in Continental army, stationed at West Point during Arnold's betrayal and was one of the first settlers of Bucksport; drowned in Penobscot ri
2 CONC ver July 12, 1793, aged 50.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gravesite Details'''
2 CONT Lt. Frye has a memorial stone in the Buck Cemetery, at the time of his death that cemetery was only for the Bucks. The Memorial stone was placed there by his grandson, in the 1880's, because the cemetery where he was buried had be
2 CONC en abandoned.
2 CONT
