1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for RHODE ISLAND with the rank of PRIVATE. [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A000166  DAR Ancestor #  A000166]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Will and Testament of Pardon Abbott:
2 CONT
2 CONT [fees for recording 35 cents]
2 CONT
2 CONT In the name of God Amen, I Pardon Abbott of Coventry in the County of Kent State of Rhode Island and being weak in body but of sound mind and meaning do make and ordain this my last Will and Testament [that is to Say] after recomm
2 CONC ending my Soul to God that gave it and my body to the earth to be buried in a decent manner at the disnation of my Executor here in after named:
2 CONT
2 CONT Firstly My will is that all my just debts and funeral charges be paid by my Executor within a convient time after my decease.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2ndly My will is that my wife Anna Abbott shall have a decent and comfortable maintenance out of the Estate that I shall here after give to my son Oliver during the time she may survive me in life to be his wished by the said Oliv
2 CONC er.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3rdly To my Seven Children namely Amey Wallens, Olney Abbott, Israel Abbott, Daniel Abbott, Elizabeth Colvin, Nany Phillips, and James Abbott I give and bequath half a dollar each to be paid by my Executor when called for after my
2 CONC  demese and that together with what they have heretofore received to be in full for their portion of my Estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4thly To my son Oliver Abbott I give and bequath my lot of land called the Rueben lot situated in Coventry containing by estimation twenty acres and one hundred and forty-six rods of land and is bounded. Southerly on land of Danie
2 CONC l Matteson, Westerly partly on land of Josiah Briggs and partly on David Burlingame, Northerly on lands of David and Sterry Burlingame and Easterly on Land of the heirs of Rueben Abbott Also on the remainder of my Estate both Real
2 CONC  and personal where so ever the same may be found lying or being to him the said Oliver his heirs and assigns forever.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lastly I do hereby Constitute and appoint my last named son Oliver Abbott to be my whole and sole Executor to this my last Will and Testament to see the same performed according to the true intent and meaning their of and I do her
2 CONC by revoke all other Wills Testaments by me in any use Willed or bequeathed satisfying this and no other to be my last Will and Testament.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Witness where of I have here unto my hand and Seal this fifteenth day of June in the year one thousand eight hundred and twenty two.
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed sealed published pronounced and declared by me the said Pardon Abbott to be my last Will and Testament in presents of these witnesses.
2 CONT
2 CONT [signed] Pardon Abbott
2 CONT
2 CONT [signed by witnesses]
2 CONT
2 CONT David Burlingame, Stephen Colvin, Ray Johnson
2 CONT __________
2 CONT
2 CONT At a Court of Probate Holden within and for the Town of Coventry on the first day of March A.D. 1828
2 CONT
2 CONT The within Will was proved approved of and ordered to be recorded and the same is recorded in the 4th book of Probate Reocrds on the 190th and 191th pages.
2 CONT
2 CONT Witness Asa Stone Probate Clerk
2 CONT
