2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT John's house was on Augusta to Winthrop Road. He is listed in the 1790 census (1-1-3-0-0) of Winthrop. John was formerly of Vassal borough. Anna died before him in 1805. Both are buried in Mt Vernon, Kennebec Co, Maine. At the tim
2 CONC e of their marriage intentions they both claimed Hallowell as their residence. Manchester Maine Early Settlers 1775-1778.
2 CONT
2 CONT On p15 of "Twenty Secluded Burial places, Northwestern Mt Vernon Area" by Clayton Dolloff, Sept 1989 the gravestone markings show him as John Hovey, Esq. d April 19.1851 abt 88 yr. and Anna d July 11, 1843 in the 75 year of her ag
2 CONC e. They are buried in "A three family burying ground stands southerly of Harold and Dorothy Kent's home on the Belgrade Road near Mount Vernon Village. The plot about thirty-five by forty feet in area, is surrounded with a stone w
2 CONC all three or four feet high. The entrance is closed with three hooked chains. There ar six marked graves within: " John and Anna Hovey, their daughter and son-in-law, Susannah and Nathaiel Hill and Rev, John Haynes and wife, Lydia
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT The Vienna Historical Society sent a letter to Miriam K. Buckley who is also researching the Hovey Family
2 CONT
