0 @N6000000006602638264@ NOTE Sackville College was founded by Robert, second Earl of Dorset, a man of great ability and
1 CONT who spoke, which was rare in those days, several languages with much fluency. His father
1 CONT was the famous Thomas Sackville, Queen Elizabeth's High Treasurer and one of the Judges
1 CONT who sent the Duke of Norfolk to the headsman's block for his complicity in the alleged
1 CONT attempt to get Mary Queen of Scots placed on the English Throne. Through the founder of
1 CONT Sackville College these two families became closely united, for this eldest son of the High
1 CONT Treasurer married Margaret, the only daughter of the beheaded Duke. He held the title but a
1 CONT short time, dying on February 27th, 1609
1 CONT
1 CONT 1. Robert Sackville, 2nd Earl of Dorset was the son of (2) Sir Thomas Sackville, 1st Earl
1 CONT of Dorset and (3) Cicely Sackville [Baker], 1st Countess of Dorset. He was born 1561; died
1 CONT 27th Feb 1609 at Withyham, Sussex; buried after 27th Feb 1609 at St Michaels Parish
1 CONT Church, Withyham, Sussex
1 CONT He married (1) Lady Margaret Howard on 4th Feb 1579 at Saffron Walden, Essex. She was
1 CONT born c 1557, daughter of Thomas Howard, 4th Duke of Norfolk and Margaret Audley; died
1 CONT 19th Aug 1591 at Withyham, Sussex; buried after 19th Aug 1591 at St Michaels Parish
1 CONT Church, Withyham, Sussex.
