0 @N6000000004548360633@ NOTE THE ANCESTORS OF JANE LEE, WIFE OF SAMUEL HYDE
1 CONT
1 CONT 1. WILLIAM BROWNE, died 14 Nov. 1611. He was pastor of the parish church in Horley, co. Surrey from 26 June 1561 to his death.
1 CONT
1 CONT His children:
1 CONT
1 CONT i. Joseph, see below.
1 CONT ii. Benjamin, died in 1636. He was the Rector of Ifield, a neighboring parish of Rusper.
1 CONT iii. Phebe
1 CONT iv. Sara
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT 2. JOSEPH BROWNE, died 15 Oct. 1633 (will dated 16 June 1633). He was clerk and pastor of the parish church at Rusper, County Surrey, England. The name of his first wife and mother of his children was MARGERY PATCHING, who was bur
1 CONC ied 15 Dec. 1605. Joseph married secondly, 12 Feb. 1606, Elizabeth Stone, a widow.
1 CONT
1 CONT Children:
1 CONT
1 CONT i. William, see below.
1 CONT ii. Stephen, probably died young as he was not mentioned in his father's will.
1 CONT iii. Joseph, probably died young as he was not mentioned in his father's will
1 CONT iv. Sara, baptized 22 Oct. 1592; married Arthur Fenner.
1 CONT v. Susan, baptized 14 Jan 1595/96, married Thomas Leachford.
1 CONT vi. Phebe, baptized 12 July 1601, married William Simons.
1 CONT iv. John, baptized 12 Aug. 1604.
1 CONT
1 CONT 3. WILLIAM BROWNE, was baptized 5 Dec. 1585 at Horley, County Surrey, England. He married 20 June 1611, at Rusper, County Sussex, England, JANE BURGIS. He came to New England after 1645 and settled at Saybrook. He died at Long Isl
1 CONC and in 1650. Jane may have died of small pox on the trip over to New England.
1 CONT
1 CONT Children:
1 CONT
1 CONT i. Joseph, baptized 8 Aug. 1613 at Rusper; probably died young as his brother John was listed as the eldest son in the NEHGR, vol of 1909.
1 CONT ii. John, baptized 15 Oct. 1615 at Rusper; came to New England with three children and his father.
1 CONT iii. Jane, baptized 13 Sept. 1618 at Rusper; was buried 21 Aug. 1620 at Rusper.
1 CONT iv. Phebe, see below,
1 CONT iv. Mary, baptized 6 Oct. 1622 at Rusper.
1 CONT v. Thomas, baptized 9 Jan. 1624 at Rusper; was buried 7 Mar. 1645 at Rusper.
1 CONT vi. Henry, baptized 28 Dec. 1626 at Rusper. He also came to New England and settled at Providence, R.I.
1 CONT
1 CONT 4. PHEBE BROWNE (BROWN), was baptized 1 Oct. 1620. She married, in England, THOMAS LEE. Phebe, her husband Thomas and their three children embarked for New England, probably sometime after 1645 and most likely came with Phebe's fa
1 CONC ther. Thomas Lee, however died of small pox enroute, so the tradition is told.
1 CONT
1 CONT Their children:
1 CONT
1 CONT i. Jane, see below.
1 CONT ii. Phebe, baptized 20 May 1642 at Rusper.
1 CONT iii. Thomas, baptized 29 Sept. 1644, settled at Lyme.
1 CONT
1 CONT . JANE LEE was baptized 12 Sept. 1640. She married SAMUEL HYDE.
1 CONT
1 CONT SOURCE:
1 CONT
1 CONT 1. Gen. 1, NEHGR, vol. 63 (1909), pg. 99.
1 CONT 2. Gen. 1-4, ibid, vol. 61 (1907) pg. 116-118.
1 CONT 3. Gen. 1-4, ibid, vol. 62 (1908) pg. 199-200
1 CONT 4. Gen. 1-4, ibid, vol. 63 (1909) pg. 100
1 CONT 5. Gen. 1-4, The American Genealogist, vol. xxv, pg. 249.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Jane LEE
1 CONT BIRTH: 12 SEP 1640, East Saybrook, CT
1 CONT CHRISTENING: 12 SEP 1640, Rusper, Sussex, England
1 CONT DEATH: 12 JAN 1722, Lebanon, New London Co., CT
1 CONT
1 CONT Father: Thomas LEE
1 CONT Mother: Phoebe BROWNE
1 CONT
