0 @N6000000001877506034@ NOTE 2nd Marquess of Powis
1 CONT known as Lord Montgomery
1 CONT viscount of Montgomery 1687
1 CONT Col of Foot 1687/88
1 CONT Page of Honour at coronation of James ii
1 CONT Deputy Lt for Anglesey, Cards, Caerns, Merioneth, Monmouth, Pembroke 1688 (all Welsh counties)
1 CONT Under arrest may - nov 1689 on suspicion of high treason
1 CONT letter 15.12.1696 saying that Lord M surrendered this morning, committed to Newgate to prevent his outlawry - but apparently tricked. The outlawry papers signed several days before
1 CONT outlawed may 1696
1 CONT under arrest dec 1696 - june 1697
1 CONT Old Bailey 5.7.1697
1 CONT bailed june 1697 by Duke of Norfolk, Earl of Darmouth, Lord Carrington, Lord Jeffrys for £5000 each. Let out due to outbreak of gaol fever
1 CONT sold his house in Lincolns Inn Fields to Duke of Newcastle 1705 for £7000
1 CONT MP Kilkenny 1705 - 1710
1 CONT MP Steyning 1708 - 1709
1 CONT built Powis House, Gt Ormond St on the site of the present Powis Place
1 CONT Living at PH 1708
1 CONT in 1712/13 PH was the French embassy, burnt down 26.6.1713
1 CONT abroad in Ghent 1700
1 CONT arrested 1715 to the Tower for suspected abetting the Pretender
1 CONT Outlawry reversed 1722 & Powis Castle restored
1 CONT Restitution of all estates and titles except Duke of Powis
1 CONT buried Hendon 28.10.1745
1 CONT Source Herbert and Clive family tree Nat Trust
