0 @N6000000003178079654@ NOTE RECORDS STATE DEATH AS 12 AUG 1749 AND ANOTHE AS 11 AUG 1749
0 @N6000000004548368042@ NOTE HYDE
1 CONT
1 CONT THE ANCESTORS OF SAMUEL HYDE, JR., SON OF SAMUEL HYDE
1 CONT
1 CONT The name Hyde (or Hide) goes back to the time of King John. The following pedigree is derived from one that was listed in Burkes "Commoners of Britain" and Burkes "American Families with British Ancestry". Both of these differ sli
1 CONC ghtly and there is no proof of a connection with the New England immigrant. The first mention of a Hyde is:
1 CONT
1 CONT 1. MATTHEW de HYDE, whose son:
1 CONT
1 CONT 2. SIR ROBERT HYDE, Knt. living during the time of Henry III (1216-1272) and Lord of the manors of Hyde and Newton in Chesshire; of Shalcross in Derbyshire; and of Haighton in Lancastershire. He married the cousin and heiress of T
1 CONC homas de Norbury, by whom he acquired the lordship of Norbury. His son:
1 CONT
1 CONT 3. ROBERT HYDE, lord of Norbury.
1 CONT
1 CONT His children:
1 CONT
1 CONT i. Sir John, see below.
1 CONT ii. Alexander, who acquired lands in Denton from his father and founded the Hydes of Denton.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT 4. JOHN HYDE, of Norbury and Hyde. HE married Isabel, daughter of SIR WILLIAM BAGGILEY, by whom obtained several estates.
1 CONT
1 CONT Children:
1 CONT
1 CONT i. John, see below.
1 CONT ii. Roger
1 CONT iii. William
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT 5. SIR JOHN HYDE was knighted before 1348 and was Lord of Norbury, Haighton and Half Hyde before 1342. He served in the French wars with the Black Prince in 1357. He married twice. The first wife has been described as Margery, dau
1 CONC ghter of Thomas Davenport and also as Margaret, daughter of Sir John Davenport. the name of the second wife is known only as Alice.
1 CONT
1 CONT Children by first wife:
1 CONT
1 CONT i. Robert, see below.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Children by second wife"
1 CONT
1 CONT ii. Thomas of Warford, married Mary, daughter of William Tabbelegh.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT 6. ROBERT HYDE, Lord of Norbury and Half Hyde, married the daughter of Robert Stavelegh.
1 CONT
1 CONT Their son:
1 CONT
1 CONT 7. ROBERT HYDE, Lord of Norbury and half Hyde, in 1435. He was wounded at Nether Alderley in 1421. He died before 1439 when a Stockport Charter was witnessed by his son:
1 CONT
1 CONT 8. JOHN HYDE, Lord of Norbury, married firstly, Matild, daughter of Hamo Massie of Rixton, Lancashire. He married secondly, before 1450, Katherine, daughter of Sir William Stanley of Hooton. He died about 1460 and was survived by 
1 CONC his eldest son by the first wife.
1 CONT
1 CONT 9. HAMON (or HAMNET) HYDE, of Norbury and half Hyde, was living in 1441. He had a licence for oratories in his manors of Norbury and Haighton 26 Sept. 1455. He married firstly, MARGARET DAVENPORT, daughter of THOMAS DAVENPORT of H
1 CONC endbury and secondly to Joan, his widow, who was living in 1477.
1 CONT
1 CONT Children by first wife:
1 CONT
1 CONT i. John, died 1478.
1 CONT ii. Thomas, see below.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Children by second wife:
1 CONT
1 CONT iii. Peres
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT 10. THOMAS HYDE, of Norbury and half Hyde, heir of his brother. He was aged 40 in 1494. He was exempted from serving on juries in Aug. 1511 and was living in 1523. He married a daughter of Kynveton, of Underwold, Co. Derby and had
1 CONC  four daughters and one son whose name was:
1 CONT
1 CONT 11. ROBERT HYDE, mentioned in 1503 as heir apparent; married firstly, MARGARET HOLAND, daughter of RICHARD HOLAND, of Denton, Leicestershire. He died in 1528.
1 CONT
1 CONT Their children:
1 CONT
1 CONT i. Hamnet, see below.
1 CONT ii. John
1 CONT iii. Agnes, married John Ardene of Alvanley and Harden.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Robert married secondly, a daughter of Robert Scargill.
1 CONT
1 CONT iv. Sir Lawrence Hyde of West Hatch, Wiltshire, married Anne, daughter of Nicholas Sybill of Chimbhams, Kent. He died 7 June 1590.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT 12. HAMNET HYDE married MARGARET WARREN, daughter of LAURENCE WARREN, of Poynton. He died before his father. His son
1 CONT
1 CONT 13. ROBERT HYDE, of Norbury and half Hyde was born about 1523. He became heir of his grandfather Robert (#11 above). He was married five times. His first wife was MARGARET DUKENFIELD, daughter of JOHN DUKENFIELD OF Dukenfield. He 
1 CONC died in 1571.
1 CONT
1 CONT His son by his first wife:
1 CONT
1 CONT 14. ROBERT HYDE of Norbury and Hyde was born about 1544 and died 22 Mar. 1614. He married BEATRICE CALVERLEY, daughter of SIR WILLIAM CALVERLEY, of Calverley, Yorkshire by Elizabeth, daughter of RICHARD SNEYD, who was the second s
1 CONC on of RICHARD SNEYDE, of Sneyde Bradwell. Beatrice died in 1624.
1 CONT
1 CONT They had eight daughters and six sons.
1 CONT
1 CONT i. Hamnet, born 1563, matriculated at Brasenose College, Oxford in 1579; married July 1583, Mary, daughter of John Warren of Poynton; died May 1643.
1 CONT ii. Robert, matriculated at Hart Hall, Oxford in 1583.
1 CONT iii. Thomas, matriculated at Christ's College, Cambridge in 1596; received a B.A. in 1599 and an M.A. in 1603. He was Rector of Wanstrow, Somerset.
1 CONT iv. William, see below.
1 CONT v. Urian
1 CONT vi. John, drowned 1605.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT 15. WILLIAM HYDE matriculated at Christ's College, Cambridge in 1597 and a contemporary at that University of Rev. Peter Bulkeley and one of the founders of Concord, Mass. He went to Leydon, Holland and later in 1635 went to Salem
1 CONC , Mass. with the Rev. Peter Bulkeley. He was one of the original founders of Hartford, Ct. with the Rev. Thomas Hooker in 1636 and removed to Saybrook in 1639. He is said to be identical with but more likely the father of:
1 CONT
1 CONT 16. WILLIAM HYDE was one of the thirty five proprietors of Norwich, Ct. in 1659 with his son Samuel and son-in-law John Post. He died 6 Jan. 1681 at Norwich.
1 CONT
1 CONT Children.
1 CONT
1 CONT i. William ? NOTE: The Norwich Vital Records called his father Senior, indicating that he had a son named William but he has not appeared in any records seen by this compiler.
1 CONT ii. Hester, born in England; married John Post.
1 CONT iii. Samuel, see below.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT 17. SAMUEL HYDE was born in Hartford, Ct. about 1637 and died in Norwich, Ct. in July 1677. He was a farmer and had lands assigned to him at Norwich West farms. He married in June 1659, JANE LEE, daughter of THOMAS LEE and PHEBE B
1 CONC ROWN.
1 CONT
1 CONT Their children:
1 CONT
1 CONT i. Elizabeth, born Aug. 1660; married May 1677, Lieut. Richard Lord..
1 CONT ii. Phebe, born Jan. 1662; married, 21 May 1682, Matthew Griswold.
1 CONT iii. Samuel, born May 1665; married 10 Dec. 1690, Elizabeth Caulkins
1 CONT iv. John, see below.
1 CONT v. William, born Jan. 1669; married 6 Jan. 1695, Anne Bushnell.
1 CONT vi. Thomas, born July 1672; married, Dec. 1697, Mary Backus.
1 CONT vii. Sarah, born Feb. 1675; died in the same year.
1 CONT viii. Jabez, born in May 1677; married Elizabeth Bushnell.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT SOURCE:
1 CONT 1. Gen. 1-16, Burke's Landed Gentry, pg 2759.
1 CONT 2. Burke's Commoners of Britain.
1 CONT 3. Gen. 16-18, Norwich Vital Records.
1 CONT 4. Gen. 17, History of Stonington, Ct.
1 CONT 5. Gen. 16-18, American Ancestry
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Samuel HYDE (Jr.)
1 CONT
1 CONT BIRTH: MAY 1665, Norwich, New London, CT
1 CONT CHRISTENING: MAY 1665, Norwich, New London, CT
1 CONT DEATH: 6 NOV 1742, Lebanon, New London, CT
1 CONT
1 CONT Father: Samuel HYDE
1 CONT Mother: Jane LEE
1 CONT
1 CONT Family 1: Elizabeth CALKINS
1 CONT
1 CONT MARRIAGE: 10 DEC 1690
1 CONT
1 CONT 1.Daniel HYDE
1 CONT ------------------------------------------------------------------------
1 CONT
