1 CONT
1 CONT 158 SAMUEL, Jr., b. May, 166', m. Elizabeth Calkins
1 CONT           (152), Dec. 16, 1690. He lived first at West
1 CONT           Farms, now Franklin, but removed to Windham
1 CONT           and afterwards to Lebanon. At the first
1 CONT           town meeting held at Windham, June 11, 1692,
1 CONT           Samuel was chosen as one of the town officers.
1 CONT           He d. Nov. 6, 1742.
1 CONT Src: Hyde-Dana   Wells, Harriette Hyde. Hyde-Dana. This book contains the genealogical history of the descendants of the Hyde and Dana family joined by marriage on June 5, 1757.  Bibliographic Information: Joe Munsell's Sons, Publ
1 CONC ishers. Albany, NY, 1904., p. 50
0 @N6000000006348490935@ NOTE His parents were Samuel Hyde and Jane Lee.
1 CONT
1 CONT II. SAMUEL HYDE was born about 1636 at hartford. In 1659 he
1 CONT married Jane Lee, daughter of Thomas Lee, an account of whose family
1 CONT is given below. Samuel Hyde seems to have lived with his father at first,
1 CONT after their removal to Norwich, in the newly built habitation, where in
1 CONT 1660 his daughter Elizabeth was born. He is reckoned among the first
1 CONT proprietors of Norwich, as is likewise his father. He died in 1677, leaving
1 CONT seven children as follows: Elizabeth (our ancestress), b. 1660, m.
1 CONT Lieut. Richard Lord; Phoebe, b. Jan. 1663, m. Matthew Griswold of Lyme;
1 CONT Samuel, b. 1665, m. Elizabeth Calkins; John, b. 1667, m. Experience Abel;
1 CONT William, b. 1670, d. 1759, m. Anne Bushnell; Thomas, b. 1672, m. Mary
1 CONT Backus; Jabez, b. 1677, m. Elizabeth Bushnell. The descendants of the
1 CONT five sons of Samuel Hyde in 1779 showed upwards of twenty families of
1 CONT Hydes, comprising 150 persons, in the town plot and western part of
1 CONT Norwich. 
1 CONT
1 CONT Hermon Alfred Kelley, Kelley Family History,  (Privately Printed. Cleveland, Cuyahoga Co., OH. 1897.).
0 @N6000000003796004621@ NOTE Hyde Family Genealogy
1 CONT http://www.renderplus.com/hartgen/htm/hyde.htm
1 CONT 17.Samuel Hyde - was born about 1637 in Hartford, CT and died Jul 1677 in Norwich, CT . He was the son of William Hyde.
1 CONT Samuel married Jane Lee Jun 1659 in Saybrook, CT. Jane was born on 12 Sep 1640 in England. She was the daughter of Thomas Lee and Phoebe Brown. She died on 12 Jan 1722/1723 in Lebanon, New London, CT .
1 CONT
1 CONT Samuel - is reckoned among the first proprietors of Norwich, as is likewise his father.
1 CONT
1 CONT The descendants of the five sons of Samuel Hyde in 1779 showed updards of twenty families of Hydes, comprising 150 persons in the town plot and western part of Norwich.
1 CONT
1 CONT "Samuel and Jann (Lee) Hyde are also the ancestors of Grover Cleveland, President of the United States. Their eldest son, John Hyde, who married experience abel, had a son James, known as Capt. James Hyde, who married Sarah Marsha
1 CONC ll. They in turn had a daughter, Abiah Hyde, who married Rev. Aaron Cleveland. Their son, William Cleavelamd and his wife Margaret Falley, were the grand-parents of Grover Cleveland."
1 CONT
1 CONT ( from A genealogical History of the Kelley family) (Sources: - 5 (pg 301) - 6)
1 CONT Children: (Quick Family Chart)
1 CONT i. John Hyde was born Dec 1667 in Norwich, CT and died on 26 Jul 1727 in Norwich, CT . See #18. below.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Hyde Family Genealogy
1 CONT http://www.renderplus.com/hartgen/htm/hyde.htm
1 CONT 18.John Hyde - was born Dec 1667 in Norwich, CT and died on 26 Jul 1727 in Norwich, CT . He was the son of Samuel Hyde and Jane Lee.
1 CONT John married Experience Abell. Experience was born Dec 1674 in Norwich, CT. She was the daughter of Sergt. Caleb Abell and Margaret Post. She died on 24 Oct 1763 in Norwich, CT .
1 CONT
1 CONT John - was a farmer and in 1719 bought a farm from Nathenial Backus at Wawecus Hill which remained in the hands of his descendants until 1859.
1 CONT
1 CONT President Grover Cleaveland is a lineal descendant of John and Experiance (Abell) Hyde. (Sources: - 5 - 7 (pg 58) )
1 CONT Children: (Quick Family Chart)
1 CONT i. John Hyde was born on 5 Dec 1698 and died on 22 Oct 1762 .
1 CONT ii. Experience Hyde was born on 7 Sep 1700 in Norwich, New London, Connecticut and died on 30 Sep 1753 . See #19. below.
1 CONT iii. Capt. James Hyde See #20. below.
0 @N6000000003076498454@ NOTE []
1 CONT
1 CONT From The History of Norwich, page 188, "John Hyde, the second son of the proprietor Samuel, married Experience Abel.  He lived upon a farm on Wawekus Hill.  Though he himself died at the age of 60, his relict lived to be nearly 90
1 CONC , and their family of nine children all lived to be heads of families, six of them ranging in age from 77 to 90 years at their decease."
