0 @N6000000007418011443@ NOTE Lieut. Governor and Judge of Rhode Island.He m. 2nd Joanna Jenks, Sep.26,1 754, who d. Mar.30,1757; m. 3rd Ruth (Phil lips) Edwards of Marblehea d, a descendant of Rev. George Phillips of Water town, Mass; she d. at Tau nton, Bris
1 CONC tol, Mass. Mar.19,1809, aged 74.
1 CONT ========================NICHOLAS TILLINGHAST, He was a merchant; town cle rk of Providence  in 175 4, and probably some years before and after tha t; was a Judge of  one of t he courts, probably C. C. P. In 1777, he was i mprisone
1 CONC d a few days, for ha ving in his possession a proclamation of Lo rd Howe, and refusing to say h ow  he came by it. From some papers relati ng the affair, it is supposed th at he had  it from his brother. He beca me a follower of R
1 CONC obert Sandeman, w ho came from  Scotland, and was the fo under in this country of a sect call ed Sandemanians; the  same that we re called Glassites in Scotland. About t he close of the war, or perha ps  before, he moved to Taunto
1 CONC n, Bristol, Mas s., where he d. Feb. 26, 179 7, aged 70  yrs. 9 m. He was Postmaster of Tau nton, during his several la tter years. Although  not educated in a colleg e, he was a fine scholar, w ell versed in the Latin language, a
1 CONC nd in the li terature of the da y. He m. (1st) SUSAN DYER, who  probably d. very soo n, s. p. He m. (2d ), Sept. 26, 1754, JOANNA ISACKS, who  d. Mar. 30, 175 7, leaving 2 chi l. He m. (3d), Feb. 11, 1762, wid. RUTH (Phillips)  ED
1 CONC WARD S, then ag ed 27 yrs. She d. in Taunton, Nov. 19, 1809, aged 74  yrs. 5 chi l., vi z. [the 2 children of his 2d wife not given]:
1 CONT (Gen. of Watertown, by Bond, p.720)
